ement Manager operating in the SAS NMS, is not in the NOC NMS.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9435369372367859, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(567.5468749999999), np.float64(1678.901611328125)), (np.float64(567.5468749999999), np.float64(1980.6086197916663)), (np.float64(2628.245361328125), np.float64(1980.6086197916663)), (np.float64(2628.245361328125), np.float64(1678.901611328125))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 42, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': 'b8ddaceff950f0c5f4b2e3b34ff4cad8', 'category': 'ListItem', 'element_id': '27bfe40a2ad040b2c9b0fd8202cea25e'}, page_content='• External Access Portal (EAP) NMS — describes the Pulse EAP system that resides outside of the primary NMS system, but supports controlled access to the primary NMS via the EAP NMS Proxy. Each EAP instance is responsible for providing limited NMS functionality to users and systems that are external to the service provider, including secondary service providers and subscribers.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9314294457435608, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(562.6926879882812), np.float64(2024.8802490234375)), (np.float64(562.6926879882812), np.float64(2262.166015625)), (np.float64(2599.135986328125), np.float64(2262.166015625)), (np.float64(2599.135986328125), np.float64(2024.8802490234375))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pd