35bb7ac58b478170491eb422f84a36e0'}, page_content='The following terms describe components of the space segment and how they relate to the Velocity Over-the-Air (OTA) system.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9534516334533691, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(567.5468749999999), np.float64(2491.304931640625)), (np.float64(567.5468749999999), np.float64(2857.3388671875)), (np.float64(2637.659536458333), np.float64(2857.3388671875)), (np.float64(2637.659536458333), np.float64(2491.304931640625))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 47, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': 'f0c2dc6ec0719a254cf67c2e7f97ebdf', 'category': 'ListItem', 'element_id': '44868bce35e2c98140b9d53bc37dc6f0'}, page_content="• Beam — Each satellite provides a collection of beams that are characterized by their footprint on the earth's surface. Depending on the satellite, the beam may have the same or different footprints for the uplink (toward the satellite) and downlink (toward the ground). A terminal must be within a beam to enter the satellite network. At any time a given beam may have zero or more associated channels. If a beam is assigned zero channels, it is unusable by terminals and is sometimes referred to as a dark beam."), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9542219042778015, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(562.9481201171875), np.float64(2899.374267578125)), (np.float64(562.9481201171875), np.float64(3322.275286458333)), (np.float64(2609.44287109375), np.float64(3322.275286458333)), (np.float64(2609.44287109375), np.float64(2899.374267578125))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 47, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': 'f0c2dc6ec0719a254cf67c2e7f97ebdf', 'category': 'ListItem', 'element_id': 'a3674ae9bb9e3aa70df6e5e15fea1b2f'}, page_content='• Channel — A satellite also provides channels and associates those channels with beams. A channel is bidirectional bandwidth in both the feeder link and the user link. It has an uplink and downlink frequency range for both. A channel is either associated with exactly one beam, or it is unused. A specific channel contains uplink and downlink carriers that form one or more iNets. The bandwidth of a channel is the sum of the bandwidth of the iNets it contains. Channels in different beams may use the same frequencies. Where beam footprints overlap, the assignment of channels to beams must'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(353.6458333333333), np.float64(3514.3013281249996)), (np.float64(353.6458333333333), np.float64(3562.900286458333)), (np.float64(1659.7896279566144), np.float64(3562.900286458333)), (np.float64(1659.7896279566144), np.float64(3514.3013281249996))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 47, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': 'f0c2dc6ec0719a254cf67c2e7f97ebdf', 'category': 'UncategorizedText', 'element_