e physical location—in other words, in a teleport.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.947075605392456, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(568.1919555664062), np.float64(655.9679947916666)), (np.float64(568.1919555664062), np.float64(952.6757202148438)), (np.float64(2604.044953125), np.float64(952.6757202148438)), (np.float64(2604.044953125), np.float64(655.9679947916666))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 51, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': '57b1f6fb64c455440de03c88d3f49360', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': '61ccaafc8e463c297fc2c929b123d77e'}, page_content='A SAS site supports a single satellite within a satellite network. This type of site provides the network interface between the IP network of the backbone network and the radio frequency (RF) links to a satellite. The space segment configuration can be scaled up by adding beams and channels to an existing satellite. Likewise, the supporting SAS can be scaled up, using additional line cards and/or possibly additional servers.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.7511181235313416, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(1046.12451171875), np.float64(2447.876953125)), (np.float64(1046.12451171875), np.float64(2497.040911458333)), (np.float64(2145.322854310781), np.float64(2497.040911458333)), (np.float64(2145.322854310781), np.float64(2447.876953125))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40',