eeb9', 'category': 'Title', 'element_id': 'c00105c477467a1b79eec0dab2877de4'}, page_content='1.3.1.2 CDC and RF Gateway Site Architecture'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9509056210517883, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(565.2640991210938), np.float64(502.8429947916665)), (np.float64(565.2640991210938), np.float64(923.3169531250002)), (np.float64(2590.343994140625), np.float64(923.3169531250002)), (np.float64(2590.343994140625), np.float64(502.8429947916665))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 52, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': 'c00105c477467a1b79eec0dab2877de4', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': '645451ec53be1b0b12c22dc6b0e94ab3'}, page_content='Using the CDC architecture, Service Providers can consolidate Packet Processing (PP) func- tions at a data center, typically within a metropolitan location, instead of within the foot- print of a satellite feeder-link. The RF gateway functions are maintained at one or more geographically remote locations. This arrangement places the hub and line cards at a site referred to as an “RF Gateway” site, and the PP and management functions at a “CDC site". As seen in the diagram, from one PP function in a central data center, this architecture sup- ports satellites having multiple feeder-links.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.6290104389190674, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(715.1363525390625), np.float64(2605.2127864583335)), (np.float64(715.1363525390625), np.float64(2653.8117447916666)), (np.float64(2471.04296875), np.float64(2653.8117447916666)), (np.float64(2471.04296875), np.float64(2605.2127864583335))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 52, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'category': 'FigureCaption', 'element_id': '98639e3da63e1e849a98b05e8312c1aa'}, page_content='Figure 1-5. Central Data Center and Radio Frequency Gateway Architecture'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9453520774841309, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(567.6304321289062), np.float64(2707.004638671875)), (np.float64(567.6304321289062), np.float64(3129.0461197916666)), (np.float64(2582.2793281249997), np.float64(3129.0461197916666)), (np.float64(2582.2793281249997), np.float64(2707.004638671875))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 52, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': '68df787dfc1f4cd815b252a37c6a83d1'}, page_content='Since a major characteristic of the CDC architecture is that the RF Gateway is located away from the Protocol Processors, across a WAN, the Velocity system also introduces mitigation that enables the system to tolerate the effects of latency, jitter, packet loss, and packet reordering for both control and data traffic exchanged by the PP and line cards. The same features and functions available in the traditional SAS are available, while accommodating terrestrial delay, jitter, packet loss and reordering between RF Gateways and the Data Center.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9379456639289856, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(568.75), np.float64(3175.2388281249996)), (np.float64(568.75), np.float64(3347.7961197916666)), (np.float64(2541.2637031249997), np.float64(3347.7961197916666)), (np.float64(2541.2637031249997), np.float64(3175.2388281249996))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 52, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': 'f7fb794c2092c6b131d813ffd63cf860'}, page_content='The CDC and RF Gateway architecture also supports Velocity system high availability. Site redundancy and switchover, with no single point of failure, are provided for both the RF Gateways and the CDC itself. Rain diversity switchover is accomplished through an RF'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(353.6458333333333), np.float64(3514.3013281249996)), (np.float64(353.6458333333333), np.float64(3562.900286458333)), (np.float64(404.59766455135417), np.float64(3562.900286458333)), (np.float64(404.59766455135417), np.float64(3514.3013281249996))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 52, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'category': 'Un