ea14993fae7e18e0380fea87b7b2', 'category': 'UncategorizedText', 'element_id': '1ba73b7348ed7ad64fd5924075c39c9f'}, page_content='•'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9336169362068176, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(575.02587890625), np.float64(400.7596614583332)), (np.float64(575.02587890625), np.float64(635.8185424804688)), (np.float64(2620.40478515625), np.float64(635.8185424804688)), (np.float64(2620.40478515625), np.float64(400.7596614583332))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 58, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': '1237ea14993fae7e18e0380fea87b7b2', 'category': 'ListItem', 'element_id': 'f3382a1944b526579f3e9ecf9581c62b'}, page_content='Antenna Control Unit (ACU) — The antenna control unit connects to the satellite router over OpenAMIP. It provides geo-location information to the satellite router, points the antenna at the satellite, and performs related functions such as providing status and, in some terminals, muting the transmitter when off-pointed or blocked.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9340560436248779, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(559.4468383789062), np.float64(681.4888281249998)), (np.float64(559.4468383789062), np.float64(916.0252864583334)), (np.float64(2581.24609375), np.float64(916.0252864583334)), (np.float64(2581.24609375), np.float64(681.4888281249998))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 58, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': '1237ea14993fae7e18e0380fea87b7b2', 'category': 'ListItem', 'element_id': 'ed82a483ea75266897d535aedbd1c6e7'}, page_content='• Built-In Ethernet Switch — Some satellite routers contain an Ethernet switch, which provides Ethernet interfaces that can be configured either as access or trunk ports. An access port carries the traffic of a single VLAN, whereas a trunk carries traffic for multiple VLANs.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.8741005063056946, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(311.1043395996094), np.float64(1010.041666666667)), (np.float64(311.1043395996094), np.float64(1097.541666666667)), (np.float64(1864.3082214166664), np.float64(1097.541666666667)), (np.float64(1864.3082214166664), np.float64(1010.041666666667))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 58, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'category': 'Title', 'element_id': '2b4ec6b46d293f032142111ad0ddd1c6'}, page_content='1.4 Velocity Network Architectures'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9487425684928894, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(565.8170166015625), np.float64(1140.8638281249998)), (np.float64(565.8170166015625), np.float64(1437.3794531249998)), (np.float64(2622.284423828125), np.float64(1437.3794531249998)), (np.float64(2622.284423828125), np.float64(1140.8638281249998))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 58, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': '2b4ec6b46d293f032142111ad0ddd1c6', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': '7391d14dde6d1595b9879016be4a71c4'}, page_content='The Velocity network is an IP network that comprises a terrestrial backbone network, backbone network peering sites/POPs (points of presence), Satellite Access Station sites, a Network Operating Center site (NOC), and fixed or mobile Satellite Terminals. The terrestrial backbone network has interfaces to the Internet, to customers’ private networks, and to network control equipment.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9355636239051819, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(564.2417602539062), np.float64(1483.572161458333)), (np.float64(564.2417602539062), np.float64(1594.150286458333)), (np.float64(2615.596435546875), np.float64(1594.150286458333)), (np.float64(2615.596435546875), np.float64(1483.572161458333))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 58, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': '2b4ec6b46d293f032142111ad0ddd1c6', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': 'e769d6e4ec5d21f5b24f60f889e6345e'}, page_content='The following diagram shows the architectural components of the Velocity network, in which the Velocity IP network is logically organized into three routing domains.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/