', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 79, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': '484d6cb6717f16c72bfe50b437c881ec', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': '2db297e86bb8094cf3931b2366ec2ab1'}, page_content='Satellite virtual networks (SVNs) allow the satellite operator to implement service provider and subscriber business models by extending a private network across the shared satellite network so that the subscriber’s remote devices can send and receive data as though they were directly connected to their private network.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9506740570068359, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(568.3898315429688), np.float64(809.0929947916666)), (np.float64(568.3898315429688), np.float64(1229.566953125)), (np.float64(2632.915771484375), np.float64(1229.566953125)), (np.float64(2632.915771484375), np.float64(809.0929947916666))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 79, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': '484d6cb6717f16c72bfe50b437c881ec', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': '541cc4cc540a8bedc969c13e20883f06'}, page_content='An SVN is analogous to a terrestrial Virtual Private Network (VPN). Both provide connectivity across a common network infrastructure while segregating the traffic of each private network, and providing each with a separate and independent IP address space. This method is called “virtual routing” in an iDirect network. Both the PP and the satellite router maintain logically separate virtual routing tables in a manner similar to router vendors’ Virtual Routing and Forwarding (VRF) features. The combination of iDirect virtual routing and VRF allows the same IP address to be used by multiple SVNs.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9145106673240662, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(568.75), np.float64(1275.759661458333)), (np.float64(568.75), np.float64(1386.337786458333)), (np.float64(2636.2012031249997), np.float64(1386.337786458333)), (np.float64(2636.2012031249997), np.float64(1275.759661458333))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 79, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': '484d6cb6717f16c72bfe50b437c881ec', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': 'd9a0a4267220608c8278eb3a5cfa8c43'}, page_content='One possible scenario of how an end-user’s SVN could be implemented by a satellite operator, is shown here.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.57188481092453, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(1167.578125), np.float64(2002.982177734375)), (np.float64(1167.578125), np.float64(2057.11474609375)), (np.float64(2027.3680419921875), np.float64(2057.11474609375)), (np.float64(2027.3680419921875), np.float64(2002.982177734375))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 79, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'category': 'FigureCaption', 'element_id': '71856781cc0fedbdbc64805584ad6a59'}, page_content='Figure 2-10. Satellite Virtual Network'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9540330767631531, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(568.75), np.float64(2110.6554947916666)), (np.float64(568.75), np.float64(2593.1086197916666)), (np.float64(2629.5657864583336), np.float64(2593.1086197916666)), (np.float64(2629.5657864583336), np.float64(2110.6554947916666))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 79, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': '97adb6aa2bbb4eb6d5e58552af210a22'}, page_content='This SVN extends from the subscriber’s private network on the left, through an MPLS (Multi- Protocol Label Switching) backbone network via an MPLS pseudo wire (PW), into and through the Satellite Access Station (SAS) including the PP, and onto and through the satellite router. At the access router the MPLS PW is terminated and mapped to a unique 802.1q-compliant VLAN tag that has the same value as the SVN’s ID. This tag is maintained through the SAS and over the air (OTA) routing domains to the satellite router. The service provider may choose to use the same VLAN tag value on the terminal LAN, or to configure the satellite router to map it to an arbitrary local VLAN tag value.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.940171480178833, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(567.0204467773438), np.float64(2639.3013281249996)), (np.float64(567.0204467773438), np.float64(2873.837786458333)), (np.float64(2607.201904296875), np.float64(2873.837786458333)), (np.float64(2607.201904296875), np.float64(2639.3013281249996))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 79, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': 'ff06b2f61fa25e98b8597ddabc27244f'}, page_content='Unicast traffic may be carried upstream or downstream within an SVN — for example, from a subscriber’s terrestrial network to equipment on the terminal LAN or vice versa. Multicast traffic may only be carried downstream within an SVN — for example, to equipment on the terminal LAN.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9361905455589294, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(568.75), np.float64(2920.030494791666)), (np.float64(568.75), np.float64(3092.587786458333)), (np.float64(2527.772216796875), np.float64(3092.587786458333)), (np.float64(2527.772216796875), np.float64(2920.030494791666))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 79, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': 'ca60a901ec9c38a627f508824a7b080c'}, page_content='Multiple SVNs may be present on a single satellite router. The GQoS service plans (SSPCs) associated with the satellite router may apply to a single SVN, or to multiple SVNs on the same satellite router.'), Document(metadata={'sou