ory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': 'e2f88a9b7b2067d4151856d7b1361967', 'category': 'Title', 'element_id': '1ac257ee30e888a6159db5be4436a0d4'}, page_content='2.3.1 Velocity Layer 3 Routing Operations'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.8912403583526611, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(568.75), np.float64(506.4888281249999)), (np.float64(568.75), np.float64(555.095703125)), (np.float64(2626.09033203125), np.float64(555.095703125)), (np.float64(2626.09033203125), np.float64(506.4888281249999))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 83, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': '1ac257ee30e888a6159db5be4436a0d4', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': 'f127747c1666261dcbe2853882bd51de'}, page_content='Layer 3 routing configuration and operations, in Velocity, are outlined in the following points:'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.942882239818573, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(560.9933471679688), np.float64(601.0013427734375)), (np.float64(560.9933471679688), np.float64(898.8739013671875)), (np.float64(2638.414794921875), np.float64(898.8739013671875)), (np.float64(2638.414794921875), np.float64(601.0013427734375))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 83, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': '1ac257ee30e888a6159db5be4436a0d4', 'category': 'ListItem', 'element_id': 'fa096dfea3f6aa521b37bb4293fa4cff'}, page_content='• When initially configuring the SAS, the service provider configures the BGP peers on the access routers and PPs , as well as an OTA BGP Peer template that defines parameters common to all terminal BGP sessions on all SVNs. Once this configuration is done, the access router and PP establish BGP sessions, begin exchanging route advertisements, and the PP is ready to peer with terminals.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(567.5468749999999), np.float64(943.9888281249998)), (np.float64(567.5468749999999), np.float64(992.5877864583334)), (np.float64(607.6595364583333), np.float64(992.5877864583334)), (np.float64(607.6595364583333), np.float64(943.9888281249998))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 83, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': '1ac257ee30e888a6159db5be4436a0d4', 'category': 'UncategorizedText', 'element_id': '6d715c7993fa7e661a2be16d878b9430'}, page_content='•'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9218922257423401, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(589.8920288085938), np.float64(943.9888281249998)), (np.float64(589.8920288085938), np.float64(1055.268798828125)), (np.float64(2650.697998046875), np.float64(1055.268798828125)), (np.float64(2650.697998046875), np.float64(943.9888281249998))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 83, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': '1ac257ee30e888a6159db5be4436a0d4', 'category': 'ListItem', 'element_id': '30f86de4974869fa2da08c68c21ba969'}, page_content='During terminal configuration, the service provider or subscriber configures a similar OTA BGP template for each SVN defined on that terminal.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9517989158630371, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(567.5468749999999), np.float64(1099.697021484375)), (np.float64(567.5468749999999), np.float64(1459.2544531249998)), (np.float64(2613.9251614583336), np.float64(1459.2544531249998)), (np.float64(2613.9251614583336), np.float64(1099.697021484375))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 83, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': '1ac257ee30e888a6159db5be4436a0d4', 'category': 'ListItem', 'element_id': '7e5b7459610643c552d1202861c3a457'}, page_content='• When a satellite router acquires into the satellite network, the PP provides it with detailed configuration information via Dynamic File Options Exchange (DFOE). This information includes the BGP OTA Peer template and the identity of the PP BGP peer within each SVN configured on the satellite router, as well as all options keys other than those required for the satellite router to acquire into the satellite network and those needed for it to function in the IP network.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9519639015197754, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(567.5468749999999), np.float64(1500.7618408203125)), (np.float64(567.5468749999999), np.float64(1925.9211197916663)), (np.float64(2627.1595364583336), np.float64(1925.9211197916663)), (np.float64(2627.1595364583336), np.float64(1500.7618408203125))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 83, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': '1ac257ee30e888a6159db5be4436a0d4', 'category': 'ListItem', 'element_id': '8bdb8744fd21603010814d17d4449b9c'}, page_content='• Once the BGP peering relationship is established, the PP and satellite router begins exchanging route advertisements. The satellite router advertises the route table to directly-connected subnets, as well as any subnets it learns via BGP sessions with routers on the terminal LAN. The PP then advertises these subnets to the access router, which then advertises them to the backbone network, and hence into the subscriber’s private network. IP packets from equipment on the subscriber’s private network can then be routed to equipment on the terminal network.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9341071248054504, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(567.5468749999999), np.float64(1972.1138281249998)), (np.float64(567.5468749999999), np.float64(2144.6711197916666)), (np.float64(2624.534536458333), np.float64(2144.6711197916666)), (np.float64(2624.534536458333), np.float64(1972.1138281249998))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 83, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': '1ac257ee30e888a6159db5be4436a0d4', 'category': 'ListItem', 'element_id': 'ef637d0cf0264062894eabe465f50d1f'}, page_content='• Similarly, the PP has already learned routes to the subscriber’s private network from the access router and advertises them to the satellite router. IP packets from equipment on the terminal network can then be routed to equipment on the terminal network.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9178261160850525, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(568.75), np.float64(2190.8638281249996)), (np.float64(568.75), np.float64(2301.4419531249996)), (np.float64(2622.585205078125), np.float64(2301.4419531249996)), (np.float64(2622.585205078125), np.float64(2190.8638281249996))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 83, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': '1ac257ee30e888a6159db5be4436a0d4', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': '467877408f710c97318353f50b94a401'}, page_content='The PP also will not deliver traffic from one SVN to another. If desired, the satellite operator may implement gateways between SVNs within the backbone network.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.8838788866996765, 'i