cation/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 88, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': '56c01d59bdb498cf508ef1b75a290050', 'category': 'Title', 'element_id': '11db1f326917f05e379ee989c5b7e288'}, page_content='2.5 Velocity Subscriber Networks and Internet'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9494670033454895, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(568.75), np.float64(528.3638281249998)), (np.float64(568.75), np.float64(948.8377864583334)), (np.float64(2622.6751614583336), np.float64(948.8377864583334)), (np.float64(2622.6751614583336), np.float64(528.3638281249998))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 88, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': '11db1f326917f05e379ee989c5b7e288', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': '6d71ab0b717194b10588ee867c9f9f30'}, page_content='The physical backbone network also provides interfaces to each subscriber’s private terrestrial network. Each of these networks is a peer network connected to the backbone network via a physical interface and protocol agreed to between the satellite operator and the subscriber. A subscriber’s network will typically have multiple interfaces to the backbone network for redundancy, and peer to the backbone network using BGP. No iDirect equipment is installed in the subscriber’s private terrestrial network. Similarly, the backbone network typically connects to the Internet via multiple BGP peering arrangements.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.90037602186203, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(295.54638671875), np.float64(1042.854166666667)), (np.float64(295.54638671875), np.float64(1130.354166666667)), (np.float64(1638.138671875), np.float64(1130.354166666667)), (np.float64(1638.138671875), np.float64(1042.854166666667))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 88, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': '56c01d59bdb498cf508ef1b75a290050', 'category': 'Title', 'element_id': '8a15332845ff5cc5cb6e53cb1b23eacc'}, page_content='2.6 The Velocity SAS Network'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9417518377304077, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(568.75), np.float64(1173.6763281249998)), (np.float64(568.75), np.float64(1346.2336197916668)), (np.float64(2578.0866197916666), np.float64(1346.2336197916668)), (np.float64(2578.0866197916666), np.float64(1173.6763281249998))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 88, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': '8a15332845ff5cc5cb6e53cb1b23eacc', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': 'f0bc123883e119cc057814879fe890c7'}, page_content='The SAS provides IP connectivity to the satellite routers within the footprint of the satellite associated with the SAS. The SAS is required to meet high-availability requirements and therefore has been architected with redundancy that provides no single point of failure.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.944346010684967, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(567.9032592773438), np.float64(1392.4263281249998)), (np.float64(567.9032592773438), np.float64(1750.9211197916663)), (np.float64(2622.419953125), np.float64(1750.9211197916663)), (np.float64(2622.419953125), np.float64(1392.4263281249998))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 88, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': '8a15332845ff5cc5cb6e53cb1b23eacc', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': 'fbd45256439b855e9729454fbcb6e992'}, page_content='The PP components function as IP routers and send and receive standards-compliant IP packets and dynamic routing updates to the backbone network, and hence to subscriber terrestrial networks. Similarly, the PP exchanges IP packets and routing updates on the OTA interface with satellite routers located in the satellite’s footprint. The SAS access routers are BGP peers of the PPs in every SVN. Likewise, satellite routers function as IP routers and are BGP peers of the PPs.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9280563592910767, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(565.85107421875), np.float64(1797.1138281249998)), (np.float64(565.85107421875), np.float64(1907.6919531249998)), (np.float64(2601.689453125), np.float64(1907.6919531249998)), (np.float64(2601.689453125), np.float64(1797.1138281249998))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 88, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': '8a15332845ff5cc5cb6e53cb1b23eacc', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': 'bb07fae090c88a46b3cc2431c3e1f8a8'}, page_content='The line cards interface with the RF subsystem over an L-Band interface for the transmission and reception of all RF signals.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.8907552361488342, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(568.75), np.float64(1953.884661458333)), (np.float64(568.75), np.float64(2002.4836197916663)), (np.float64(2392.29443359375), np.float64(2002.4836197916663)), (np.float64(2392.29443359375), np.float64(1953.884661458333))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 88, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': '8a15332845ff5cc5cb6e53cb1b23eacc', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': '2d07d474d86f9c7fd88726d1b011b154'}, page_content='All SAS components function as IP hosts for management and administrative traffic.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.8561378717422485, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(568.75), np.float64(2093.792421875)), (np.float64(568.75), np.float64(2161.8601302083334)), (np.float64(2543.7834111582806), np.float64(2161.8601302083334)), (np.float64(2543.7834111582806), np.float64(2093.792421875))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 88, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': '56c01d59bdb498cf508ef1b75a290050', 'category': 'Title', 'element_id': '94006285eefbae5b7b3527389501b05c'}, page_content='2.6.1 Velocity SAS Network — Layer 1 Physical Architecture'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9495840072631836, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(568.75), np.float64(2203.378173828125)), (np.float64(568.75), np.float64(2563.941953125)), (np.float64(2608.857177734375), np.float64(2563.941953125)), (np.float64(2608.857177734375), np.float64(2203.378173828125))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 88, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': '94006285eefbae5b7b3527389501b05c', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': 'e533f43eaf38dc9c8f5d0a4cbe278844'}, page_content='The SAS LAN is architected with a high performance switching fabric. The SAS LAN relies on redundant SAS switches and access routers as well as key features of that networking equipment to provide a highly available service. These features include Virtual Port Channel (VPC), Link Aggregation Control Protocol (LACP), Port Channel, etc. For a more complete description, including redundancy and automatic failover for Velocity components, see SAS Site Redundancy on page 191 and its subsections.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_