tiple RF Gateways are used for a satellite, a CMS is required. (An alternative approach, using Two-Line Element Sets (TLE) was introduced in the RF Gateway Redundancy Feature in Velocity 4.0.) The CMS provides measurement information that is used by the PP to ensure the downstream NCR timestamps agree at the satellite. This is what allows Seamless Beam Switch of a remote terminal between different beams on the same satellite landing at different RF Gateways. In this configuration, PP LCC will not activate iNets until timing information is available.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.5848742127418518, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(1203.1336669921875), np.float64(3036.6611328125)), (np.float64(1203.1336669921875), np.float64(3087.665911458333)), (np.float64(1998.7042236328125), np.float64(3087.665911458333)), (np.float64(1998.7042236328125), np.float64(3036.6611328125))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 98, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'category': 'FigureCaption', 'element_id': '5e9dd14babaf2e3b3a586a3cf3b7fa54'}, page_content='Figure 2-25. Multiple RF Gateways'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.8439289331436157, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(557.3984985351562), np.float64(3142.4263281249996)), (np.float64(557.3984985351562), np.float64(3253.004453125)), (np.float64(2575.0241197916666), np.float64(3253.004453125)), (np.float64(2575.0241197916666), np.float64(3142.4263281249996))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_wid