568.75), np.float64(506.4888281249999)), (np.float64(568.75), np.float64(741.0252864583334)), (np.float64(2634.91748046875), np.float64(741.0252864583334)), (np.float64(2634.91748046875), np.float64(506.4888281249999))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 108, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': 'eb8af96e305543a92b4a784b212f5568', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': 'c191c5d75954895ada95508bddd724af'}, page_content='Header compression PEP is used to reduce the bandwidth usage of UDP and RTP (Real-Time Protocol) packets. UDP packets have 28 bytes of header overhead in every packet transmitted over IPv4 networks. VoIP (Voice over Internet Protocol) packets in RTP can be compressed even more as they have an additional 12-byte header.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9323853850364685, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(568.75), np.float64(787.2179947916666)), (np.float64(568.75), np.float64(1021.7544531250002)), (np.float64(2621.763703125), np.float64(1021.7544531250002)), (np.float64(2621.763703125), np.float64(787.2179947916666))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 108, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': 'eb8af96e305543a92b4a784b212f5568', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': '989f706bec70beb4c9c00aa16580092c'}, page_content='cRTP significantly reduces bandwidth usage over the air. UDP header compression follows the specification in RFC 3095/3545, Compressing IP/UDP/RTP Headers for Low-Speed Serial Links. This RFC defines both cRTP (header compression for RTP packets) and UDP header compression (for other UDP packets).'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9231690168380737, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(567.9055786132812), np.float64(1067.947161458333)), (np.float64(567.9055786132812), np.float64(1178.5252864583335)), (np.float64(2480.638671875), np.float64(1178.5252864583335)), (np.float64(2480.638671875), np.float64(1067.947161458333))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 108, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': 'eb8af96e305543a92b4a784b212f5568', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': 'bb862e5de240fa613d13d53335d4ea79'}, page_content='Header compression is performed only on packets which have a length below a certain threshold. Above that threshold, bandwidth savings with compression is not significant.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9421698451042175, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(662.9013671875), np.float64(1217.4263281249998)), (np.float64(662.9013671875), np.float64(1761.8586197916663)), (np.float64(2584.211619791666), np.float64(1761.8586197916663)), (np.float64(2584.211619791666), np.float64(1217.4263281249998))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 108, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': 'eb8af96e305543a92b4a784b212f5568', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': '1960b20ca89b53340e3cf2c2f929d049'}, page_content='Compressed Real-Time Protocol (cRTP)—The satellite operator can enable cRTP to significantly reduce the bandwidth requirements of VoIP flows. cRTP is implemented using standard header compression techniques. It allows for better use of real-time bandwidth, especially for RTP-based applications that use large numbers of small packets, since the 40-byte IP/UDP/RTP header often accounts for a significant fraction of the total packet length. iDirect has implemented a standard header compression scheme including heuristic-based RTP detection with negative cache support for misidentified UDP streams. For example, G729 voice RTP results in less than 12 Kbps (uncompressed is 24 Kbps).'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9150488972663879, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(299.1293640136719), np.float64(1855.875)), (np.float64(299.1293640136719), np.float64(1945.2000732421875)), (np.float64(2173.102783203125), np.float64(1945.2000732421875)), (np.float64(2173.102783203125), np.float64(1855.875))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 108, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': '2a8c03e924d188d9bc354a8b2065f420', 'category': 'Title', 'element_id': '5441bc336299485c1fc4e8131db770c4'}, page_content='2.16 Velocity Routing and Control Protocols'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/