d': '53127e5a4b7d440153d42ee652690510', 'category': 'Title', 'element_id': '6c81c88dfaa502e052396473a4adf9c4'}, page_content='3.1.1 Acquisition Signaling Carriers (ASC)'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9482078552246094, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(564.1338500976562), np.float64(1367.650390625)), (np.float64(564.1338500976562), np.float64(1729.0461197916663)), (np.float64(2589.251220703125), np.float64(1729.0461197916663)), (np.float64(2589.251220703125), np.float64(1367.650390625))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 116, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': '6c81c88dfaa502e052396473a4adf9c4', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': 'fe39294bc6e338e3eacf3c6b64edeac2'}, page_content='The signaling carrier is a way to inform terminals of the current satellite network configuration — more specifically, beam footprint and or/and parameters such as outbound carrier frequency, symbol rate and/or polarization. The acquisition signaling carrier is a Velocity signaling carrier in which the SAS broadcasts the satellite configuration on a single satellite uplink, which the satellite in turn replicates on a number of downlinks in different beams. This signaling carrier has no return channel.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9463032484054565, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(563.0166015625), np.float64(1773.9647216796875)), (np.float64(563.0166015625), np.float64(2071.7544531249996)), (np.float64(2591.065786458333), np.float64(2071.7544531249996)), (np.float64(2591.065786458333), np.float64(1773.9647216796875))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 116, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': '6c81c88dfaa502e052396473a4adf9c4', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': '5288c59a1e5fb8d508a70ec48264fa0b'}, page_content='Terminals require this information in order to join (or come into) the satellite network. This information exchange is one-way (downstream only), and is necessary to allow satellite network operators to reconfigure their satellite. If a change in downstream carrier configuration, in terms of frequency or symbol rate, is not properly communicated to a terminal, it is likely to become stranded.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.8676623702049255, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(567.8129272460938), np.float64(2116.630615234375)), (np.float64(567.8129272460938), np.float64(2166.5461197916666)), (np.float64(2179.3837890625), np.float64(2166.5461197916666)), (np.float64(2179.3837890625), np.float64(2116.630615234375))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 116, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': '6c81c88dfaa502e052396473a4adf9c4', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': '129da5616822a9ea8f5e49586f9da6b0'}, page_content='There are several reasons that can lead to a change in carriers, including:'), Document(metadata={'source':