ication/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 125, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': '5068438b99415680a8ee8602a8a27dd3', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': '57043aaad1461707f47a463a5fa87329'}, page_content='Digital communication systems employ waveform pulse shaping using identical matched filters at the transmit and receive sides to limit the occupied bandwidth required by a carrier and to maximize the received signal-to-noise ratio (SNR). The matched filters used for linear modulation signals belong to a class of Nyquist filters having Raised-Cosine filter shapes with different carrier roll-off factors.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9366271495819092, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(567.2286376953125), np.float64(1315.8638281249998)), (np.float64(567.2286376953125), np.float64(1550.400286458333)), (np.float64(2559.439453125), np.float64(1550.400286458333)), (np.float64(2559.439453125), np.float64(1315.8638281249998))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 125, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': '5068438b99415680a8ee8602a8a27dd3', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': 'db7d0066a1da9504e022a0b4e4a28573'}, page_content='The roll-off factor of a digital filter defines how much more bandwidth the filter occupies than that of an ideal brick wall filter, which defines the theoretical minimum occupied bandwidth. This dictates the guard band requirement for the carrier. The DVB-S2 standard specifies roll-off factors of 20%, 25%, and 35%.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9486677646636963, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(563.5172119140625), np.float64(1596.5929947916663)), (np.float64(563.5172119140625), np.float64(1955.087786458333)), (np.float64(2601.2741197916666), np.float64(1955.087786458333)), (np.float64(2601.2741197916666), np.float64(1596.5929947916663))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 125, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': '5068438b99415680a8ee8602a8a27dd3', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': '33d05aaca438a7074b016845c9cc83bd'}, page_content='iDirect has reduced the DVB-S2 roll-off factor (and, therefore, the required carrier guard band) to as low as 5% of the carrier symbol rate. With a 5% roll-off factor, the transmitted spectrum more closely resembles the ideal brick wall spectrum with occupied bandwidth at 1.05 times the carrier symbol rate. Not all DVB-S2 carriers support a 5% guard band. Specifically, DVB-S2 carriers below 10 Msps require a guard band of at least 10%. In addition, guard bands of 10% or 5% require a minimum MODCOD of QPSK-1/2.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9096516370773315, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(568.75), np.float64(2043.134661458333)), (np.float64(568.75), np.float64(2106.3169531249996)), (np.float64(2267.78662109375), np.float64(2106.3169531249996)), (np.float64(2267.78662109375), np.float64(2043.134661458333))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 125, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'category': 'Title', 'element_id': '6b5312dc52ac9bfe8a57ced7bbf0a242'}, page_content='3.2.2.2 Guard Band Reduction for Improved Throughput'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9471395611763, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(565.0924682617188), np.float64(2150.759661458333)), (np.float64(565.0924682617188), np.float64(2447.275286458333)), (np.float64(2623.258494791666), np.float64(2447.275286458333)), (np.float64(2623.258494791666), np.float64(2150.759661458333))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 125, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': '6b5312dc52ac9bfe8a57ced7bbf0a242', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': 'dd119939d256cbe52e32b43fb71d1fa0'}, page_content='A lower bandwidth requirement between carriers makes it possible to fit a higher bit rate carrier into the same occupied bandwidth or to fit additional carriers into the same overall bandwidth. The example in this section shows how a lower guard band requirement can allow a satellite operator to increase the information rate of a DVB-S2 carrier without changing the occupied bandwidth and allotted power.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9286670088768005, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(813.318603515625), np.float64(2527.3955078125)), (np.float64(813.318603515625), np.float64(2833.861083984375)), (np.float64(2584.928955078125), np.float64(2833.861083984375)), (np.float64(2584.928955078125), np.float64(2527.3955078125))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 125, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': 'da8bfb7200dee84ad947cebd364fa0cc'}, page_content='NOTE: Increasing the information rate of existing carriers may affect the link budget of the satellite network. This is especially true for upstream carriers since uplink power control (UPC) will automatically increase the transmit power of the satellite terminals. Consult with the link budget provider prior to adjusting carrier configurations.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.939006507396698, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(564.5849609375), np.float64(2967.4263281249996)), (np.float64(564.5849609375), np.float64(3201.962786458333)), (np.float64(2633.784912109375), np.float64(3201.962786458333)), (np.float64(2633.784912109375), np.float64(2967.4263281249996))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 125, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': '1cfae6e7af914b5cb72a0ba54145a41d'}, page_content='3.2.2 shows the increase in information rate that can be achieved on a DVB-S2 downstream carrier by decreasing the guard band while holding the occupied bandwidth constant. The calculations were performed using the 8PSK-8/9 MODCOD. In the example, reducing the guard band from 20% to 5% of the symbol rate results in a 14.29% increase in information rate.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.45919016003608704, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(353.6458333333333), np.float64(3511.257080078125)), (np.float64(353.6458333333333), np.float64(3628.525286458333)), (np.float64(1945.850830078125), np.float64(3628.525286458333)), (np.float64(1945.850830078125), np.float64(3511.257080078125))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 125, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': '6911a657dbdeac1e992e915edd277dd4'}, page_content='ST Engineering iDirect Proprietary | Confidentiality: Public Technical Reference Guide | iDirect Velocity™ | T0001665 | Revision 1'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.2753419876098633, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(2570.3854166666665), np.float64(3514.3013281249996)), (np.float64(2570.3854166666665), np.float64(3562.900286458333)), (np.float64(2624.1318359375), np.float64(3562.900286458333)), (np.float64(2624.1318359375), np.float64(3514.3013281249996))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 125, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058