ent='Table 3-1. Increasing Information Rate by Reducing Guard Band'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9183716773986816, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(567.5301513671875), np.float64(1135.3221614583333)), (np.float64(567.5301513671875), np.float64(1198.5044531249996)), (np.float64(2117.152099609375), np.float64(1198.5044531249996)), (np.float64(2117.152099609375), np.float64(1135.3221614583333))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 126, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': '155839f1223290a6a930e6f325e2e5a6', 'category': 'Title', 'element_id': '7153e1b55cd15c1ac2b0d277bdafb989'}, page_content='3.2.2.3 Group Delay and Downstream Performance'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.948749303817749, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(568.6716918945312), np.float64(1242.947161458333)), (np.float64(568.6716918945312), np.float64(1849.3586197916663)), (np.float64(2576.177001953125), np.float64(1849.3586197916663)), (np.float64(2576.177001953125), np.float64(1242.947161458333))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 126, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': '7153e1b55cd15c1ac2b0d277bdafb989', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': '727dc789606946dc93ddc12a51501912'}, page_content='DVB-S2 waveform performance is affected on terminals when operated under channel conditions characterized by high transponder group delay. Such atypical conditions are encountered in single-carrier-per-transponder applications with certain transponder model types and to the extent symbol rate occupies the transponder bandwidth depending on the configured roll-off factor. When the symbol rate exceeds 75% of transponder bandwidth (18/27/40.5 Msps for 24/36/54 MHz transponders), customers are encouraged to check the cascaded IMUX (input multiplexer) and OMUX (output multiplexer) filter group delay of the transponder, usually available from the satellite operator. These plots or specifications capture the peak-to-peak ripple (in nanoseconds) of the group delay at different frequency offsets from the transponder center.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9456892609596252, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(568.75), np.float64(1899.197161458333)), (np.float64(568.75), np.float64(2195.712786458333)), (np.float64(2610.9384765625), np.float64(2195.712786458333)), (np.float64(2610.9384765625), np.float64(1899.197161458333))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 126, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': '7153e1b55cd15c1ac2b0d277bdafb989', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': '58b5be215e483d7f9b3df54429cea424'}, page_content='The demodulator handles the group delay levels with robust equalizers usually up to 1.5 sym- bol periods across symbol rate bandwidth with negligible SNR degradation. Group delay exceeding 1.5 symbols periods (i.e. approximately 43.8 ns peak-topeak based on the 34.285 Msps with 5% ROF carrier on a 36 MHz transponder) will result in noticeable SNR degradation and negatively affect link performance.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9281309247016907, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(568.75), np.float64(2245.5513281249996)), (np.float64(568.75), np.float64(2356.1294531249996)), (np.float64(2615.3623046875), np.float64(2356.1294531249996)), (np.float64(2615.3623046875), np.float64(2245.5513281249996))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 126, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': '7153e1b55cd15c1ac2b0d277bdafb989', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': '08ee567cebe3b0064d329afa6317f1c4'}, page_content='A group delay exceeding these limits usually requires symbol rate/roll-off factor reduction to keep away from the group delay edges for satisfying identified limits.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.8994476199150085, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(568.75), np.float64(2444.1763281249996)), (np.float64(568.75), np.float64(2507.358619791666)), (np.float64(2002.8238525390625), np.float64(2507.358619791666)), (np.float64(2002.8238525390625), np.float64(2444.1763281249996))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 126, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d