T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 128, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': 'c5cebbc8e455ddee967c45747b6feb99', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': 'acba20caf2e70a97d3d8183115df0cb9'}, page_content='The Velocity downstream carrier operation uses DVB-S2 with ACM. ACM enables each satellite terminal to operate at its most efficient coding and modulation scheme at any moment in time, depending on the location within the satellite contour, the antenna size, and the atmospheric conditions. The ACM algorithm evaluates current channel conditions through a return channel to determine the ideal modulation and FEC rate for each individual DVB-S2 frame and makes adjustments in real time.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9493582844734192, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(568.75), np.float64(933.0513281249998)), (np.float64(568.75), np.float64(1229.566953125)), (np.float64(2625.15185546875), np.float64(1229.566953125)), (np.float64(2625.15185546875), np.float64(933.0513281249998))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 128, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': 'c5cebbc8e455ddee967c45747b6feb99', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': '8524bb222950f35c8b345e8372370c28'}, page_content='The downstream carrier provides communication from the SAS to the satellite terminals or in the case of the CDC/RF GW architecture, from the RF Gateway to the satellite terminals. For each iNet, only one downstream carrier is present. Using time-division multiplexing (TDM), it is possible to allocate traffic for both individual (unicast) and multiple (multicast) satellite terminals in a single shared carrier.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9530842900276184, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(566.79052734375), np.float64(1275.759661458333)), (np.float64(566.79052734375), np.float64(1696.2336197916663)), (np.float64(2637.5137031249997), np.float64(1696.2336197916663)), (np.float64(2637.5137031249997), np.float64(1275.759661458333))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 128, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': 'c5cebbc8e455ddee967c45747b6feb99', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': '53271c65d311ecf1b3095ae14154e21c'}, page_content='The protocol processors at the SAS or at the CDC in the case of the CDC/RF Gateway architecture, use the Group Quality of Service (GQoS) configuration to determine which satellite terminals receive which TDM blocks. The information transmitted on the downstream carrier is broadcast to all satellite terminals, however, only the intended recipients receive it. This method is achieved by marking each IP packet, sent over the air, with the unique HDLC (high-level data link control) address of the targeted satellite terminal. The modems ignore packets that does not have its address.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.7207012176513672, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(1143.5777587890625), np.float64(2827.6086197916666)), (np.f