', 'element_id': '02a59243824a7bd593cf58f92f348542'}, page_content='The proprietary upstream iDirect waveform consists of short blocks of known symbols (pilots) distributed evenly throughout the burst as shown in the diagram.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9463089108467102, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(568.75), np.float64(1122.634661458333)), (np.float64(568.75), np.float64(1481.9849853515625)), (np.float64(2560.05224609375), np.float64(1481.9849853515625)), (np.float64(2560.05224609375), np.float64(1122.634661458333))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 133, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': '3352403fbaf470173c88ecde8256f4fa', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': '10c910d8cbf977a03af433e4275eed3e'}, page_content='The payload of each burst consists of a fixed 170-byte block coded using a 2D 16-State FEC code at rates published in the iDirect Velocity Link Budget Analysis Guide. The pilot structure is optimized to provide a frequency tolerance of up to 1.5% of the symbol rate across all modulation and FEC rate combinations. The C/N dynamic range and granularity permits the use of adaptive coding and modulation on the inbound channel by configuring heterogeneous inroute groups with multiple carriers.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.4005880355834961, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(961.0919189453125), np.float64(1713.177490234375)), (np.float64(961.0919189453125), np.float64(1767.9110107421875)), (np.float64(2238.5439453125), np.float64(1767.9110107421875)), (np.float64(2238.5439453125), np.float64(1713.177490234375))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 133, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'category': 'FigureCaption', 'element_id': '11befa41704627a8b41bdcbde7415718'}, page_content='Figure 3-12. TDMA Burst Format with Distributed Pilots'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.8633372783660889, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(562.8037109375), np.float64(1852.66796875)), (np.float64(562.8037109375), np.float64(1925.749267578125)), (np.float64(1379.7984619140625), np.float64(1925.749267578125)), (np.float64(1379.7984619140625), np.float64(1852.66796875))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 133, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'category': 'Title', 'element_id': 'dd5e25de715326d998ee74e241f8343f'}, page_content='3.4.2 Spread Spectrum'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9459488391876221, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(568.75), np.float64(1964.4580078125)), (np.float64(568.75), np.float64(2326.962786458333)), (np.float64(2629.492869791666), np.float64(2326.962786458333)), (np.float64(2629.492869791666), np.float64(1964.4580078125))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 133, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': 'dd5e25de715326d998ee74e241f8343f', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': '42752376472480e654b343db664a5d7b'}, page_content='Spread spectrum is employed in iDirect networks to minimize adjacent satellite interference (ASI). ASI can occur in applications such as Comms-on-the-Move (COTM) because the small antennas (typically sub-meter) used on mobile vehicles have a small aperture size, large beam width, and high pointing error. Enabling spread spectrum reduces the spectral density of the transmission to where it is low enough to avoid interfering with adjacent satellites.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9259134531021118, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(568.75), np.float64(2372.526123046875)), (np.float64(568.75), np.float64(2545.7127864583335)), (np.float64(2628.765625), np.float64(2545.7127864583335)), (np.float64(2628.765625), np.float64(2372.526123046875))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 133, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': 'dd5e25de715326d998ee74e241f8343f', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': 'a0ab101494750c20ed6b677b9db899d4'}, page_content='Although this feature may be useful for other applications, such as overpowering interference or hiding carriers from hostile jammers, customers should consult with iDirect sales engineering to ensure that a specific application is appropriate for this technology.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9344976544380188, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(568.75), np.float64(2590.7802734375)), (np.float64(568.75), np.float64(2826.441953125)), (np.float64(2581.404328125), np.float64(2826.441953125)), (np.float64(2581.404328125), np.float64(2590.7802734375))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 133, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': 'dd5e25de715326d998ee74e241f8343f', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': '33e23501248fd2a8c86463927ea13fb2'}, page_content='iDirect spread spectrum is an extension of BPSK modulation. The signal is spread over wider bandwidth according to a spreading factor (SF) selected for the carrier in the NMS user interface. For a TDMA upstream carrier, the satellite operator can select from one of four options: No Spreading, 2, 4, or 8.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9449273347854614, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(568.75), np.float64(2872.634661458333)), (np.float64(568.75), np.float64(3231.129453125)), (np.float64(2642.010009765625), np.float64(3231.129453125)), (np.float64(2642.010009765625), np.float64(2872.634661458333))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 133, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': 'dd5e25de715326d998ee74e241f8343f', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': '232f74401da064596ffb10938eabb367'}, page_content='Each symbol in a spread burst is called a “chip” with an associated chip rate that incorporates the spreading factor into the symbol rate. For example, selecting a spread factor of 4 means the chip rate is four times the symbol rate, hence occupying a larger bandwidth and resulting in lower spectral efficiencies compared to non-spread BPSK waveforms. The pilot structure in spread spectrum TDMA is optimized to provide a frequency tolerance of up to 1.5% of the symbol rate.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.4986126124858856, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(353.6458333333333), np.float64(3510.312744140625)), (np.float64(353.6458333333333), np.float64(3628.525286458333)), (np.float64(1948.06689453125), np.float64(3628.525286458333)), (np.float64(1948.06689453125), np.float64(3510.312744140625))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 133, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': 'dd5e25de715326d998ee74e241f8343f', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': 'fac369746349d6ffe2fa64a1fbdc73db'}, page_content='ST Engineering iDirect Proprietary | Confidentiality: Public Technical Reference Guide | iDirect Velocity™ | T0001665 | Revision 1'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.2775711119174957, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(2570.3854166666665), np.float64(3514.3013281249996)), (n