inst adverse channel effects such as rain fade. A heterogeneous inroute group, in relation to a homogeneous inroute group, is illustrated in the diagram.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.8543548583984375, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(699.006103515625), np.float64(1650.0044531249996)), (np.float64(699.006103515625), np.float64(1698.7813720703125)), (np.float64(2477.737060546875), np.float64(1698.7813720703125)), (np.float64(2477.737060546875), np.float64(1650.0044531249996))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 136, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'category': 'Title', 'element_id': 'e9916dba2709b91bd4627d447a70ce13'}, page_content='Figure 3-13. Heterogeneous Inroute Groups vs. Homogeneous Inroute Groups'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9388141632080078, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(565.626708984375), np.float64(1753.3638281249998)), (np.float64(565.626708984375), np.float64(1925.9211197916663)), (np.float64(2633.4668281249997), np.float64(1925.9211197916663)), (np.float64(2633.4668281249997), np.float64(1753.3638281249998))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 136, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': 'e9916dba2709b91bd4627d447a70ce13', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': '96481708781884e8b907dfeed07661bf'}, page_content='The protocol processor assigns time slots on upstream carriers to individual satellite terminals according to their current demand and capability, as determined by the channel state. Inroute group configuration automatically adapts over time to maximize system efficiency.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9302805066108704, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(567.5468749999999), np.float64(1972.1138281249998)), (np.float64(567.5468749999999), np.float64(2082.6919531249996)), (np.float64(2638.33349609375), np.float64(2082.6919531249996)), (np.float64(2638.33349609375), np.float64(1972.1138281249998))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 136, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': 'e9916dba2709b91bd4627d447a70ce13', 'category': 'ListItem', 'element_id': '8e29bbb4353d78e8c45c055f3561f612'}, page_content='• Inroute Group (IG) — A fixed portion of space segment bandwidth and power partitioned into TDMA carriers with different properties.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9295419454574585, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(566.2698974609375), np.float64(2128.884661458333)), (np.float64(566.2698974609375), np.float64(2239.462786458333)), (np.float64(2564.0), np.float64(2239.462786458333)), (np.float64(2564.0), np.float64(2128.884661458333))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 136, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': 'e9916dba2709b91bd4627d447a70ce13', 'category': 'ListItem', 'element_id': '42a89be23d8d1eb8312b30a54c269b6c'}, page_content='• Inroute Group Composition (IGC) — A set of carrier definitions assigned to an inroute group.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9478298425674438, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(568.75), np.float64(2285.6554947916666)), (np.float64(568.75), np.float64(2583.14794921875)), (np.float64(2633.6126614583336), np.float64(2583.14794921875)), (np.float64(2633.6126614583336), np.float64(2285.6554947916666))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 136, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': 'e9916dba2709b91bd4627d447a70ce13', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': '27242495f0ed018ce9d732a30275300c'}, page_content='The IGC assigned to an inroute group determines how the bandwidth in the inroute group is partitioned in real time. An inroute group can include carriers with different symbol rates and MODCODs. Note, however, that the symbol rates and center frequencies of the individual carriers remain the same in all IGCs. The IGC currently assigned to the inroute group defines the MODCODs of the various carriers in the group.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9468919038772583, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(568.75), np.float64(2628.3638281249996)), (np.float64(568.75), np.float64(3234.775286458333)), (np.float64(2634.050161458333), np.float64(3234.775286458333)), (np.float64(2634.050161458333), np.float64(2628.3638281249996))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 136, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': 'e9916dba2709b91bd4627d447a70ce13', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': 'd9b7f419e0ffa7e5b8835b6cb526f92a'}, page_content='The MODCODs of the upstream carriers do not vary frame by frame. The protocol processor assigns TDMA slots to individual satellite terminals on the upstream carriers based on the upstream link conditions of the individual satellite terminals. In the short term, satellite terminals adapt to changing conditions by frequency hopping among carriers with different properties. Over time, the protocol processor may also adjust the configuration of the inroute group by selecting different IGCs as network conditions change. Whenever a different IGC is assigned to the inroute group, the MODCODs of the upstream carriers change to match the configuration of the newly-applied IGC. Thus, the system automatically adapts in two ways: frame-by-frame through satellite terminal frequency hopping, and longer term by selecting the optimal IGC for the prevailing conditions.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.3118821382522583, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(353.6458333333333), np.float64(3514.3013281249996)), (np.float64(353.6458333333333), np.float64(3562.900286458333)), (np.float64(430.0836416027083), np.float64(3562.900286458333)), (np.float64(430.0836416027083), np.float64(3514.3013281249996))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 136, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': 'e9916dba2709b91bd4627d447a70ce13', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': 'b1d0d56af2e3e71d170772f57bb41d14'}, page_content='102'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.5252713561058044, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(1059.429443359375), np.float64(3509.6015625)), (np.float64(1059.429443359375), np.float64(3628.525286458333)), (np.float64(2629.1923828125), np.float64(3628.525286458333)), (np.float64(2629.1923828125), np.float64(3509.6015625))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 136, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': 'e9916dba2709b91bd4627d447a70ce13', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': 'dced76675d8f42323dc0c385841d356b'}, page_content='ST Engineering iDirect Proprietary | Confidentiality: Public Technical Reference Guide | iDirect Velocity™ | T0001665 | Revision 1'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9053808450698853, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(1774.2812499999998), np.float64(251.28049479166657)), (np.float64(1774.2812499999998), np.float64(299.87945312500017)), (np.float64(2634.0205078125), np.float64(299.87945312500017)), (np.float64(2634.0205078125), np.float64(251.28049479166657))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 137, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'category': 'Header', 'element_id': 'd9c985bb4d4ef85b67de729a194b266c'}, page_content='3.5.2.1 Differentiating C/N0 and C/N'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(568.75), np.float64(391.57216145833326)), (np.float64(568.75), np.float64(468.86638020833277)), (np.float64(1681.469104766354), np.float64(468.86638020833277)), (np.float64(1681.469104766354), np.float64(391.57216145833326))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 137, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': 'd9c985bb4d4ef85b67de729a194b266c', 'category': 'UncategorizedText', 'element_id': '58121ed977436c1c794a40eaf786caf8'}, page_content='3.5.2.1 Differentiating C/N0 and C/N'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9429338574409485, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(565.09423828125), np.float64(515.8950781250002)), (np.float64(565.09423828125), np.float64(823.2924218749998)), (np.float64(2587.384765625), np.float64(823.2924218749998)), (np.float64(2587.384765625), np.float64(515.8950781250002))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 137, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': 'd9c985bb4d4ef85b67de729a194b266c', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': 'dfeffe3c5b43dbd95740e44d1102eb22'}, page_content='With the introduction of A-TDMA, most upstream TDMA signal quality are now expressed in terms of C/N0 (carrier-power to noise-spectral-density ratio). In previous (non-adaptive) releases, the signal quality was expressed in terms of C/N (carrier-power to noise-power ratio). This section explains why this metric was changed and the relationship between C/N and C/N0.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9429224133491516, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(567.3056030273438), np.float64(858.6034114583334)), (np.float64(567.3056030273438), np.float64(1155.1190364583338)), (np.float64(2624.7532864583327), np.float64(1155.1190364583338)), (np.float64(2624.7532864583327), np.float64(858.6034114583334))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 137, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': 'd9c985bb4d4ef85b67de729a194b266c', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': '8cfca0e03e0bb5f3e3497bfeedd03d6c'}, page_content='C/N depends on the bandwidth of the upstream carrier. Using C/N as the signal quality metric makes it difficult to view inroute groups of upstream carriers with different symbol rates in a unified way. Since A-TDMA allows carriers in the same inroute group to have different symbol rates, it is necessary to use a measure such as C/N0 that is independent of the signal characteristics.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9465884566307068, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(568.75), np.float64(1201.3117447916668)), (np.float64(568.75), np.float64(1560.60107421875)), (np.float64(2606.852244791666), np.float64(1560.60107421875)), (np.float64(2606.852244791666), np.float64(1201.3117447916668))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 137, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': 'd9c985bb4d4ef85b67de729a194b266c', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': '9a47f3e1f87b0c3284733ad166693393'}, page_content='C/N is always qualified by a corresponding measurement bandwidth. The received carrier power (C) has a certain value, given the various system parameters and link conditions. However, the additive noise is defined in terms of its spectral density (N0). It has a much larger bandwidth than the signal. The total noise power (N) in a receiver is the product of N0 and the measurement bandwidth (B). In iDirect documentation that uses C/N, such as the iDirect Link Budget Analysis Guide, B is assumed to equal the symbol rate of the carrier.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.941611111164093, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(568.75), np.float64(1605.9992447916668)), (np.float64(568.75), np.float64(1840.535703125)), (np.float64(2630.9619140625), np.float64(1840.535703125)), (np.float64(2630.9619140625), np.float64(1605.9992447916668))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 137, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': 'd9c985bb4d4ef85b67de729a194b266c', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': '65b00d9c654b3dc3f9587b0cbbb8a310'}, page_content='An adaptive system constantly evaluates and compares the received C/N on one carrier with what can be achieved on another carrier. For example, if a line card is receiving a satellite terminal at a C/N of 11 dB on a carrier with a symbol rate of 1 Msps, what can be achieved on a 2 Msps carrier? In this example, the corresponding C/N on the 2 Msps carrier is 8 dB.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9380987286567688, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(568.75), np.float64(1886.7284114583333)), (np.float64(568.75), np.float64(2132.1465885416665)), (np.float64(2608.128286458333), np.float64(2132.1465885416665)), (np.float64(2608.128286458333), np.float64(1886.7284114583333))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 137, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': 'd9c985bb4d4ef85b67de729a194b266c', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': '27198c3baae84e1e598ca1b7c7bb8b97'}, page_content='Although the carrier power (C) is the same for both carriers, doubling the bandwidth doubles the noise power. Therefore, the C/N is halved (lowered by 3 dB). Rather than making comparisons with arbitrary references (and risking mistakes and confusion), the iDirect system uses C/N0 as the common measure.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9412614107131958, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(568.75), np.float64(2167.457578125)), (np.float64(568.75), np.float64(2401.9940364583335)), (np.float64(2648.6689453125), np.float64(2401.9940364583335)), (np.float64(2648.6689453125), np.float64(2167.457578125))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 137, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': 'd9c985bb4d4ef85b67de729a194b266c', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': 'be7150ee0b1d76ea41a63c4984096a61'}, page_content='C/N0 can be thought of as the C/N achievable in a bandwidth of 1 Hz. The fact that this is a stand-alone measure that does not need to be qualified by any signal properties is the primary reason the iDirect system now uses C/N0 extensively to measure and characterize upstream performance.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(568.75), np.float64(2448.1867447916666)), (np.float64(568.75), np.float64(2507.6674218749995)), (np.float64(2110.982453125), np.float64(2507.6674218749995)), (np.float64(2110.982453125), np.float64(2448.1867447916666))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 137, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': 'd9c985bb4d4ef85b67de729a194b266c', 'category': 'UncategorizedText', 'element_id': '3a81949b18c3d9294a92a03137a1641c'}, page_content='C/N0 is equal to C/N + 10log10(Symbol Rate) and is expressed in dBHz.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.8793843984603882, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(565.48486328125), np.float64(2544.9107031249996)), (np.float64(565.48486328125), np.float64(2604.391380208333)), (np.float64(2256.8271484375), np.float64(2604.391380208333)), (np.float64(2256.8271484375), np.float64(2544.9107031249996))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 137, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': 'd9c985bb4d4ef85b67de729a194b266c', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': '381ba7c5919937b05ebea02ec888d2cd'}, page_content='For this example: C/N0 = 11 + 10log10(1x106) = 8 + 10log10(2x106) = 71 dBHz'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9328378438949585, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(568.75), np.float64(2641.634661458333)), (np.float64(568.75), np.float64(2825.0372135416665)), (np.float64(2590.227244791667), np.float64(2825.0372135416665)), (np.float64(2590.227244791667), np.float64(2641.634661458333))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 137, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': 'd9c985bb4d4ef85b67de729a194b266c', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': 'cbd7049cd8d298ed3918593ed7a1e42d'}, page_content='Demodulation thresholds can also be expressed in terms of C/N0. The carrier MODCOD corresponds to a certain threshold C/N. The C/N threshold combined with the symbol rate is used during operation to compute the carrier threshold C/N0.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9393724203109741, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(568.75), np.float64(2860.384661458333)), (np.float64(568.75), np.float64(3105.766380208333)), (np.float64(2642.46630859375), np.float64(3105.766380208333)), (np.float64(2642.46630859375), np.float64(2860.384661458333))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 137, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': 'd9c985bb4d4ef85b67de729a194b266c', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': '108f7b037aea1e6f564d13935f40b550'}, page_content='A satellite terminal is allowed to transmit on a given upstream carrier when the C/N0 that can be achieved is greater than or equal to the C/N threshold - C/N0 of the carrier. The C/N0 is therefore a direct and unified measure of the ability to use any of the available carriers in the inroute group. This is another useful property of C/N0.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.4935893714427948, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(353.6458333333333), np.float64(3510.259765625)), (np.float64(353.6458333333333), np.float64(3628.525286458333)), (np.float64(1944.142333984375), np.float64(3628.525286458