nt='• IGC Selection Interval — The frequency (in seconds) at which the IGC selection algorithm is executed.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9361190795898438, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(565.2037963867188), np.float64(1060.6554947916666)), (np.float64(565.2037963867188), np.float64(1233.2127864583335)), (np.float64(2580.7646484375), np.float64(1233.2127864583335)), (np.float64(2580.7646484375), np.float64(1060.6554947916666))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 140, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': '8ac14db2b0a40d6f4b4aebb891208758', 'category': 'ListItem', 'element_id': 'a2d5ee9d4e9ee26f287f513656216d07'}, page_content='• Allowed Dropout Fraction — The fraction of active satellite terminals allowed to drop out of the network. These satellite terminals are unable to stay in the network on the most protected carrier and are logged out by the UCP.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.93399977684021, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(662.8201293945312), np.float64(1272.1138281249998)), (np.float64(662.8201293945312), np.float64(1506.650286458333)), (np.float64(2627.1595364583336), np.float64(1506.650286458333)), (np.float64(2627.1595364583336), np.float64(1272.1138281249998))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 140, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': '8ac14db2b0a40d6f4b4aebb891208758', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': '0734cb3c174f466ba4519098e1e46c0a'}, page_content='The selection algorithm attempts to select an IGC that does not allow the number of satellite terminals that drop out of the network to exceed the Allowed Dropout Fraction. If the Allowed Dropout Fraction is exceeded for all IGCs, the default IGC is selected for the inroute group.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9394372701644897, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(567.5468749999999), np.float64(1552.8429947916663)), (np.float64(567.5468749999999), np.float64(1787.3794531249998)), (np.float64(2603.353515625), np.float64(1787.3794531249998)), (np.float64(2603.353515625), np.float64(1552.8429947916663))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 140, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': '8ac14db2b0a40d6f4b4aebb891208758', 'category': 'ListItem', 'element_id': 'f52f8bedb78a8de1b5018efa20e1aace'}, page_content='• Maximum Allowed Downlink Fade — The maximum downlink (hub-side) fade (in dBs) allowed for the current IGC before a new IGC is selected. This parameter is only used if periodic hub side fade is measured by a teleport RF subsystem or through a beacon receiver configured in the network.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9108278155326843, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(567.5468749999999), np.float64(1833.572161458333)), (np.float64(567.5468749999999), np.float64(1944.466796875)), (np.float64(2587.8473697409368), np.float64(1944.466796875)), (np.float64(2587.8473697409368), np.float64(1833.572161458333))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 140, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': '8ac14db2b0a40d6f4b4aebb891208758', 'category': 'ListItem', 'element_id': '5755d22bbe557b1e3e3f852f45c92b50'}, page_content='• Default IGC — The IGC selected if the dropout rate is exceeded for all IGCs defined for the inroute group or if the downlink fade exceeds the maximum allowed downlink fade.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9178924560546875, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(828.6759643554688), np.float64(2029.377685546875)), (np.float64(828.6759643554688), np.float64(2326.962786458333)), (np.float64(2557.0866197916666), np.float64(2326.962786458333)), (np.float64(2557.0866197916666), np.float64(2029.377685546875))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 140, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': '41df66c663d4dd3bf1f46317dd4b54d9'}, page_content='NOTE: A severe downlink fade is observed at the SAS as the simultaneous fading of all satellite terminals. iDirect recommends including a very robust IGC among those defined for the inroute group to allow the system to operate during a severe downlink fade, rather than collapsing entirely or risk driving the user uplinks to saturation by UCP.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9037948250770569, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(844.5139770507812), np.float64(2365.8638281249996)), (np.float64(844.5139770507812), np.float64(2538.4211197916666)), (np.float64(2554.388703125), np.float64(2538.4211197916666)), (np.float64(2554.388703125), np.float64(2365.8638281249996))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 140, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': '62a9cac6843e883ce3d3ba99d0d007ae'}, page_content='Velocity also supports rain diversity switchover, which avoids weather impact through the use of a second SAS site. See Automatic Rain Diversity Switchover on page 182.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.896007776260376, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(565.2970581054688), np.float64(2668.0840885416665)), (np.float64(565.2970581054688), np.float64(2721.5684635416665)), (np.float64(1116.859375), np.float64(2721.5684635416665)), (np.float64(1116.859375), np.float64(2668.0840885416665))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 140, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'category': 'Title', 'element_id': '636b49d7a3ac08ea340fe4c7559f7f1b'}, page_content='Long-Term Adaptivity'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9465571641921997, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(563.7030639648438), np.float64(2765.38427734375)), (np.float64(563.7030639648438), np.float64(3125.400286458333)), (np.float64(2630.440786458333), np.float64(3125.400286458333)), (np.float64(2630.440786458333), np.float64(2765.38427734375))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 140, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': '636b49d7a3ac08ea340fe4c7559f7f1b', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': '37a9d417cdec9ba724fe43965766f536'}, page_content='Long-term adaptivity is a manual process that uses system feedback to refine the IGC configurations. Using the NMS user interface, satellite operators can view A-TDMA operational statistics. These statistics include IGC usage, the distribution of signal quality, and the number of satellite terminals logged off due to network conditions. The system planner uses these statistics to review and revise the IGC definitions and system parameters discussed in the previous sections.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.8965484499931335, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(568.75), np.float64(3213.447161458333)), (np.float64(568.75), np.float64(3276.6294531249996)), (np.float64(2378.2587890625), np.float64(3276.6294531249996)), (np.float64(2378.2587890625), np.float64(3213.447161458333))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 140, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'category': 'Title', 'element_id': '4bccf22ed2c5d651d28bc07c710e8ec2'}, page_content='3.5.2.3 Fade Margin and Measurement Interval Calculations'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9365271329879761, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(568.75), np.float64(3321.072161458333)), (np.float64(568.75), np.float64(3431.650286458333)), (np.float64(2640.2480781249997), np.float64(3431.650286458333)), (np.float64(2640.2480781249997), np.float64(3321.072161458333))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 140, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': '4bccf22ed2c5d651d28bc07c710e8ec2', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': '290fe6e651d1a0d11096c36a97558e3c'}, page_content='This section provides some general guidance on how suitable values for the signal quality measurement frequency and fade margins can be established. The default values provided are'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.42840373516082764, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(353.6458333333333), np.float64(3514.3013281249996)), (np.float64(353.6458333333333), np.float64(3562.900286458333)), (np.float64(430.628662109375), np.float64(3562.900286458333)), (np.float64(430.628662109375), np.float64(3514.3013281249996))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 140, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'category': 'Title', 'element_id': 'c924e34941fc3af9786f18edc6e2222e'}, page_content='106'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.2544329762458801, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(1270.314697265625), np.float64(3514.3013281249996)), (np.float64(1270.314697265625), np.float64(3562.900286458333)), (np.float64(2638.843017578125), np.float64(3562.900286458333)), (np.float64(2638.843017578125), np.float64(3514.3013281249996))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 140, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': 'c924e34941fc3af9786f18edc6e2222e', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': '13f9773b1b1aca77cd165a025fa4287e'}, page_content='ST Engineering iDirect Proprietary | Confidentiality: Public'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.5252833366394043, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(1060.02783203125), np.float64(3579.9263281249996)), (np.float64(1060.02783203125), np.float64(3628.525286458333)), (np.float64(2630.736328125), np.float64(3628.525286458333)), (np.float64(2630.736328125), np.float64(3579.9263281249996))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 140, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': 'c924e34941fc3af9786f18edc6e2222e', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': 'e0b604c1be8269d2afa3ce8573499cbc'}, page_content='Technical Reference Guide | iDirect Velocity™ | T0001665 | Revision 1'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9266038537025452, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(1492.3125), np.float64(251.28049479166657)), (np.float64(1492.3125), np.float64(299.87945312500017)), (np.float64(2624.909656776094), np.float64(299.87945312500017)), (np.float64(2624.909656776094), np.float64(251.28049479166657))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 141, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'category': 'Header', 'element_id': 'a56fbc65fdf9e49edeb3597e3dafc7f7'}, page_content='3.5.2.4 C/N Dynamic Range for Individual Carriers'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9195621013641357, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(562.1343383789062), np.float64(400.7596614583332)), (np.float64(562.1343383789062), np.float64(511.3377864583335)), (np.float64(2374.63720703125), np.float64(511.3377864583335)), (np.float64(2374.63720703125), np.float64(400.7596614583332))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 141, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': 'a56fbc65fdf9e49edeb3597e3dafc7f7', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': '1ddc6b483369d6e48688a622bef640d8'}, page_content='expected to be adequate to get the system running in most situations; any further optimization is left to the satellite operator as part of the long-term adaptivity.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9475634694099426, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(568.75), np.float64(557.5304947916666)), (np.float64(568.75), np.float64(978.0044531250002)), (np.float64(2634.552001953125), np.float64(978.0044531250002)), (np.float64(2634.552001953125), np.float64(557.5304947916666))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 141, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': 'a56fbc65fdf9e49edeb3597e3dafc7f7', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': '995162b7017be91a3e3a06e752260f21'}, page_content='Terminals are expected to transmit a traffic burst at least once every measurement interval, which is a user configurable value recorded under “Measurement Spacing”. The fade depth and fade slope are normally assessed after each such interval using a sliding record of a pre- configured number of recent measurements. Following a non-zero power control command or change of nominal carrier (including IGC change), the measurement history is reset. In clear weather, changes are relatively rare in comparison to scenarios involving significant fade events. The total system reaction time accounts for processing time and a round-trip delay.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9480273127555847, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(568.75), np.float64(1024.197161458333)), (np.float64(568.75), np.float64(1692.587786458333)), (np.float64(2639.38134765625), np.float64(1692.587786458333)), (np.float64(2639.38134765625), np.float64(1024.197161458333))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 141, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': 'a56fbc65fdf9e49edeb3597e3dafc7f7', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': '72a4de1bb66e2886c4efc87f6095881e'}, page_content='The M1 margin is intended to cover measurement uncertainties as well as allow for the system reaction time for fade detection; a value of 1.0 dB has been found to be a suitable default for handling 0.1 dB/s fade slope with detection uncertainties. In the presence of time-varying fade, this parameter is closely related to the spacing between measurements. Hence, an additional trade-off can be accessed, between margin and overhead. Dedicated measurement “probe” bursts are only used by terminals that are typically idle. Actual traffic bursts are also used for the measurements, so there is no measurement overhead for an active terminal. Therefore, for systems with active terminals, a “low margin” setting will be the preference. The “low-overhead” setting is intended for systems that serve as back-up to other communications means, or other situations where a large population of terminals is normally idling, so it is desirable to keep the overhead low.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9493577480316162, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(566.6570434570312), np.float64(1738.7804947916663)), (np.float64(566.6570434570312), np.float64(2159.2544531249996)), (np.float64(2615.164744791666), np.float64(2159.2544531249996)), (np.float64(2615.164744791666), np.float64(1738.7804947916663))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 141, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': 'a56fbc65fdf9e49edeb3597e3dafc7f7', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': 'b222dc05983c194d19401c289e5864cb'}, page_content='The M2 system hysteresis margin is intended to prevent spurious switching of the nominal carrier. It should be set higher than the power control step size supported by the terminals. Initial experience suggests that this margin also caters effectively for a number of additional minor uncertainties; a value of 0.6 dB has been found to be a suitable default for a variety of situations. In extreme cases, terminals may be forced to log out because the system cannot keep up with the rapid carrier changes. If the M2 is set too high, capacity will be wasted because the carrier usage (time slot assignments) will be more conservative than necessary.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9475656151771545, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(568.75), np.float64(2205.447161458333)), (np.float64(568.75), np.float64(2563.941953125)), (np.float64(2586.6178697916666), np.float64(2563.941953125)), (np.float64(2586.6178697916666), np.float64(2205.447161458333))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 141, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': 'a56fbc65fdf9e49edeb3597e3dafc7f7', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': 'bcf2eb23b3c8301f03736d403a723fc3'}, page_content='The M3 margin is applied to acquisition bursts for the purpose of selecting an initial nominal carrier: its value is related to the C/N estimation accuracy for this signal. The M3 margin is also used to accommodate initial uncertainties in EIRP (Effective Isotropic Radiated Power) settings, BUC (block up-converter) gain variation with frequency. A fixed value of 2 dB is suggested based on initial experience, design analyses of the RF components, and the relevant estimation algorithms.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9182788133621216, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(568.75), np.float64(2651.9888281249996)), (np.float64(568.75), np.float64(2715.171119791666)), (np.float64(2081.913175662396), np.float64(2715.171119791666)), (np.float64(2081.913175662396), np.float64(2651.9888281249996))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 141, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': 'a56fbc65fdf9e49edeb3597e3dafc7f7', 'category': 'Title', 'element_id': '682384d0dfd7a3f96cbeff467af68106'}, page_content='3.5.2.4 C/N Dynamic Range for Individual Carriers'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9484926462173462, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(568.75), np.float64(2759.6138281249996)), (np.float64(568.75), np.float64(3242.066953125)), (np.float64(2588.841828125), np.float64(3242.066953125)), (np.float64(2588.841828125), np.float64(2759.6138281249996))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 141, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': '682384d0dfd7a3f96cbeff467af68106', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': '5cf8795c741d57c11b7f5790ab4f8fb7'}, page_content='For any given carrier in an inroute group, the MODCODs used in the various compositions should be chosen such that the range of variation of the threshold C/N does not exceed approximately 5 dB. This restriction is associated with the finite dynamic range inherent in any digital demodulator design. If the constraint is violated, the sudden, large variation in signal level happening at IGC changes may result in temporarily increased rates of lost or bursts with error. These episodes typically last for a few seconds, until the demodulator automatic gain control is able to adjust. A higher range of threshold variation can be used if these temporary episodes of increased errors are acceptable.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9294859170913696, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(564.3838500976562), np.float64(3288.259661458333)), (np.float64(564.3838500976562), np.float64(3398.837786458333)), (np.float64(2530.626220703125), np.float64(3398.837786458333)), (np.float64(2530.626220703125), np.float64(3288.259661458333))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 141, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': '682384d0dfd7a3f96cbeff467af68106', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': '6a352960eee14351e2e257431d8b979b'}, page_content='The 5 dB range is more than sufficient to vary a carrier from BPSK r=1/2 to QPSK r=2/3 or QPSK r=3/4 to 8PSK r=4/5, for example.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.47804173827171326, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(352.9780578613281), np.float64(3514.3013281249996)), (np.float64(352.9780578613281), np.float64(3562.900286458333)), (np.float64(1686.8992919921875), np.float64(3562.900286458333)), (np.float64(1686.8992919921875), np.float64(3514.3013281249996))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 141, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': '682384d0dfd7a3f96cbeff467af68106', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': 'e0c519cd1dd044dcea3f8d948bdeeef3'}, page_content='ST Engineering iDirect Proprietary | Confidentiality: Public'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.5113803148269653, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(353.6458333333333), np.float64(3579.9263281249996)), (np.float64(353.6458333333333), np.float64(3628.525286458333)), (np.float64(1921.875732421875), np.float64(3628.525286458333)), (np.float64(1921.875732421875), np.float64(3579.9263281249996))), 