'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 142, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'category': 'Header', 'element_id': '8eb9e49cbf92ca4c9d67d63a7bf8aa42'}, page_content='3.5.2.5 C/N0 Dynamic Range for Inroute Group'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(568.75), np.float64(391.57216145833326)), (np.float64(568.75), np.float64(468.86638020833277)), (np.float64(1982.6101229050519), np.float64(468.86638020833277)), (np.float64(1982.6101229050519), np.float64(391.57216145833326))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 142, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': '8eb9e49cbf92ca4c9d67d63a7bf8aa42', 'category': 'UncategorizedText', 'element_id': 'c66186da60b922fc81d568bfcc1c4a95'}, page_content='3.5.2.5 C/N0 Dynamic Range for Inroute Group'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9491773247718811, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(568.75), np.float64(515.8950781250002)), (np.float64(568.75), np.float64(874.3898697916671)), (np.float64(2634.12646484375), np.float64(874.3898697916671)), (np.float64(2634.12646484375), np.float64(515.8950781250002))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 142, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': '8eb9e49cbf92ca4c9d67d63a7bf8aa42', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': '70b49aee12686cae27a454011c598959'}, page_content='In order to make the best use of the available capacity, individual terminals may be assigned time slots on any carrier in the inroute group for which it is able to close the link budget. Disadvantaged terminals have priority for the time slots on the more protected carriers, but when there is no specific demand for these slots, they may be assigned to any terminals. The Free Slot Assignment (FSA) feature ensures all slots do indeed get assigned, to the extent possible.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9490231871604919, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(568.75), np.float64(920.5825781250002)), (np.float64(568.75), np.float64(1279.077369791667)), (np.float64(2622.237661458333), np.float64(1279.077369791667)), (np.float64(2622.237661458333), np.float64(920.5825781250002))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 142, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': '8eb9e49cbf92ca4c9d67d63a7bf8aa42', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': '5f696462464322f4df9be2aa6d1a0ac7'}, page_content='The transmit power required on any carrier is proportional to the carrier demodulation threshold expressed as C/N0; that is, the C/N threshold plus allowance for the symbol rate. Therefore, within a very short span of time, the terminal may be required to transmit on carriers with power requirements that differ by as much as the overall span of C/N0 threshold values in the inroute group. This includes the various compositions, since they can change instantaneously on any frame boundary.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9480189085006714, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(568.75), np.float64(1325.270078125)), (np.float64(568.75), np.float64(1683.7648697916668)), (np.float64(2625.810578125), np.float64(1683.7648697916668)), (np.float64(2625.810578125), np.float64(1325.270078125))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 142, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': '8eb9e49cbf92ca4c9d67d63a7bf8aa42', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': 'c7d77c1f5ef4e756e09773cc9914e184'}, page_content="All terminals have a finite dynamic range of transmitter power/EIRP. At one end, this is limited by the maximum power of the BUC. At the other end, it is limited by the level-control attenuators and by stability considerations. The total dynamic range of an iDirect modem's IF output power is large; however, not all of it is available to accommodate signal differences. In particular, substantial allowances must be made in order to accommodate differences in BUC gain and IF cable losses."), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9449383020401001, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(568.75), np.float64(1733.6034114583333)), (np.float64(568.75), np.float64(2030.1190364583333)), (np.float64(2613.045654296875), np.float64(2030.1190364583333)), (np.float64(2613.045654296875), np.float64(1733.6034114583333))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 142, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': '8eb9e49cbf92ca4c9d67d63a7bf8aa42', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': 'd825dc1a97eebc881619077da058ed4e'}, page_content='For all iDirect modems, the dynamic range available for real-time adjustment of burst power is 15 dB. Hence, the inroute group should be arranged such that the difference between the lowest and highest C/N0 threshold of the carriers that any terminal needs to access does not exceed it. This 15 dB constraint, which applies across all compositions, is not very limiting if taken into consideration when designing the inroute group and its compositions.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9411330819129944, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(568.75), np.float64(2079.72216796875)), (np.float64(568.75), np.float64(2377.3681640625)), (np.float64(2638.060578125), np.float64(2377.3681640625)), (np.float64(2638.060578125), np.float64(2079.72216796875))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 142, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': '8eb9e49cbf92ca4c9d67d63a7bf8aa42', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': '6ecc10327d90306ace7f10fb05724684'}, page_content='A 15 dB fade is a very rare event, even in extreme locations. As an example, the city of Recife in Brazil (the 0.01% rainfall rate is 69 mm/hr, old climatic zone “N”) has an elevation of 20°to a satellite, 15 dB still corresponds to 99.9% availability at Ku-band and 99.3% at Ka-band. For a location with slightly more moderate but still substantial rainfall (Montreal, 38 mm/hr, old zone “K”), the figures are 99.99% at Ku-band and 99.85% at Ka-band.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9241076707839966, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(568.75), np.float64(2464.5200781249996)), (np.float64(568.75), np.float64(2527.7023697916666)), (np.float64(1694.081298828125), np.float64(2527.7023697916666)), (np.float64(1694.081298828125), np.float64(2464.5200781249996))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 142, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': '8eb9e49cbf92ca4c9d67d63a7bf8aa42', 'category': 'Title', 'element_id': '869b67265c5cd8d5fa4121576166fe03'}, page_content='3.5.2.6 Maximum Power and Control'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9479759335517883, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(568.75), np.float64(2572.145078125)), (np.float64(568.75), np.float64(3116.5773697916666)), (np.float64(2638.169953125), np.float64(3116.5773697916666)), (np.float64(2638.169953125), np.float64(2572.145078125))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 142, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': '869b67265c5cd8d5fa4121576166fe03', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': '71b56532a69a2a1be546bb0d62976d5d'}, page_content='For A-TDMA to work well in the network, it is important that maximum transmit power is set accurately. To maintain the transmit power value close to the ODU (outdoor unit) limit, it is recommended to perform 1 dB compression tests corresponding to beam center frequency on ODUs that do not support Modem-BUC calibration. Having accurate maximum power settings can be challenging for beam switching satellite terminals, as the variation in gain flatness of a BUC can impact the maximum power used in UPC for a given terminal in different beams and requires maximum power determined per beam. For ODUs that support Modem-BUC calibration the maximum power at L-band is predetermined across RF band prior to network entry and over the air 1dB compression testing is not necessary across any of the beams.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9335095882415771, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(562.497314453125), np.float64(3162.770078125)), (np.float64(562.497314453125), np.float64(3335.327369791666)), (np.float64(2551.654328125), np.float64(3335.327369791666)), (np.float64(2551.654328125), np.float64(3162.770078125))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 142, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': '869b67265c5cd8d5fa4121576166fe03', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': 'e3c7f267997581899e961603ab1aa2a8'}, page_content='Power control transitions typically occur during rain fades and changes in inroute compositions. CRC are observed when a remote drastically changes it