ing iDirect Proprietary | Confidentiality: Public Technical Reference Guide | iDirect Velocity™ | T0001665 | Revision 1'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9032211303710938, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(1900.5729166666663), np.float64(251.28049479166657)), (np.float64(1900.5729166666663), np.float64(299.87945312500017)), (np.float64(2633.48876953125), np.float64(299.87945312500017)), (np.float64(2633.48876953125), np.float64(251.28049479166657))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 143, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'category': 'Header', 'element_id': 'f43ef7c0f0d139ba2be05b8a9b98dd0f'}, page_content='3.5.2.7 Frame-Filling Efficiency'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9353605508804321, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(560.0997314453125), np.float64(400.7596614583332)), (np.float64(560.0997314453125), np.float64(511.3377864583335)), (np.float64(2558.2897447916666), np.float64(511.3377864583335)), (np.float64(2558.2897447916666), np.float64(400.7596614583332))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 143, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': 'f43ef7c0f0d139ba2be05b8a9b98dd0f', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': '84315734ab6ded0b03cea260c15f2b77'}, page_content='another. As they try to self-correct through the uplink power control, there are chances of CRCs happening during the short transition period.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9275332689285278, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(568.75), np.float64(599.3846614583333)), (np.float64(568.75), np.float64(662.5669531249997)), (np.float64(1546.4279833205728), np.float64(662.5669531249997)), (np.float64(1546.4279833205728), np.float64(599.3846614583333))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 143, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': 'f43ef7c0f0d139ba2be05b8a9b98dd0f', 'category': 'Title', 'element_id': '9c420c76d2ad7fce4e9cccfad5306620'}, page_content='3.5.2.7 Frame-Filling Efficiency'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9499911665916443, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(568.75), np.float64(707.0096614583332)), (np.float64(568.75), np.float64(1251.441953125)), (np.float64(2623.9147447916666), np.float64(1251.441953125)), (np.float64(2623.9147447916666), np.float64(707.0096614583332))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 143, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': '9c420c76d2ad7fce4e9cccfad5306620', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': '915a2d77a520621ac80c0110c5342ed1'}, page_content='The multi-frequency TDMA frame employed in the iDirect inroute provides a very flexible transmission capacity resource for a population of terminals — even when those terminals present the system with very disparate and highly dynamic capacity demands. In ideal conditions, the frame can be filled 100% — that is, all time slots on all carriers can be used to transport user data. For frame filling efficiency, tests with real-world arrangements, in terms of carrier rates and numbers of terminals, typically provide filling efficiencies above 98% on all carriers. This section discusses some of the real-world constraints that force the filling efficiency to slightly lower than 100% in some cases, as well as some constraints that determine the actual spectral efficiency.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9493238925933838, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(568.75), np.float64(1297.634661458333)), (np.float64(568.75), np.float64(2028.0044531249998)), (np.float64(2632.675048828125), np.float64(2028.0044531249998)), (np.float64(2632.675048828125), np.float64(1297.634661458333))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 143, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': '9c420c76d2ad7fce4e9cccfad5306620', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': 'a4b82ce8bf5da7e999865b181f9e1588'}, page_content='Time slots in the iDirect system can have very different durations. The main constraint currently imposed is that all slots have the same payload size (170 bytes). The choice of symbol rates, FEC rates, and modulation schemes on different carriers impacts the number of symbols in a burst. Time slot boundaries typically do not align between carriers in the inroute group. Since the terminals can only transmit on one carrier at a time, assigning a slot on one carrier will generally prevent it from using more than one time slot on all other carriers. This phenomenon, known as shadowing, is a process that assigns specific slots to specific terminals in an attempt to minimize any issues. The problem is effectively eliminated when the number of terminals is far greater than the number of carriers. A slot that cannot be assigned to one terminal, due to shadowing or for other reasons, can be assigned to another terminal with higher probability. This, when combined with a sophisticated algorithm, allows the iDirect system to achieve the 98+% figure noted above.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9457202553749084, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(568.75), np.float64(2074.197161458333)), (np.float64(568.75), np.float64(2370.712786458333)), (np.float64(2619.160888671875), np.float64(2370.712786458333)), (np.float64(2619.160888671875), np.float64(2074.197161458333))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 143, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': '9c420c76d2ad7fce4e9cccfad5306620', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': '155c64f23ea3139f2b7bd679d477129d'}, page_content='It is possible to create artificial situations where the task of filling the frame completely becomes impossible or impractical. Either with a very small number of terminals or a small number of carriers and, in particular, if the time slot durations vary widely between carriers, the achievable frame filling may be reduced substantially due to excessive shadowing. This is not a major issue in most practical situations.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.950740396976471, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(568.75), np.float64(2416.9054947916666)), (np.float64(568.75), np.float64(2837.379453125)), (np.float64(2646.037841796875), np.float64(2837.379453125)), (np.float64(2646.037841796875), np.float64(2416.9054947916666))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 143, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': '9c420c76d2ad7fce4e9cccfad5306620', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': '6130af5bc07c1c885a847ebb02cb269e'}, page_content='Generally, frame filling works well for simple inroute groups with only two types of carriers. However, as the inroute groups become more complex with multiple carriers, frame filling efficiencies are lowered to the 80% and 90% range. Additionally, depending on the GQoS rules configured for the inroute group, a distortion of allocation for each satellite terminal may occur. This issue is more apparent for complex A-TDMA use cases that require multiple types of carriers. For these complex A-TDMA use cases, additional trade-offs are required with some over provisioning of bandwidth for disadvantaged carriers.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.8940672278404236, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(568.75), np.float64(2928.688255208333)), (np.float64(568.75), np.float64(2996.755963541666)), (np.float64(2278.671630859375