852, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(559.7456665039062), np.float64(528.3638281249998)), (np.float64(559.7456665039062), np.float64(824.8794531250002)), (np.float64(2606.830810546875), np.float64(824.8794531250002)), (np.float64(2606.830810546875), np.float64(528.3638281249998))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 147, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': '9503f5749166d994d526cef35949e290', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': '1bc49f205bb9669183634643c79f71cb'}, page_content="The iDirect Uplink Control process (UCP) executes at the SAS to bring satellite terminals into the network and to maintain the correct frequency, power, and timing during uplink operation. Then, the UCP continuously monitors each satellite terminal's upstream performance and instructs the satellite terminal to adjust its transmission as required to remain within acceptable limits. This section discusses both phases of TDMA uplink control."), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9426179528236389, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(568.75), np.float64(871.0721614583332)), (np.float64(568.75), np.float64(1043.873046875)), (np.float64(2614.7216796875), np.float64(1043.873046875)), (np.float64(2614.7216796875), np.float64(871.0721614583332))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 147, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': '9503f5749166d994d526cef35949e290', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': '710c1a2658babd081cef3a815d04d670'}, page_content='By default, the system allows for up to 1.7 ms of uncertainty in start-of-frame (SOF) timing. The 1.7 ms timing uncertainty consists of ±0.1 degree of satellite station keeping uncertainty and approximately 50 miles of satellite terminal position uncertainty.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9401402473449707, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(561.4380493164062), np.float64(1089.822161458333)), (np.float64(561.4380493164062), np.float64(1324.3586197916668)), (np.float64(2595.3678697916666), np.float64(1324.3586197916668)), (np.float64(2595.3678697916666), np.float64(1089.822161458333))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 147, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': '9503f5749166d994d526cef35949e290', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': '9264014d79cd5954fe8bacd38f73aa8b'}, page_content='This variation in symbol timing is accounted for during satellite terminal acquisition by providing a larger guard band in the TDMA frame for acquisition slots than for traffic slots. A larger guard band in the acquisition slot prevents the acquiring satellite terminal from bursting into the traffic slots allocated to other satellite terminals.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9425995349884033, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(568.31396484375), np.float64(1370.5513281249998)), (np.float64(568.31396484375), np.float64(1667.0669531249998)), (np.float64(2574.728515625), np.float64(1667.0669531249998)), (np.float64(2574.728515625), np.float64(1370.5513281249998))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 147, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': '9503f5749166d994d526cef35949e290', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': '9386d212464e54809cb3f3f51c878642'}, page_content="Frequency offset is the difference between the nominal frequency at which the satellite terminal transmits and the frequency at which the SAS demodulator receives the upstream carrier. Frequency offset occurs even after the satellite terminal's clock is synchronized to the SAS clock. The SAS down converter equipment and the Doppler Effect due to satellite and satellite terminal motion are major contributors to frequency offset."), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9485065340995789, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(568.75), np.float64(1713.259661458333)), (np.float64(568.75), np.float64(2071.7544531249996)), (np.float64(2616.657470703125), np.float64(2071.7544531249996)), (np.float64(2616.657470703125), np.float64(1713.259661458333))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 147, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': '9503f5749166d994d526cef35949e290', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': 'a1ffef4c707da58d28dac86c085aee0e'}, page_content='A satellite terminal attempts to join an iDirect TDMA network by sending an acquisition burst to the SAS in an upstream carrier acquisition slot, in contention or invitation mode. To join the network, the satellite terminal must transmit the acquisition burst at a power level that allows the burst to be successfully demodulated by the hub line card (HLC) receiving the upstream carrier. Uplink control selects the initial nominal upstream carrier for the satellite terminal based on the measured C/N of the acquisition burst.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9463430643081665, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(561.63134765625), np.float64(2117.947161458333)), (np.float64(561.63134765625), np.float64(2478.083740234375)), (np.float64(2634.7793281249997), np.float64(2478.083740234375)), (np.float64(2634.7793281249997), np.float64(2117.947161458333))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 147, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': '9503f5749166d994d526cef35949e290', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': '37eea814dfb9c4b32275e270269fd441'}, page_content='This initial selection is based on the acquisition margin configured in the NMS user interface on the M3 Margin tab of the Inroute Group Profile configuration. The acquisition margin is separate from the normal margins, due to the larger uncertainty of the C/N estimation on the acquisition burst and to allow for other system uncertainties, such as BUC aging and frequency response variations. After the satellite terminal has joined the network, the UCP at the SAS takes over to keep the satellite terminal in the network at the correct power.'), Document(m