d': 'a2cc79fb447e519d32fe07da6e337a6d', 'category': 'ListItem', 'element_id': 'a16e3b67bba6e7ab2a48ee77de630b28'}, page_content='• About the Uplink Control Process on page 113 describes uplink power control in iDirect networks.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9408696889877319, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(563.2610473632812), np.float64(714.3013281249998)), (np.float64(563.2610473632812), np.float64(1010.8169531250002)), (np.float64(2620.815786458333), np.float64(1010.8169531250002)), (np.float64(2620.815786458333), np.float64(714.3013281249998))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 148, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': 'a2cc79fb447e519d32fe07da6e337a6d', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': '64f50012125dd310ebfa672693057062'}, page_content='Each upstream carrier in an inroute group can have a different MODCOD, symbol rate, and spreading factor. Specific values for these upstream carrier parameters, which are collectively called the satellite terminal reference carrier, are entered along with the TDMA initial transmit power. The value configured for the TDMA initial transmit power is defined in relation to the configured reference carrier parameters.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9411229491233826, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(568.75), np.float64(1057.009661458333)), (np.float64(568.75), np.float64(1354.1624755859375)), (np.float64(2634.451203125), np.float64(1354.1624755859375)), (np.float64(2634.451203125), np.float64(1057.009661458333))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 148, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': 'a2cc79fb447e519d32fe07da6e337a6d', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': 'e95e851df38bfa285af1119eb5800808'}, page_content='A satellite terminal may acquire into the network on any upstream carrier in the inroute group. When sending an acquisition burst on an upstream carrier with characteristics that differ from the configured reference carrier, the satellite terminal uses its reference carrier parameters to adjust the initial transmit power so the acquisition burst is received by the HLC within the correct C/N range for that carrier.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9400418996810913, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(568.75), np.float64(1399.7179947916666)), (np.float64(568.75), np.float64(1634.2544531249998)), (np.float64(2638.2793281249997), np.float64(1634.2544531249998)), (np.float64(2638.2793281249997), np.float64(1399.7179947916666))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 148, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': 'a2cc79fb447e519d32fe07da6e337a6d', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': '68bc10d2e6f2955cb94926ec142d96fd'}, page_content='In a burst mode demodulator, the gain must be set at some nominal point prior to the arrival of a data burst so that the burst is correctly detected and demodulated. Since a single HLC receives bursts from many different remote modems, it constantly calculates the optimal gain point by taking into account the average levels of all bursts arriving at that HLC.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9359850883483887, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(568.1517944335938), np.float64(1680.447161458333)), (np.float64(568.1517944335938), np.float64(1853.0044531249998)), (np.float64(2607.277587890625), np.float64(1853.0044531249998)), (np.float64(2607.277587890625), np.float64(1680.447161458333))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 148, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': 'a2cc79fb447e519d32fe07da6e337a6d', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': 'e8591c1bea9f6506bc057da139428d3f'}, page_content='If all the bursts arrive at similar C/N levels, the average C/N is close to the optimal value for all bursts. However, if many bursts arrive at varying C/N levels, the higher-level and lower- level bursts can skew the average such that the average is no longer optimal.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9436383843421936, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(568.75), np.float64(1899.197161458333)), (np.float64(568.75), np.float64(2196.107177734375)), (np.float64(2617.373046875), np.float64(2196.107177734375)), (np.float64(2617.373046875), np.float64(1899.197161458333))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 148, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': 'a2cc79fb447e519d32fe07da6e337a6d', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': '5b64e570c71e108ec2227cda71ff9ca0'}, page_content='The nominal C/N range is 2 dB. The actual range at which bursts can be optimally detected is approximately 8 dB, centered at the nominal gain point. As shown in the following diagram, under ideal circumstances, the average C/N of all satellite terminals on the upstream carrier is equal to the center of the UCP adjustment range. Notice that the optimal detection range extends below the threshold C/N of the upstream carrier.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.6324178576469421, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(1117.4324951171875), np.float64(2783.387451171875)), (np.float64(1117.4324951171875), np.float64(2836.103411458333)), (np.float64(2079.349609375), np.float64(2836.103411458333)), (np.float64(2079.349609375), np.float64(2783.387451171875))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 148, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'category': 'Title', 'element_id': '7f0673dfefea192a6831045bdc00a607'}, page_content='Figure 3-17. Optimal C/N Detection Range'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9368504881858826, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(557.4503784179688), np.float64(2890.8638281249996)), (np.float64(557.4503784179688), np.float64(3063.4211197916666)), (np.float64(2594.864990234375), np.float64(3063.4211197916666)), (np.float64(2594.864990234375), np.float64(2890.8638281249996))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 148, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': '7f0673dfefea192a6831045bdc00a607', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': 'c7e1a8602dc41ece5c952200b055779b'}, page_content='If the TDMA transmit initial power of a satellite terminal is not set correctly, network performance can be negatively affected. Post-acquisition, the center point of the 8 dB wide detection range is set at the C/N value at the time of acquisition.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9342036843299866, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(565.83251953125), np.float64(3108.096923828125)), (np.float64(565.83251953125), np.float64(3406.129453125)), (np.float64(2620.779328125), np.float64(3406.129453125)), (np.float64(2620.779328125), np.float64(3108.096923828125))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 148, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': '7f0673dfefea192a6831045bdc00a607', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': 'c81210c051a0b29b32545fb30aa3bb02'}, page_content='Satellite terminals joining the network with initial transmit power set too high skew the average C/N to be above the center of the UCP adjustment range, as shown in the following diagram. Since UCP updates may occur as infrequently as every 20 seconds, it can take a minute or more for satellite terminals with too much initial power to decrease their power to be within the nominal range. During this period the optimal detection range does not include'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.38581690192222595, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(353.5863952636719), np.float64(3514.3013281249996)), (np.float64(353.5863952636719), np.float64(3562.900286458333)), (np.float64(434.4986267089844), np.float64(3562.900286458333)), (np.float64(434.4986267089844), np.float64(3514.3013281249996))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 148, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': '7f0673dfefea192a6831045bdc00a607', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': '7b0271787170caa7d6b5382ca16d414b'}, page_content='114'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(1315.1614583333333), np.float64(3514.3013281249996)), (np.float64(1315.1614583333333), np.float64(3562.900286458333)), (np.float64(2621.2687946232813), np.float64(3562.900286458333)), (np.float64(2621.2687946232813), np.float64(3514.3013281249996))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 148, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': '7f0673dfefea192a6831045bdc00a607', 'category': 'UncategorizedText', 'element_id': 'acfc87eecf8596b61021b584052a8111'}, page_content='ST Engineering iDirect Proprietary | Confidentiality: Public'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.46447622776031494, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(1065.3385009765625), np.float64(3579.9263281249996)), (np.float64(1065.3385009765625), np.float64(3628.525286458333)), (np.float64(2621.335645833333), np.float64(3628.525286458333)), (np.float64(2621.335645833333), np.float64(3579.9263281249996))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 148, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': '7f0673dfefea192a6831045bdc00a607', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': '7d4526beec3258ca29cd24431004f422'}, page_content='Technical Reference Guide | iDirect Velocity™ | T0001665 | Revision 1'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9173251986503601, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(2146.484375), np.float64(251.28049479166657)), (np.float64(2146.484375), np.float64(299.87945312500017)), (np.float64(2634.659912109375), np.float64(299.87945312500017)), (np.float64(2634.659912109375), np.float64(251.28049479166657))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 149, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'category': 'Header', 'element_id': '5883b029fd8773bb13ea9f3228f524b3'}, page_content='3.6.2 UCP Operation'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9343770146369934, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(566.9464111328125), np.float64(400.7596614583332)), (np.float64(566.9464111328125), np.float64(573.3169531250002)), (np.float64(2519.06201171875), np.float64(573.3169531250002)), (np.float64(2519.06201171875), np.float64(400.7596614583332))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 149, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': '5883b029fd8773bb13ea9f3228f524b3', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': 'b9ee1701fe68c3930a515e17c87d86af'}, page_content='the threshold C/N and the performance of satellite terminals experiencing rain fade may degrade. Those satellite terminals could drop out of the network because their bursts no longer fall within the optimal detection range.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.5951805114746094, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(714.4840087890625), np.float64(1151.9090576171875)), (np.float64(714.4840087890625), np.float64(1204.7584228515625)), (np.float64(2464.1515528360937), np.float64(1204.7584228515625)), (np.float64(2464.1515528360937), np.float64(1151.9090576171875))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 149, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'category': 'Title', 'element_id': '3b35007380153a11d6dff27f40fc4600'}, page_content='Figure 3-18. Skewed C/N Detection Range — Initial Transmit Power Too High'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9372977614402771, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(558.4624633789062), np.float64(1255.630126953125)), (np.float64(558.4624633789062), np.float64(1616.1971435546875)), (np.float64(2638.862661458333), np.float64(1616.1971435546875)), (np.float64(2638.862661458333), np.float64(1255.630126953125))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 149, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': '3b35007380153a11d6dff27f40fc4600', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': '5702044e4d4f5e146337e0ac8092214b'}, page_content='Satellite terminals joining the network with initial transmit power set too low skew the average C/N to be below the center of the UCP adjustment range, as shown in the following diagram. This could cause satellite terminals coming into the network at the higher end (for example, 14 dB) to experience some distortion in the demodulation process. Additionally, a satellite terminal acquiring at below the C/N threshold may experience a large number of CRC errors after joining the network until its power is sufficiently increased.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.6029499769210815, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(721.38916015625), np.float64(2154.166015625)), (np.float64(721.38916015625), np.float64(2209.228271484375)), (np.float64(2459.9131086709376), np.float64(2209.228271484375)), (np.float64(2459.9131086709376), np.float64(2154.166015625))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 149, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'category': 'Title', 'element_id': 'f292e196f07e529cf9ae66531f05c6b4'}, page_content='Figure 3-19. Skewed C/N Detection Range — Initial Transmit Power Too Low'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9495511054992676, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(568.556640625), np.float64(2257.27099609375)), (np.float64(568.556640625), np.float64(2684.484619140625)), (np.float64(2636.0189114583327), np.float64(2684.484619140625)), (np.float64(2636.0189114583327), np.float64(2257.27099609375))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 149, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': 'f292e196f07e529cf9ae66531f05c6b4', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': '92b40a829ad4f2e625299bc7f0e29e06'}, page_content='As in the case where the initial power was set too high, since UCP updates may occur as infrequently as every 20 seconds, it may take a minute or more for carriers with initial power set too low to increase their power to within the nominal range. During this time, terminals operating under clear sky conditions could drop out of the network because the bursts no longer fall within the optimal detection range. Satellite terminals trying to acquire with a C/N value of greater than 13 dB may not acquire the network. Bursts can still be detected below the threshold C/N but the probability of detection and demodulation is reduced.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.8694289326667786, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(568.75), np.float64(2775.563255208333)), (np.float64(568.75), np.float64(2843.630963541666)), (np.float64(1302.2142333984375), np.float64(2843.630963541666)), (np.float64(1302.2142333984375), np.float64(2775.563255208333))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 149, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'category': 'Title', 'element_id': '41f7476f864e6a7c6d8bc36650c1a49c'}, page_content='3.6.2 UCP Operation'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9324284791946411, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(568.75), np.float64(2885.552490234375)), (np.float64(568.75), np.float64(3121.754453125)), (np.float64(2518.848876953125), np.float64(3121.754453125)), (np.float64(2518.848876953125), np.float64(2885.552490234375))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 149, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': '41f7476f864e6a7c6d8bc36650c1a49c', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': 'c77510ae487251cec756023007fd2362'}, page_content='After the satellite terminal has acquired the network, the UCP continuously corrects the frequency, symbol timing and power while the satellite terminal is in the network. For satellite terminals in adaptive inroute groups, the UCP process is also responsible for switching satellite terminals to new nominal upstream carriers as required.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9354320764541626, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(568.75), np.float64(3167.947161458333)), (np.float64(568.75), np.float64(3340.504453125)), (np.float64(2621.3991197916666), np.float64(3340.504453125)), (np.float64(2621.3991197916666), np.float64(3167.947161458333))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 149, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': '41f7476f864e6a7c6d8bc36650c1a49c', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': '0dcc9361cc0fdb3792af1672dbc77c55'}, page_content="A satellite terminal's nominal carrier is the upstream carrier with the highest threshold C/N0 the satellite terminal can sustain and is allowed to use. All power control and other real-time corrections are related to the nominal carrier."), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.432151198387146, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(353.6458333333333), np.float64(3507.41357421875)), (np.float64(353.6458333333333), np.float64(3628.525286458333)), (np.float64(1937.2957763671875), np.float64(3628.525286458333)), (np.float64(1937.2957763671875), np.float64(3507.41357421875))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 149, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': '41f7476f864e6a7c6d8bc36650c1a49c', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': 'c80418f0103e4208c42c210af41f4538'}, page_content='ST Engineering iDirect Proprietary | Confidentiality: Public Technical Reference Guide | iDirect Velocity™ | T0001665 | Revision 1'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.5227898955345154, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(2544.864583333333), np.float64(3514.3013281249996)), (np.float64(2544.864583333333), np.float64(3562.900286458333)), (np.float64(2624.311279296875), np.float64(3562.900286458333)), (np.float64(2624.311279296875), np.float64(3514.3013281249996))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 149, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': '41f7476f864e6a7c6d8bc36650c1a49c', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': '5d4e8580dbc8c452f66b87df2d3ea851'}, page_content='115'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.888569712638855, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(347.71722412109375), np.float64(251.28049479166657)), (np.float64(347.71722412109375), np.float64(299.87945312500017)), (np.float64(1125.4729056447916), np.float64(299.87945312500017)), (np.float64(1125.4729056447916), np.float64(251.28049479166657))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 150, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'category': 'Header', 'element_id': '7b2172fdb40b73b2be737152054ea1a9'}, page_content='3.6.2.1 UCP Correction Processing'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9325813055038452, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(568.75), np.float64(391.57216145833326)), (np.float64(568.75), np.float64(454.75445312499966)), (np.float64(1624.0741195586982), np.float64(454.75445312499966)), (np.float64(1624.0741195586982), np.float64(391.57216145833326))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 150, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': '7b2172fdb40b73b2be737152054ea1a9', 'category': 'Title', 'element_id': 'b9c04c3b9b139fb28b3152198aedbbfd'}, page_content='3.6.2.1 UCP Correction Processing'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9424057006835938, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(565.3402709960938), np.float64(499.1971614583332)), (np.float64(565.3402709960938), np.float64(733.7336197916668)), (np.float64(2583.521728515625), np.float64(733.7336197916668)), (np.float64(2583.521728515625), np.float64(499.1971614583332))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 150, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': 'b9c04c3b9b139fb28b3152198aedbbfd', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': '349a6c7e17961feaad7affecd6215652'}, page_content='The SAS periodically sends UCP correction information to the satellite terminal. By default, the SAS sends this information every 20 seconds to stationary satellite terminals. For high- speed mobile satellite terminals, UCP correction information should be sent to the satellite terminal more often (for example, Aero terminals every 2 seconds).'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9404164552688599, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(567.478759765625), np.float64(779.9263281249998)), (np.float64(567.478759765625), np.float64(1014.4627864583334)), (np.float64(2596.315786458333), np.float64(1014.4627864583334)), (np.float64(2596.315786458333), np.float64(779.9263281249998))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 150, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': 'b9c04c3b9b139fb28b3152198aedbbfd', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': '9841201846f00106dbae19a45fcbecca'}, page_content='In order for the UCP algorithm to function correctly, the terminal must periodically transmit bursts on the TDMA upstream carrier even when idle. Stationary satellite terminals send a minimum of 1 burst every 2 seconds by default. For high-speed mobile applications, some satellite terminal model types require a user to send a minimum of 1 burst per second.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9353107810020447, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(568.75), np.float64(1060.6554947916666)), (np.float64(568.75), np.float64(1295.2457275390625)), (np.float64(2640.5762031249997), np.float64(1295.2457275390625)), (np.float64(2640.5762031249997), np.float64(1060.6554947916666))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 150, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': 'b9c04c3b9b139fb28b3152198aedbbfd', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': '002bbb30a8f95f2d870fcf4efac89904'}, page_content="An idle satellite terminal automatically increases the frequency at which it transmits bursts to the SAS when a fade condition is detected. For a satellite terminal in an adaptive inroute group, this allows the SAS to monitor a fast fade and move the satellite terminal to a more protected carrier before the SAS can no longer detect the satellite terminal's bursts."), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9345003366470337, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(568.75), np.float64(1383.2388281249998)), (np.float64(568.75), np.float64(1446.4211197916666)), (np.float64(1414.4056396484375), np.float64(1446.4211197916666)), (np.float64(1414.4056396484375), np.float64(1383.2388281249998))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 150, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': '7b2172fdb40b73b2be737152054ea1a9', 'category': 'Title', 'element_id': 'bf1094fe4095d91c519d11899326f3ce'}, page_content='3.6.2.2 UCP Symbol Timing'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9513351917266846, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(568.75), np.float64(1490.8638281249998)), (np.float64(568.75), np.float64(1973.3169531249998)), (np.float64(2630.5137031249997), np.float64(1973.3169531249998)), (np.float64(2630.5137031249997), np.float64(1490.8638281249998))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 150, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': 'bf1094fe4095d91c519d11899326f3ce', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': '263e398e8d145f13420e3848861bae0e'}, page_content="Satellite terminals transmitting on the same TDMA carrier must time their transmissions so that all bursts arrive at the SAS modem burst demodulator in sequence and without collisions. To achieve correct burst timing synchronization, each satellite terminal uses its own geographic coordinates, the geographic coordinates of the SAS, and the longitude of the satellite to calculate a Frame Start Delay (FSD). The different FSDs of the satellite terminals compensate for the variation in transmission delay between the individual satellite terminals and the SAS. The satellite terminal adds the FSD to the frame start time received from the SAS to derive the satellite terminal's TDMA frame start time."), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9393007159233093, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(567.136474609375), np.float64(2019.509661458333)), (np.float64(567.136474609375), np.float64(2254.0461197916666)), (np.float64(2549.7919921875), np.float64(2254.0461197916666)), (np.float64(2549.7919921875), np.float64(2019.509661458333))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 150, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': 'bf1094fe4095d91c519d11899326f3ce', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': '265fd5fa91db6c4d09cfbb7d47d19a23'}, page_content="During network operation, the symbol timing changes as the satellite moves within the station-keeping box. Symbol timing can also change due to timing Doppler shifts in mobile satellite terminals. The UCP at the SAS adjusts the satellite terminal's symbol offset by averaging timing drifts every UCP period and sending corrections to the satellite terminal."), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9431277513504028, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(566.4884643554688), np.float64(2300.2388281249996)), (np.float64(566.4884643554688), np.float64(2534.7752864583335)), (np.float64(2578.0866197916666), np.float64(2534.7752864583335)), (np.float64(2578.0866197916666), np.float64(2300.2388281249996))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 150, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': 'bf1094fe4095d91c519d11899326f3ce', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': '55931ee115bc76283ab50b57f337baca'}, page_content='The guard band between bursts for a TDMA upstream carrier is automatically set during IGC carrier configuration in the NMS user interface. The configured guard band depends on the lowest symbol rate in the IGC and accounts for timing Doppler shifts in addition to system timing uncertainties.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9262159466743469, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(568.75), np.float64(2622.822161458333)), (np.float64(568.75), np.float64(2686.0044531249996)), (np.float64(1568.7783203125), np.float64(2686.0044531249996)), (np.float64(1568.7783203125), np.float64(2622.822161458333))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 150, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': '7b2172fdb40b73b2be737152054ea1a9', 'category': 'Title', 'element_id': '66ff87682514b11825ef3832972ad7f7'}, page_content='3.6.2.3 UCP Frequency Tracking'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9430158734321594, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(568.75), np.float64(2730.447161458333)), (np.float64(568.75), np.float64(3026.962786458333)), (np.float64(2606.2324531249997), np.float64(3026.962786458333)), (np.float64(2606.2324531249997), np.float64(2730.447161458333))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 150, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': '66ff87682514b11825ef3832972ad7f7', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': '3ad6a4187bf9859a412fb843819126c9'}, page_content='Frequency drifts are caused by clock drifts in various components of the system. These drifts are primarily due to temperature variations and the age and quality of the oscillators. The protocol processor tracks frequency offsets over every UCP period and sends corrections to the satellite terminals. The satellite terminals then adjust their transmit frequencies accordingly.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9420561790466309, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(567.048583984375), np.float64(3073.155494791666)), (np.float64(567.048583984375), np.float64(3307.691953125)), (np.float64(2619.6491197916666), np.float64(3307.691953125)), (np.float64(2619.6491197916666), np.float64(3073.155494791666))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 150, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': '66ff87682514b11825ef3832972ad7f7', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': '5bee4921ebdb4af03e570f7f5d58d897'}, page_content="For mobile satellite terminals, Doppler shifts also contribute to frequency drift. These additional frequency drifts in mobile satellite terminals are primarily caused by variation in the satellite terminals' speed. In high-speed COTM applications, the protocol processor uses a predictive algorithm to correct for frequency drifts."), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.31040921807289124, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(353.39111328125), np.float64(3514.3013281249996)), (np.float64(353.39111328125), np.float64(3562.900286458333)), (np.float64(430.8372802734375), np.float64(3562.900286458333)), (np.float64(430.8372802734375), np.float64(3514.3013281249996))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 150, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': '66ff87682514b11825ef3832972ad7f7', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': 'c17b0ef2a29a93d3359c4b4c06adab78'}, page_content='116'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.5179848670959473, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(1063.4027099609375), np.float64(3507.51318359375)), (np.float64(1063.4027099609375), np.float64(3628.525286458333)), (np.float64(2625.500244140625), np.float64(3628.525286458333)), (np.float64(2625.500244140625), np.float64(3507.51318359375))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 150, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': '66ff87682514b11825ef3832972ad7f7', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': '65912a78770566c56fee18707d238f6a'}, page_content='ST Engineering iDirect Proprietary | Confidentiality: Public Technical Reference Guide | iDirect Velocity™ | T0001665 | Revision 1'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9254339337348938, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(1562.8004150390625), np.float64(251.28049479166657)), (np.float64(1562.8004150390625), np.float64(299.87945312500017)), (np.float64(2631.173095703125), np.float64(299.87945312500017)), (np.float64(2631.173095703125), np.float64(251.28049479166657))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 151, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'category': 'Header', 'element_id': '3b6841df0e6b1ee113fe66fcd5e6eab0'}, page_content='3.6.2.4 UCP Power Control and Fade Detection'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9199087023735046, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(568.75), np.float64(391.57216145833326)), (np.float64(568.75), np.float64(454.75445312499966)), (np.float64(2009.02734375), np.float64(454.75445312499966)), (np.float64(2009.02734375), np.float64(391.57216145833326))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 151, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': '3b6841df0e6b1ee113fe66fcd5e6eab0', 'category': 'Title', 'element_id': 'be12fc582cfe621a1d6ffc962cf934dd'}, page_content='3.6.2.4 UCP Power Control and Fade Detection'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9424869418144226, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(563.150390625), np.float64(499.1971614583332)), (np.float64(563.150390625), np.float64(733.7336197916668)), (np.float64(2596.7532864583336), np.float64(733.7336197916668)), (np.float64(2596.7532864583336), np.float64(499.1971614583332))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 151, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': 'be12fc582cfe621a1d6ffc962cf934dd', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': '97035dc3a6900a268643804b287f53cf'}, page_content='The demodulator at the SAS functions optimally when the received power spectral density is similar for all satellite terminals. Therefore, the goal of the UCP is to adjust the individual transmit powers of the satellite terminals so that all satellite terminals are received at the same C/N as measured at the SAS.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9498094916343689, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(568.75), np.float64(779.9263281249998)), (np.float64(568.75), np.float64(1200.4002864583335)), (np.float64(2561.060578125), np.float64(1200.4002864583335)), (np.float64(2561.060578125), np.float64(779.9263281249998))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 151, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': 'be12fc582cfe621a1d6ffc962cf934dd', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': '2accbe45ff59dda65b0e116d5d84dd4d'}, page_content="For a given terminal, the C/N may vary due to fade conditions or as mobile terminals move across the satellite footprint, requiring the UCP to adjust the satellite terminal's transmit power to keep the C/N within range. To normalize the C/N across satellite terminals, the protocol processor averages the C/N deviations detected by the Rx line cards for each satellite terminal. If the deviations are within the acceptable range of the target C/N, no corrections are sent to the satellite terminal. If the deviations are outside the acceptable range, the SAS sends corrections to the satellite terminal until the C/N is within range."), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.946008026599884, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(568.75), np.float64(1246.5929947916666)), (np.float64(568.75), np.float64(1605.087786458333)), (np.float64(2630.7324531249997), np.float64(1605.087786458333)), (np.float64(2630.7324531249997), np.float64(1246.5929947916666))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 151, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': 'be12fc582cfe621a1d6ffc962cf934dd', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': '8900d4ff0a0c2a8449ee169366f8f6f5'}, page_content="The power control algorithm has been designed to accommodate the heterogeneous nature of the upstream carriers in adaptive inroute groups. The goal of the power control algorithm is for each satellite terminal to be received at the target C/N on the best carrier the satellite terminal can receive at any given time. Therefore, the power control algorithm is responsible not only for adjusting the satellite terminal's power on the current nominal carrier, but also for selecting a new nominal carrier when required."), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9331332445144653, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(564.7069702148438), np.float64(1651.2804947916663)), (np.float64(564.7069702148438), np.float64(1823.837786458333)), (np.float64(2552.347036458333), np.float64(1823.837786458333)), (np.float64(2552.347036458333), np.float64(1651.2804947916663))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 151, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': 'be12fc582cfe621a1d6ffc962cf934dd', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': '8474c2da7872c4497e3645f3f3635774'}, page_content='The target C/N is calculated based on the C/N thresholds for the inroutes from the iDirect Link Budget Analysis Guide and the following margins configured in the NMS, the details of which are described in Fade Margin and Measurement Interval Calculations on page 106.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9314308762550354, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(567.5468749999999), np.float64(1870.0304947916663)), (np.float64(567.5468749999999), np.float64(2043.575927734375)), (np.float64(2566.456411458333), np.float64(2043.575927734375)), (np.float64(2566.456411458333), np.float64(1870.0304947916663))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 151, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': 'be12fc582cfe621a1d6ffc962cf934dd', 'category': 'ListItem', 'element_id': '0dc2af82388282548175852fe582cd2c'}, page_content='• Fade Slope Margin (M1) — allows for an incremental fade, which can occur during the reaction time of the power control algorithm, as well as the uncertainty in the C/N0 estimations.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9172075390815735, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(565.90966796875), np.float64(2088.22705078125)), (np.float64(565.90966796875), np.float64(2199.3586197916666)), (np.float64(2554.878173828125), np.float64(2199.3586197916666)), (np.float64(2554.878173828125), np.float64(2088.22705078125))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 151, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': 'be12fc582cfe621a1d6ffc962cf934dd', 'category': 'ListItem', 'element_id': 'f2a91d2a493e7a1ef9f86aea53628c06'}, page_content='• Hysteresis Margin (M2) — is added to the fade slope margin to prevent unnecessarily frequent switching between carriers.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9346179962158203, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(568.75), np.float64(2245.5513281249996)), (np.float64(568.75), np.float64(2480.087786458333)), (np.float64(2635.047119140625), np.float64(2480.087786458333)), (np.float64(2635.047119140625), np.float64(2245.5513281249996))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 151, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': 'be12fc582cfe621a1d6ffc962cf934dd', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': '24788e2e6ad50f8d898d72b613dcf4eb'}, page_content='The system adds the sum of these two margins to the C/N thresholds to determine the target C/Ns for each carrier in the inroute group. The target values and margins are adjusted automatically by the power control algorithm as necessary, based on the MODCOD and symbol rate of each carrier. Highlights of the UCP power control algorithm include:'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9529997110366821, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(566.658935546875), np.float64(2523.975830078125)), (np.float64(566.658935546875), np.float64(2884.918701171875)), (np.float64(2639.1178697916666), np.float64(2884.918701171875)), (np.float64(2639.1178697916666), np.float64(2523.975830078125))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 151, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': 'be12fc582cfe621a1d6ffc962cf934dd', 'category': 'ListItem', 'element_id': '7c849081e2a50e7b631bd7927c28abd4'}, page_content="• If a satellite terminal's C/N falls below the target C/N, the power control algorithm increases the satellite terminal's transmit power (if possible) to bring the receive signal back up to the target level. If the satellite terminal's power cannot be increased on the nominal carrier and a more protected carrier is available, the satellite terminal's nominal carrier is changed to the more robust carrier. This keeps the satellite terminal in the network at the expense of diminished throughput."), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(567.5468749999999), np.float64(2930.967994791666)), (np.float64(567.5468749999999), np.float64(2979.566953125)), (np.float64(607.6595364583333), np.float64(2979.566953125)), (np.float64(607.6595364583333), np.float64(2930.967994791666))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 151, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': 'be12fc582cfe621a1d6ffc962cf934dd', 'category': 'UncategorizedText', 'element_id': '3e631578e0a17710519b6904a53c667e'}, page_content='•'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9263337850570679, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(579.650390625), np.float64(2930.967994791666)), (np.float64(579.650390625), np.float64(3165.504453125)), (np.float64(2613.597036458333), np.float64(3165.504453125)), (np.float64(2613.597036458333), np.float64(2930.967994791666))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 151, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': 'be12fc582cfe621a1d6ffc962cf934dd', 'category': 'ListItem', 'element_id': 'd96f8a458b03f68647d15b15a49c9d1d'}, page_content='If the satellite terminal is consistently below the threshold defined by the target C/N minus the hysteresis margin on the most protected carrier in the inroute group, the satellite terminal is logged out of the network. A satellite terminal that has been logged out must re-acquire the network before it can continue to transmit user traffic.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.935912549495697, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(567.5468749999999), np.float64(3211.697161458333)), (np.float64(567.5468749999999), np.float64(3384.254453125)), (np.float64(2627.378286458333), np.float64(3384.254453125)), (np.float64(2627.378286458333), np.float64(3211.697161458333))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 151, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': 'be12fc582cfe621a1d6ffc962cf934dd', 'category': 'ListItem', 'element_id': '15f9fee60d2a96760ff598aac1f653ae'}, page_content="• If there is additional power headroom available over the satellite terminal's current C/N plus the hysteresis margin, the power control algorithm looks for a more efficient carrier with a higher MODCOD at which the satellite terminal can maintain the target C/N. If"), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(353.6458333333333), np.float64(3514.3013281249996)), (np.float64(353.6458333333333), np.float64(3562.900286458333)), (np.float64(1659.7896279566144), np.float64(3562.900286458333)), (np.float64(1659.7896279566144), np.float64(3514.3013