51e274ec34eb6b156f51cb334bbadef7'}, page_content='Global Bandwidth Management (GBWM) is the Velocity™ subsystem that manages global bandwidth capacity across the entire satellite network — a constellation of beams potentially from multiple spot beam and broad beam satellites. All beams on all satellites defined in the global satellite network contribute bandwidth to a single pool that is managed by GBWM, giving service providers the flexibility to create service plans for a single beam or across multiple beams on multiple satellites.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9414079785346985, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(563.544921875), np.float64(933.0513281249998)), (np.float64(563.544921875), np.float64(1107.1873779296875)), (np.float64(2580.97509765625), np.float64(1107.1873779296875)), (np.float64(2580.97509765625), np.float64(933.0513281249998))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 154, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': '8c742a33b25d34f3db6b67646f971b54', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': '5f653f368e1d4f9f228c62d46df9a0cd'}, page_content='This Velocity functionality supports advanced service providers with a high degree of flexibility in subdividing satellite bandwidth and creating groups of satellite terminals with various levels of service plans tailored to the characteristics of supported user applications.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.888450026512146, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(835.63232421875), np.float64(1188.6025390625)), (np.float64(835.63232421875), np.float64(1489.131103515625)), (np.float64(2574.331411458333), np.float64(1489.131103515625)), (np.float64(2574.331411458333), np.float64(1188.6025390625))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 154, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': '1562c6d8d29e7a12dc160ade8c7cd1cf'}, page_content="NOTE: Many service providers will be familiar with the existing iDirect bandwidth management and Group Quality of Service (GQoS) of the Evolution platform. In many ways, Velocity's GBWM can be viewed as an extension of the existing GQoS architecture - from satellite networks that operated on single transponders, to satellite networks spanning multiple beams and satellites."), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.913037121295929, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(819.1966552734375), np.float64(1527.322161458333)), (np.float64(819.1966552734375), np.float64(1888.4752197265625)), (np.float64(2578.571044921875), np.float64(1888.4752197265625)), (np.float64(2578.571044921875), np.float64(1527.322161458333))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 154, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': '0533556e47843a5a835e0101a593d464'}, page_content='Criteria used for packet classification and the iNet demand and allocation tree structure are essentially the same in Evolution GQoS and Velocity GBWM. However, GBWM introduces a number of new concepts and features, such as SAS and system-wide QoS enforcement, Fair Access Policies (FAP), and geographic scope. Knowledge of Evolution GQoS can be useful, but is only the core of a broader set of features available in Velocity GBWM.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9233759045600891, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(567.7398071289062), np.float64(2023.1554947916663)), (np.float64(567.7398071289062), np.float64(2133.7336197916666)), (np.float64(2645.05322265625), np.float64(2133.7336197916666)), (np.float64(2645.05322265625), np.float64(2023.1554947916663))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 154, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': 'e9e6af71d8c8fd83a758020a4b720722'}, page_content='The remaining topics of this section describe some of the over-arching components of Velocity networks, including:'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.8686397671699524, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(673.2760416666666), np.float64(2179.9263281249996)), (np.float64(673.2760416666666), np.float64(2228.525286458333)), (np.float64(1127.7099609375), np.float64(2228.525286458333)), (np.float64(1127.7099609375), np.float64(2179.9263281249996))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'pag