PCs and GSPs, see Subscriber Service Plans on page 137.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.946837306022644, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(563.8363037109375), np.float64(1246.5929947916666)), (np.float64(563.8363037109375), np.float64(1667.0669531249998)), (np.float64(2617.0605781249997), np.float64(1667.0669531249998)), (np.float64(2617.0605781249997), np.float64(1246.5929947916666))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 157, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': 'be62017351cf37e89c6df7395c951017', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': '5ced793150c9a007c3c9e18b35fd808a'}, page_content='The relationships between services and the partitioning of bandwidth between them are represented by the configured GBWM tree. Each service plan — whether a GSP or an SSPP/SSPC — is represented as a node in that tree. The GBWM subsystem uses the GBWM tree to create, at runtime, GQE (Global QoS Enforcement) trees at the SAS, NOC, and iNet levels, and allocates available satellite bandwidth to fulfill the demand of subscribers in real-time according to those GQE trees, their service plan parameters, variations in available bandwidth, contention, and congestion.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.8786795139312744, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(857.41552734375), np.float64(1753.3638281249998)), (np.float64(857.41552734375), np.float64(1925.9211197916663)), (np.float64(2594.3470364583336), np.float64(1925.9211197916663)), (np.float64