is greater than configured capacity), there will be no extra capacity to allocate. If GSP is heavily subscribed, extra allocation will be done until the configured capacity of the GSP is reached.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.933881402015686, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(747.465087890625), np.float64(674.1971614583332)), (np.float64(747.465087890625), np.float64(908.7336197916668)), (np.float64(2534.63623046875), np.float64(908.7336197916668)), (np.float64(2534.63623046875), np.float64(674.1971614583332))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 161, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': 'f1590142928ba822ab908ffe73f37c09', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': '9c98537f044f1a3786aec82e129463de'}, page_content='Real-time traffic fluctuations can result from a sudden increase in demand from terminals using a specific GSP in one or more iNets. This happens when actual demand for existing terminals suddenly increases by a large percentage value or when new terminal(s) enter a sparsely populated iNet(s) using that GSP.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9339721202850342, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(751.0416666666666), np.float64(947.6346614583332)), (np.float64(751.0416666666666), np.float64(1244.1502864583335)), (np.float64(2604.455810546875), np.float64(1244.1502864583335)), (np.float64(2604.455810546875), np.float64(947.6346614583332))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 161, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': 'f1590142928ba822ab908ffe73f37c09', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': '6825b5bf45fdd672132f3726627a7dea'}, page_content='If the traffic fluctuation (increase) is more than 5%, there will be a delay of up to 10 seconds to catch up with the new demand by the GQE process. During this time, there will be less distribution than actual demand. TCP traffic flows usually adjust automatically to this fluctuation. However, for UDP traffic flows, some traffic losses are likely to be encountered.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.912537693977356, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(745.2227783203125), np.float64(1283.0513281249998)), (np.float64(745.2227783203125), np.float64(1393.6294531249998)), (np.float64(2550.60009765625), np.float64(1393.6294531249998)), (np.float64(2550.60009765625), np.float64(1283.0513281249998))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 161, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': 'f1590142928ba822ab908ffe73f37c09', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': 'ece25af0622a367e8d49792f17a49866'}, page_content='For GSPs that have on average 10 or more active terminals per iNet, the impact is expected to be relatively negligible.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9389730095863342, 'i