adata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9417407512664795, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(568.691650390625), np.float64(907.5304947916665)), (np.float64(568.691650390625), np.float64(1142.066953125)), (np.float64(2634.310302734375), np.float64(1142.066953125)), (np.float64(2634.310302734375), np.float64(907.5304947916665))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 167, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': '5e8e645c0e29999d91ff0891faa0716f'}, page_content="A GSP node may be configured to allocate bandwidth using “Absolute” (strict priority) mode, or using “Per Allocation” mode. Both modes perform multiple bandwidth allocation rounds; they differ in which nodes are included in a given round, and how much of the nodes' demand is satisfied in that round."), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9396523237228394, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(559.4063110351562), np.float64(1188.259661458333)), (np.float64(559.4063110351562), np.float64(1422.7961197916666)), (np.float64(2601.293701171875), np.float64(1422.7961197916666)), (np.float64(2601.293701171875), np.float64(1188.259661458333))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 167, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': 'b8976e9c4b73f27fba7aedce24ff901f'}, page_content="In absolute mode, the allocation rounds are organized by child node priority from highest priority node to lowest priority node until the available bandwidth is exhausted. Within a priority round, there are two sub-rounds — one for demand that conforms to the child node's configured CIR, and another for its remaining demand, subject to its configured MIR."), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9349841475486755, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(568.75), np.float64(1468.9888281249998)), (np.float64(568.75), np.float64(1579.5669531249998)), (np.float64(2627.369384765625), np.float64(1579.5669531249998)), (np.float64(2627.369384765625), np.float64(1468.9888281249998))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 167, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': '017c69c96cc2f68671e0ca3def1a0575'}, page_content='If multiple child nodes are configured with the same priority, an allocation fairness algorithm determines bandwidth allocation. Refer to Allocation Fairness Algorithms on page 134.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.7349365949630737, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(1122.5897216796875), np.float64(2401.0461197916666)), (np.float64(1122.5897216796875), np.float64(2449.6450781249996)), (np.float64(2069.362548828125), np.float64(2449.6450781249996)), (np.float64(2069.362548828125), np.float64(2401.0461197916666))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'l