pload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': '91684fa637ef28411d671ff83ae6ca25', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': '61f62c71cc8c5493021f39e4c3ca3c1e'}, page_content='The GBWM bandwidth allocation algorithm allocates iNet excess capacity in upstream (after meeting all the demand iNet) equally to all active terminals in the iNet. It is possible, therefore, for a satellite terminal to receive more bandwidth than the configured maximum. However, it strictly enforces the downstream allocation based real-time demand and no excess capacity distribution on iNet downstream direction.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9191341996192932, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(568.75), np.float64(2101.4679947916666)), (np.float64(568.75), np.float64(2164.650286458333)), (np.float64(1739.162353515625), np.float64(2164.650286458333)), (np.float64(1739.162353515625), np.float64(2101.4679947916666))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 168, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': 'f18b3441442e6a7ba774ed7c435205df', 'category': 'Title', 'element_id': 'f8ab58fe804a170fbddf49720a3bba52'}, page_content='4.4.3.2 Allocation Fairness Algorithms'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9415149092674255, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(568.75), np.float64(2204.754150390625)), (np.float64(568.75), np.float64(2505.6086197916666)), (np.float64(2562.766357421875), np.float64(2505.6086197916666)), (np.float64(2562.766357421875), np.float64(2204.754150390625))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 168, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': 'f8ab58fe804a170fbddf49720a3bba52', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': '97d3b752f60bb3d261ae0c462df36e14'}, page_content='GBWM provides the service provider with the ability to specify how equally-deserving child service plans share a bandwidth allocation from their parent GSP, when the child service plans demand exceeds the GSP received allocation—in other words, there is bandwidth contention. Allocation fairness is the method of determining how this allocation is shared among GSP child service plans.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.8151820302009583, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(821.319580078125), np.float64(2579.159423828125)), (np.float64(821.319580078125), np.float64(2952.953369140625)), (np.float64(2568.242869791666), np.float64(2952.953369140625)), (np.float64(2568.242869791666), np.float64(2579.159423828125))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 168, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': '38886c5fb28b2fe9881ec9c79eaa7c1c'}, page_content='NOTE: 1) Allocation fairness only applies when there is contention between service plans configured with the same priority. 2) The concept of inbound fairness is not related to the allocation fairness methods described here. Inbound fairness is comparable to the configuration of base MODCOD on the outbound. For additional details, see Inbound Fairness Base Bitrate (for SSPCs only) on page 159.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9085633754730225, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(561.7667236328125), np.float64(3087.7388281249996)), (np.float64(561.7667236328125), np.float64(3198.316953125)), (np.float64(2624.156005859375), np.float64(3198.316953125)), (np.float64(2624.156005859375), np.float64(3087.7388281249996))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 168, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': '6ecb7d2b8956d649630d1f7d94ec4e93'}, page_content='The GBWM system provides a choice of several allocation fairness algorithms. These options support various business models. The allocation fairness algorithms are:'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9198230504989624, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(658.90673828125), np.float64(3242.231689453125)), (np.float64(658.90673828125), np.float64(3417.066953125)), (np.float64(2612.430369791666), np.float64(3417.066953125)), (np.float64(2612.430369791666), np.float64(3242.231689453125))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 168, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 