al details on FAP, see Fair Access Policy on page 325.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.937979519367218, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(566.6538696289062), np.float64(776.2804947916666)), (np.float64(566.6538696289062), np.float64(948.8377864583334)), (np.float64(2582.352244791666), np.float64(948.8377864583334)), (np.float64(2582.352244791666), np.float64(776.2804947916666))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 178, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': '4f4d6919173cec893dbfaa54ecef7082', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': '01d0bf3bec889a8af8192c0f2bc3e496'}, page_content='Service providers may optionally specify the terminal types and SVNs that may be used with the GSP. This restriction is enforced on any child GSPs or SSPCs created below the GSP parent.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.7999866604804993, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(845.2135416666666), np.float64(1035.134661458333)), (np.float64(845.2135416666666), np.float64(1083.7336197916668)), (np.float64(2548.72021484375), np.float64(1083.7336197916668)), (np.float64(2548.72021484375), np.float64(1035.134661458333))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 178, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': 'c9dd835d25d78d5e41ba4609f6e37c79'}, page_content='NOTE: There is no explicit limit on the number of GSPs that can be created.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9085910320281982, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(568.75), np.float64(1211.8846614583333)), (np.float64(568.75), np.float64(1275.0669531249996)), (np.float64(2286.8169750628126), np.float64(1275.0669531249996)), (np.float64(2286.8169750628126), np.float64(1211.8846614583333))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 178, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'category': 'Title', 'element_id': 'b4c2569ab76729d6c9c83088915761eb'}, page_content='4.5.3.1 GSP Configuration and QoS Service Mode Options'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9383583068847656, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(568.75), np.float64(1319.509661458333)), (np.float64(568.75), np.float64(1554.0461197916666)), (np.float64(2635.281982421875), np.float64(1554.0461197916666)), (np.float64(2635.281982421875), np.float64(1319.509661458333))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 178, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': 'b4c2569ab76729d6c9c83088915761eb', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': '748c905e60b8a6aa7d0217d2a054b971'}, page_content='Before creating and configuring Group Service Plans, Velocity network operators should have specified the QoS Service Mode in which the system will operate — the Symbol-based mode of operation or the IP-based mode of operation. These options, which are mutually exclusive, are selected at the Velocity Network level.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9407385587692261, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(568.4892578125), np.float64(1600.2388281249998)), (np.float64(568.4892578125), np.float64(1897.496337890625)), (np.float64(2638.315786458333), np.float64(1897.496337890625)), (np.float64(2638.315786458333), np.float64(1600.2388281249998))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 178, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': 'b4c2569ab76729d6c9c83088915761eb', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': 'e818c74e2526327de7b0b7d718280870'}, page_content='If the Symbol-based mode is specified, Group Service Plan configuration supports data rates in terms of Mbps at a nominal MODCOD, which is equivalent to Symbols/s or MHz. Bandwidth allocation algorithms are based on symbols. As such, the system translates the configured MIR/CIR (Mbps) to symbols using the configured nominal MODCOD, and thereby scales the demand accordingly. QoS Stats are reported in bytes and contain the L2 overhead.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.946658194065094, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(568.75), np.float64(1942.947161458333)), (np.float64(568.75), np.float64(2301.4419531249996)), (np.float64(2622.061767578125), np.float64(2301.4419531249996)), (np.float64(2622.061767578125), np.float64(1942.947161458333))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 178, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': 'b4c2569ab76729d6c9c83088915761eb', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': '185ac65169090b691ba43db37be94927'}, page_content='If the IP-Based option is specified, Satellite Operators and Service Providers create and configure Group Service Plans (GSPs) with CIR/MIR specified as a Mbps data rate and thereby offer Mbps as a Service. Service Providers can provision and manage bandwidth at the GSP/SSPC level at a real IP rate, with MIR enforcement at the GSP level. Bandwidth demand, allocation, and usage statistics for both GSPs and SSPCs are monitored at the real IP rate for unicast traffic.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9518720507621765, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(568.75), np.float64(2346.52392578125)), (np.float64(568.75), np.float64(2830.087786458333)), (np.float64(2636.565786458333), np.float64(2830.087786458333)), (np.float64(2636.565786458333), np.float64(2346.52392578125))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 178, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': 'b4c2569ab76729d6c9c83088915761eb', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': '4ed047acfb3383bc89ec8e5e67032041'}, page_content='In the IP-based mode, system bandwidth allocation algorithms are all natively performed in Mbps. In general, the Mbps mode is more accurate than the symbols mode - both in bandwidth allocation and statistics measurements, for both GSPs and SSPCs. Also, in Mbps mode, the GBWM management is in pure IP bytes (with no OTA overhead for unicast traffic), which ultimately results in stats that are more accurate. Furthermore, MIR is strictly enforced for downstream traffic for GSPs and SSPCs, and for upstream traffic for GSPs. The GBWM bandwidth allocation algorithm does not strictly enforce MIR for upstream traffic at the SSPC level of the GQE Tree when the iNet contains excess bandwidth.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.8977736234664917, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(568.75), np.float64(2874.02392578125)), (np.float64(568.75), np.float64(2986.8586197916666)), (np.float64(2427.0322265625), np.float64(2986.8586197916666)), (np.float64(2427.0322265625), np.float64(2874.02392578125))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 178, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': 'b4c2569ab76729d6c9c83088915761eb', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': '5539162d7512eec085c85447f91e82a3'}, page_content='See Operating in Symbol-based Mode on page 176 and Operating in IP-based Mode on page 176.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9158142805099487, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(568.75), np.float64(3074.9054947916666)), (np.float64(56