), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 179, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': '42b820d00a675a1f17c6c53bf4757873', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': '94e4812850304f02b9f763b7e7c2496d'}, page_content='A GSP may have a geographic scope that is global (the entire satellite network). Alternatively, a regional geographic scope may be configured as a specific region. A regional geographic scope is defined as a collection of one or more beams or service areas. Beams forming a region may or may not be adjacent, and may be provided by the same or different satellites.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9524971842765808, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(568.0795288085938), np.float64(1366.9054947916666)), (np.float64(568.0795288085938), np.float64(1787.3794531249998)), (np.float64(2635.39208984375), np.float64(1787.3794531249998)), (np.float64(2635.39208984375), np.float64(1366.9054947916666))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 179, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': '42b820d00a675a1f17c6c53bf4757873', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': '69336034743d1f99c8c289d7c5bc0f98'}, page_content='In previous Velocity releases, GSP regional geoscopes were based on regions that only consisted of beams and satellites, which did not allow operators to specify custom geographic areas where they intended to sell a service. Ne