ntrolled by the SAS QoS Enforcer. For additional bandwidth allocation information, see Global Bandwidth Allocation on page 165.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9388054609298706, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(568.75), np.float64(2531.736083984375)), (np.float64(568.75), np.float64(2771.754453125)), (np.float64(2636.25146484375), np.float64(2771.754453125)), (np.float64(2636.25146484375), np.float64(2531.736083984375))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 196, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': '7a58259a1ce6c7625e726502ea380eb9', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': '5a70614547f2e1df80e23f6655a0bac0'}, page_content='The CIR/MIR parameters of each node are adjusted dynamically by the GQE, but bandwidth is allocated to SSPCs on satellite terminals by the iNet QoS engine. During bandwidth allocation to parent nodes, only the configuration properties of parent nodes are considered, while the demand is derived from children nodes.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(353.6458333333333), np.float64(3514.3013281249996)), (np.float64(353.6458333333333), np.float64(3562.900286458333)), (np.float64(430.0836416027083), np.float64(3562.900286458333)), (np.float64(430.0836416027083), np.float64(3514.3013281249996))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 196, 'file_directory': 