'2413f0e5af1279cfe09ac4ac251b8039', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': 'c583057ea440d5593c7a91c734ed1e91'}, page_content="The SSPC is the source of demand for the Global QoS enforcement engine. The GQE structure is a tree hierarchy, in which every node's demand is the aggregated demand of all children nodes. On the downstream (outbound), the demand is generated every 100 milliseconds. On the upstream (inbound), it is generated every 125 milliseconds."), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9430109858512878, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(568.3858642578125), np.float64(2850.759661458333)), (np.float64(568.3858642578125), np.float64(3085.2961197916666)), (np.float64(2587.529328125), np.float64(3085.2961197916666)), (np.float64(2587.529328125), np.float64(2850.759661458333))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 197, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': '2413f0e5af1279cfe09ac4ac251b8039', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': 'e0fc04a059d117518cc91936a3fc68d3'}, page_content='The iNet QoS algorithm works by calculating demand, bottom up, for every node of the GQE tree. The nodes at the bottom, which are SSPCs, gather demand from service levels in the VRs. These demands are grouped according to the configured priority for the SSPCs, with higher priority groups taking precedence over lower priority groups.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9410316348075867, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(564.4244384765625), np.float64(3131.4888281249996)), (np.float64(564.4244384765625), np.float64(3428.004453125)), (np.float64(2640.940786458333), np.float64(3428.004453125)), (np.float64(2640.940786458333), np.float64(3131.4888281249996))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 197, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': '2413f0e5af1279cfe09ac4ac251b8039', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': '8f064e8dac19022c22cd10f917bde00e'}, page_content='Satellite bandwidth is then allocated top-down for every node of the GQE tree. The priority allocation is based on two cycles — CIR round and best-effort round. The engine offers two types of priorities — absolute and per-allocation-round. For absolute priority, nodes are grouped based on their configured priority, and the round of allocations applies to the higher priority node before moving to the next priority level. For per-allocation-round priority, nodes'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.5555800199508667, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(353.6458333333333), np.float64(3514.3013281249996)), (np.float64(353.6458333333333), np.float64(3562.900286458333)), (np.float64(1680.7574462890625), np.float64(3562.900286458333)), (np.float64(1680.7574462890625), np.float64(3514.3013281249996))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 197, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': '2413f0e5af1279cfe09ac4ac251b8039', 'categ