priority applies to the round of allocation, serving CIR by priority, then moves on to the best-effort round of allocation.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9037083983421326, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(568.75), np.float64(557.5304947916666)), (np.float64(568.75), np.float64(606.1294531250002)), (np.float64(2621.185302734375), np.float64(606.1294531250002)), (np.float64(2621.185302734375), np.float64(557.5304947916666))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 198, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': '2ca2ca78e9aa18ef777074ff512bf7af', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': '0e8b5668c61f1d28915cfd3b9c8ddc35'}, page_content='The following concepts provide more detail of the iNet QoS demand and allocation algorithm:'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9473252892494202, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(556.280517578125), np.float64(650.013671875)), (np.float64(556.280517578125), np.float64(948.9119873046875)), (np.float64(2604.737661458333), np.float64(948.9119873046875)), (np.float64(2604.737661458333), np.float64(650.013671875))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 198, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': '2ca2ca78e9aa18ef777074ff512bf7af', 'category': 'ListItem', 'element_id': '44d164ae683e1f46042e42b6247ad97e'}, page_content='• Outbound Demand — On the DVB-S2 ACM outbound, the service level demand is generated in bytes for the next 100 ms. The demand reported by the SSPC is the maximum of rate-demand and depth-demand. The rate-demand is an estimation of how many bytes are classified in the service level queue for the next 100 ms interval. The depth-demand measures the number of bytes already in the service level queue.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9523084163665771, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(567.5468749999999), np.float64(995.0304947916665)), (np.float64(567.5468749999999), np.float64(1415.7523193359375)), (np.float64(2635.8001614583336), np.float64(1415.7523193359375)), (np.float64(2635.8001614583336), np.float64(995.0304947916665))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 198, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': '2ca2ca78e9aa18ef777074ff512bf7af', 'category': 'ListItem', 'element_id': 'ec71133e0742ebda49b47c4177d424b9'}, page_content="• Inbound Demand — Each SSPC generates upstream demand based on the upstream IP packets received by the satellite terminal that match the SSPC's service levels. The demand is sent to the SAS every 125 ms to request allocation of slots in the next TDMA frame. All nodes report demand up the tree in slots. The demand is converted into the number of slots by dividing the demand, in bytes, by the configured size of the time-slot. Each node in the tree aggregates demand from its child nodes and sends it up the tree in slots."), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9359572529792786, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(560.5173950195312), np.float64(1461.697161458333)), (np.float64(560.5173950195312), np.float64(1634.786376953125)), (np.float64(2586.544953125), np.float64(1634.786376953125)), (np.float64(2586.544953125), np.float64(1461.697161458333))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 198, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': '2ca2ca78e9aa18ef777074ff512bf7af', 'category': 'ListItem', 'element_id': 'd7a7f7a76cab0be3ba4801e672af3a89'}, page_content='• Outbound Allocation — On the ACM outbound, all node allocations are based on scaled information rate. For SSPCs, the scaled information rate is converted based on the scaling factor of the current operating MODCOD.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9180576205253601, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(590.3018188476562), np.float64(1676.04736328125)), (np.float64(590.3018188476562), np.float64(1792.870361328125)), (np.float64(2530.4443359375), np.float64(1792.870361328125)), (np.float64(2530.4443359375), np.float64(1676.04736328125))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 198, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': '2ca2ca78e9aa18ef777074ff512bf7af', 'category': 'ListItem', 'element_id': '636ff7f3edd053af6721acfec355a092'}, 