nt(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9027897119522095, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(568.75), np.float64(394.8340885416665)), (np.float64(568.75), np.float64(462.9017968750001)), (np.float64(1736.198974609375), np.float64(462.9017968750001)), (np.float64(1736.198974609375), np.float64(394.8340885416665))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 199, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': '69d7d98d1950ce34e669a478e96ab4e5', 'category': 'Title', 'element_id': '156208350c93db0d65979f902393357f'}, page_content='4.6.3 Global Bandwidth Allocation'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9405677914619446, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(568.75), np.float64(506.4888281249999)), (np.float64(568.75), np.float64(741.0252864583334)), (np.float64(2611.43017578125), np.float64(741.0252864583334)), (np.float64(2611.43017578125), np.float64(506.4888281249999))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 199, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': '156208350c93db0d65979f902393357f', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': 'd022ad8ce99d9eab030ca4aee96511a2'}, page_content='The Global QoS Enforcer (GQE) is the portion of the GBWM system that maintains the GQE tree based on the GSPs created by service providers. Each GSP node in an iNet is dynamically assigned a CIR/MIR by the GQE, based on changes in the aggregate traffic demand from satellite terminals for that GSP node.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9388365745544434, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(564.0449829101562), np.float64(787.2179947916666)), (np.float64(564.0449829101562), np.float64(1021.7544531250002)), (np.float64(2595.112661458333), np.float64(1021.7544531250002)), (np.float64(2595.112661458333), np.float64(787.2179947916666))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 199, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': '156208350c93db0d65979f902393357f', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': 'fe9c90756704c8b259285e9260974a32'}, page_content='The GQE is distributed between the NOC and all SASs. The NOC GQE adjusts the CIR/MIR of GSP nodes in the SAS GQE tree, based on the aggregate demand from each SAS. The SAS QoS Enforcer, in turn, performs CIR/MIR adjustments for each GSP node in all of its iNets, based on the aggregate demands from each iNet.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.6124005317687988, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(1218.8170166015625), np.float64(2528.6502864583335)), (np.float64(1218.8170166015625), np.float64(2577.2492447916666)), (np.float64(1979.8887939453125), np.float64(2577.2492447916666)), (np.float64(1979.8887939453125), np.float64(2528.6502864583335))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 199, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'category': 'FigureCaption', 'element_id': '4c37dce82641e8768c5f1bc0b98f7d90'}, page_content='Figure 4-18. Global QoS Enforcer'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9346970915794373, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(566.4672241210938), np.float64(2632.009661458333)), (np.float64(566.4672241210938), np.float64(2990.7958984375)), (np.float64(2604.4459947916666), np.float64(2990.7958984375)), (np.float64(2604.4459947916666), np.float64(2632.009661458333))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 199, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': 'ad403cdc4cdbdcab7c52bae5a7241933'}, page_content='The GQE dynamically adjusts CIR and MIR at the iNet level based on the global bandwidth hierarchy built from GSPs, aggregate demand, load balancing considerations, and satellite terminal distribution across the system. The CIR/MIR for the service provider is calculated dynamically by the GQE, based on traffic demand and usage from each iNet. Traffic bandwidth management is performed by the Global QoS Enforcer by maintaining a dedicated bandwidth partition node at each iNet QoS enforcement tree.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.41793888807296753, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(353.6458333333333), np.float64(3509.81787109375)), (np.float64(353.6458333333333), np.float64(3628.525286458333)), (np.float64(1942.176513671875), np.float64(3628.525286458333)), (np.float64(1942.176513671875), np.float64(3509.81787109375))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 199, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': 'b0a23cdc8f206f4e4966b2af4c14d455'}, page_content='ST Engineering iDirect Proprietary | Confidentiality: Public Technical Reference Guide | iDirect Velocity™ | T0001665 | Revision 1'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.5051665306091309, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(2544.864583333333), np.float64(3514.3013281249996)), (np.float64(2544.864583333333), np.float64(3562.900286458333)), (np.float64(2624.36865234375), np.float64(3562.900286458333)), (np.float64(2624.36865234375), np.float64(3514.3013281249996))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 199, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': '641fd41ba759fc8db02b54c02ebb3a89'}, page_content='165'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9260883331298828, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(350.0), np.float64(251.28049479166657)), (np.float64(350.0), np.float64(299.87945312500017)), (np.float64(1136.492919921875), np.float64(299.87945312500017)), (np.float64(1136.492919921875), np.float64(251.28049479166657))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 200, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'category': 'Header', 'element_id': '9800dd672cb07c1def62b2308ed952f3'}, page_content='4.6.3 Global Bandwidth Allocation'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.7620328664779663, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(1074.62109375), np.float64(1835.9419531249996)), (np.float64(1074.62109375), np.float64(1884.5409114583329)), (np.float64(2118.84790793375), np.float64(1884.5409114583329)), (np.float64(2118.84790793375), np.float64(1835.9419531249996))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 200, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'category': 'FigureCaption', 'element_id': '938bbd1de8ac83d92493ed06f2c34bfb'}, page_content='Figure 4-19. Dynamic Bandwidth Management'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9360562562942505, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(568.75), np.float64(1939.3013281249998)), (np.float64(568.75), np.float64(2111.8586197916666)), (np.float64(2523.6704671521866), np.float64(2111.8586197916666)), (np.float64(2523.6704671521866), np.float64(1939.3013281249998))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 200, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': '6ccddce44331073f13a61004e1b3a51c'}, page_content='In case of a failure of the GQE, or when communication to it is lost, the SAS bandwidth manager sends bandwidth demands to the GQE in the backup NOC. Data is continually replicated between the primary and backup GQEs, making the backup GQE a hot standby.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9462193250656128, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(564.4471435546875), np.float64(2158.0513281249996)), (np.float64(564.4471435546875), np.float64(2578.5252864583335)), (np.float64(2631.315786458333), np.float64(2578.5252864583335)), (np.float64(2631.315786458333), np.float64(2158.0513281249996))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 200, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': '01bb31bb41d10a7f5a4e314b0af5181e'}, page_content='If there is no backup GQE, or if there is a loss of communication between the SAS and both NOCs, the SAS continues to distribute its dynamic CIR/MIR to its iNets based on its last allocation before loss of communication with the NOC. Additionally, all satellite terminal bandwidth management functionality, including service scheduling and FAP enforcement, will also run at the SAS during the NOC outage. The GQE assumes the SAS is operating autonomously with the last allocated dynamic CIR/MIR and continues the dynamic adjustments to the other SASs.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9412803053855896, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(567.2501220703125), np.float64(2624.7179947916666)), (np.float64(567.2501220703125), np.float64(2921.2336197916666)), (np.float64(2609.841828125), np.float64(2921.2336197916666)), (np.float64(2609.841828125), np.float64(2624.7179947916666))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 200, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': '068f28b103ca80d28db539d791ba53d2'}, page_content='In case of a SAS failover, as soon as the switchover is completed and the GQE starts receiving data from the backup SAS, which has now become the active SAS, global enforcement resumes at this new active SAS. If the newly active SAS is a partial SAS (i.e. not populated with line cards sufficient to provide coverage to all channels), the shift in the allocation to the SAS will happen automatically as demand from the partial SAS is reduced.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.370508074760437, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(353.6458333333333), np.float64(3514.3013281249996)), (np.float64(353.6458333333333), np.float64(3562.900286458333)), (np.float64(430.5961608886719), np.float64(3562.900286458333)), (np.float64(430.5961608886719), np.float64(3514.3013281249996))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13