s child nodes exceeds the allocation the GSP has received — i.e. there is bandwidth contention. These options support various business models and may be combined, as described in Allocation Fairness Algorithms on page 134.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.8885849714279175, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(833.5853271484375), np.float64(888.1849975585938)), (np.float64(833.5853271484375), np.float64(1124.5694580078125)), (np.float64(2586.544953125), np.float64(1124.5694580078125)), (np.float64(2586.544953125), np.float64(888.1849975585938))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 202, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': 'a1c084177c7079344d0f702468b31f36'}, page_content='NOTE: Allocation fairness only applies when there is contention; when there is no contention, all nodes below the GSP receive their demand, subject to their configured CIR and MIR. Allocation fairness happens at the iNet level. It is done using the dynamic CIR/MIR assigned to the GSP nodes by the GQE process.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9059410691261292, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(566.0177001953125), np.float64(1261.1763281249998)), (np.float64(566.0177001953125), np.float64(1309.7752864583335)), (np.float64(1911.2237548828125), np.float64(1309.7752864583335)), (np.float64(1911.2237548828125), np.float64(1261.1763281249998))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified':