), np.float64(251.28049479166657)), (np.float64(346.337890625), np.float64(299.87945312500017)), (np.float64(865.2625732421875), np.float64(299.87945312500017)), (np.float64(865.2625732421875), np.float64(251.28049479166657))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 218, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'category': 'Header', 'element_id': '49c922d8274c41be287cd0e8d3c9e00b'}, page_content='5.1.1.2 Physical Layer'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.7301665544509888, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(865.4843749999999), np.float64(1777.6086197916661)), (np.float64(865.4843749999999), np.float64(1826.2075781249996)), (np.float64(2328.140524896302), np.float64(1826.2075781249996)), (np.float64(2328.140524896302), np.float64(1777.6086197916661))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 218, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'category': 'FigureCaption', 'element_id': '79e75c480ed9e0d91f269d20b759c19f'}, page_content='Figure 5-2. Before Rain Diversity Switchover - SAS Configuration'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9428816437721252, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(568.75), np.float64(1880.9679947916663)), (np.float64(568.75), np.float64(2239.462786458333)), (np.float64(2631.425161458333), np.float64(2239.462786458333)), (np.float64(2631.425161458333), np.float64(1880.9679947916663))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 218, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': '0e06196966b4ff351dddb1dcc085576d'}, page_content='Under normal operation, traffic flows through the primary site, traverses the backbone network and terminates at the primary site PP. The primary site PP uses the tunnel VLAN/SVN (virtual local area network/satellite virtual network) to send data to the appropriate transmit (Tx) line cards. The data is then sent over the air to the user terminal. In the reverse direction, traffic from the terminal lands at the receive (Rx) line cards, and is sent to the primary site PP over the same tunnels.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9487193822860718, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(568.75), np.float64(2285.6554947916666)), (np.float64(568.75), np.float64(2582.1711197916666)), (np.float64(2642.2890625), np.float64(2582.1711197916666)), (np.float64(2642.2890625), np.float64(2285.6554947916666))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 218, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': '6b1580895e630b85568b07eee5d94cd6'}, page_content="Since the diversity site lies within the same beam footprint as the primary site, all inbound traffic to the primary site over the satellite is also received at the diversity site. This traffic is ignored by the diversity site's PP. Further, there is no outbound traffic from the diversity site as the Tx line cards in the diversity site are muted. It is also important to note that in normal operation there is no user traffic on the backbone network from the diversity site."), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9413838982582092, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(568.75), np.float64(2628.3638281249996)), (np.float64(568.75), np.float64(2986.8586197916666)), (np.float64(2641.1230781249997), np.float64(2986.8586197916666)), (np.float64(2641.1230781249997), np.float64(2628.3638281249996))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 218, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': '52b39c2526ecb0462967e0973235524d'}, page_content="Upon deciding to switch to the rain diversity site, the primary site's PP mutes the Tx line cards of the affected iNets in the primary SAS and begins sending user traffic through the tunnels between the PPs in the primary SAS and the line cards in the diversity SAS over the terrestrial backbone network. The Tx line cards are unmuted and over the air traffic is established at the diversity site. Line cards are logically part of the same IF (intermediate frequency) domain."), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9467281103134155, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(568.75), np.float64(3032.916015625)), (np.float64(568.75), np.float64(3329.566953125)), (np.float64(2605.6491197916666), np.float64(3329.566953125)), (np.float64(2605.6491197916666), np.float64(3032.916015625))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 218, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': '003247554f819d48878391e5898c1ce7'}, page_content='iNets are switched between the Rain Diversity and Primary SASs based on iNet priority. This allows Rain Diversity Switchover (RDS) to be used with a backup site that does not contain a full complement of equipment. If the equipment at the diversity/backup site cannot support all user traffic switching over, iNets that remain on the nominal path may experience packet loss and other service interruption due to the rain-fade event at the primary site.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.322005033493042, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(353.6458333333333), np.float64(3514.3013281249996)), (np.float64(353.6458333333333), np.float64(3562.900286458333)), (np.float64(433.0162048339844), np.float64(3562.900286458333)), (np.float64(433.0162048339844), np.float64(3514.3013281249996))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 218, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': '659dc1b8997283fe2588ac270b53991e'}, page_content='184'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9