': 0.933759868144989, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(561.2694702148438), np.float64(400.7596614583332)), (np.float64(561.2694702148438), np.float64(511.3377864583335)), (np.float64(2470.00341796875), np.float64(511.3377864583335)), (np.float64(2470.00341796875), np.float64(400.7596614583332))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 222, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': '6182749e06a7d92eb0336c2b29fae5bd', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': 'c61b1794cfcdce6f49516ac55075c083'}, page_content='The Velocity network operating prior switching over to a rain diversity configuration is illustrated in the diagram below.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.8463786840438843, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(754.1302490234375), np.float64(2291.6711197916666)), (np.float64(754.1302490234375), np.float64(2340.2700781249996)), (np.float64(2422.0207332296354), np.float64(2340.2700781249996)), (np.float64(2422.0207332296354), np.float64(2291.6711197916666))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 222, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'category': 'FigureCaption', 'element_id': '7fd6bbb3e8ad710337b366e9eec9a594'}, page_content='Figure 5-5. Before Rain Diversity Switchover - RF Gateway Configuration'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9509374499320984, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(568.75), np.float64(2395.0304947916666)), (np.float64(568.75), np.float64(2753.525286458333)), (np.float64(2588.8782864583336), np.float64(2753.525286458333)), (np.float64(2588.8782864583336), np.float64(2395.0304947916666))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 222, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': 'db102a660494382542a6007270dc7f0a'}, page_content='Under normal operation, traffic traverses the backbone network and terminates at the RF Gateway Primary Site. The Primary Site uses the tunnel VLAN/SVN (virtual local area network/satellite virtual network) to send data to the appropriate transmit (Tx) line cards. The data is then sent over the air to the user terminal. In the reverse direction, traffic from the terminal lands at the receive (Rx) line cards, and is sent to the primary site PP over the same tunnels.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9316514730453491, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(561.046875), np.float64(2799.7179947916666)), (np.float64(561.046875), np.float64(2910.2961197916666)), (np.float64(2562.3730781249997), np.float64(2910.2961197916666)), (np.float64(2562.3730781249997), np.float64(2799.7179947916666))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 222, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': '563d045efde183e718581b4a737499a9'}, page_content='Since the Diversity RF Gateway lies within the same beam footprint as the Primary Site, all inbound traffic to the Primary Site over the satellite is also received at the Diversity Site.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9400115013122559, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(568.75), np.float64(2956.4888281249996)), (np.float64(568.75), np.float64(3253.004453125)), (np.float64(2626.0293281249997), np.float64(3253.004453125)), (np.float64(2626.0293281249997), np.float64(2956.4888281249996))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 222, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': 'c6bfd7ad50bf2856c7aea2b94cb9df2c'}, page_content="Upon deciding to switch to the Diversity Site, the CDC's PP mutes the Tx line cards of the affected iNets in the Primary RF Gateway Site and begins sending user traffic through the tunnels between the PPs in the RF Gateway Primary Site and the line cards in the RF Gateway Diversity Site over the terrestrial backbone network. The Tx line cards are unmuted and over the air traffic is established at the Diversity site."), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9252337217330933, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(568.75), np.float64(3299.197161458333)), (np.float64(568.75), np.float64(3409.775286458333)), (np.float64(2606.998078124999), np.float64(3409.775286458333)), (np.float64(2606.998078124999), np.float64(3299.197161458333))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 222, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': 'f119fe388f382447fc27c8fd2d9fc756'}, page_content='iNets are switched between the Diversity RF Gateway and Primary RF Gateway based on iNet priority. This allows Rain Diversity Switchover (RDS) to be used with a backup site that does'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.33634594082832336, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(353.6458333333333), np.float64(3514.3013281249996)), (np.float64(353.6458333333333), np.float64(3562.900286458333)), (np.float64(432.1209716796875), np.float64(3562.900286458333)), (np.float64(432.1209716796875), np.float64(3514.3013281249996))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 222, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': 'c20f4218cab4ed25f9b1a086ab61dbb2'}, page_content='188'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.45104819536209106, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(1063.6112060546875), np.float64(3509.0849609375)), (np.float64(1063.6112060546875), np.float64(3628.525286458333)), (np.float64(2628.670166015625), np.float64(3628.525286458333)), (np.float64(2628.670166015625), n