nd all global bandwidth management (GBWM) features, the network operator may install a backup NOC. It contains the same Velocity components as the primary NOC — a NOC Pulse NMS and a GBWM cluster.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9365012645721436, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(568.75), np.float64(1253.884661458333)), (np.float64(568.75), np.float64(1426.4419531249998)), (np.float64(2625.190786458333), np.float64(1426.4419531249998)), (np.float64(2625.190786458333), np.float64(1253.884661458333))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 235, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': '8e543b6b960d5bcb5abeeb9211cc49e6'}, page_content='NOC component redundancy ensures that a failure of any component does not cause a service outage or degradation of Velocity system performance. For a description of component redundancy, see Component Redundancy on page 207.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.8681250214576721, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(568.75), np.float64(1517.7507552083334)), (np.float64(568.75), np.float64(1585.8184635416667)), (np.float64(1703.2435302734375), np.float64(1585.8184635416667)), (np.float64(1703.2435302734375), np.float64(1517.7507552083334))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 235, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd