 Velocity network, An IF domain defines a specific IF frequency range that supports carrier operation on a satellite\'s outbound and inbound. Velocity supports what is referred to as "symmetric IF domains," and "asymmetric IF Domains."'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9343039989471436, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(561.81494140625), np.float64(717.9471614583332)), (np.float64(561.81494140625), np.float64(952.4836197916668)), (np.float64(2555.336619791666), np.float64(952.4836197916668)), (np.float64(2555.336619791666), np.float64(717.9471614583332))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 242, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': '5e60d8366eec96fa31d1e5875a3fe61b', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': '4a2f102f99a7af4055c50c54c05fa169'}, page_content='A symmetric IF Domain is one in which inbound and outbound carriers are grouped into a single IF Domain, and where each IF Domain supports a combination of both Rx and Tx line cards, and is based on a one-to-one relationship with a single up-converter and down- converter.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9471931457519531, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(568.75), np.float64(1002.3221614583332)), (np.float64(568.75), np.float64(1298.8377864583335)), (np.float64(2636.602244791666), np.float64(1298.8377864583335)), (np.float64(2636.602244791666), np.float64(1002.3221614583332))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 242, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': '5e60d8366eec96fa31d1e5875a3fe61b', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': '0f560701d38ea7cacc5fb76b69e31f6f'}, page_content='An asymmetric IF Domain is one in which the configuration of both inbound or outbound car- riers is possible. In this case, the NMS supports configuration of separate elements, for inbound IF Domains that contain only Rx line cards; and for outbound IF Domains that can only contain Tx line cards. Asymmetric IF Domains support all traffic flows in both CDC and SAS sites.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9154115915298462, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(568.75), np.float64(1348.6763281249998)), (np.float64(568.75), np.float64(1459.2544531249998)), (np.float64(2498.0263671875), np.float64(1459.2544531249998)), (np.float64(2498.0263671875), np.float64(1348.6763281249998))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 242, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': '5e60d8366eec96fa31d1e5875a3fe61b', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': '4bb43b70d314b09d7a3008828b35598e'}, page_content='An IF domain can support one or more iNets. Any line cards in an IF domain that are not assigned to an iNet are standby line cards.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.7267909049987793, 'is_extracted': 'true', '