c association between a particular iNet and line cards. When a PP gets a list of iNets that consist of one Tx and one or more Rx line cards per iNet, it starts assigning unallocated line cards to the iNets until it runs out of unallocated line cards.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9521703720092773, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(566.101806640625), np.float64(1341.384661458333)), (np.float64(566.101806640625), np.float64(1700.4752197265625)), (np.float64(2633.510986328125), np.float64(1700.4752197265625)), (np.float64(2633.510986328125), np.float64(1341.384661458333))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 243, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': 'b68da6b944f818f71f20f07e36aac8a6', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': '3a6a1c50e5e68cfadaf1c7a976d4904f'}, page_content='The following diagram is an example of the line card distribution to IF domains in a single chassis. In this example, there are two different IF domains (A and B). IF Domain A supports one iNet with a primary Tx line card, a standby Tx line card, and two Rx line cards. IF Domain B supports two iNets, with one Tx line card and one Rx line card each. A tunnel connects the PP cluster to the active line cards. Traffic flows between the terminals and a Web server in the Internet or the subscriber’s private network.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9146613478660583, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(582.0377807617188), np.float64(1744.948974609375)),