p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9479554891586304, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(568.721923828125), np.float64(1934.2947998046875)), (np.float64(568.721923828125), np.float64(2294.150286458333)), (np.float64(2634.815786458333), np.float64(2294.150286458333)), (np.float64(2634.815786458333), np.float64(1934.2947998046875))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 253, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': '5c3bb27b4537d3d8bca37dde14bb3cfa'}, page_content='Each Velocity and Pulse server provides two physical ports for connection to the SAS switching fabric. These ports are bonded using Link Aggregation Control Protocol (LACP) to dynamically form a dynamic Link Aggregation Group (LAG) or with the switch as per 802.3ad. Similarly, each line card provides two physical ports for connection to the SAS switching fabric. These ports are bonded but do not support LACP; static port groups must be configured on the switch.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9495348930358887, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(568.75), np.float64(2340.0703125)), (np.float64(568.75), np.float64(2698.8377864583335)), (np.float64(2608.0553697916666), np.float64(2698.8377864583335)), (np.float64(2608.0553697916666), np.float64(2340.0703125))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 253, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': '57151dcb5f3b798aed6e33711fd802c7'}, page_content='The SAS LAN is architected with a redundant switching fabric it uses on redundant SAS switches as well as key features of that networking equipment to provide a highly available service. These features include Virtual Port Channel (VPC), LACP, Port Channel, etc. In the example architecture, shown in the above diagram, every server and line card is dual-homed to two top-of-rack fabric extenders, which are in turn dual-homed to the core switching fabric, using the Nexus switch enhanced VPC feature.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9407380819320679, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(564.7586059570312), np.float64(2745.0304947916666)), (np.float64(564.7586059570312), np.float64(3041.5461197916666)), (np.float64(2620.815786458333), np.float64(3041.5461197916666)), (np.float64(2620.815786458333), np.float64(2745.0304947916666))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 253, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': 'cc3d08b732e8ee655bff297572511853'}, page_content='This diagram also shows a pair of access routers. These routers are also dual-homed to the SAS switch. Typically, the SAS access routers connect to the backbone network via a redundant pair of edge routers and standard IP and/or MPLS (Multi-Protocol Label Switching) protocols. The use of these protocols and BGP between the access router and PPs ensure that data connectivity is preserved even if a router should fail.'), 