ons; and second, is building of real-time streaming applications to transform or react to streams of data. The first of these two general applications represents the Kafka implementation in Pulse 2.6.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9405600428581238, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(568.75), np.float64(1556.4888281249998)), (np.float64(568.75), np.float64(1791.025286458333)), (np.float64(2641.424560546875), np.float64(1791.025286458333)), (np.float64(2641.424560546875), np.float64(1556.4888281249998))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 259, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': 'eca957307c5e7d5a86461806f9c8914b', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': '5f4ff5cf1345c369b8d3b6329de166a2'}, page_content='Kafka both publishes and subscribes to streams of records, similar to a message queue; it stores streams of records, using fault-tolerant methods; and it processes streams of records as they occur. This combination of messaging, storage, and stream processing is essential to the Kafka role as a streaming platform.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9467532634735107, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(568.75), np.float64(1837.2179947916663)), (np.float64(568.75), np.float64(2134.04736328125)), (np.float64(2639.7012031249997), np.float64(2134.04736328125)), (np.float64(2639.7012031249997), np.float64(1837.2179947916663))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 259, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': 'eca957307c5e7d5a86461806f9c8914b', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': '132a79a9b4f9a68b813487a91d027500'}, page_content='Kafka is run as a cluster on one or more servers that can span multiple sites. The Kafka cluster stores streams of records in categories called topics, where each record consists of a key, a value, and a time-stamp. Client/server communication is accomplished with a simple, high- performance, language-agnostic TCP protocol. The Kafka implementation in Pulse operates using three core APIs:'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9140022397041321, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(673.2760416666666), np.float64(2177.30810546875)), (np.float64(673.2760416666666), np.float64(2290.80712890625)), (np.float64(2557.697021484375), np.float64(2290.80712890625)), (np.float64(2557.697021484375), np.float64(2177.30810546875))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 259, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': 'eca957307c5e7d5a86461806f9c8914b', 'category': 'ListItem', 'element_id': '8a8a387b8e327e36e39767cbf5731d8a'}, page_content='• Producer API: allows an application to publish a stream of records to one or more Kafka topics — it pushes messages from the application into different topics.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_