.float64(871.0721614583332)), (np.float64(565.4735717773438), np.float64(1167.5877864583335)), (np.float64(2645.96337890625), np.float64(1167.5877864583335)), (np.float64(2645.96337890625), np.float64(871.0721614583332))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 265, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': '853e3ab7e957237bdc0e95fa11afe4a3', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': '7db7ae771bfc8499b8ce3776919da82c'}, page_content='The discrete data engine (DDE) process receives all event messages from any initiating source, including other NMS processes, SAS processes, network components, and external systems. The DDE process generates alarms and incidents based on rules and algorithms. An extensible action framework automatically invokes actions and notifications for events, alarms, or incidents.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9322875142097473, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(568.75), np.float64(1213.6297607421875)), (np.float64(568.75), np.float64(1448.3169531249998)), (np.float64(2618.65625), np.float64(1448.3169531249998)), (np.float64(2618.65625), np.float64(1213.6297607421875))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 265, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': '853e3ab7e957237bdc0e95fa11afe4a3', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': 'b3e218a1432e0f64e161202fdae89f43'}, page_content='Data path generated events are pushed from the data path to the DDE in the SAS NMS, where they are stored. The NMS state model at the SAS evaluates these events and converts them into the appropriate alarms. Alarms are pushed to the NOC NMS, where they are stored. Optionally, alarms may be grouped together into incidents for easier handling.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9369490742683411, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(568.75), np.float64(1498.1554947916666)), (np.float64(568.75), np.float64(1732.6919531249998)), (np.float64(2586.7637031249997), np.float64(1732.6919531249998)), (np.float64(2586.7637031249997), np.float64(1498.1554947916666))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 265, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': '853e3ab7e957237bdc0e95fa11afe4a3', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': '8e7e58aef554a8da80be21a247a8cb79'}, page_content='When the Kafka for events is switched on, the events generated at the SAS or received from the datapath are pushed to Kafka topic “event”. The event topic is mirrored to the NOC by Kafka Mirror Maker running at NOC. When kafka is On for events, events processing will not happen on SAS so no events are stored at SAS.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.8540622591972351, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(567.909912109375), np.float64(1823.1947021484375)), (np.float64(567.909912109375), np.float64(1892.0684635416667)), (np.float64(1278.2108154296875), np.float64(1892.0684635416667)), (np.float64(1278.2108154296875), np.float64(1823.1947021484375))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 265, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': 'baf774f3ca217003067531222def3298', 'category': 'Title', 'element_id': 'f263f21f8080461c0a2030246fb6fbf5'}, page_content='6.4.4 Stats Manager'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9380429983139038, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(568.75), np.float64(1934.166259765625)), (np.float64(568.75), np.float64(2232.1711197916666)), (np.float64(2576.491943359375), np.float64(2232.1711197916666)), (np.float64(2576.491943359375), np.float64(1934.166259765625))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 265, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': 'f263f21f8080461c0a2030246fb6fbf5', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': '83f85ce77a0474f45b3bd6705d05fa08'}, page_content='The stats manager process handles querying, caching, and storage requests for statistics generated by any source. Multiple Stats Manager instances are created dependent upon the setting of the Stats Manager instantiation parameter, which is configured based on the estimated size of network elements. An instance of Stats Manager may be used for either historical statistics or for real-time statistics.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9415062665939331, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(567.0865478515625), np.float64(2278.3638281249996)), (np.float64(567.0865478515625), np.float64(2574.879453125)), (np.float64(2624.352244791666), np.float64(2574.879453125)), (np.float64(2624.352244791666), np.float64(2278.3638281249996))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 265, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': 'f263f21f8080461c0a2030246fb6fbf5', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': 'fe7765b4641600e161ab613524bf7983'}, page_content='In order to reduce storage requirements, some statistics are only stored when their value changes. These are referred to as status metrics. An example of a status metric is the beam a terminal is currently operating in, which is expected to change at most once every few minutes. In other words, status refers to statistics that do not change very often, and the system is only interested in their current value and when they change.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9388914704322815, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(568.75), np.float64(2621.072161458333)), (np.float64(568.75), np.float64(2793.629453125)), (np.float64(2578.706411458333), np.float64(2793.629453125)), (np.float64(2578.706411458333), np.float64(2621.072161458333))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 265, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': 'f263f21f8080461c0a2030246fb6fbf5', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': '7106b8fcffb04765b9670f0d9727fe82'}, page_content='The stats manager process is located in the NOC and at each SAS. The NOC will host two different processes, one for historical data and one for real-time global QoS statistics. Each SAS instance is dedicated to real-time and streaming requests for both statistics and status.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.947218120098114, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(568.75), np.float64(2839.822161458333)), (np.float64(568.75), np.float64(3198.316953125)), (np.float64(2637.2949531249997), np.float64(3198.316953125)), (np.float64(2637.2949531249997), np.float64(2839.822161458333))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 265, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': 'f263f21f8080461c0a2030246fb6fbf5', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': 'a50c181d55034651814b31616761e70b'}, page_content='Real-time data is stored at the SAS at 30-second resolution. Historical data is stored at the NOC at 5-minute resolution. Stats management profiles determine how long stats and statuses are stored. The configuration of the stats management profiles and the number of elements in the network determine the storage utilization for the NMS. Typically, important stats will be stored for 10 days at the SAS and for 400 days at the NOC. Lower importance stats would be stored for 2 days at the SAS and 10 days at the NOC.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.929