, 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 268, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': '2b7090a0abe1f00f69b64aeccd4465b7', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': '3658dec83a0f320cb504aba1d0349549'}, page_content='The EAP is a separate instantiation of the NMS that runs in a mode specifically designed to provide access to limited NMS configuration, statistics, and reporting functionality for secondary service providers, subscribers, and sales representatives. The EAP also has configuration capabilities that allow an EAP user with the correct permissions to create, modify, and delete network elements. The data source for the EAP is the NOC/backup NOC NMS and not the datapath itself. The NOC forwards data to the EAP on a regular basis (by default, every 5 minutes). As the EAP has a local data store for stats and events, it prevents large report queries from affecting the main NOC NMS. EAP user accounts are configured in the NOC.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9362934231758118, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(568.4407958984375), np.float64(3124.197161458333)), (np.float64(568.4407958984375), np.float64(3296.754453125)), (np.float64(2594.8574531249997), np.float64(3296.754453125)), (np.float64(2594.8574531249997), np.float64(3124.197161458333))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 268, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': '2b