implest form the satellite terminal will comprise a satellite router, BUC (block up-converter), LNB (low noise block converter), feed assembly, and antenna. This equipment may vary based on whether the satellite terminal is deployed in a fixed or mobile application."), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9413309693336487, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(568.75), np.float64(871.0721614583332)), (np.float64(568.75), np.float64(1044.0067138671875)), (np.float64(2624.45947265625), np.float64(1044.0067138671875)), (np.float64(2624.45947265625), np.float64(871.0721614583332))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 275, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': '819750d206a5453eed1d1b6ec27a9fe9', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': '2a4b086e0797c573d185a1f6d4e01388'}, page_content='Customer applications often require additional satellite terminal capabilities. Support for additional capabilities such as antenna controllers, multi-band LNBs and BUCs, and frequency translation are provided by the Velocity solution.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.8643583059310913, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(563.0257568359375), np.float64(1131.046142578125)), (np.float64(563.0257568359375), np.float64(1205.5079345703125)), (np.float64(1336.3314208984375), np.float64(1205.5079345703125)), (np.float64(1336.3314208984375), np.float64(1131.046142578125))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 275, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': '68d3eee888d8dfa5749c8589d741b38d', 'category': 'Title', 'element_id': 'fef9e9f131d1f1f1684161c75a1e939b'}, page_content='7.2.1 Satellite Router'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9497960805892944, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(563.37109375), np.float64(1245.9781494140625)), (np.float64(563.37109375), np.float64(1667.0669531249998)), (np.float64(2613.7793281249997), np.float64(1667.0669531249998)), (np.float64(2613.7793281249997), np.float64(1245.9781494140625))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 275, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': 'fef9e9f131d1f1f1684161c75a1e939b', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': '70509184f5450d8f6ed7c2e52ff1ba89'}, page_content='The satellite router is the processing and modem component of a satellite terminal; it provides LAN connectivity to users and IF connectivity in the L-band to the radio frequency (RF) section of the satellite terminal. The satellite router acts as a network node in an iNet where the iNet is providing mobile satellite terminals with the capability of using different satellites, different beams on a given spacecraft, or different service channels within a given beam. The satellite router also directs the operation of internal satellite terminal components, including the antenna control unit (ACU), the BUC, and the LNB.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9039976596832275, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(568.75), np.float64(1758.3757552083334)), (np.float64(568.75), np.float64(1826.4434635416667)), (np.float64(1602.95361328125), np.float64(1826.4434635416667)), (np.float64(1602.95361328125), np.float64(1758.3757552083334))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 275, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': '68d3eee888d8dfa5749c8589d741b38d', 'category': 'Title', 'element_id': 'f38dc41f299c8e999fde96e9b4f0b1c4'}, page_content='7.2.2 Built-In Ethernet Switch'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.935182511806488, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(566.1215209960938), np.float64(1870.0304947916663)), (np.float64(566.1215209960938), np.float64(2104.5669531249996)), (np.float64(2588.404328125), np.float64(2104.5669531249996)), (np.float64(2588.404328125), np.float64(1870.0304947916663))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 275, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': 'f38dc41f299c8e999fde96e9b4f0b1c4', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': 'a3547125e1dd3ac6d326de84eade423d'}, page_content='Each terminal, depending on the type, is supported by one or more Ethernet ports built into the satellite router. Ethernet interfaces can be configured either as access ports or trunk ports. Trunks carry the traffic of multiple virtual local area networks (VLANs) over a single link and allow you to extend VLANs across the network.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.8158241510391235, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(762.2713623046875), np.float64(2190.8638281249996)), (np.float64(762.2713623046875), np.float64(2301.4419531249996)), (np.float64(2383.15576171875), np.float64(2301.4419531249996)), (np.float64(2383.15576171875), np.float64(2190.8638281249996))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 275, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': '626b34a5e6695db91e9f741b7dfe24cb'}, page_content='NOTE: If a terminal does not contain a switch, it has only one Ethernet port/interface, for which there may be some functional limitation.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.8946253061294556, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(566.1492919921875), np.float64(2432.854921875)), (np.float64(566.1492919921875), np.float64(2500.9226302083334)), (np.float64(1103.392822265625), np.float64(2500.9226302083334)), (np.float64(1103.392822265625), np.float64(2432.854921875))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 275, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'category': 'Title', 'element_id': '22ff4c3538790c8743ac233fdc2c4538'}, page_content='7.2.3 Antenna'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9379690885543823, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(567.6821899414062), np.float64(2544.509661458333)), (np.float64(567.6821899414062), np.float64(2779.0461197916666)), (np.float64(2607.326203125), np.float64(2779.0461197916666)), (np.float64(2607.326203125), np.float64(2544.509661458333))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 275, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': '22ff4c3538790c8743ac233fdc2c4538', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': '630ef8f6cd1e87edecdcadad1fa8c036'}, page_content='Antennas using either linear or circular polarization are supported. The polarization is a property of the antenna and can be controlled through OpenAMIP (Open Antenna Modem Interface Protocol). This feature also enables the system to operate in multiple polarizations if the antenna subsystem supports more than one polarization.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9465203881263733, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(568.75), np.float64(2825.2388281249996)), (np.float64(568.75), np.float64(3307.691953125)), (np.float64(2616.620361328125), np.float64(3307.691953125)), (np.float64(2616.620361328125), np.float64(2825.2388281249996))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 275, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': '22ff4c3538790c8743ac233fdc2c4538', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': 'b69c49a5a020b2df805629ad08356d8a'}, page_content="Transmissions from antennas having non-circular apertures can cause interference with satellites near the intended satellite when the wider axis of the elliptical beam that these antennas project aligns with the geostationary arc. This type of aperture is common with the flat-panel phased-array antennas often used with aeronautical terminals. The extent of the interference with neighboring satellites will depend upon the alignment of the projected beam pattern with the geostationary arc, with the amount of alignment being related to a combination of the aircraft's geo-location and the local attitude of the aircraft. The satellite router can work in conjunction with the ACU to limit or stop transmissions based upon the"), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.468548983335495, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(353.6458333333333), np.float64(3512.020751953125)), (np.float64(353.6458333333333), np.float64(3628.525286458333)), (np.float64(1940.9881591796875), np.float64(3628.525286458333)), (np.float64(1940.9881591796875), np.float64(3512.020751953125))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 275, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': '22ff4c3538790c8743ac233fdc2c4538', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': '7d6035d6b8d889bbeb20b4836c17b8e9'}, page_content='ST Engineering iDirect Proprietary | Conf