2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': 'd92eee0b66dfd524cea0a37a014a17d7', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': '5a6545f5a86cdd6e5cd4d1c8649160f8'}, page_content='NAT is commonly used to remap one IP address space into another by modifying the IP address in the IP packet headers as they transit a router such as the satellite terminal. However, protocols that embed explicit IP addresses in their payload do not work correctly with NAT.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9369091987609863, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(560.4593505859375), np.float64(2912.7388281249996)), (np.float64(560.4593505859375), np.float64(3209.254453125)), (np.float64(2620.925161458333), np.float64(3209.254453125)), (np.float64(2620.925161458333), np.float64(2912.7388281249996))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 281, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': 'd92eee0b66dfd524cea0a37a014a17d7', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': 'fc5f64a03f880246a730a80b345feef3'}, page_content='When NAT is enabled on the satellite terminal, the satellite router supports a Session Initiation Protocol Application layer Gateway (SIP ALG). The ALG replaces the original IP addresses in the SIP packet payload with the NATed IP addresses in the IP packet header. The SIP ALG is configurable per VLAN and may be used for NAT traversal on an SVN that will carry SIP traffic. However, the operator can disable SIP ALG even if NAT is enabled.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.8801