.pdf', 'parent_id': 'b0114c782c54932a585574978fc67994', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': 'c22cbbd7fa0280d66fc9b7908c782dbe'}, page_content='Some satellite terminal equipment malfunctions and errors (for example, pointing error, excessive BUC power) result in the immediate shutdown of the inbound. In this case, messaging the error back to the SAS immediately is not possible. It stores these errors locally until it is again able to transmit them to the SAS or the satellite router is reset.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9277183413505554, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(568.75), np.float64(726.6049218749998)), (np.float64(568.75), np.float64(794.6726302083334)), (np.float64(1466.0731201171875), np.float64(794.6726302083334)), (np.float64(1466.0731201171875), np.float64(726.6049218749998))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 286, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': 'b0114c782c54932a585574978fc67994', 'category': 'Title', 'element_id': '367a07540fd2e776e08c284a489302e0'}, page_content='7.4.3 Switch Management'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9503765106201172, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(567.506103515625), np.float64(838.2596614583332)), (np.float64(567.506103515625), np.float64(1196.754453125)), (np.float64(2636.6751614583336), np.float64(1196.754453125)), (np.float64(2636.6751614583336), np.float64(838.2596614583332))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 286, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': '367a07540fd2e776e08c284a489302e0', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': 'b3c0f1d23bbc18121e4e5b28d3c7279a'}, page_content="Before being loaded with its configuration, the satellite router's switch will operate with all ports isolated from each other and each port will be connected only to the CPU on the satellite router. This behavior provides protection from allowing temporary connectivity between ports on the switch that the user has configured to be on separate VLANs. It also allows accessibility to the satellite router's web-based user interface from any port before the switch has been configured."), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.936394989490509, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(568.75), np.float64(1242.947161458333)), (np.float64(568.75), np.float64(1479.4976806640625)), (np.float64(2604.117869791666), np.float64(1479.4976806640625)), (np.float64(2604.117869791666), np.float64(1242.947161458333))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 286, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': '367a07540fd2e776e08c284a489302e0', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': 'ca5e32f38bbf80e22d6b6b36cfc56634'}, page_content="Once the user's configuration has been loaded, however, the user will want the switch to act as a switch. Any ports assigned to the same VLAN will be connected so the traffic on that VLAN will be switched between those ports. This should occur for packets on that VLAN, regardless of what other VLANs have been assigned to those ports."), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.8504641056060791, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(567.6739501953125), np.float64(1562.6697998046875)), (np.float64(567.6739501953125), np.float64(1638.658935546875)), (np.float64(1151.4140625), np.float64(1638.658935546875)), (np.float64(1151.4140625), np.float64(1562.6697998046875))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 286, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': 'b0114c782c54932a585574978fc67994', 'category': 'Title', 'element_id': 'e74ad53c3e09946e9d2ba4441e7bd65e'}, page_content='7.4.4 OpenAMIP'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9499561786651611, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(565.9463500976562), np.float64(1677.595947265625)), (np.float64(565.9463500976562), np.float64(2100.9211197916666)), (np.float64(2621.505615234375), np.float64(2100.9211197916666)), (np.float64(2621.505615234375), np.float64(1677.595947265625))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 286, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': 'e74ad53c3e09946e9d2ba4441e7bd65e', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': '157ad0192c5bbef841ba34aa370bebe2'}, page_content='OpenAMIP is an IP-based protocol that facilitates the exchange of information between an ACU and a satellite router. When a mobile terminal passes through multiple satellite footprints, OpenAMIP allows the satellite router to command the antenna controller to move the antenna from pointing at the current satellite to pointing at the next satellite. Also, by providing the satellite router with a means to notify the antenna controller of changes to the receive frequency and polarization, it enables the use of automatic beam switching (ABS) to transfer connectivity from one satellite beam to another.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9100193977355957, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(568.636474609375), np.float64(2141.3388671875)), (np.float64(568.636474609375), np.float64(2258.595703125)), (np.float64(2540.01318359375), np.float64(2258.595703125)), (np.float64(2540.01318359375), np.float64(2141.3388671875))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 286, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': 'e74ad53c3e09946e9d2ba4441e7bd65e', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': 'd8256d4af5c9f06347e1cea28e372cef'}, page_content='In addition, OpenAMIP enables service providers and their customers to meet government regulations by commanding the antenna to mute the signal in “no transmit” zones.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9339023232460022, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(568.75), np.float64(2301.635986328125)), (np.floa