minal is initially deployed it is configured to have the information required to receive a signaling carrier.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9519580006599426, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(568.75), np.float64(1188.259661458333)), (np.float64(568.75), np.float64(1732.6919531249998)), (np.float64(2597.5189114583336), np.float64(1732.6919531249998)), (np.float64(2597.5189114583336), np.float64(1188.259661458333))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 294, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': '4cc71e917e4dfb4e208649a620ed329a', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': '7692fdf9ec830d229c6f4f775f8f2abe'}, page_content="Upon initial power up, the terminal will select, from the satellites in its constellation configuration, the satellite to which it is visible and closest. The satellite will be considered as visible only if the terminal’s elevation angle is between the minimum and maximum look angle configured for the given terminal type. A relative preference can be configured for each satellite, to influence the terminal's selection when it is in situations where the closest satellite may not be the best first choice for most terminals. Once a satellite has been selected and the terminal's antenna is pointing to that satellite, the terminal will lock to a signaling carrier on that satellite and receive additional information regarding the physical layer in order to establish 2-way communication."), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9467339515686035, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(565.5919189453125), np.float64(1778.884661458333)), (np.float64(565.5919189453125), np.float64(2075.400286458333)), (np.float64(2592.6334947916666), np.float64(2075.400286458333)), (np.float64(2592.6334947916666), np.float64(1778.884661458333))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 294, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': '4cc71e917e4dfb4e208649a620ed329a', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': '5a93e81b84fd846aba598b4d3fff2d0a'}, page_content='Once 2-way communication is established, the terminal will begin the process of authentication to establish mutual trust with the network. After mutual trust is established, the terminal will receive additional configuration information through the DFOE process. During this time the terminal will also report its geo-location. The terminal uses the information from the DFOE process and completes the acquisition process.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9451941847801208, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(563.0306396484375), np.float64(2121.294189453125)), (np.float64(563.0306396484375), np.float64(2480.087786458333)), (np.float64(2631.768310546875), np.float64(2480.087786458333)), (np.float64(2631.768310546875), np.float64(2121.294189453125))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 294, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': '4cc71e917e4dfb4e208649a620ed329a', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': '21903964116bedcdb90d640936fe0194'}, page_content='A terminal that has been out of network that begins the acquisition process will use information cached prior to going out of network. The use of cached information is intended to minimize the acquisition time of terminals that were previously in network. In the event a terminal is unable to complete the acquisition process based on the cached information, it will execute the acquisition process as if it was initially deployed. As long as the terminal can receive the signaling carrier it should not become stranded.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.8771563172340393, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(568.75), np.float64(2569.580322265625)), (np.float64(568.75), np.float64(2639.4642968749995)), (np.float64(1816.99755859375), np.float64(2639.4642968749995)), (np.float64(1816.99755859375), np.float64(2569.580322265625))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 294, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': '6718b519381e2075d00f0b176f6ec6c6', 'category': 'Title', 'element_id': '8ea87b1a19b91d4aa93469687f943f6f'}, page_content='7.9.1 Network Acquisition Sequence'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.8830610513687134, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(568.75), np.float64(2682.583984375)), (np.float64(568.75), np.float64(2731.650286458333)), (np.float64(1775.6253662109375), np.float64(2731.650286458333))