lowing diagram. This type of switch occurs when the terminal switches between iNets of the same polarization, but different frequencies.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.7769443988800049, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(883.1666666666666), np.float64(2331.775286458333)), (np.float64(883.1666666666666), np.float64(2380.3742447916666)), (np.float64(2310.4843348285413), np.float64(2380.3742447916666)), (np.float64(2310.4843348285413), np.float64(2331.775286458333))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 307, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'category': 'FigureCaption', 'element_id': '8633219f76fca30237986390725e556c'}, page_content='Figure 7-9. Beam Switching, during switch, Make-before-Break'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.8425753712654114, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(568.75), np.float64(2435.134661458333)), (np.float64(568.75), np.float64(2483.7336197916666)), (np.float64(2624.72265625), np.float64(2483.7336197916666)), (np.float64(2624.72265625), np.float64(2435.134661458333))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 307, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': '01fdff9dd68b6e83ff8af2322c3f2613'}, page_content='With Make-before-Break, once a decision to switch has been made traffic will flow as follows.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.948922872543335, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(568.75), np.float64(2529.9263281249996)), (np.float64(568.75), np.float64(2826.441953125)), (np.float64(2636.5293281249997), np.float64(2826.441953125)), (np.float64(2636.5293281249997), np.float64(2529.9263281249996))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 307, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': '33d452ea3d3ba161d02f2d465ee5f2a9'}, page_content='User traffic will traverse the terrestrial network to the PP cluster. (Subsequent actions in the support of a beam switch are transparent to the external network. It is important to note that this terrestrial path is unaffected during a beam switch. The PP will replicate the terminal’s downstream traffic onto the new iNet. User traffic will traverse tunnels between the PP cluster and line cards that support the new beam.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9429834485054016, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(568.75), np.float64(2872.634661458333)), (np.float64(568.75), np.float64(3231.129453125)), (np.float64(2625.0084947916666), np.float64(3231.129453125)), (np.float64(2625.0084947916666), np.float64(2872.634661458333))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 307, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': 'a9958ea2de77db79922f26b806201bc8'}, page_content='The second receiver receives the traffic on the next carrier while the terminal continues to receive the traffic on the current carrier. This allows timing synchronization and transmitter configuration to occur that will eliminate or minimize data loss as the transmitter begins to send traffic in the new beam. If the terminal is not detected in the new beam by the SAS, the beam switch will abort. If the terminal is detected the switch process will continue. The switch process completes by making the first receiver inactive.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9367634654045105, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(564.0145874023438), np.float64(3277.322161458333)), (np.float64(564.0145874023438), np.float64(3449.879453125)), (np.float64(2581.878286458333), np.float64(3449.879453125)), (np.float64(2581.878286458333), np.float64(3277.322161458333))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 307, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': '20b56ff85fb6a1892a4d22ddcdbec24e'}, page_content='It is important to note a few key features of this switch. First, the data flow is through the same PP server, which means there is no change to the external networking. That is, there are no routing updates or MAC table changes needed. There are also no networking changes'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_uplo