ore-Make (BBM), is illustrated in the following diagram. BBM switch does not require dual RF receive paths and is thus more compatible with single- receiver remotes, band or polarization changes, or future operational modes such as multicast overlay. The old connection must be broken before the new one is made.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9325491189956665, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(562.1908569335938), np.float64(787.2179947916666)), (np.float64(562.1908569335938), np.float64(1021.7544531250002)), (np.float64(2624.6074531249997), np.float64(1021.7544531250002)), (np.float64(2624.6074531249997), np.float64(787.2179947916666))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 309, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': '01cb6d233ff22125e6436ab52ff5ac09', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': '68e94ff814250b9be932286d1b04d54c'}, page_content='For iQ200 and the 9-series modems, Break-before-Make is the only supported mode of switch. The connection is broken even when there is no Polarization or Frequency band change. Newer Sabine remotes such as the iQ 800 support Fast Break-before-Make beam switching that significantly reduce traffic disruption time.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.8372753262519836, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(845.1770833333333), np.float64(1108.0513281249998)), (np.float64(845.1770833333333), np.float64(1342.5877864583333)), (np.float64(2526.839599609375), np.float64(1342.5877864583333)), (np.float64(2526.839599609375), np.float64(1108.0513281249998))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 309, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': '75514a939c5bf2218bced93ee322cffb'}, page_content='NOTE: The system automatically determines if Make-before-Break or Break- before-Make is needed based on the terminal NMS configuration. No special configuration is needed other than correct configuration of channel polarizations.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.555655300617218, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(641.627197265625), np.float64(3152.0877864583335)), (np.float64(641.627197265625), np.float64(3200.6867447916666)), (np.float64(2553.138671875), np.float64(3200.6867447916666)), (np.float64(2553.138671875), np.float64(3152.0877864583335))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 309, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': 'b7e519fe5e7c6eb96cb4e766eef9d91d'}, page_content='Figure 7-11. Beam Switching, multiple beams (during switch), Break-before-Make'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9282646179199219, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(564.7395629882812), np.float64(3255.447161458333)), (np.float64(564.7395629882812), np.floa