M) Values'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9002218842506409, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(583.0562744140625), np.float64(399.4775695800781)), (np.float64(583.0562744140625), np.float64(511.3377864583335)), (np.float64(2467.1074531249997), np.float64(511.3377864583335)), (np.float64(2467.1074531249997), np.float64(399.4775695800781))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 318, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': '6848070ca760979482efb2671a27a87b', 'category': 'ListItem', 'element_id': '4002a58b4e64136067f70c751a5f08d2'}, page_content='Best Effort Demand — the portion of the bandwidth request (demand) above the configured CIR, but less than the configured MIR (capped by the MIR value).'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(567.5468749999999), np.float64(400.7596614583332)), (np.float64(567.5468749999999), np.float64(449.35861979166685)), (np.float64(607.6595364583333), np.float64(449.35861979166685)), (np.float64(607.6595364583333), np.float64(400.7596614583332))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 318, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': '6848070ca760979482efb2671a27a87b', 'category': 'UncategorizedText', 'element_id': '600c8bb9e3b0fad0cb74757f82f9ccc2'}, page_content='•'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9488112926483154, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(568.75), np.float64(557.5304947916666)), (np.float64(568.75), np.float64(854.0461197916668)), (np.float64(2644.549560546875), np.float64(854.0461197916668)), (np.float64(2644.549560546875), np.float64(557.5304947916666))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 318, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': '6848070ca760979482efb2671a27a87b', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': '9194feb564b4c62d830f586f14c05f4b'}, page_content='The following diagram show three cases to illustrate examples of how parameters A and B, which are used in the congestion metric calculation, are being calculated. Each of these cases has a Total Capacity, a CIR Demand, and a Best Effort demand. These are all demands at the top level nodes of the QoS allocation tree for the iNet.Consider the three cases as shown in the following diagram.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.584044337272644, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(1131.703125), np.float64(2102.087786458333)), (np.float64(1131.703125), np.float64(2150.6867447916666)), (np.float64(2063.658447265625), np.float64(2150.6867447916666)), (np.float64(2063.658447265625), np.float64(2102.087786458333))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 318, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'category': 'Title', 'element_id': 'aa45e4f158c94bd6d8fafd48a75c7afd'}, page_content='Figure 7-18. Congestion Metric Examples'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9488710165023804, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(568.75), np.float64(2205.447161458333)), (np.float64(568.75), np.float64(2625.9211197916666)), (np.float64(2608.8574531249997), np.float64(2625.9211197916666)), (np.float64(2608.8574531249997), np.float64(2205.447161458333))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 318, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': 'aa45e4f158c94bd6d8fafd48a75c7afd', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': 'cf6ac903e82121fe5ace3ffe58a7ffa5'}, page_content='The CIR and MIR are set, in a dynamic manner, based on the global bandwidth manager. Furthermore, the demand from terminals can vary from one moment to the next. These two influences combined will cause the total CIR Demand and Best Effort Demand to vary up and down as a function of time. Also, the Total Capacity on the inbound can change based on the current inroute group selection, and the capacity on the outbound can change based on configuration changes in the outbound carrier and the current efficiency, in terms of IP bits per-symbol for the outbound DVB-S2 carrier using ACM.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9407376646995544, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(565.767578125), np.float64(2672.1138281249996)), (np.float64(565.767578125), np.float64(3092.821044921875)), (np.float64(2598.5397447916666), np.float64(3092.821044921875)), (np.float64(2598.5397447916666), np.float64(2672.1138281249996))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 318, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': 'aa45e4f158c94bd6d8fafd48a75c7afd', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': 'c8a55c8ca52e2413072223928ad2a426'}, page_content='In Case 1, the iNet has met both the CIR Demand and the MIR Demand — hence there is “Negative Congestion” for both A & B, and the iNet is uncongested. In Case 3, the CIR Demand and the MIR Demand are both obviously greater than the Total Capacity — hence there is “Positive Congestion” for both A & B, and the iNet is congested. Finally, in Case 2, the CIR Demand is met, and the MIR Demand is not met — hence there is “Negative Congestion for A” CIR, and “Positive Congestion for B” MIR. Whether or not this is defined as congestion, is a policy decision that is input to the computation as configurable parameters.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.31911858916282654, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(352.12579345703125), np.float64(3514.3013281249996)), (np.float64(352.12579345703125), np.float64(3562.900286458333)), (np.float64(432.7628479003906), np.float64(3562.900286458333)), (np.float64(432.7628479003906), np.float64(3514.3013281249996))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 318, 'file_directory': '/va