out_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 330, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': 'fa9ac378c884aa6d47100ac4788e557c'}, page_content='NOTE: The Antenna Control Unit (ACU) is required to reliably provide accurate location and time from satellite navigation system(s) over the arctic region so that the terminal can find HEO Satellite position and velocity through TLE entries.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.8764970302581787, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(568.75), np.float64(1525.4263281249998)), (np.float64(568.75), np.float64(1588.6086197916666)), (np.float64(1516.6744384765625), np.float64(1588.6086197916666)), (np.float64(1516.6744384765625), np.float64(1525.4263281249998))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 330, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'category': 'Title', 'element_id': '81b96bd6c1871d0e1864cc298ec79402'}, page_content='7.14.1.1 Acquisition Algorithm'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9099035263061523, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(568.75), np.float64(1632.4437255859375)), (np.float64(568.75), np.float64(1743.6294531249998)), (np.float64(2496.26025390625), np.float64(1743.6294531249998)), (np.float64(2496.26025390625), np.float64(1632.4437255859375))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 330, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': '81b96bd6c1871d0e1864cc298ec79402', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': '05781382eb0b73d85b022617ef284ce7'}, page_content='To operate in NGSO satellite networks, the Acquisition Algorithm includes the following features:'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9401031136512756, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(566.8110961914062), np.float64(1787.385009765625)), (np.float64(566.8110961914062), np.float64(2086.337786458333)), (np.float64(2630.122802734375), np.float64(2086.337786458333)), (np.float64(2630.122802734375), np.float64(1787.385009765625))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 330, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': '81b96bd6c1871d0e1864cc298ec79402', 'category': 'ListItem', 'element_id': 'efdddbaefb7bbf16e0504a77fcc8a77d'}, page_content='• A Two-Line Element (TLE) orbital description can be configured to define the orbit and movement of a satellite. The TLE defines the HEO Satellite orbit and can be used to predict its location given epoch time. The GPS receiver equipped at the remote terminal provides the GPS location and time. The TLE set, which contains multiple HEO Satellites, coupled with GPS time, defines the location and movement of each satellite over time.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9564981460571289, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(567.5468749999999), np.float64(2129.1005859375)), (np.float64(567.5468749999999), np.float64(2492.51611328125)), (np.float64(2632.210693359375), np.float64(2492.51611328125)), (np.float64(2632.210693359375), np.float64(2129.1005859375))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 330, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': '81b96bd6c1871d0e1864cc298ec79402', 'category': 'ListItem', 'element_id': 'bb3eb29349bb0bd44b2ee64febeff6f3'}, page_content='• TLE and beam map data are dynamically refreshed. The TLE file accuracy degrades with time; therefore, the operator must update TLE data periodically. After the remote terminal finds the proper satellite and locks with its downstream carrier, it receives the latest TLE info from PP and uses it for timing correction during acquisition or normal in- network operation. Beam maps for NGSO satellites must be dynamic, to account for satellite and beam motion, and the potential for channel reassignments.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(567.5468749999999), np.float64(2537.2179947916666)), (np.float64(567.5468749999999), np.float64(2585.816953125)), (np.float64(607.6595364583333), np.float64(2585.816953125)), (np.float64(607.6595364583333), np.float64(2537.2179947916666))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 330, 'file_directory': '/var/f