rs/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9410749673843384, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(568.75), np.float64(528.3638281249998)), (np.float64(568.75), np.float64(762.9002864583334)), (np.float64(2587.4564114583336), np.float64(762.9002864583334)), (np.float64(2587.4564114583336), np.float64(528.3638281249998))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 335, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': '73d512476d998f8469652ee1cde2b0d2', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': '73d8d14c105886555e515af14caa5fb7'}, page_content='Velocity can support satellites with up to 15 degrees of inclination without terminal acquisition issues and without sacrificing spectral efficiency. This can help mitigate service degradation on congested beams by enabling satellite operators to access older satellites at an inclined orbit.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.811821460723877, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(867.7083333333333), np.float64(849.1971614583332)), (np.float64(867.7083333333333), np.float64(959.7752864583334)), (np.float64(2558.26123046875), np.float64(959.7752864583334)), (np.float64(2558.26123046875), np.float64(849.1971614583332))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 335, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': '5dc3698a126ac897917a2d7486c56402'}, page_content='NOTE: iHub and ILC linecards are required to use this feature for an Inclined Orbit Satellite.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9519627094268799, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(566.3839721679688), np.float64(1097.1138281249998)), (np.float64(566.3839721679688), np.float64(1703.525286458333)), (np.float64(2622.810791015625), np.float64(1703.525286458333)), (np.float64(2622.810791015625), np.float64(1097.1138281249998))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 335, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': '81eb8d54724353bdc0c34e16e27c0531'}, page_content="To support this, operators can input TLE information and longitude information when configuring a satellite. TLE configuration is available beginning in Pulse 4.0; and beginning in Velocity Release 4.0, Velocity software can utilize TLE information, if available (otherwise it will just use longitude). It is not mandatory to upload TLE information for GEO or GIO Satellites. Existing GEO networks can still be configured in the legacy way; and when adding new GEO satellites, the operator can choose to add TLE information or defer that. If TLE is not configured, as satellites begin to become inclined, the operator can continue configuring longitude and latitude wander for the satellite. However, the terminal's tolerance for orbital inclination will be limited to 2 - 4 degrees depending on the geo-locations of the hub and terminal."), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9430668950080872, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(568.75), np.float64(1749.7179947916663)), (np.float64(568.75), np.float64(2046.2336197916663)), (np.float64(2613.597036458333), np.float64(2046.2336197916663)), (np.float64(2613.597036458333), np.float64(1749.7179947916663))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 335, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': '8656d219006b02e0716644879d8aafea'}, page_content="As a satellite begins to drift, operators can update their configurations with TLE information. This ensures that the Protocol Processors (PP) and linecards can compensate for timing and Doppler effects caused by satellite movement. While the hub side can only compensate for about half of the timing and Doppler variation, this adjustment significantly extends the satellite's usable life, even for non-upgraded terminals."), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9324512481689453, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(568.75), np.float64(2092.4263281249996)), (np.float64(568.75), np.float64(2326.962786458333)), (np.float64(2600.685302734375), np.float64(2326.962786458333)), (np.float64(2600.685302734375), np.float64(2092.4263281249996))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 335, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': '09490f9320547ac175343808a487517a'}, page_content="As the satellite's inclination increases, operators can initiate terminal upgrades to Velocity Release 4.0. Upgraded terminals can compensate for residual timing and Doppler errors that the hub alone cannot correct. However, terminals that cannot undergo upgrades will eventually need to be excluded from the GIO iNets."), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9343312978744507, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(568.75), np.float64(2373.1554947916666)), (np.float64(568.75), np.float64(2545.7127864583335)), (np.float64(2637.076203124999), np.float64(2545.7127864583335)), (np.float64(2637.076203124999), np.float64(2373.1554947916666))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 335, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': '292ea584b69ffc6bc67b2e26bbf38c0a'}, page_content='Eventually, the system determines (based on a configured inclination threshold) that the orbit type is GIO. This will cause the PP to not switch a terminal into the satellite if the terminal does not report GIO capability.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9498084783554077, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(568.75), np.float64(2591.9054947916666)), (np.float64(568.75), np.float64(3198.316953125)), (np.float64(2636.0189114583327), np.float64(3198.316953125)), (np.float64(2636.0189114583327), np.float64(2591.9054947916666))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 335, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': '2cf9e174b33a2d421c23e3d0ea4bd52e'}, page_content='Inclination will have the greatest effect on terminals at high latitudes or near beam edges. The effects are most pronounced at the Northern and Southern extremes of the inclination, when timing offset is most extreme. This mainly affects acquisition; once in the network, UCP can compensate a substantial amount of offset. Terminals can be upgraded gradually. Hub- side GIO support will actually keep many terminals operating much longer as the transition progresses. Eventually, the operator does need to upgrade terminals, especially those operating in high latitudes or near the edges of beams, which are now moving due to the inclination. Some old terminals can probably linger for years if not in high latitudes or near beam edges. Terminals that cannot be upgraded will eventually have to be excluded from the GIO iNets.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.44368863105773926, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(353.6458333333333), np.float64(3508.643310546875)), (np.float64(353.6458333333333), np.float64(3628.525286458333)), (np.float64(1939.307373046875), np.float64(3628.525286458333)), (np.float64(1939.307373046875), np.float64(3508.643310546875))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 335, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': '68f74116f3e4b8d1578ccbf6ea4deb6a'}, page_content='ST Engineering iDirect Proprietary | Confidentiality: Public Technical Reference Guide | iDirect Velocity™ | T0001665 | Revision 1'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.502467155456543, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(2544.864583333333), np.float64(3514.3013281249996)), (np.float64(2544.864583333333), np.float64(3562.900286458333)), (np.float64(2623.709228515625), np.float64(3562.900286458333)), (np.float64(2623.709228515625), np.float64(3514.3013281249996))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 335, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': '30ba6c10f8242351ebcaf838bb796f8c'}, page_content='301'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.8708598017692566, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(350.0), np.float64(251.28049479166657)), (np.float64(350.0), np.float64(299.87945312500017)), (np.float64(1459.9105224609375), np.float64(299.87945312500017)), (np.float64(1459.9105224609375), np.float64(251.28049479166657))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 336, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'category': 'Header', 'element_id': '24d31f9dbf6411abe75ba40831437270'}, page_content='7.15 Enhanced Inclined Orbit Support in Velocity'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9178338050842285, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(833.8025512695312), np.float64(437.5934753417969)), (np.float64(833.8025512695312), np.float64(801.376953125)), (np.float64(2585.378286458333), np.float64(801.376953125)), (np.float64(2585.378286458333), np.float64(437.5934753417969))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 336, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': '31599dc638e69b477e07577a68f10793'}, page_content='NOTE: The full benefit of this feature is realized only when both the hub side and remote side software are at 4.0 version. If only the hub side is running 4.0, the hub side will still provide its half of the compensation, hence providing improvement in incline orbit performance. In this configuration, the actual tolerance depends on the geo-locations of the hub and remotes. Please contact TAC for more details.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.3193666636943817, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(352.8869934082031), np.float64(3514.3013281249996)), (np.float64(352.8869934082031), np.float64(3562.900286458333)), (np.float64(430.0836416027083), np.float64(3562.900286458333)), (np.float64(430.0836416027083), np.float64(3514.3013281249996))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 336, 'f