rrativeText', 'element_id': '084edb77e80e61fac9fa74487646b2be'}, page_content='The Centroid-Based Initial Beam Selection uses an improved beam selection algorithm on the terminal to make optimal initial beam selection. This new algorithm significantly improves the initial beam selection at a terminal over the previous approach in a constellation with non-circular beams and/or mixed wide/spot beams.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9541469216346741, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(564.862060546875), np.float64(809.0929947916666)), (np.float64(564.862060546875), np.float64(1167.5877864583335)), (np.float64(2633.502685546875), np.float64(1167.5877864583335)), (np.float64(2633.502685546875), np.float64(809.0929947916666))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 337, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': '1d0cfe92c14ced4af9aef26ec0181869', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': 'ea86e00a3416a7e887786983bac3ab71'}, page_content='Beam selection logic is used at acquisition by all terminals. For discreet terminals, the beam selection decision is made continuously and not just at acquisition or when a terminal nears a beam edge. Excluding the notion of hysteresis, the previous logic selected the beam in which the modem is furthest from the nearest beam edge. In the case of network operators that use a combination of spot and broad beams, a number of the spot beams might not be selected. For example:'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'point