 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(287.1470642089844), np.float64(2212.4931640625)), (np.float64(287.1470642089844), np.float64(2301.11767578125)), (np.float64(2591.076171875), np.float64(2301.11767578125)), (np.float64(2591.076171875), np.float64(2212.4931640625))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 346, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': '8bb1de6d1f6acccc88db24d458ede3fb', 'category': 'Title', 'element_id': 'ae951d5534dbb28f9dca277ab8685a2d'}, page_content='8.5 Mitigating Skew Impairment in Mobile Terminals'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9405843615531921, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(568.75), np.float64(2343.9888281249996)), (np.float64(568.75), np.float64(2578.5252864583335)), (np.float64(2632.0234375), np.float64(2578.5252864583335)), (np.float64(2632.0234375), np.float64(2343.9888281249996))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 346, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': 'ae951d5534dbb28f9dca277ab8685a2d', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': 'f753b3c7c6867c80222ede4a31a81be7'}, page_content='Proper and efficient operation of terminals with radiation patterns that are not circularly symmetric, most often, will require special provisions in order to comply with regulatory off- axis limits. This is particularly the case of antennas mounted in a fixed relation to a vehicle, such as on the fuselage of an aircraft or the roof of some other vehicle.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9421494603157043, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(568.75), np.float64(2624.7179947916666)), (np.float64(568.75), np.float64(2859.254453125)), (np.float64(2618.599365234375), np.float64(2859.254453125)), (np.float64(2618.599365234375), np.float64(2624.7179947916666))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 346, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': 'ae951d5534dbb28f9dca277ab8685a2d', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': '43e51e1f8e72b7b477ef3a920196670f'}, page_content='The orientation of the beam pattern with respect to the geostationary arc, as seen from the terminal location, is known as the “skew angle”. This section first takes a brief look at terminals that operate with non-circular radiation patterns, and then describes the methods used in Velocity systems to mitigate the resulting skew impairment in these terminals.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.8996478915214539, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(568.75), np.float64(2950.563255208333)), (np.float64(568.75), np.float64(3018.630963541666)), (np.float64(1862.295166015625), np.float64(3018.630963541666)), (np.float64(1862.295166015625), np.float64(2950.563255208333))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 346, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': '8bb1de6d1f6acccc88db24d458ede3fb', 'category': 'Title', 'element_id': '40fcd5a91eb3d7cbf3eb8b0153562556'}, page_content='8.5.1 Non-Circular Aperture Antennas'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.950360119342804, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(563.77294921875), np.float64(3061.569580078125)), (np.float64(563.77294921875), np.float64(3421.789794921875)), (np.float64(2632.263703125), np.float64(3421.789794921875)), (np.float64(2632.263703125), np.float64(3061.569580078125))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 346, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': '40fcd5a91eb3d7cbf3eb8b0153562556', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': '3f040727e5088f5aa4c0b66d6ca5130f'}, page_content="Low-profile, or flat-panel, antennas commonly used for aeronautical terminals have a non- circular aperture that causes transmissions from these antennas to project a beam that is elliptical rather than circular, with the major axis of the ellipse being horizontal to the platform on which the antenna is mounted. Alignment of the minor axis of this ellipse along the geostationary arc produces the antenna's widest projection onto this arc, which can easily result in the transmitted signal projecting across multiple satellites."), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.4504272937774658, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(349.84942626953125), np.float64(3514.3013281249996)), (np.float64(349.84942626953125), np.float64(3562.900286458333)), (np.float64(430.0836416027083), np.float64(3562.900286458333)), (np.float64(430.0836416027083), np.float64(3514.3013281249996))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 346, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': '40fcd5a91eb3d7cbf3eb8b0153562556', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': '1f949cdb9216a1df4111223235550665'}, page_content='312'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.4617166221141815, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(1063.702880859375), np.float64(3508.947998046875)), (np.float64(1063.702880859375), np.float64(3628.525286458333)), (np.float64(2630.156494140625), np.float64(3628.525286458333)), (np.float64(2630.156494140625), np.float64(3508.947998046875))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 346, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': '40fcd5a91eb3d7cbf3eb8b0153562556', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': '9186facabb94d6da02594e35d678f199'}, page_content='ST Engineering iDirect Proprietary | Confidentiality: Public Technical Reference Guide | iDirect Velocity™ | T0001665 | Revision 1'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.919403076171875, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(1763.7083333333333), np.float64(251.28049479166657)), (np.float64(1763.7083333333333), np.float64(299.87945312500017)), (np.float64(2629.70458984375), np.float64(299.87945312500017)), (np.float64(2629.70458984375), np.float64(251.28049479166657))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 347, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'category': 'Header', 'element_id': '146c55c140e79cf936717e97cf850295'}, page_content='8.5.1 Non-Circular Aperture Antennas'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9530088901519775, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(568.75), np.float64(400.7596614583332)), (np.float64(568.75), np.float64(945.1919531250002)), (np.float64(2620.633494791666), np.float64(945.1919531250002)), (np.float64(2620.633494791666), np.float64(400.7596614583332))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 347, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': '146c55c140e79cf936717e97cf850295', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': 'fb0aba039aab3ab1da4f17bd6b0704e2'}, page_content="Conversely, alignment of the minor axis of this ellipse along the geostationary arc produces the antenna's narrowest projection onto the arc, greatly reducing the projected pattern's reach to neighboring satellites. So, if the antenna is located directly north or south of the satellite and the antenna platform is horizontal to the local horizon, the projected pattern will cross the geostationary arc along the pattern's minor axis, thereby minimizing the transmitted signal's impact on neighboring satellites along that arc (See Figure 8-3 a). If, however, the antenna is located directly east or west of the satellite, the projected pattern's major axis will align with the geostationary arc, thereby maximizing the transmitted signal’s impact on neighboring satellites (See Figure 8-3 b)."), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.7259144186973572, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(661.4270833333333), np.float64(1697.4002864583329)), (np.float64(661.4270833333333), np.float64(1745.9992447916661)), (np.float64(2532.22942265526), np.float64(1745.9992447916661)), (np.float64(2532.22942265526), np.float64(1697.4002864583329))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 347, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'category': 'FigureCaption', 'element_id': 'aea21b3a0e1985c8b534e12a929373fd'}, page_content='Figure 8-3. Low-Profile Antenna a) Favorable Alignment b) Unfavorable Alignment'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9463601112365723, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(568.75), np.float64(1800.759661458333)), (np.float64(568.75), np.float64(2159.2544531249996)), (np.float64(2640.357453125), np.float64(2159.2544531249996)), (np.float64(2640.357453125), np.float64(1800.759661458333))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 347, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': '2adb42cfe4e77aedb5672b66a677919f'}, page_content='Local tilt of the antenna platform can also affect the alignment between the projected pattern and the geostationary arc. If the platform is not locally horizontal, and is tilted about an axis connecting the panel to the satellite, the projected pattern will also be tilted about that axis by the same amount. This local tilt and the tilt related to the geo-location of the antenna together determine the total amount of misalignment of the projected pattern to the geostationary arc.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9466180801391602, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(568.2254028320312), np.float64(2205.447161458333)), (np.float64(568.2254028320312), np.float64(2625.96142578125)), (np.float64(2630.149119791666), np.float64(2625.96142578125)), (np.float64(2630.149119791666), np.float64(2205.447161458333))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 347, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': '16532ecbeb442dc2eb114ca04b41de7d'}, page_content="The amount of misalignment of the projected pattern's minor axis with the geostationary arc is referred to as the skew angle. When the minor axis is aligned with the arc, the skew angle is 0°, and when the minor axis is perpendicular to the arc, the skew angle is 90°. Other possible values of skew angle lie between these extremes. At a skew angle of 0°, the projected pattern is producing the narrowest projection onto the arc, while at a skew angle of 90°, the projected pattern is producing the widest projection onto the arc. So, as the skew angle increases, the impact the transmission has on neighboring satellites also increases."), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9422008991241455, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(568.75), np.float64(2672.1138281249996)), (np.float64(568.75), np.float64(3402.4836197916666)), (np.float64(2634.195994791666), np.float64(3402.4836197916666)), (np.float64(2634.195994791666), np.float64(2672.1138281249996))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 347, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': '3d7a13aeae6678f999564944dea7f1eb'}, page_content='The satellite router and the antenna controller on a terminal using an antenna prone to generating skew-related interference on adjacent satellites work together to determine the amount of skew and take action to limit the amount of interference. The amount of power spectral density (PSD) allowed at different skew angles can be configured for a terminal, and the terminal will limit its transmit power to ensure the PSD limits are not exceeded at the current amount of skew. Limits on the amount of allowable skew can also be configured, and the terminal will mute its transmissions whenever those limits are exceeded. The PSD and skew limits can be configured separately, where the terminal will either limit PSD or limit skew. The terminal can also be configured to limit PSD within some range of skew, imposing a limit on both. This latter approach allows a wider range of skew to be supported without trying to support operation at an especially low transmit power, allowing an operator to trade average efficiency for link reliability under dynamically varying skew conditions.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.30133891105651855, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(353.6458333333333), np.float64(3514.3013281249996)), (np.float64(353.6458333333333), np.float64(3562.900286458333)), (np.float64(1679.666259765625), np.float64(3562.900286458333)), (np.float64(1679.666259765625), np.float64(3514.3013281249996))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 347, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': '09ab9eadc144d1a6b3f7fa0d423394ac'}, page_content='ST Engineering iDirect Proprietary | Confidentiality: Public'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.4067300260066986, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(353.6458333333333), np.float64(3579.9263281249996)), (np.float64(353.6458333333333), np.float64(3628.525286458333)), (np.float64(1927.6229248046875), np.float64(3628.525286458333)), (np.float64(1927.6229248046875), np.float64(3579.9263281249996))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 347, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'category': 