ument(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.8796408176422119, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(568.75), np.float64(394.8340885416665)), (np.float64(568.75), np.float64(464.0043640136719)), (np.float64(2518.8525390625), np.float64(464.0043640136719)), (np.float64(2518.8525390625), np.float64(394.8340885416665))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 348, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': '9bae8b0ceac6f42113f951e37453f41d', 'category': 'Title', 'element_id': '19d464d2cfa4404cfc5329d1d9bb375a'}, page_content='8.5.2 PSD Limits Per Beam, Terminal, and Regulatory Area'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9461843967437744, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(562.144287109375), np.float64(506.4888281249999)), (np.float64(562.144287109375), np.float64(866.884765625)), (np.float64(2644.8427734375), np.float64(866.884765625)), (np.float64(2644.8427734375), np.float64(506.4888281249999))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 348, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': '19d464d2cfa4404cfc5329d1d9bb375a', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': '571d69de35a374c00a03b3009ba5e940'}, page_content='Velocity PSD (power spectral density) Limits Per Beam, Terminal Type, and Regulatory Area (RA) supersedes how skew parameters and PSD limits were configured and applied in earlier releases— Reference Skew and Reference C/N per Channel, for a terminal, were based strictly on the RA page configuration. Previously, regardless of beam switches and the number of points at which the terminal intersected different RAs, in which beam performance could be quite different, the configured worst-case PSD limit of the RA page was always applied.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9291731715202332, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(560.8571166992188), np.float64(911.1763281249998)), (np.float64(560.8571166992188), np.float64(1145.7127864583335)), (np.float64(2613.3418281249997), np.float64(1145.7127864583335)), (np.float64(2613.3418281249997), np.float64(911.1763281249998))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 348, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': '19d464d2cfa4404cfc5329d1d9bb375a', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': '77d7d0cd92501ee688713254b9b22c26'}, page_content='How RA and skew parameters were configured and applied, introduced operational inefficiencies and limitations. Terminals could not use better available carriers, due to the restricted Max C/N, or at times had to mute due to restricted skew limit or the unavailability of carriers due to limited Max C/N.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9516482353210449, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(567.4490966796875), np.float64(1195.4345703125)), (np.float64(567.4490966796875), np.float64(1678.0044531249998)), (np.float64(2624.52197265625), np.float64(1678.0044531249998)), (np.float64(2624.52197265625), np.float64(1195.4345703125))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 348, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': '19d464d2cfa4404cfc5329d1d9bb375a', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': 'b6625ce77da362e621f3f2967b8a6636'}, page_content='With the introduction of this feature, Satellite operators can now define skew versus PSD lim- its with enough granularity to function accurately in every beam and in every RA; and ter- minals are not restricted to the worst-case beam in the RA. Instead, the terminal uses parameters configured specifically for the current beam (channel) at the point which the beam intersects the RA. As such, slot assignments for affected terminals can use better car- riers that improve inbound efficiency. The reference point (skew, C/N) that ties the relative skew versus PSD limit increase curve to a specific C/N limit at every skew value is now set dif- ferently in each beam/channel.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.908390462398529, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(568.4677734375), np.float64(1766.0513281249998)), (np.float64(568.4677734375), np.float64(1829.2336197916666)), (np.float64(1436.2174072265625), np.float64(1829.2336197916666)), (np.float64(1436.2174072265625), np.float64(1766.0513281249998))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 348, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': '9bae8b0ceac6f42113f951e37453f41d', 'category': 'Title', 'element_id': '1b6b7702e2213d10f6640158f9173676'}, page_content='8.5.2.1 Feature Description'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.947523295879364, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(568.75), np.float64(1872.9207763671875)), (np.float64(568.75), np.float64(2170.1919531249996)), (np.float64(2608.4928697916666), np.float64(2170.1919531249996)), (np.float64(2608.4928697916666), np.float64(1872.9207763671875))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 348, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': '1b6b7702e2213d10f6640158f9173676', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': '50d460268c9b872ed711033ae88d3512'}, page_content='The ability to configure a reference skew and PSD limit per regulatory area, beam, and RF Terminal Type is an enhancement of the Real Skew feature. This configurability allows the PSD limit curve to "shift" up or down as a whole in each region, while still maintaining its shape. RA compliance is enhanced greatly and terminal muting, due to skew limits, is largely reduced.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9149964451789856, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(568.75), np.float64(2216.384661458333)), (np.float64(568.75), np.float64(2326.962786458333)), (np.float64(2628.33837890625), np.float64(2326.962786458333)), (np.float64(2628.33837890625), np.float64(2216.384661458333))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 348, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': '1b6b7702e2213d10f6640158f9173676', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': '467c074c54e0e7c55fe8a06accd6795d'}, page_content='Some key characteristics of PSD Limit per Terminal Type, Channel, and RA configurability are listed below:'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9130440354347229, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(668.882080078125), np.float64(2373.1554947916666)), (np.float64(668.882080078125), np.float64(2483.7336197916666)), (np.float64(2400.142578125), np.float64(2483.7336197916666)), (np.float64(2400.142578125), np.float64(2373.1554947916666))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 348, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': '1b6b7702e2213d10f6640158f9173676', 'category': 'ListItem', 'element_id': '511586808b2eb5bcf902d873703ddf2d'}, page_content='• Reference Skew Limits and Reference C/N can be configured manually per RA/Channel/Terminal Type'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.8827215433120728, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(673.2760416666666), np.float64(2529.9263281249996)), (np.float64(673.2760416666666), np.float64(2578.5252864583335)), (np.float64(2427.0698242187