b53f915f1223594605', 'category': 'Title', 'element_id': 'd2092560c93b087d3f1de86eb93b322c'}, page_content='8.5.2.2 Configuration Considerations'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9481649994850159, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(568.75), np.float64(499.1971614583332)), (np.float64(568.75), np.float64(859.5877075195312)), (np.float64(2625.427978515625), np.float64(859.5877075195312)), (np.float64(2625.427978515625), np.float64(499.1971614583332))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 350, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': 'd2092560c93b087d3f1de86eb93b322c', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': 'cd007c11414ab12c7b520dcfdcf213f3'}, page_content='Prior to Velocity 3.0, the PSD vs Skew angle curve along with reference values for Skew and Maximum C/N, were configured on the Pulse RA page; however, the Max C/N and Regulatory Offset (RO) maps are beam dependent and not enforced by the RA parameters. The choice, however, of the reference Max C/N is based on the Max C/N link budget per beam. Within an RA, or group of RAs where the same curve is configured, the same reference Skew value should result in many different Max C/N results, as the performance across the beam varies.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9525871276855469, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(564.8399658203125), np.float64(907.5304947916665)), (np.float64(564.8399658203125), np.float64(1389.9836197916666)), (np.float64(2639.702880859375), np.float64(1389.9836197916666)), (np.float64(2639.702880859375), np.float64(907.5304947916665))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 350, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': 'd2092560c93b087d3f1de86eb93b322c', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': 'f27b172aeae68a9efbfb3085624ee60d'}, page_content="As new Terminal Types are deployed, using the Channel configuration, the NMS operator has the option to enter a record for each RA that intersects the channel's beam. Each record con- tains the RA ID, the Channel, a Skew Reference Angle, and a Skew Reference Max C/N for that RA ID. The table must be entered in its entirety—otherwise if it is omitted, the new imple- mentation is not applied and the Reference Skew Angle and Reference C/N parameters in the RA configuration are used as defaults, to cover the case where per-channel (iNet) con- figuration have not been entered. RA-level defaults will be applied to any Channel/RF Ter- minal Type not configured for the current RA."), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.8571738004684448, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(565.1389770507812), np.float64(1441.99951171875)), (np.float64(565.1389770507812), np.float64(1495.712786458333)), (np.float64(1222.5926513671875), np.float64(1495.712786458333)), (np.float64(1222.5926513671875), np.float64(1441.99951171875))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 350, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9