: Public Technical Reference Guide | iDirect Velocity™ | T0001665 | Revision 1'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9161288142204285, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(1992.1562499999995), np.float64(251.28049479166657)), (np.float64(1992.1562499999995), np.float64(299.87945312500017)), (np.float64(2625.40771484375), np.float64(299.87945312500017)), (np.float64(2625.40771484375), np.float64(251.28049479166657))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 361, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'category': 'Header', 'element_id': '0e85e077ea0cea944a1f80afbd36ffb0'}, page_content='9.2.2 FAP Allowance Period'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.8742119669914246, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(568.75), np.float64(391.6843566894531)), (np.float64(568.75), np.float64(465.2435607910156)), (np.float64(1530.9385986328125), np.float64(465.2435607910156)), (np.float64(1530.9385986328125), np.float64(391.6843566894531))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 361, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': '0e85e077ea0cea944a1f80afbd36ffb0', 'category': 'Title', 'element_id': '56db195d0c3da59fa139f7ba5203f103'}, page_content='9.2.2 FAP Allowance Period'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9389320611953735, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(568.75), np.float64(506.4888281249999)), (np.float64(568.75), np.float64(679.0461197916668)), (np.float64(2636.3834947916666), np.float64(679.0461197916668)), (np.float64(2636.3834947916666), np.float64(506.4888281249999))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 361, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': '56db195d0c3da59fa139f7ba5203f103', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': '43b42dbc4f3f98402dc6cbd2b68eb166'}, page_content='The allowance period is the applicable period of time in which the transfer volume is being tracked. The allowance period can be a 24-hour, 7-day, or 30-day period. There are two types of allowance period — fixed or rolling.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9333385229110718, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(567.5468749999999), np.float64(725.2388281249998)), (np.float64(567.5468749999999), np.float64(960.7960815429688)), (np.float64(2621.289744791666), np.float64(960.7960815429688)), (np.float64(2621.289744791666), np.float64(725.2388281249998))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 361, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': '56db195d0c3da59fa139f7ba5203f103', 'category': 'ListItem', 'element_id': '5213d9e2097538c0984bb38fb7549add'}, page_content='• Fixed Allowance — If the allowance period is configured as fixed, the normal volume allowance is credited to the service plan at the beginning of the allowance period. If the entire allowance is consumed before the end of the allowance period, the service plan will require overage or Top-Up in order to continue consuming data.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9504044055938721, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(567.5468749999999), np.float64(1002.692626953125)), (np.float64(567.5468749999999), np.float64(1426.4419531249998)), (np.float64(2592.208984375), np.float64(1426.4419531249998)), (np.float64(2592.208984375), np.float64(1002.692626953125))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 361, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': '56db195d0c3da59fa139f7ba5203f103', 'category': 'ListItem', 'element_id': '43cd12c982ac8c88edb3cbadc22b673a'}, page_content="• Rolling Allowance — If the allowance period is configured as rolling, the service plan's regular allowance is credited in increments over the duration of the allowance period. Rolling allowance periods are intended to avoid situations at the end of the allowance period where the entire allowance has been consumed, and the service plan owner is throttled or forced to consume overage or Top-Up allowances (described below). For rolling allowance periods, the user must also specify the update interval at which the periodic allowance is credited to the service plan."), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9495173692703247, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(557.67822265625), np.float64(1467.96142578125)), (np.float64(557.67822265625), np.float64(1771.5123291015625)), (np.float64(2608.452392578125), np.float64(1771.5123291015625)), (np.float64(2608.452392578125), np.float64(1467.96142578125))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 361, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': '56db195d0c3da59fa139f7ba5203f103', 'category': 'ListItem', 'element_id': '83df914535d2b636e7054b5869c85141'}, page_content='• Once the entire allowance has been consumed, if there is no overage or Top-Up available, the service plan must wait until a certain number of bytes (referred to as the rolling restoration) are returned to the account via the rolling updates before consumption of data can continue. The time it takes for these bytes to be returned to the allowance is the recovery period.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.8763225674629211, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(568.75), np.float64(1860.4590885416667)), (np.float64(568.75), np.float64(1928.526796875)), (np.float64(1534.41259765625), np.float64(1928.526796875)), (np.float64(1534.41259765625), np.float64(1860.4590885416667))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 361, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': '0e85e077ea0cea944a1f80afbd36ffb0', 'category': 'Title', 'element_id': '7c5bfb5bf7271b7326fe1e86d7ee2f42'}, page_content='9.2.3 FAP Restoration Rules'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9329432249069214, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(568.75), np.float64(1971.0203857421875)), (np.float64(568.75), np.float64(2144.6711197916666)), (np.float64(2503.9668281249997), np.float64(2144.6711197916666)), (np.float64(2503.9668281249997), np.float64(1971.0203857421875))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 361, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': '7c5bfb5bf7271b7326fe1e86d7ee2f42', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': '9981feae34d14dcd755e56164791c722'}, page_content='Restoration rules are conditions that need to be fulfilled before service is restored to normal, after being throttled or suspended. These rules cannot be removed by the user, although one of the restoration rules is configurable.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9221783876419067, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(567.7850952148438), np.float64(2190.8638281249996)), (np.float64(567.7850952148438), np.float64(2301.4419531249996)), (np.float64(2588.752197265625), np.float64(2301.4419531249996)), (np.float64(2588.752197265625), np.float64(2190.8638281249996))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 361, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T'