he HTTP redirect feature, described in FAP HTTP Redirect on page 332. At the same time, the system generates an event notification that may trigger an external billing OSS/BSS to query the owner for permission to enter the overage state, or the user may receive the event notification via the EAP."), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9419599175453186, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(568.75), np.float64(1290.3429947916666)), (np.float64(568.75), np.float64(1587.6019287109375)), (np.float64(2638.7532864583327), np.float64(1587.6019287109375)), (np.float64(2638.7532864583327), np.float64(1290.3429947916666))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 364, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': 'b30d0bcc4833241fd57984362629a84c', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': '78126d2fc69e0737b809d96803591e57'}, page_content='Using the NMS Web UI, Pulse provides the ability to approve the overage state for a SSPC and GSP using either the Pulse UI (see the FAP Overage Approval probe commands in Configuring Velocity Networks using Pulse) or the associated Pulse API (See iDirect DevTool ). Note that the event requesting approval to enter the overage state is only sent once. If no response is received from the user, the assumption is that he does not wish to enter the overage state.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9398086667060852, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(568.75), np.float64(1633.0513281249998)), (np.float64(568.75), np.float64(