ument(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.8747153282165527, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(568.4544677734375), np.float64(400.7596614583332)), (np.float64(568.4544677734375), np.float64(449.35861979166685)), (np.float64(813.610335580729), np.float64(449.35861979166685)), (np.float64(813.610335580729), np.float64(400.7596614583332))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 373, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': 'f39376421e745879f1a2fb59fdd7fee6', 'category': 'Title', 'element_id': 'c551eb5d0a7cd5e3939352094ec238e5'}, page_content='Operation:'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9522913098335266, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(568.283203125), np.float64(495.5513281249999)), (np.float64(568.283203125), np.float64(916.0252864583334)), (np.float64(2635.5449531249997), np.float64(916.0252864583334)), (np.float64(2635.5449531249997), np.float64(495.5513281249999))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 373, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': 'c551eb5d0a7cd5e3939352094ec238e5', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': 'bc033c81986206c4841fe2331a042ebb'}, page_content='A Satellite Operator has deployed a satellite that provides a number of overlapping 2-way spot beams, which support continuous coverage across a wide geographic area covering the flight path of aeronautical terminals. These spot beams occupy the same frequency band but may use one of two different polarizations. The same satellite supports two 1-way overlay beams that operate in the same frequency band as the 2-way beams. They each use one of the two available downlink polarizations, and have identical footprints on the ground. See the following illustration.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9500832557678223, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(566.8412475585938), np.float64(962.2179947916665)), (np.float64(566.8412475585938), np.float64(1382.6919531249998)), (np.float64(2612.831411458333), np.float64(1382.6919531249998)), (np.float64(2612.831411458333), np.float64(962.2179947916665))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 373, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': 'c551eb5d0a7cd5e3939352094ec238e5', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': 'ebb05297b37edd396e0edd42c13e48d7'}, page_content='In this example, as illustrated in the diagram, the mobile terminal starts its service in the area covered by SB-1A and travels to the area served by SB-6A. The terminal exchanges unicast traffic on a 2-way spot beam, using the primary receiver, while simultaneously using its secondary receiver to receive multicast traffic from a 1-way overlay beam. As the aircraft traverses its flight path, the terminal switches between the 2-way spot beam using a break- before-make switch. When a 2-way beam is not available, the terminal continues to receive persistent multicast on its secondary receiver.'), Document(me