p.float64(568.2427978515625), np.float64(400.7596614583332)), (np.float64(568.2427978515625), np.float64(511.3377864583335)), (np.float64(2639.0449531249997), np.float64(511.3377864583335)), (np.float64(2639.0449531249997), np.float64(400.7596614583332))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 387, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': 'ca47724cd8428dc6634f8dd9b03fa5ea', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': '884a6fa8e252dd637701255eedcd52b6'}, page_content='These stats, on a per frame basis, are represented in a binary form, where a value of TRUE (1) = CIR/MIR Achieved; and a value of FALSE (0) = CIR/MIR Not Achieved.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.950013279914856, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(568.75), np.float64(557.5304947916666)), (np.float64(568.75), np.float64(978.0044531250002)), (np.float64(2615.237661458333), np.float64(978.0044531250002)), (np.float64(2615.237661458333), np.float64(557.5304947916666))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 387, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': 'ca47724cd8428dc6634f8dd9b03fa5ea', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': 'e849ba9cfc3a7b3be87eedf46328e265'}, page_content='These stats, although important and are used in SLAs with end customers, they provide no information regarding what percentage of the CIR/MIR was met in terms of bandwidth (bytes). An iNet that is relatively congested, can be used to illustrate this concept. For a relatively large percentage of the time, the SSPCs for the terminals in this iNet are barely getting the contracted CIR bandwidth. Let us assume the cir_fullfillment is 50%. However the amount of bandwidth they (the SSPCs) are getting is very close to the CIR but is below it for 50% of the time.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9538454413414001, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(568.75), np.float64(1024.197161458333)), (np.float64(568.75), np.float64(1444.6711197916666)), (np.float64(2637.659536458333), np.float64(1444.6711197916666)), (np.float64(2637.659536458333), np.float64(1024.197161458333))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 387, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': 'ca47724cd8428dc6634f8dd9b03fa5ea', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': 'e1207414f8634b398e7697b316d7a89f'}, page_content='The SSPC usually represents an application, used by the end customer and that will have certain bandwidth demands. Assuming that the application receives 99% of its CIR for 99 % of the time, then this would likely be sufficient and is not likely to introduce any noticeable degradation in service. This performance of 99% can be reported using the CIR/MIR Fulfillment Ratio stat. If the SLAs are based on these stats, the first stat would be dismal at 50% while the second stat would be very good at 99%. The Service Provider use the Fulfillment Ratio Stat to differentiate the SLA.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.8930692076683044, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(568.75), np.float64(1532.7179947916666)), (np.float64(568.75), np.float64(1595.900286458333)), (np.float64(2076.943359375), np.float64(1595.900286458333)), (np.float64(2076.943359375), np.float64(1532.7179947916666))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 387, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': 'ca47724cd8428dc6634f8dd9b03fa5ea', 'category': 'Title', 'element_id': 'bdde431c5e1b1f91de52702c6be0236f'}, page_content='11.4.1.1 Configuring the Fulfillment Window Size'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9447786211967468, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(564.0045166015625), np.float64(1640.3429947916663)), (np.float64(564.0045166015625), np.float64(1936.8586197916663)), (np.float64(2606.384033203125), np.float64(1936.8586197916663)), (np.float64(2606.384033203125), np.float64(1640.3429947916663))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 387, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': 'bdde431c5e1b1f91de52702c6be0236f', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': '566ea32f5e5f5154aa8aad82b6965cd2'}, page_content='The fulfillment window size is configurable for each terminal SSPP, independently for downstream and upstream directions of the SSPC. The units are in frames, translated to seconds, where for downstream, one frame unit represents 100 ms; and for upstream, one frame unit represents 125 ms. The fulfillment window size that is configured for the CIR/MIR Fulfillment Stats is also used for the corresponding Fulfillment Ratio Stat.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9491884708404541, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(568.75), np.float64(1983.0513281249998)), (np.float64(568.75), np.float64(2403.525286458333)), (np.float64(2624.44873046875), np.float64(2403.525286458333)), (np.float64(2624.44873046875), np.float64(1983.0513281249998))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 387, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': 'bdde431c5e1b1f91de52702c6be0236f', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': 'ea0ee62d034cf6c30347bbd875c46eda'}, page_content='In a real application, having relatively relaxed fulfillment requirements, there would be no noticeable degradation in application performance if the allocation of the demand is delayed by a certain amount— for example, with file transfer or directory replication. These applications are expected to be tolerant of delays in allocation and are not critical with respect to variations in bandwidth over time. In this case we might use a large fulfillment window, for example 5 seconds. In the downstream we would configure 50 (50*0.1 = 5) and in the upstream we configure 40 (40*0.125 = 5).'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.940911054611206, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(568.75), np.float64(2449.7179947916666)), (np.float64(568.75), np.float64(2746.2336197916666)), (np.float64(2618.199462890625), np.float64(2746.2336197916666)), (np.float64(2618.199462890625), np.float64(2449.7179947916666))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 387, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': 'bdde431c5e1b1f91de52702c6be0236f', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': '814e5e1b506fceb77910c99b8bafa8f4'}, page_content='The customer might also have a low-latency, low-jitter application such as VoIP that requires timely responses and has more stringent timing constraints. Assuming the operator determines a fulfillment window of 0.5 seconds is needed in this case—then the window settings for downstream and upstream would be 5 and 4 respectively. The assumption is that the operator will use different SSPCs for the different applications.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9360361099243164, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(564.4107055664062), np.float64(2792.4263281249996)), (np.float64(564.4107055664062), np.float64(3088.941953125)), (np.float64(2584.036376953125), np.float64(3088.941953125)), (np.float64(2584.036376953125), np.float64(2792.4263281249996))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 387, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': 'bdde431c5e1b1f91de52702c6be0236f', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': 'd9a597d2a9a8ddf5974ec78c5cd49784'}, page_content='If we continue with this example, and the operator puts both applications in the same SSPC then the window size must be set for the more stringent of applications, to meet the requirements of the transactional application. This will likely be more expensive as we are guaranteeing a level of service that is not required for the more relaxed application of file transfer/directory replication.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.46198439598083496, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(353.6458333333333), np.float64(3510.02880859375)), (np.float64(353.6458333333333), np.float64(3628.525286458333)), (np.float64(1943.73095703125), np.float64(3628.525286458333)), (np.float64(1943.73095703125), np.float64(3510.02880859375))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 387, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': 'bdde431c5e1b1f91de52702c6be0236f', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': '454b2891c111412c5c3499a0d194cb8f'}, page_content='ST Engineering iDirect Proprietary | Confidentiality: Public Technical Reference Guide | iDirect Velocity™ | T0001665 | Revision 1'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.5336760878562927, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(2544.864583333333), np.float64(3514.3013281249996)), (np.float64(2544.864583333333), np.float64(3562.900286458333)), (np.float64(2624.076904296875), np.float64(3562.900286458333)), (np.float64(2624.076904296875), np.float64(3514.3013281249996))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'la