', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 400, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': '1e5b893e7f54baa04e0f084370b61025', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': 'ba0e9fc45808129625fe13bc5c9ed083'}, page_content='Service Delimiting Tags (SDTs) associate Ethernet frames with specific SVNs. The Velocity iDirect system supports IEEE 802.1Q VLAN tags type of SDT.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9429084062576294, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(568.75), np.float64(965.8638281249998)), (np.float64(568.75), np.float64(1200.4002864583335)), (np.float64(2638.972036458333), np.float64(1200.4002864583335)), (np.float64(2638.972036458333), np.float64(965.8638281249998))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 400, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': '1e5b893e7f54baa04e0f084370b61025', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': 'bc1e69bc09bd76f2295980f48cc31d27'}, page_content='VLAN tags allow the Layer 2 emulation to provide traditional VLAN VPN functionality. When VLAN tags are used, only the outermost tag of an Ethernet frame determines the SVN to which the frame belongs. The SVN number is the VLAN ID of the first VLAN tag in the frame. Any additional inner VLAN tags are passed through transparently.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.6062041521072388, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(1250.4479166666667), np.float64(1639.0669531249996)), (np.float64(1250.4479166666667), np.float64(1687.823974609375)), (np.float64(1949.720703125), np.float64(1687.823974609375)), (np.float64(1949.720703125), np.float64(1639.0669531249996))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 400, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'category': 'Title', 'element_id': 'aa0cb36ebdf9a21f9db96eed18931891'}, page_content='Figure 12-4. SDT Mode = VLAN'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9440416693687439, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(565.2792358398438), np.float64(1742.4263281249998)), (np.float64(565.2792358398438), np.float64(1976.962786458333)), (np.float64(2617.3522447916666), np.float64(1976.962786458333)), (np.float64(2617.3522447916666), np.float64(1742.4263281249998))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 400, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': 'aa0cb36ebdf9a21f9db96eed18931891', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': '11bd51f3ba72bf03f8a64f07d091f293'}, page_content='SDTs are always used on the hub side. It is the responsibility of the Gateway CE to add the appropriate SDT for downstream traffic; it is the responsibility of the iDirect hub to add the appropriate SDT for upstream traffic. The hub SDT Mode is a global setting for VLAN. The hub and its associated gateway CE should be configured in the same mode.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9395670890808105, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(568.75), np.float64(2023.1554947916663)), (np.float64(568.75), np.float64(2195.712786458333)), (np.float64(2640.618896484375), np.float64(2195.712786458333)), (np.float64(2640.618896484375), np.float64(2023.1554947916663))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 400, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': 'aa0cb36ebdf9a21f9db96eed18931891', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': 'b27d3e9561c4f03d69d51230e9fbe34e'}, page_content='SDTs are optional on the remote side. When used, it is the responsibility of the CE attached to the remote modem to add the appropriate SDT for upstream traffic; it is the responsibility of the remote to add the appropriate SDT for downstream traffic.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9414153099060059, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(563.049560546875), np.float64(2241.9054947916666)), (np.float64(563.049560546875), np.float64(2476.4419531249996)), (np.float64(2603.097036458333), np.float64(2476.4419531249996)), (np.float64(2603.097036458333), np.float64(2241.9054947916666))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 400, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': 'aa0cb36ebdf9a21f9db96eed18931891', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': '5c51a2f4f573fea683e4502a518fd3fe'}, page_content='SDTs can be omitted on the remote side by configuring a remote LAN port as an Access Port and associating the port with a single SVN. All Ethernet frames received on the port are transmitted on the configured SVN. The hub tags the frame based on the SVN ID and hub SDT Mode before sending the frame to the hub CE.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.8892063498497009, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(568.41845703125), np.float64(2522.634661458333)), (np.float64(568.41845703125), np.float64(2571.2336197916666)), (np.float64(1956.5084947916664), np.float64(2571.2336197916666)), (np.float64(1956.5084947916664), np.float64(2522.634661458333))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 400, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': 'aa0cb36ebdf9a21f9db96eed18931891', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': '71342a1458c29f49646f8daafdf1e95e'}, page_content='12.3 displays the Service Delineating Tag (SDT) support matrix.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(1259.1249999999998), np.float64(2639.3013281249996)), (np.float64(1259.1249999999998), np.float64(2687.9002864583335)), (np.float64(1934.526532170677), np.float64(2687.9002864583335)), (np.float64(1934.526532170677), np.float64(2639.3013281249996))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 4