ed in the payload are not accelerated. IPv6 TCP packets are never accelerated.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.8998202085494995, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(313.54166666666663), np.float64(2366.2916666666665)), (np.float64(313.54166666666663), np.float64(2453.7916666666665)), (np.float64(1839.4396545), np.float64(2453.7916666666665)), (np.float64(1839.4396545), np.float64(2366.2916666666665))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 404, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'category': 'Title', 'element_id': '0a594f74768895f852f992b228dfa51f'}, page_content='12.8 Advanced Header Compression'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9417537450790405, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(568.75), np.float64(2497.1138281249996)), (np.float64(568.75), np.float64(2669.6711197916666)), (np.float64(2632.0908203125), np.float64(2669.6711197916666)), (np.float64(2632.0908203125), np.float64(2497.1138281249996))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 404, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': '0a594f74768895f852f992b228dfa51f', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': '636ebe1ff6d70791b180203f4aa898f9'}, page_content='Robust Header Compression (ROHC) is a standardized method to compress the IP, UDP, UDP- Lite, RTP, and TCP headers of Internet packets. Currently, ROHCv2 compression only supports Layer 2 traffic.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9514738321304321, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(564.5526733398438), np.float64(2715.8638281249996)), (np.float64(564.5526733398438), np.float64(3136.337786458333)), (np.float64(2638.1334947916666), np.float64(3136.337786458333)), (np.float64(2638.1334947916666), np.float64(2715.8638281249996))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 404, 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'parent_id': '0a594f74768895f852f992b228dfa51f', 'category': 'NarrativeText', 'element_id': '150e19ac5125f9d492d386cfba585bdb'}, page_content='The iDirect ROHCv2 implementation extended the standard compression profiles to include the compression of Ethernet headers with stacked VLAN tags. Enabling the compression of Ethernet headers will almost completely remove the additional header overhead associated with L2oS in comparison to Layer 3. Compression of additional headers will allow L2oS to surpass the overhead efficiency of the traditional Layer 3 networks. The overall efficiency gain depends on the size of the Ethernet frames. With ROHCv2, the smaller the average frame size, the better the efficiency gain.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.9329954385757446, 'is_extracted': 'true', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(563.588134765625), np.float64(3182.530494791666)), (np.float64(563.588134765625), np.float64(3293.1086197916666)), (np.float64