d to the Backup NOC, and the Private Network cloud is connected to the Backup NOC as well.\n\n5. **Backup CDC (Central Data Center)**: This is a green circle located on the right side of the diagram, connected to the Core Network.\n\n6. **Primary CDC (Central Data Center)**: This is another green circle located on the right side of the diagram, connected to the Core Network.\n\n7. **Rain Diversity / Backup SAS (Satellite Access System)**: This is a yellow circle located below the Core Network. It is connected to the Primary SAS (Satellite Access System) and the RF Gateways.\n\n8. **Primary SAS**: This is a yellow circle located below the Core Network, connected to the Rain Diversity / Backup SAS and the Satellite Terminals.\n\n9. **Satellite Terminals**: These are represented by four white rectangles with satellite dishes on the left and right sides of the diagram, connected to the Primary SAS and the Rain Diversity / Backup SAS.\n\n10. **RF Gateways**: These are two green circles located below the Core Network, connected to the Primary CDC and the Rain Diversity / Backup SAS.\n\nThe diagram uses lines to represent connections between different components, and the colors (blue, green, yellow, and purple) are used to differentiate between different types of systems or services. The diagram is designed to show the redundancy and connectivity of the network, with multiple paths and backup systems in place.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(568.75), np.float64(1028.125)), (np.float64(568.75), np.float64(2435.4166666666665)), (np.float64(2625.0), np.float64(2435.4166666666665)), (np.float64(2625.0), np.float64(1028.125))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 51, 'image_path': '/Users/prathod/Proje