port**: This is a large circle encompassing the entire network architecture, labeled as "Teleport."\n\nThe diagram shows the flow of data from the satellite terminals through the RF System, Hub Chassis, and various clusters and switches, ultimately reaching the Core Network. The connections are represented by lines, and the components are labeled with their respective names.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(823.9583333333333), np.float64(1002.6041666666666)), (np.float64(823.9583333333333), np.float64(2552.083333333333)), (np.float64(2369.7916666666665), np.float64(2552.083333333333)), (np.float64(2369.7916666666665), np.float64(1002.6041666666666))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 52, 'image_path': '/Users/prathod/Projects/Rag_based_q-a_boat_over_own_doc/src/q&a_boat/figures/figure-52-8.jpg', 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'category': 'Image', 'element_id': '6b4ff117b11b365397cedc6d612309a4', 'source_image': '/Users/prathod/Projects/Rag_based_q-a_boat_over_own_doc/src/q&a_boat/figures/figure-52-8.jpg'}, page_content='[IMAGE DESCRIPTION]\nSource File: /Users/prathod/Projects/Rag_based_q-a_boat_over_own_doc/src/q&a_boat/figures/figure-52-8.jpg\nThe image is a network diagram illustrating a satellite-based communication system. Here is a detailed description of the components and their connections:\n\n1. **Satellite**: At the top of the diagram, there is a satellite depicted with three feeder links pointing towards it. These feeder links are labeled as "Feeder Links."\n\n2. **RF Gateways**:\n   - There are three RF Gateways labeled as "RF Gateway #1," "RF Gateway #2," and "Backup RF Gateway #3." These gateways are connected to the satellite via the feeder links.\n   - Each RF Gateway is connected to the "Core / Backbone Network."\n\n3. **Core / Backbone Network**: This is the central network hub that connects all the components. It is shown as a cloud shape and is connected to:\n   - The "Corporate Network."\n   - The "Internet."\n   - The "Primary CDC" and "Backup CDC" (Central Data Centers).\n   - The "NOC" (Network Operations Center) and "Backup NOC."\n\n4. **Corporate Network**: This is a cloud shape representing a corporate network that is connected to the Core / Backbone Network.\n\n5. **Internet**: This is another cloud shape representing the internet, which is also connected to the Core / Backbone Network.\n\n6. **Primary CDC and Backup CDC**: These are two Central Data Centers, each with a "Packet Processing" label. The Primary CDC and Backup CDC are connected to the Core / Backbone Network.\n\n7. **NOC and Backup NOC**: These are the Network Operations Centers, with the Backup NOC being a secondary or redundant system. Both are connected to the Core / Backbone Network.\n\nThe diagram shows a redundant and interconnected network design, with multiple points of connection and failover capabilities to ensure reliability and redundancy.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(568.75), np.float64(936.9791666666666)), (np.float64(568.75), np.float64(1111.9791666666665)), (np.float64(743.7499999999999), np.float64(1111.9791666666665)), (np.float64(743.7499999999999), np.float64(936.9791666666666))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 53, 'image_path': '/Users/prathod/Projects/Rag_based_q-a_boat_over_own_doc/src/q&a_boat/figures/figure-53-9.jpg', 'file_directory': '/var/folders/