Vehicle and Drilling Rig**: On the right side of the image, there is a depiction of a military vehicle and a drilling rig enclosed in a yellow circle. Both are connected to the satellite by white lines, indicating communication links.\n\n3. **Satellite Access Station (SAS)**: Below the satellite, there is a device labeled "SAS" (Satellite Access Station). This device is connected to the satellite by a red line, indicating a bidirectional communication link. The SAS is also connected to the Internet by a red line, indicating that it can relay data to the Internet.\n\n4. **Internet**: On the far right of the image, there is a cloud labeled "Internet," which represents the global network. The SAS is connected to the Internet, suggesting that it can send data to the broader internet infrastructure.\n\nThe image uses different colors to distinguish between the satellite, the ground-based devices, the SAS, and the Internet. The white lines represent communication links, while the red lines represent bidirectional communication links. The yellow, blue, and white circles help to visually group the different types of devices.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(758.3333333333333), np.float64(1669.7916666666665)), (np.float64(758.3333333333333), np.float64(2810.9374999999995)), (np.float64(2431.770833333333), np.float64(2810.9374999999995)), (np.float64(2431.770833333333), np.float64(1669.7916666666665))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 58, 'image_path': '/Users/prathod/Projects/Rag_based_q-a_boat_over_own_doc/src/q&a_boat/figures/figure-58-12.jpg', 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'category': 'Image', 'element_id': 'c3b10704e4cc457d698df63ae02e0932', 'source_image': '/Users/prathod/Projects/Rag_based_q-a_boat_over_own_doc/src/q&a_boat/figures/figure-58-12.jpg'}, page_content='[IMAGE DESCRIPTION]\nSource File: /Users/prathod/Projects/Rag_based_q-a_boat_over_own_doc/src/q&a_boat/figures/figure-58-12.jpg\nThe image is a network diagram illustrating a network architecture with multiple components and connections. Here is a detailed description:\n\n1. **Network Components:**\n   - **Primary NOC (Network Operations Center):**\n     - Contains servers labeled as "GBWM," "NOC Pulse NMS," and "Kubernetes Cluster (Kafka)."\n     - Connected to the "Backbone Network."\n   - **Backup NOC:**\n     - Contains servers labeled as "NOC Pulse NMS," "GBWM," and "Kubernetes Cluster (Kafka)."\n     - Connected to the "Backbone Network."\n   - **Primary SAS (Satellite Access System):**\n     - Contains servers labeled as "Hub Chassis," "SAS NMS," "PP," and "Kubernetes Cluster (Kafka)."\n     - Connected to the "Backbone Network."\n   - **Backup and Rain Diversity SAS:**\n     - Contains servers labeled as "Hub Chassis," "SAS NMS," "PP," and "Kubernetes Cluster (Kafka)."\n     - Connected to the "Backbone Network."\n   - **Satellite Terminals:**\n     - Connected to the "Primary SAS."\n   - **EAP (Edge Access Point):**\n     - Connected to the "Primary NOC" and "Backup NOC."\n   - **Internet and Private Network:**\n     - Connected to the "Backup NOC" and "Backup and Rain Diversity SAS."\n\n2. **Labels and Connections:**\n   - The diagram includes labels such as "Hub Chassis," "SAS NMS," "PP," "Kubernetes Cluster (Kafka)," "NOC Pulse NMS," "GBWM," "EAP," "Internet," and "Private Network."\n   - The "Backbone Network" is the central hub connecting all the components.\n\n3. **Visual Elements:**\n   - The diagram uses circles to represent different sections of the network.\n   - Servers and other components are depicted as rectangular boxes.\n   - The "Satellite Terminals" are represented by satellite dishes.\n   - The "EAP" is represented by a small rectangular box with an antenna.\n\nThis diagram illustrates a robust network architecture with redundancy and diversity, ensuring that the network can operate efficiently and reliably in various scenarios.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(568.75), np.float64(696.3541666666666)), (np.float64(568.75), np.float64(1797.3958333333333)), (np.float64(2625.0), np.float64(1797.3958333333333)), (np.float64(2625.0), np.float64(696.3541666666666))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 59, 'image_path': '/Users/prathod/Projects/Rag_based_q-a_boat_over_own_doc/src/q&a_boat/figures/figure-59-13.jpg', 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'category': 'Image', 'element_id': 'db31d8d9da2e599571da196cf3410cad', 'source_image': '/Users/prathod/Projects/Rag_based_q-a_boat_over_own_doc/src/q&a_boat/figures/figure-59-13.jpg'}, page_content='[IMAGE DESCRIPTION]\nSource File: /Users/prathod/Projects/Rag_based_q-a_boat_over_own_doc/src/q&a_boat/figures/figure-59-13.jpg\nThe image is a detailed network diagram illustrating a satellite-based communication system, specifically labeled as "Per SVN" (Satellite Virtual Network). The diagram includes various network components and their interconnections, along with IPv4 and IPv6 routing protocols used in different domains.\n\n### Components and Labels:\n1. **Access Router**: Located on the far left, connected to a "SAS Switch" via an Ethernet interface (eth0).\n2. **SAS Switch**: Connected to a "PP Server" and an "iDirect Hub" via an Ethernet interface (eth0).\n3. **PP Server**: Connected to the "iDirect Hub" and an "Antenna" via an Ethernet interface (eth0).\n4. **iDirect Hub**: Connected to two "Satellite Terminals" (ST1 and ST2) via satellite connections (sat0).\n5. **Satellite Terminals (ST1 and ST2)**: Connected to two "Customer Equipment" (CE1 and CE2) via Ethernet interfaces (eth0).\n6. **Customer Equipment (CE1 and CE2)**: Connected to the "Access Router" via Ethernet interfaces (eth0).\n\n### Routing Domains:\n- **SAS Routing Domain**: Includes the Access Router, SAS Switch, and PP Server.\n- **OTA Routing Domain**: Includes the iDirect Hub and the two Satellite Terminals.\n- **Terminal Routing Domain**: Includes the two Customer Equipment devices (CE1 and CE2).\n\n### IPv4 and IPv6 Routing Protocols:\n- **IPv4**:\n  - BGP4+ (Border Gateway Protocol version 4+)\n  - Static routing\n- **IPv6 (partial)**:\n  - BGP4+ (Border Gateway Protocol version 4+)\n  - Static routing\n\n### Key:\n- **CE**: Customer Equipment\n- **SAS**: Satellite Access Station\n- **ST**: Satellite Terminal\n\n### Additional Notes:\n- The diagram highlights the use of BGP4+ and static routing for both IPv4 and IPv6 in different routing domains.\n- The "iDirect Hub" acts as a central hub for satellite communication, connecting to multiple satellite terminals.\n- The "Satellite Terminals" (ST1 and ST2) are connected to the Customer Equipment (CE1 and CE2) via Ethernet interfaces, indicating a direct connection for data exchange.\n\nThis diagram provides a clear overview of the network architecture and the protocols used for routing in a satellite-based communication system.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(984.3749999999999), np.float64(1159.375)), (np.float64(984.3749999999999), np.float64(2916.6666666666665)), (np.float64(2205.7291666666665), np.float64(2916.6666666666665)), (np.float64(2205.7291666666665), np.float64(1159.375))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 61, 'image_path': '/Users/prathod/Projects/Rag_based_q-a_boat_over_own_doc/src/q&a_boat/figures/figure-61-14.jpg', 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'category': 'Image', 'element_id': '4fe6bc7c084b55240e10270c1e6cb074', 'source_image': '/Users/prathod/Projects/Rag_based_q-a_boat_over_own_doc/src/q&a_boat/figures/figure-61-14.jpg'}, page_content='[IMAGE DESCRIPTION]\nSource File: /Users/prathod/Projects/Rag_based_q-a_boat_over_own_doc/src/q&a_boat/figures/figure-61-14.jpg\nThe image consists of two diagrams labeled (a) and (b), both illustrating the relationship between a Satellite Operator, Service Providers, and Subscribers in a satellite communication system.\n\n### Diagram (a):\n- **Satellite Operator**: At the top, there is a box labeled "Satellite Operator."\n- **Service Provider(s)**: Below the Satellite Operator, there is a box labeled "Service Provider(s)" with an arrow pointing downward.\n- **Service Provider(s)**: Two boxes labeled "Service Provider(s)" are shown, each with an arrow pointing downward.\n- **Subscriber(s)**: Below each "Service Provider(s)" box, there are two boxes labeled "Subscriber(s)" with an arrow pointing downward.\n\n### Diagram (b):\n- **Satellite Operator acting as Service Provider**: At the top, there is a box labeled "Satellite Operator acting as Service Provider."\n- **Service Provider(s)**: Below the Satellite Operator acting as Service Provider, there are two boxes labeled "Service Provider(s)" with an arrow pointing downward.\n- **Subscriber(s)**: Below each "Service Provider(s)" box, there are two boxes labeled "Subscriber(s)" with an arrow pointing downward.\n\n### Key Observations:\n- Both diagrams show a hierarchical structure where the Satellite Operator is at the top, followed by Service Providers, and then Subscribers.\n- Diagram (a) shows a scenario where the Service Providers are separate entities from the Satellite Operator, while in Diagram (b), the Satellite Operator acts as a Service Provider itself.\n- The arrows indicate the direction of communication or service provision.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(590.625), np.float64(3128.1249999999995)), (np.float64(590.625), np.float64(3303.1249999999995)), (np.float64(765.6249999999999), np.float64(3303.1249999999995)), (np.float64(765.6249999999999), np.float64(3128.1249999999995))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 61, 'image_path': '/Users/prathod/Projects/Rag_based_q-a_boat_over_own_doc/src/q&a_boat/figures/figure-61-15.jpg', 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'category': 'Image', 'element_id': '2594703e14066f83cb979852d5c7b3e1', 'source_image': '/Users/prathod/Projects/Rag_based_q-a_boat_over_own_doc/src/q&a_boat/figures/figure-61-15.jpg'}, page_content='[IMAGE DESCRIPTION]\nSource File: /Users/prathod/Projects/Rag_based_q-a_boat_over_own_doc/src/q&a_boat/figures/figure-61-15.jpg\nThe image appears to be a pixelated representation of a blue gift box with a white interior. The box is open, and there is a blue ribbon tied around it, with a small blue bow on top. The ribbon and bow are also pixelated, maintaining the same blue color scheme as the box. There is no text, numbers, charts, or diagrams visible in the image. The overall design is simple and minimalistic, with a focus on the blue color and the shape of the gift box.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_