VN 1, SVN 2, SVN 3, and SVN 4.\n   - SVN 1 and SVN 3 are connected to the PP Cluster via yellow lines.\n   - SVN 2 and SVN 4 are not directly connected to the PP Cluster but are part of the network.\n\n4. **RADIUS Servers (DP 1, DP 2, DP 3, DP 4)**:\n   - On the left side of the diagram, there are four RADIUS Servers labeled as DP 1, DP 2, DP 3, and DP 4.\n   - Each RADIUS Server is connected to the DCN via gray lines, indicating a connection or data exchange.\n\n5. **Connections**:\n   - The RADIUS Servers (DP 1, DP 2, DP 3, DP 4) are connected to the DCN.\n   - The PP Cluster (PP Servers) is connected to the DCN.\n   - The terminals (SVN 1, SVN 2, SVN 3, SVN 4) are connected to the PP Cluster.\n\n6. **Text Labels**:\n   - The text labels include "DCN," "PP Cluster," "PP Server," "Terminal Proxy," "RADIUS Client," "RADIUS Server," and "SVN" (System Version Number).\n\nThe diagram appears to illustrate a network architecture where the PP Cluster acts as a central hub for communication, with the RADIUS Servers and terminals connected to it via the DCN. The PP Servers within the PP Cluster seem to be responsible for managing the terminals and possibly acting as a proxy or client for RADIUS authentication.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.3920394778251648, 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(326.14520263671875), np.float64(402.056640625)), (np.float64(326.14520263671875), np.float64(526.2471923828125)), (np.float64(405.620361328125), np.float64(526.2471923828125)), (np.float64(405.620361328125), np.float64(402.056640625))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 115, 'image_path': '/Users/prathod/Projects/Rag_based_q-a_boat_over_own_doc/src/q&a_boat/figures/figure-115-61.jpg', 'file_directory': '/var/folder