equency, which is the frequency of the wanted channel.\n   - The waveforms are also scaled in frequency, as indicated by the factors `(1+a1)`, `(1+a)`, and `(1+a3)`.\n\n4. **Interference Level**:\n   - The ACI level is indicated by the dashed line that intersects the waveforms. The ACI level is measured in dBc and is shown at the rightmost part of the diagram.\n\n5. **Notations**:\n   - The notations `(1+a1)`, `(1+a)`, and `(1+a3)` suggest that these are scaling factors that can vary, possibly depending on the system parameters or the channel conditions.\n\nThis diagram is commonly used in the analysis of interference in communication systems, particularly in the context of digital modulation and the performance of receivers in the presence of adjacent channel interference.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(827.6041666666666), np.float64(1775.5208333333333)), (np.float64(827.6041666666666), np.float64(2774.4791666666665)), (np.float64(2362.5), np.float64(2774.4791666666665)), (np.float64(2362.5), np.float64(1775.5208333333333))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 128, 'image_path': '/Users/prathod/Projects/Rag_based_q-a_boat_over_own_doc/src/q&a_boat/figures/figure-128-71.jpg', 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'category': 'Image', 'element_id': '20912af9e1eff2580537c4d446b690d5', 'source_image': '/Users/prathod/Projects/Rag_based_q-a_boat_over_own_doc/src/q&a_boat/figures/figure-128-71.jpg'}, page_content='[IMAGE DESCRIPTION]\nSource File: /Users/prathod/Projects/Rag_based_q-a_boat_over_own_doc/src/q&a_boat/figures/figure-128-71.jpg\nThe image illustrates a satellite communication system, specifically a DVB-S2 (Digital Video Broadcasting - Satellite Second Generation) network. Here is a detailed description of the image:\n\n1. **Hub/Teleport Location**: At the bottom left of the image, there is a satellite dish labeled "Hub/Teleport Location." This is the central point from which the signal is transmitted.\n\n2. **DVB-S2 Downstream Carrier**: Above the satellite dish, there is a label that reads "DVB-S2 Downstream Carrier." This indicates the type of modulation and coding scheme used for the downstream transmission.\n\n3. **Uplink and Downlink**: Below the satellite dish, there are two labels: "Uplink" and "Downlink." The uplink is the direction from the remote sites to the hub, while the downlink is the direction from the hub to the remote sites.\n\n4. **Broadcast to All Network Remotes**: At the top of the image, there is a label that reads "Broadcast to All Network Remotes." This indicates that the signal from the hub is broadcast to all remote sites.\n\n5. **Remote Sites**: There are five remote sites labeled as Remote A, Remote B, Remote C, Remote D, and Remote E. Each remote site has a satellite dish and a transmission equipment setup, which is connected to the hub via the uplink.\n\n6. **Color Coding**: The image uses different colors to represent the signal paths:\n   - Blue: Represents the uplink signal from the remote sites to the hub.\n   - Yellow: Represents the downlink signal from the hub to the remote sites.\n   - Green, Red, and Blue: These colors represent the broadcast signal to all network remotes, with each color indicating a different remote site.\n\nThe image effectively demonstrates the flow of signals in a satellite communication network, highlighting the uplink and downlink processes and the broadcast to all remote sites.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(590.625), np.float64(729.1666666666666)