ge_path': '/Users/prathod/Projects/Rag_based_q-a_boat_over_own_doc/src/q&a_boat/figures/figure-131-73.jpg', 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'category': 'Image', 'element_id': 'e61b07ea2eebe01b1b43b0b185f6b0db', 'source_image': '/Users/prathod/Projects/Rag_based_q-a_boat_over_own_doc/src/q&a_boat/figures/figure-131-73.jpg'}, page_content='[IMAGE DESCRIPTION]\nSource File: /Users/prathod/Projects/Rag_based_q-a_boat_over_own_doc/src/q&a_boat/figures/figure-131-73.jpg\nThe image is a flowchart illustrating the data transmission process between a Protocol Processor Server and a Satellite Terminal using DVB-S2 (Digital Video Broadcasting - Satellite Second Generation) technology. Here is a detailed description of the components and their interactions:\n\n1. **Protocol Processor Server:**\n   - This is the starting point of the flowchart.\n   - It sends "Data with MODCOD" to the DVB-S2 Tx (Transmitter).\n\n2. **DVB-S2 Tx (Transmitter):**\n   - The data with MODCOD is processed by the DVB-S2 Tx.\n   - The output from the DVB-S2 Tx is labeled as "Downstream DVB-S2 ACM Flow," which is sent to the Satellite Terminal.\n\n3. **Satellite Terminal:**\n   - The Satellite Terminal receives the "Downstream DVB-S2 ACM Flow" and processes it.\n   - The Satellite Terminal then sends "Upstream TDMA Flow" back to the Protocol Processor Server.\n\n4. **Protocol Processor Server (Continued):**\n   - The "Upstream TDMA Flow" is received by the Protocol Processor Server.\n   - The Server also receives "Remote SNR Feedback" from the Satellite Terminal.\n   - The Server processes this feedback and adjusts the "Queue Fullness Throttle" to manage the queue\'s fullness.\n\nThe flowchart uses arrows to indicate the direction of data flow and text boxes to describe the different components and their functions. The colors used are green for data flow, yellow for feedback and control signals, and blue for the main processing components.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(915.1041666666666), np.float64(2132.8125)), (np.float64(915.1041666666666), np.float64(2974.9999999999995)), (np.float64(2275.0), np.float64(2974.9999999999995)), (np.float64(2275.0), np.float64(2132.8125))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 131, 'image_path': '/Users/prathod/Projects/Rag_based_q-a_boat_over_own_doc/src/q&a_boat/figures/figure-131-74.jpg', 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'category': 'Image', 'element_id': '6984d202a8971076fc8c524306f134af', 'source_image': '/Users/prathod/Projects/Rag_based_q-a_boat_over_own_doc/src/q&a_boat/figures/figure-131-74.jpg'}, page_content='[IMAGE DESCRIPTION]\nSource File: /Users/prathod/Projects/Rag_based_q-a_boat_over_own_doc/src/q&a_boat/figures/figure-131-74.jpg\nThe image is a diagram explaining the concept of "Steady State Margin" and "Fast Fade State Margin" in the context of signal-to-noise ratio (SNR) measurements, likely in a communication or satellite system. Here\'s a detailed description:\n\n1. **Steady State Margin (0.5 dB):**\n   - At the top of the image, there is a section labeled "Steady State Margin" with a value of "0.5 dB."\n   - Below this label, there is a bullet point that states: "If two consecutive SNR measurements are more than 0.5 dB apart."\n   - To the right of this text, there is a small icon of a sun with rays extending outward, symbolizing a stable or steady state.\n\n2. **Fast Fade State Margin (0.5 dB + 1.0 dB):**\n   - At the bottom of the image, there is a section labeled "Fast Fade State Margin" with a value of "0.5 dB + 1.0 dB."\n   - Below this label, there is a bullet point that states: "While drop rate higher than 0.3 dB / second."\n   - To the left of this text, there is a diagram of a cloud with rain falling from it, symbolizing a fast fading condition. An arrow is pointing from the cloud to the right, indicating a drop in signal strength.\n   - At the bottom left corner, there is a note stating "Reports: 1 second," indicating that reports are made every second in this state.\n\nThe image uses these visual elements to convey the difference between steady state and fast fade conditions in terms of SNR measurements and the criteria for reporting these conditions.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(590.625), np.float64(2027.0833333333333)), (np.float64(590.625), np.float64(2202.083333333333)), (np.float64(765.6249999999999), np.float64(2202.083333333333)), (np.float64(765.6249999999999), np.float64(2027.0833333333333))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 132, 'image_path': '/Users/prathod/Projects/Rag_based_q-a_boat_over_own_doc/src/q&a_boat/figures/figure-132-75.jpg', 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'category': 'Image', 'element_id': '4c9218d05c5daa4530aa6d7addddaff4', 'source_image': '/Users/prathod/Projects/Rag_based_q-a_boat_over_own_doc/src/q&a_boat/figures/figure-132-75.jpg'}, page_content='[IMAGE DESCRIPTION]\nSource File: /Users/prathod/Projects/Rag_based_q-a_boat_over_own_doc/src/q&a_boat/figures/figure-132-75.jpg\nThe image appears to be a pixelated representation of a blue gift box with a white interior. The box is open, and there is a blue ribbon tied around it, with a small blue bow on top. The ribbon and bow ar