elecommunications or network management system. Here is a detailed description:\n\n1. **Global Bandwidth Pool**: At the top of the diagram, there is a purple box labeled "Global Bandwidth Pool," which serves as the main source of bandwidth.\n\n2. **Unicast BW Partition 1**: Below the "Global Bandwidth Pool," there is a blue box labeled "Unicast BW Partition 1." This partition is further divided into three sub-partitions:\n   - **Unicast BW Partition 1.1**\n   - **Unicast BW Partition 1.2**\n   - **Unicast BW Partition 1.3**\n\n3. **Unicast BW Partition 2**: To the right of "Unicast BW Partition 1," there is another blue box labeled "Unicast BW Partition 2." This partition is divided into two sub-partitions:\n   - **Unicast BW Partition 2.1**\n   - **Unicast BW Partition 2.2**\n\n4. **Multicast BW Partition 3**: To the far right, there is a green box labeled "Multicast BW Partition 3." This partition is divided into one sub-partition:\n   - **Unicast BW Partition 3.1**\n\n5. **Subscriber Service Plans**: Each of the sub-partitions (1.1, 1.2, 1.3, 2.1, 2.2, and 3.1) is further divided into specific subscriber service plans. These are represented by yellow boxes with the following labels:\n   - **Subscriber Service Plan 1.1.1**\n   - **Subscriber Service Plan 1.2.1**\n   - **Subscriber Service Plan 1.2.2**\n   - **Subscriber Service Plan 1.3.1**\n   - **Subscriber Service Plan 2.1**\n   - **Subscriber Service Plan 2.2**\n   - **Subscriber Service Plan 3.1**\n\nThe diagram uses a hierarchical structure to show how bandwidth is allocated from the global pool to specific partitions and then to individual subscriber service plans. The lines connecting the boxes indicate the flow of bandwidth from the global pool to the partitions and then to the service plans.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(590.625), np.float64(2336.9791666666665)), (n