based_q-a_boat_over_own_doc/src/q&a_boat/figures/figure-173-104.jpg'}, page_content='[IMAGE DESCRIPTION]\nSource File: /Users/prathod/Projects/Rag_based_q-a_boat_over_own_doc/src/q&a_boat/figures/figure-173-104.jpg\nThe image is a diagram illustrating the allocation of bandwidth from a "Global Bandwidth Pool" to two different services, GSP1 and GSP2, which are categorized as "Regional" and "Global," respectively. The diagram is divided into two sections, each showing a different scenario.\n\n### Top Section:\n1. **Beam Color Key**:\n   - GSP1 is represented by blue.\n   - GSP2 is represented by yellow.\n   - GSPs 1 & 2 are represented by green.\n\n2. **Scenario Description**:\n   - A satellite is shown transmitting to a ship.\n   - The ship is within the coverage area of both GSP1 and GSP2, as indicated by the overlapping green circles labeled "GSPs 1 & 2."\n   - The blue and yellow circles represent the coverage areas of GSP1 and GSP2, respectively.\n   - The blue and yellow circles overlap, indicating that the ship is within the coverage of both services.\n\n3. **Bandwidth Allocation**:\n   - The Global Bandwidth Pool is shown at the top.\n   - The bandwidth is allocated to GSP1 and GSP2.\n   - GSP1 is labeled as "Regional" and is allocated a portion of the bandwidth.\n   - GSP2 is labeled as "Global" and is allocated a portion of the bandwidth.\n   - The bandwidth is further divided into two sub-pools: SSPC1 and another sub-pool (not labeled).\n\n### Bottom Section:\n1. **Beam Color Key**:\n   - The same color coding is used as in the top section.\n\n2. **Scenario Description**:\n   - The satellite is again shown transmitting to a ship.\n   - The ship is now only within the coverage area of GSP2, as indicated by the overlapping green and yellow circles labeled "GSPs 1 & 2."\n   - The blue circle representing GSP1 is not overlapping with the ship, indicating that the ship is not within the coverage area of GSP1.\n\n3. **Bandwidth Allocation**:\n   - The Global Bandwidth Pool is shown at the top.\n   - The bandwidth is allocated to GSP1 and GSP2.\n   - GSP1 is labeled as "Regional" and is allocated a portion of the bandwidth.\n   - GSP2 is labeled as "Global" and is allocated a portion of the bandwidth.\n   - The bandwidth is further divided into two sub-pools: SSPC1 and another sub-pool (not labeled).\n\n### Key Observations:\n- The top section shows that the ship is within the coverage area of both GSP1 and GSP2, and the bandwidth is allocated to both services.\n- The bottom section shows that the ship is only within the coverage area of GSP2, and the bandwidth is allocated to GSP2.\n\nThis diagram illustrates how the bandwidth is dynamically allocated based on the coverage area of the services.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(568.75), np.float64(936.9791666666666)), (np.float64(568.75), np.float64(2275.0)), (np.float64(2625.0), np.float64(2275.0)), (np.float64(2625.0), np.float64(936.9791666666666))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 177, 'image_path': '/Users/prathod/Projects/Rag_based_q-a_boat_over_own_doc/src/q&a_boat/figures/figure-177-105.jpg', 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'category': 'Image', 'element_id': '5a5e362794b95b2e2a8b08da56e3317d', 'source_image': '/Users/prathod/Projects/Rag_based_q-a_boat_over_own_doc/src/q&a_boat/figures/figure-177-105.jpg'}, page_content='[IMAGE DESCRIPTION]\nSource File: /Users/prathod/Projects/Rag_based_q-a_boat_over_own_doc/src/q&a_boat/figures/figure-177-105.jpg\nThe image is a detailed diagram illustrating the structure of a GBWM (Geographic Bandwidth Weighted Multicast) tree, which is used in network