h': '/Users/prathod/Projects/Rag_based_q-a_boat_over_own_doc/src/q&a_boat/figures/figure-202-127.jpg', 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'category': 'Image', 'element_id': 'f025dd515e6583423cd80d3131654e42', 'source_image': '/Users/prathod/Projects/Rag_based_q-a_boat_over_own_doc/src/q&a_boat/figures/figure-202-127.jpg'}, page_content='[IMAGE DESCRIPTION]\nSource File: /Users/prathod/Projects/Rag_based_q-a_boat_over_own_doc/src/q&a_boat/figures/figure-202-127.jpg\nThe image is a diagram explaining the allocation of symbols to GSP (Generic Service Profile) nodes in a network, with a focus on bandwidth fairness. Here is a detailed description:\n\n### Diagram Structure:\n1. **Main Node: GSP**\n   - At the top of the diagram, there is a central node labeled "GSP."\n   - An arrow points from the top of the diagram to the "GSP" node, indicating the allocation of resources to this node.\n\n2. **Allocation to GSP:**\n   - The text "Allocation: 100 KSymbols" is written next to the arrow pointing to the "GSP" node, indicating that 100 KSymbols are allocated to the GSP.\n\n3. **Child Nodes:**\n   - Two child nodes are connected to the "GSP" node:\n     - **GSP-A**\n     - **GSP-B**\n\n4. **Allocation to Child Nodes:**\n   - Each child node has an arrow pointing to it with the text "Allocation 50 KSymbols," indicating that 50 KSymbols are allocated to each child node.\n\n### Textual Information:\n- **GSP Allocation Fairness = Bandwidth Fairness (default):**\n  - This statement indicates that the default configuration ensures bandwidth fairness.\n\n- **Configuration:**\n  - **GSP-A and GSP-B are equal in priority/cost, but with different nominal MODCODs:**\n    - This means that both GSP-A and GSP-B have the same priority and cost, but they use different modulation and coding schemes (MODCODs).\n  - **GSP-B has a higher CIR = 9 Mbps:**\n    - The CIR (Committed Information Rate) for GSP-B is 9 Mbps, which is higher than GSP-A\'s CIR.\n  - **Allocation = 100 KSymbols (100 ms allocation period):**\n    - The total allocation period is 100 milliseconds, and the total allocation is 100 KSymbols.\n\n### Result:\n- **Symbols allocated to the GSP are allocated equally between child nodes (of equal cost, priority):**\n  - This result indicates that the 100 KSymbols allocated to the GSP are divided equally between GSP-A and GSP-B, despite their different CIRs and MODCODs.\n\n### Additional Information:\n- **GSP-A:**\n  - CIR = 3 Mbps\n  - Nominal MODCOD = 16PSK 8/9\n- **GSP-B:**\n  - CIR = 9 Mbps\n  - Nominal MODCOD = 8PSK 3/4\n\nThis diagram illustrates how bandwidth is allocated in a network where the GSP is the root node, and its resources are divided equally between two child nodes, GSP-A and GSP-B, despite their different CIRs and MODCODs.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(590.625), np.float64(813.0208333333333)), (np.float64(590.625), np.float64(988.0208333333333)), (np.float64(765.6249999999999), np.float64(988.0208333333333)), (np.float64(765.6249999999999), np.float64(813.0208333333333))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 203, 'image_path': '/Users/prathod/Projects/Rag_based_q-a_boat_over_own_doc/src/q&a_boat/figures/figure-203-128.jpg', 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'category': 'Image', 'element_id': '7dae09e44930e300568f94c6f32a661c', 'source_image': '/Users/prathod/Projects/Rag_based_q-a_boat_over_own_doc/src/q&a_boat/figures/figure-203-128.jpg'}, page_content='[IMAGE DESCRIPTION]\nSource File: /Users/prathod/Projects/Rag_based_q-a_boat_over_own_doc/src/q&a_boat/figures/figure-203-128.jpg\nThe image appears to be a pixelated representation of a blue gift box with a white interior. The box is open, and there is a blue ribbon tied around it, with a small blue bow on top. The ribbon and bow are also pixelated, maintaining the same blue color scheme as the box. There is no text, numbers, charts, or diagrams visible in the image. The overall design is simple and minimalistic, with a focus on the blue color and the shape of the gift box.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(568.75), np.float64(1378.125)), (np.float64(568.75), np.float64(2143.75)), (np.float64(2625.0), np.float64(2143.75)), (np.float64(2625.0), np.float64(1378.125))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 203, 'image_path': '/Users/prathod/Projects/Rag_based_q-a_boat_over_own_doc/src/q&a_boat/figures/figure-203-129.jpg', 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'category': 'Image', 'element_id': 'b03b8d3dcfd34768079f5fab7c7b5710', 'source_image': '/Users/prathod/Projects/Rag_based_q-a_boat_over_own_doc/src/q&a_boat/figures/figure-203-129.jpg'}, page_content='[IMAGE DESCRIPTION]\nSource File: /Users/prathod/Projects/Rag_based_q-a_boat_over_own_doc/src/q&a_boat/figures/figure-203-129.jpg\nThe image is a diagram explaining the concept of GSP (Generalized Scheduling Policy) allocation fairness in the context of bandwidth management. Here is a detailed description:\n\n### Title:\n- The title at the top right corner reads: "GSP Allocation Fairness = Bandwidth Fairness."\n\n### Configuration:\n- The configuration details are listed on the right side of the image:\n  - SSPC-A and SSPC-B are equal in priority/cost but have different base MODCODs.\n  - GSP-B has a higher CIR (Committed Information Rate) than GSP-A (3 Mbps vs 9 Mbps).\n  - The allocation is 100 symbols over a 100 ms allocation period.\n\n### Diagram:\n- The diagram is divided into two main sections:\n  1. **GSP (Generalized Scheduling Policy)**\n  2. **SSPC-A and SSPC-B**\n\n#### GSP:\n- The GSP is at the top of the diagram.\n- It allocates 100 symbols to SSPC-A and SSPC-B.\n\n#### SSPC-A and SSPC-B:\n- Each section represents a sub-system (SSPC-A and SSPC-B) receiving an allocation.\n- Both SSPC-A and SSPC-B receive 50 symbols each.\n\n#### Details for SSPC-A:\n- **CIR = 3 Mbps**\n- **Operating MODCOD = 8PSK 3/4**\n- **Effective bandwidth delivered: 1.025 Mbps**\n\n#### Details for SSPC-B:\n- **CIR = 9 Mbps**\n- **Operating MODCOD = QPSK 3/4**\n- **Effective bandwidth delivered: 0.685 Mbps**\n\n### Result:\n- The text on the right side states: "Equal allocation of symbols to SSPC-A and SSPC-B resulting in a lower effective allocation to SSPC-B."\n- The effective bandwidth allocations are calculated as follows:\n  - **SSPC-A @ 8PSK 3/4:** \\((50/100 \\text{ ms}) \\times (2.05) = 1.025 \\text{ Mbps}\\)\n  - **SSPC-B @ QPSK 3/4:** \\((50/100 \\text{ ms}) \\times (1.37) = 0.685 \\text{ Mbps}\\)\n\n### Summary:\n- The diagram illustrates how the GSP allocates 100 symbols to SSPC-A and SSPC-B, resulting in different effective bandwidths due to their different CIRs and MODCODs. Despite the equal allocation of symbols, the effective bandwidth delivered to SSPC-B is lower than that of SSPC-A, demonstrating the concept of bandwidth fairness in GSP allocation.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(590.625), np.float64(2304.1666666666665)), (np.float64(590.625), np.float64(2479.1666666666665)), (np.float64(765.6249999999999), np.float64(2479.1666666666665)), (np.float64(765.6249999999999), np.float64(2304.1666666666665))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 203, 'image_path': '/Users/prathod/Projects/Rag_based_q-a_boat_over_own_doc/src/q&a_boat/figures/figure-203-130.jpg', 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'category': 'Image', 'element_id': 'fb789fa0f4ef2e50e854ae6e4ce78141', 'source_image': '/Users/prathod/Projects/Rag_based_q-a_boat_over_own_doc/src/q&a_boat/figures/figure-203-130.jpg'}, page_content='[IMAGE DESCRIPTION]\nSource File: /Users/prathod/Projects/Rag_based_q-a_boat_over_own_doc/src/q&a_boat/figures/figure-203-130.jpg\nThe image appears to be a pixelated representation of a blue gift box with a white interior. The box is open, and there is a blue ribbon tied around it, with a small blue bow on top. The ribbon and bow are also pixelated, maintaining the same blue color scheme as the box. There is no text, numbers, charts, or diagrams visible in the image. The overall design is simple and minimalistic, with a focus on the blue color and the shape of the gift box.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(568.75), np.float64(430.2083333333333)), (np.float64(568.75), np.float64(1188.5416666666665)), (np.float64(2625.0), np.float64(1188.5416666666665)), (np.float64(2625.0), np.float64(430.2083333333333))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 204, 'image_path': '/Users/prathod/Projects/Rag_based_q-a_boat_over_own_doc/src/q&a_boat/figures/figure-204-131.jpg', 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'category': 'Image', 'element_id': '6da3026d26094101f0faa095eebf3b07', 'source_image': '/Users/prathod/Projects/Rag_based_q-a_boat_over_own_doc/src/q&a_boat/figures/figure-204-131.jpg'}, page_content='[IMAGE DESCRIPTION]\nSource File: /Users/prathod/Projects/Rag_based_q-a_boat_over_own_doc/src/q&a_boat/figures/figure-204-131.jpg\nThe image is a diagram illustrating the allocation of bandwidth in a network using the concept of Guaranteed Service Points (GSPs). Here is a detailed description:\n\n1. **Title and Main Elements**:\n   - The diagram is titled "GSP Allocation Fairness = CIR Fairness."\n   - It shows a hierarchical structure with a parent GSP and two child GSPs (GSP-A and GSP-B).\n\n2. **Parent GSP**:\n   - The parent GSP is at the top of the diagram.\n   - It has an allocation of 8 Mbps.\n\n3. **Child GSPs**:\n   - **GSP-A** is on the left side.\n   - **GSP-B** is on the right side.\n   - Both GSPs have an allocation of 2 Mbps and 6 Mbps, respectively.\n\n4. **Configuration Details**:\n   - The configuration states that GSP-A and GSP-B are equal in priority/cost and nominal MODCOD.\n   - GSP-B has a higher CIR (Committed Information Rate) of 9 Mbps.\n\n5. **Result**:\n   - The allocation to the parent GSP is divided according to the ratio of the CIRs of the child GSPs.\n\n6. **Specific Values**:\n   - GSP-A has a CIR of 3 Mbps and a nominal MODCOD of 16PSK 8/9.\n   - GSP-B has a CIR of 9 Mbps and a nominal MODCOD of 16PSK 8/9.\n\nThe diagram visually represents the allocation process where the parent GSP divides its bandwidth based on the CIRs of its child GSPs, ensuring fairness in bandwidth distribution.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(590.625), np.float64(1381.7708333333333)), (np.float64(590.625), np.float64(1556.7708333333333)), (np.float64(765.6249999999999), np.float64(1556.7708333333333)), (np.float64(765.6249999999999), np.float64(1381.7708333333333))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 204, 'image_path': '/Users/prathod/Projects/Rag_based_q-a_boat_over_own_doc/src/q&a_boat/figures/figure-204-132.jpg', 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'category': 'Image', 'element_id': '31e0a2c108e1116ca8461a542d65011a', 'source_image': '/Users/prathod/Projects/Rag_based_q-a_boat_over_own_doc/src/q&a_boat/figures/figure-204-132.jpg'}, page_content='[IMAGE DESCRIPTION]\nSource File: /Users/prathod/Projects/Rag_based_q-a_boat_over_own_doc/src/q&a_boat/figures/figure-204-132.jpg\nThe image appears to be a pixelated representation of a blue rectangular shape with a white interior. The edges of the rectangle are jagged, indicating that the image is low-resolution or has been pixelated. There is no text, numbers, charts, or diagrams visible within the rectangle. The overall appearance suggests that this might be a simplified or abstract representation of a shape, possibly a gift box or a similar object, given the shape and the way it is presented. The blue color could represent a ribbon or a bow, which is often associated with gift wrapping.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(656.25), np.float64(2227.6041666666665)), (np.float64(656.25), np.float64(2920.3124999999995)), (np.float64(2533.8541666666665), np.float64(2920.3124999999995)), (np.float64(2533.8541666666665), np.float64(2227.6041666666665))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 204, 'image_path': '/Users/prathod/Projects/Rag_based_q-a_boat_over_own_doc/src/q&a_boat/figures/figure-204-133.jpg', 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'category': 'Image', 'element_id': '9b0770cd8bf85889fef448a9e83839bf', 'source_image': '/Users/prathod/Projects/Rag_based_q-a_boat_over_own_doc/src/q&a_boat/figures/figure-204-133.jpg'}, page_content='[IMAGE DESCRIPTION]\nSource File: /Users/prathod/Projects/Rag_based_q-a_boat_over_own_doc/src/q&a_boat/figures/figure-204-133.jpg\nThe image is a flowchart explaining the process of GSP (Guaranteed Service Profile) allocation fairness in a network system. Here is a detailed description:\n\n1. **Title and Main Components:**\n   - The flowchart is titled "GSP Allocation Fairness."\n   - It explains the allocation process relative to CIR (Committed Information Rate) in the CIR round and relative to MIR (Maximum Information Rate) in the MIR round.\n   - It mentions that GSP-A and GSP-B are equal in priority and cost, but have different combinations of CIR and MIR.\n\n2. **Allocation Process:**\n   - The total allocation is 12 Mb/s.\n   - The system first allocates based on CIR in the CIR round.\n   - The remaining allocation is then used to satisfy the MIR demand in the MIR round.\n\n3. **Details of GSP-A and GSP-B:**\n   - **GSP-A:**\n     - CIR = 3 Mb/s\n     - MIR = 6 Mb/s\n   - **GSP-B:**\n     - CIR = 6 Mb/s\n     - MIR = 9 Mb/s\n\n4. **Allocation Steps:**\n   - **CIR Round:**\n     - The total demand of GSP-A and GSP-B in the CIR round is 9 Mb/s.\n     - The allocation is 12 Mb/s, which is sufficient to satisfy the CIR demand.\n     - The remaining capacity is 12 - (6 + 3) = 3 Mb/s.\n\n   - **MIR Round:**\n     - The total remaining MIR demand is 15 - 9 = 6 Mb/s.\n     - The allocation is based on the MIR ratio.\n     - GSP-A will get an additional allocation of 6/15 * 3 = 1.2 Mb/s.\n     - GSP-B will get an additional allocation of 9/15 * 3 = 1.8 Mb/s.\n     - Therefore, the total allocation for GSP-A is 1.2 + 3 = 4.2 Mb/s.\n     - The total allocation for GSP-B is 1.8 + 6 = 7.8 Mb/s.\n\n5. **Conclusion:**\n   - The MIR allocation is based on the MIR and not the CIR ratios.\n   - The allocation is fair as it considers both CIR and MIR demands.\n\nThis flowchart illustrates how the system ensures that both GSP-A and GSP-B receive their guaranteed service profiles based on their CIR and MIR demands, ensuring fairness in the allocation process.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(568.75), np.float64(2034.3749999999998)), (np.float64(568.75), np.float64(2945.833333333333)), (np.float64(2625.0), np.float64(2945.833333333333)), (np.float64(2625.0), np.float64(2034.3749999999998))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 205, 'image_path': '/Users/prathod/Projects/Rag_based_q-a_boat_over_own_doc/src/q&a_boat/figures/figure-205-134.jpg', 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'category': 'Image', 'element_id': 'fc7cf67368c8b7ebbd52a62d28b13944', 'source_image': '/Users/prathod/Projects/Rag_based_q-a_boat_over_own_doc/src/q&a_boat/figures/figure-205-134.jpg'}, page_content='[IMAGE DESCRIPTION]\nSource File: /Users/prathod/Projects/Rag_based_q-a_boat_over_own_doc/src/q&a_boat/figures/figure-205-134.jpg\nThe image is a detailed diagram explaining the process of GSP (Generalized Scheduling Policy) allocation fairness in a communication system, specifically focusing on the allocation of symbols to SSPCs (Subscribers\' Service Partitions) based on their base MODCOD (Modulation and Coding Scheme) configurations.\n\n### Key Elements in the Image:\n\n1. **Title and Main Concept:**\n   - The title at the top right reads: "GSP Allocation Fairness = Base MODCOD."\n   - It explains that the allocation of symbols to the GSP (Generalized Scheduling Policy) is based on the base MODCOD configuration of the SSPCs (Subscribers\' Service Partitions).\n\n2. **Configuration:**\n   - The configuration states that the SSPCs for Terminal-A and Terminal-B are equal in priority/cost.\n   - The allocation is 100 KSymbols (in a 100-ms allocation period).\n\n3. **Result:**\n   - The symbols allocated to the GSP are divided according to the base MODCOD configuration of the two SSPCs.\n\n4. **SSPC-A and SSPC-B Details:**\n   - **SSPC-A on Terminal-A:**\n     - CIR (Committed Information Rate) = 3 Mbps.\n     - Base MODCOD = 8PSK 3/4.\n     - Operational MODCOD = 8PSK 3/4.\n     - Effective CIR delivered = 820 Kbps.\n     - Allocation = 40 KSymbols.\n   - **SSPC-B on Terminal-B:**\n     - CIR (Committed Information Rate) = 3 Mbps.\n     - Base MODCOD = QPSK 3/4.\n     - Operational MODCOD = 8PSK 3/5.\n     - Effective CIR delivered = 822 Kbps.\n     - Allocation = 60 KSymbols.\n\n5. **Calculation of Effective Allocations:**\n   - **SSPC-A:**\n     - Internal cost for 8PSK 3/4 = 0.617.\n     - Allocation = 1.62/(1.62+2.42) * 100 = 40 KSymbols.\n   - **SSPC-B:**\n     - Internal cost for QPSK 3/4 = 0.413.\n     - Allocation = 2.42/(1.62+2.42) * 100 = 60 KSymbols.\n\n6. **Effective Allocations:**\n   - SSPC-A @ 8PSK 3/4: (40 KSymbols/100 ms) * (2.05) = 820 Kbps.\n   - SSPC-B @ QPSK 3/4: (60 KSymbols/100 ms) * (1.37) = 822 Kbps.\n\n### Diagram:\n- The diagram shows a flowchart with the following steps:\n  - **GSP (Generalized Scheduling Policy):** Receives an allocation of 100 KSymbols.\n  - **SSPC-A on Terminal-A:** Receives an allocation of 40 KSymbols.\n  - **SSPC-B on Terminal-B:** Receives an allocation of 60 KSymbols.\n\n### Summary:\nThe image illustrates how the GSP allocates symbols to SSPCs based on their base MODCOD configurations, ensuring fairness in the allocation process. The allocation is calculated using the internal costs of the MODCODs, and the effective CIR delivered to each terminal is determined by the allocation and the operational MODCOD.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(590.625), np.float64(3106.2499999999995)), (np.float64(590.625), np.float64(3281.2499999999995)), (np.float64(765.6249999999999), np.float64(3281.2499999999995)), (np.float64(765.6249999999999), np.float64(3106.2499999999995))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 205, 'image_path': '/Users/prathod/Projects/Rag_based_q-a_boat_over_own_doc/src/q&a_boat/figures/figure-205-135.jpg', 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'category': 'Image', 'element_id': 'fed080b5c0bdba6d0fa4d6e9b2afa5b2', 'source_image': '/Users/prathod/Projects/Rag_based_q-a_boat_over_own_doc/src/q&a_boat/figures/figure-205-135.jpg'}, page_content='[IMAGE DESCRIPTION]\nSource File: /Users/prathod/Projects/Rag_based_q-a_boat_over_own_doc/src/q&a_boat/figures/figure-205-135.jpg\nThe image appears to be a pixelated representation of a blue gift box with a white interior. The box is open, and there is a blue ribbon tied around it, with a small blue bow on top. The ribbon and bow are also pixelated, maintaining the same blue color scheme as the box. There is no text, numbers, charts, or diagrams visible in the image. The overall design is simple and minimalistic, with a focus on the blue color and the shape of the gift box.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(568.75), np.float64(1895.8333333333333)), (np.float64(568.75), np.float64(2847.395833333333)), (np.float64(2625.0), np.float64(2847.395833333333)), (np.float64(2625.0), np.float64(1895.8333333333333))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 206, 'image_path': '/Users/prathod/Projects/Rag_based_q-a_boat_over_own_doc/src/q&a_boat/figures/figure-206-136.jpg', 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'category': 'Image', 'element_id': 'da3c64597552203808486434b5047484', 'source_image': '/Users/prathod/Projects/Rag_based_q-a_boat_over_own_doc/src/q&a_boat/figures/figure-206-136.jpg'}, page_content='[IMAGE DESCRIPTION]\nSource File: /Users/prathod/Projects/Rag_based_q-a_boat_over_own_doc/src/q&a_boat/figures/figure-206-136.jpg\nThe image is a flowchart and text-based diagram explaining the process of GSP (Generalized Symbol Pool) allocation fairness in a communication system, specifically in the context of a system with two SSPCs (Symbol Signaling Point Codes) for Terminal-A and Terminal-B. The diagram is divided into several sections, each explaining a step in the allocation process.\n\n### Flowchart Section:\n1. **GSP Allocation:**\n   - The diagram starts with a box labeled "GSP" which is the Generalized Symbol Pool.\n   - An arrow points from the "GSP" box to two other boxes labeled "SSPC on Terminal-A" and "SSPC on Terminal-B," indicating that the GSP is divided into these two parts.\n   - Each of these boxes has an allocation value:\n     - "SSPC on Terminal-A" is allocated 44.75 KSymbols.\n     - "SSPC on Terminal-B" is allocated 55.25 KSymbols.\n   - The total allocation is 100 KSymbols.\n\n2. **SSPC on Terminal-A:**\n   - The box for Terminal-A has the following details:\n     - CIR (Committed Information Rate) = 3 Mbps.\n     - Base MODCOD (Modulation and Coding Scheme) = 8PSK 3/4.\n     - Oper. MODCOD (Operating MODCOD) = 8PSK 3/4.\n     - Effective CIR delivered = 918 kbps.\n   - The allocation for Terminal-A is 44.75 KSymbols.\n\n3. **SSPC on Terminal-B:**\n   - The box for Terminal-B has the following details:\n     - CIR (Committed Information Rate) = 3 Mbps.\n     - Base MODCOD (Modulation and Coding Scheme) = QPSK 3/4.\n     - Oper. MODCOD (Operating MODCOD) = 8PSK 3/5.\n     - Effective CIR delivered = 920 kbps.\n   - The allocation for Terminal-B is 55.25 KSymbols.\n\n### Textual Section:\n- **GSP Allocation Fairness = Operating MODCOD**\n- **Configuration:**\n  - SSPCs for Terminal-A and Terminal-B are equal in priority/cost.\n  - Allocation = 100 KSymbols (in 100-ms allocation period).\n- **Result:**\n  - Symbols allocated to GSP are divided according to the base MODCOD configuration of the two SSPCs.\n- **SSPC-A:**\n  - Internal cost for 8PSK 3/4 = 0.617, (1/0.617 = 1.62).\n  - Allocation = 1.62/(1.62+2.0) * 100 = 44.75 KSymbols.\n- **SSPC-B:**\n  - Internal cost for 8PSK 3/5 = 0.501, (1/0.501 = 2.0).\n  - Allocation = 2.0/(1.62+2.0) * 100 = 55.25 KSymbols.\n- **Effective allocations:**\n  - SSPC-A @ 8PSK 3/4: 44.8 Ksymbols * (2.05) = 918 kbps.\n  - SSPC-B @ 8PSK 3/5: 55.1 Ksymbols * (1.67) = 920 kbps.\n\n### Summary:\nThe diagram illustrates how the GSP is divided between two SSPCs based on their operating MODCODs and internal costs. The allocation is calculated to ensure fairness, with Terminal-B receiving a slightly higher allocation due to its lower internal cost for the 8PSK 3/5 MODCOD. The effective CIR delivered to each terminal is calculated based on the allocation and the operating MODCOD.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(568.75), np.float64(430.2083333333333)), (np.float64(568.75), np.float64(3018.7499999999995