e: /Users/prathod/Projects/Rag_based_q-a_boat_over_own_doc/src/q&a_boat/figures/figure-217-143.jpg\nThe image is a detailed diagram of a satellite communication system, specifically a dual-site setup with diversity for redundancy. Here is a breakdown of the components and their connections:\n\n1. **Satellite**: At the top right, there is a satellite with two beams labeled as \\( t_1, \\text{fade}_1 \\) and \\( t_2, \\text{fade}_2 \\). These labels indicate the time and fade conditions for the respective beams.\n\n2. **Diversity Site**:\n   - **GPS PPS**: A GPS and PPS (Precision Pulse Signal) receiver is shown, which provides precise timing and synchronization.\n   - **PP**: Likely a power amplifier or preamplifier.\n   - **Switch**: A switch is used to route signals.\n   - **Upstream Router**: This router connects the diversity site to the primary site.\n   - **RCM**: Radio Control Module.\n   - **Linecards**: These are line cards that handle the transmission (Tx) and reception (Rx) of signals. There are two sets of linecards, one for IF Domain A and one for IF Domain B, as indicated by the color coding in the legend.\n   - **IF Connections**: These are the interfaces for the intermediate frequency (IF) signals.\n\n3. **Primary Site**:\n   - **GPS PPS**: Similar to the diversity site, this provides GPS and PPS signals.\n   - **PP**: Likely a power amplifier or preamplifier.\n   - **Switch**: A switch is used to route signals.\n   - **Upstream Router**: This router connects the primary site to the backbone network.\n  '), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(590.625), np.float64(2362.5)), (np.float64(590.625), np.float64(2537.5)), (np.float64(765.6249999999999), np.float64(2537.5)), (np.float64(765.6249999999999), np.float64(2362.5))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 217, 'image_path': '/Users/prathod/Projects/Rag_based_q-a_boat_over_own_doc/src/q&a_boat/figures/figure-217-144.jpg', 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'category': 'Image', 'element_id': 'aa1b7c642adbfc529aa8cd17f9184949', 'source_image': '/Users/prathod/Projects/Rag_based_q-a_boat_over_own_doc/src/q&a_boat/figures/figure-217-144.jpg'}, page_content='[IMAGE DESCRIPTION]\nSource File: /Users/prathod/Projects/Rag_based_q-a_boat_over_own_doc/src/q&a_boat/figures/figure-217-144.jpg\nThe image is a simple, pixelated illustration of a shopping bag. The bag is predominantly white with a blue outline and a blue handle. There is a small blue flower or leaf design on the top right corner of the bag. The background is plain white, and there are two horizontal blue lines at the top and bottom of the image, framing the bag. There is no text, numbers, charts, or diagrams present in the image.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(568.75), np.float64(430.2083333333333)), (np.float64(568.75), np.float64(1724.4791666666665)), (np.float64(2625.0), np.float64(1724.4791666666665)), (np.float64(2625.0), np.float64(430.2083333333333))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 218, 'image_path': '/Users/prathod/Projects/Rag_based_q-a_boat_over_own_doc/src/q&a_boat/figures/figure-218-145.jpg', 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'category': 'Image', 'element_id': '5a62e74653ecae0e03666a2b2e28c7a9', 'source_image': '/Users/prathod/Projects/Rag_based_q-a_boat_over_own_doc/src/q&a_boat/figures/figure-218-145.jpg'}, page_content='[IMAGE DESCRIPTION]\nSource File: /Users/prathod/Projects/Rag_based_q-a_boat_over_own_doc/src/q&a_boat/figures/figure-218-145.jpg\nThe image is a detailed diagram illustrating a satellite communication system, specifically focusing on the transmission and reception of signals between a satellite, a primary site, a diversity site, and a user terminal. Here is a breakdown of the components and their interconnections:\n\n### Components and Labels:\n1. **Satellite**: At the top right, there is a satellite depicted with multiple antennas. Signals are shown being transmitted and received from this satellite.\n2. **User Terminal**: Below the satellite, there are two user terminals, each with an antenna, indicating the reception of signals from the satellite.\n3. **Primary Site**: Located in the lower middle section, this site includes:\n   - **GPS PPS**: A GPS receiver providing precise time and position data.\n   - **Upstream Router**: A router used for upstream communication.\n   - **Switch**: A network switch used for managing data flow.\n   - **RCM (Radio Communication Module)**: A module responsible for radio communication.\n   - **Linecards**: These are likely used for signal processing and transmission/reception.\n   - **IF Domain A and B**: These represent different frequency domains for signal transmission and reception.\n   - **IF Connections**: The connections between the RCM and the linecards.\n   - **RFSI Interface**: This interface is used for real-time signal information (t1, t2, fade1, fade2).\n   - **3rd Party Range Measurement**: This is a measurement tool used to assess the range of the signals.\n4. **Diversity Site**: Located in the upper middle section, this site includes:\n   - **GPS PPS**: Similar to the primary site, this site also has a GPS receiver.\n   - **Upstream Router**: A router used for upstream communication.\n   - **Switch**: A network switch used for managing data flow.\n   - **RCM (Radio Communication Module)**: A module responsible for radio communication.\n   - **Linecards**: These are likely used for signal processing and transmission/reception.\n   - **IF Domain A and B**: These represent different frequency domains for signal transmission and reception.\n   - **IF Connections**: The connections between the RCM and the linecards.\n   - **Modulated Signals**: These are the signals being transmitted and received by the satellite.\n\n### Connections and Signals:\n- **Modulated Signals**: Green arrows represent modulated signals being transmitted from the satellite to the user terminals.\n- **IF Domain A and B**: Red and blue arrows represent the transmission and reception of signals in different frequency domains.\n- **Plain IP**: Purple arrows represent plain IP data being transmitted from the web server to the primary site.\n- **Tunnel**: Brown arrows represent tunneling of data, likely for secure or specific network paths.\n- **GPS PPS**: Black arrows represent the transmission of GPS time and position data.\n- **RFSI Interface**: The interface is used for real-time signal information (t1, t2, fade1, fade2), which is shown as a connection between the primary site and the diversity site.\n\n### Key:\n- **IF Domain A**: Red arrows.\n- **IF Domain B**: Blue arrows.\n- **Plain IP**: Purple arrows.\n- **Tunnel**: Brown arrows.\n- **Modulated Signals**: Green arrows.\n\n### Summary:\nThe diagram illustrates a satellite communication system where signals are transmitted and received between a satellite, a primary site, a diversity site, and user terminals. The system'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(568.75), np.float64(528.6458333333333)), (np.float64(568.75), np.float64(1811.9791666666665)), (np.float64(2625.0), np.float64(1811.9791666666665)), (np.float64(2625.0), np.float64(528.6458333333333))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 219, 'image_path': '/Users/prathod/Projects/Rag_based_q-a_boat_over_own_doc/src/q&a_boat/figures/figure-219-146.jpg', 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'category': 'Image', 'element_id': '6ea26e343a90b6040261b3c3529f5692', 'source_image': '/Users/prathod/Projects/Rag_based_q-a_boat_over_own_doc/src/q&a_boat/figures/figure-219-146.jpg'}, page_content='[IMAGE DESCRIPTION]\nSource File: /Users/prathod/Projects/Rag_based_q-a_boat_over_own_doc/src/q&a_boat/figures/figure-219-146.jpg\nThe image is a detailed diagram illustrating a satellite communication system, specifically focusing on the transmission and reception of signals between a web server, a satellite, and user terminals. Here is a breakdown of the components and their interconnections:\n\n### Components and Labels:\n1. **Web Server**: Located on the left side of the diagram, it is connected to the "Backbone Network" via a purple line labeled "Plain IP."\n2. **Backbone Network**: This is the main network infrastructure that connects the web server to the primary and diversity sites.\n3. **Primary Site**:\n   - **Upstream Router**: This device is connected to the "Backbone Network" and the "Switch."\n   - **Switch**: Connected to the "Upstream Router" and the "Linecards."\n   - **Linecards**: These are connected to the "RCM" (Radio Control Module) and the "IF connections" (Intermediate Frequency connections). The "IF connections" are further divided into "IF Domain A" and "IF Domain B," with "IF Domain A" being red and "IF Domain B" being blue.\n   - **GPS PPS**: Positioned above the "Primary Site," it is connected to the "Switch."\n   - **3rd Party Range Measurement**: Located below the "Primary Site," it is connected to the "Switch" and the "Linecards."\n4. **Diversity Site**:\n   - **Upstream Router**: Similar to the "Primary Site," it is connected to the "Switch."\n   - **Switch**: Connected to the "Upstream Router" and the "Linecards."\n   - **Linecards**: These are connected to the "RCM" and the "IF connections." The "IF connections" are also divided into "IF Domain A" and "IF Domain B," with "IF Domain A" being red and "IF Domain B" being blue.\n   - **GPS PPS**: Positioned above the "Diversity Site," it is connected to the "Switch."\n5. **Satellite**:\n   - **Satellite Antenna**: Located at the top right of the diagram, it is connected to the "IF connections" from both the "Primary Site" and the "Diversity Site."\n   - **IF connections**: These are divided into "IF Domain A" and "IF Domain B," with "IF Domain A" being red and "IF Domain B" being blue.\n   - **Modulated Signals**: Green arrows indicate the transmission of modulated signals from the "Primary Site" and the "Diversity Site" to the "Satellite."\n   - **Fade**: The diagram includes "t1, fade1" and "t2, fade2," which likely represent time delays and signal fading effects.\n6. **User Terminal**:\n   - **User Terminal Antenna**: Located on the right side of the diagram, it receives the modulated signals from the "Satellite."\n   - **User Terminal**: This is the final destination of the modulated signals.\n\n### Key:\n- **IF Domain A**: Red\n- **IF Domain B**: Blue\n- **Plain IP**: Purple\n- **Tunnel**: Brown\n- **Modulated Signals**: Green\n\n### Summary:\nThe diagram illustrates the flow of data from a web server through a backbone network to a satellite, which then transmits the data to user terminals. The system includes redundancy with a "Diversity Site" to'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(590.625), np.float64(2005.2083333333333)), (np.float64(590.625), np.float64(2180.208333333333)), (np.float