p80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'category': 'Image', 'element_id': '9d25e3484bf6b1e69f3faa218ab87d62', 'source_image': '/Users/prathod/Projects/Rag_based_q-a_boat_over_own_doc/src/q&a_boat/figures/figure-227-156.jpg'}, page_content='[IMAGE DESCRIPTION]\nSource File: /Users/prathod/Projects/Rag_based_q-a_boat_over_own_doc/src/q&a_boat/figures/figure-227-156.jpg\nThe image is a diagram illustrating a network architecture, specifically a redundant network setup. Here is a detailed description:\n\n1. **Primary NOC (Network Operations Center)**:\n   - Located at the top left of the diagram.\n   - Connected to the backbone network via a thick line.\n\n2. **Backbone Network**:\n   - Represented by a cloud-like shape in the center of the diagram.\n   - The cloud is connected to multiple buildings, indicating the backbone network\'s role in connecting various parts of the network.\n\n3. **Buildings and Their Roles**:\n   - **Primary SAS 1**: Located below the Primary NOC. It is marked with a red "X," indicating it is not active. It is connected to the Backup/Diversity SAS 1.\n   - **Primary SAS 2**: Located below the backbone network. It is active, as indicated by the blue color.\n   - **Primary SAS 3**: Located below the backbone network. It is active, as indicated by the blue color.\n   - **Backup/Diversity SAS 1**: Located below the Primary SAS 1. It is active, as indicated by the blue color.\n   - **Backup/Diversity SAS 2**: Located below the Primary SAS 2. It is active, as indicated by the blue color.\n   - **Backup/Diversity SAS 3**: Located below the Primary SAS 3. It is active, as indicated by the blue color.\n\n4. **Key Legend**:\n   - Located at the top right of the diagram.\n   - It shows two icons: one blue and one gray.\n   - The blue icon is labeled "active," and the gray icon is labeled "standby."\n\n5. **Text Labels**:\n   - The diagram includes labels for each building and its role, such as "Primary NOC," "Backbone Network," "Primary SAS 1," "Primary SAS 2," "Primary SAS 3," "Backup/Diversity SAS 1," "Backup/Diversity SAS 2," and "Backup/Diversity SAS 3."\n\nThis diagram illustrates a network architecture where the Primary NOC is connected to a backbone network, which in turn connects to multiple sites (SAS 1, SAS 2, SAS 3) that are either primary or backup/diversity. The red "X" on Primary SAS 1 indicates it is not active, while the other sites are active. The key legend helps to distinguish between active and standby systems.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(568.75), np.float64(1997.9166666666665)), (np.float64(568.75), np.float64(2555.7291666666665)), (np.float64(2625.0), np.float64(2555.7291666666665)), (np.float64(2625.0), np.float64(1997.9166666666665))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 228, 'image_path': '/Users/prathod/Projects/Rag_based_q-a_boat_over_own_doc/src/q&a_boat/figures/figure-228-157.jpg', 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'category': 'Image', 'element_id': '7d2c312c9d2431ac121a7a58340e2673', 'source_image': '/Users/prathod/Projects/Rag_based_q-a_boat_over_own_doc/src/q&a_boat/figures/figure-228-157.jpg'}, page_content='[IMAGE DESCRIPTION]\nSource File: /Users/prathod/Projects/Rag_based_q-a_boat_over_own_doc/src/q&a_boat/figures/figure-228-157.jpg\nThe image is a diagram illustrating a network architecture, specifically a backbone network with a satellite connection to a terminal. Here is a detailed description of the components and their arrangement:\n\n1. **Backbone Network**:\n   - On the left side of the diagram, there is a section labeled "Backbone Network."\n\n2. **Network Components**:\n   - **SAS NMS (System Administration and Support Network Management System)**: This is a central management system for the network.\n   - **Access Router**: This is a router that connects the backbone network to the PPs (Point-to-Point) section.\n   - **PPs (Point-to-Point)**: These are the Point-to-Point connections that link the Access Router to the Line Cards.\n   - **Line Cards**: These are the devices that handle the actual data transmission.\n   - **RFS (Radio Frequency Switch)**: This is a device that manages the radio frequency connections.\n   - **Satellite**: This is the satellite link that connects the network to the Terminal.\n   - **Terminal**: This is the end device that receives the data from the satellite.\n\n3. **Dual Path Configuration**:\n   - The diagram shows two paths for the network traffic:\n     - **Standby Primary SAS**: This is the standby path for the primary System Administration and Support (SAS) network.\n     - **Active Backup/Diversity SAS**: This is the active path for the backup or diversity System Administration and Support (SAS) network.\n\n4. **Connections**:\n   - The Access Router is connected to the PPs, which are then connected to the Line Cards.\n   - The Line Cards are connected to the RFS.\n   - The RFS is connected to the Satellite, which then connects to the Terminal.\n\n5. **Overall Structure**:\n   - The diagram shows a robust network architecture with redundancy (dual paths) to ensure reliability and failover capabilities in case of a primary system failure.\n\nThis diagram is likely used in a technical or engineering context to explain the network design and its components.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(743.7499999999999), np.float64(430.2083333333333)), (np.float64(743.7499999999999), np.float64(2114.583333333333)), (np.float64(2450.0), np.float64(2114.583333333333)), (np.float64(2450.0), np.float64(430.2083333333333))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 231, 'image_path': '/Users/prathod/Projects/Rag_based_q-a_boat_over_own_doc/src/q&a_boat/figures/figure-231-158.jpg', 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'category': 'Image', 'element_id': '6faa96ba548cac679d5e913bf6d9f6de', 'source_image': '/Users/prathod/Projects/Rag_based_q-a_boat_over_own_doc/src/q&a_boat/figures/figure-231-158.jpg'}, page_content='[IMAGE DESCRIPTION]\nSource File: /Users/prathod/Projects/Rag_based_q-a_boat_over_own_doc/src/q&a_boat/figures/figure-231-158.jpg\nThe image is a detailed network diagram illustrating the architecture of a network operations center (NOC) and its components. Here is a breakdown of the elements present in the diagram:\n\n1. **NOC (Network Operations Center) Circle**:\n   - Contains the following components:\n     - Pulse NOC NMS (Network Management System)\n     - Kubernetes Cluster\n     - Kafka Cluster\n\n2. **Primary CDC (Central Data Center) Circle**:\n   - Contains the following components:\n     - iGW (Internet Gateway) Mode: Active\n     - Pulse SAS NMS (Network Management System) Mode: Active\n     - Kubernetes Cluster\n     - Kafka Cluster\n\n3. **Backup CDC (Central Data Center) Circle**:\n   - Contains the following components:\n     - iGW (Internet Gateway) PP Mode: BAK-DIV\n     - Pulse SAS NMS (Network Management System) Mode: Standby\n     - Kubernetes Cluster\n     - Kafka Cluster\n\n4. **RF Gateways**:\n   - There are six RF Gateways labeled as:\n     - RF Gateway #1\n     - RF Gateway #2\n     - RF Gateway #3\n     - RF Gateway #4\n     - RF Gateway #5\n     - RF Gateway #6\n   - Each gateway is connected to a hub and a ULC (possibly a user login controller or similar device).\n\n5. **Connections and Data Flows**:\n   - Arrows indicate the direction of data flow and connections between the components.\n   - Specific data flows are labeled as:\n     - Option File Updates\n     - Database Replication\n     - Stats, Status, and Events\n\nThe diagram illustrates a redundant and scalable network architecture with active and standby modes for the CDCs, ensuring high availability and disaster recovery capabilities. The NOC is the central hub, managing the primary and backup CDCs, and the RF gateways are connected to the network for data transmission and management.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(674.4791666666666), np.float64(944.2708333333333)), (np.float64(674.4791666666666), np.float64(2384.375)), (np.float64(2519.270833333333), np.float64(2384.375)), (np.float64(2519.270833333333), np.float64(944.2708333333333))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 232, 'image_path': '/Users/prathod/Projects/Rag_based_q-a_boat_over_own_doc/src/q&a_boat/figures/figure-232-159.jpg', 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'category': 'Image', 'element_id': '4ee74d484ecfc9703b739b5e15b995be', 'source_image': '/Users/prathod/Projects/Rag_based_q-a_boat_over_own_doc/src/q&a_boat/figures/figure-232-159.jpg'}, page_content='[IMAGE DESCRIPTION]\nSource File: /Users/prathod/Projects/Rag_based_q-a_boat_over_own_doc/src/q&a_boat/figures/figure-232-159.jpg\nThe image is a detailed network diagram illustrating the architecture of a network operations center (NOC) and its components. Here is a breakdown of the elements present in the diagram:\n\n### Central Elements:\n1. **NOC (Network Operations Center)**:\n   - At the top center of the diagram, there is a large circle labeled "NOC."\n   - Inside this circle, there are two smaller circles:\n     - One labeled "Pulse NOC NMS" with three server racks.\n     - Another labeled "Kubernetes Kafka Cluster" with three server racks.\n\n2. **Database Replication**:\n   - Arrows point from the "Pulse NOC NMS" and "Kubernetes Kafka Cluster" to a central point labeled "Database Replication."\n\n3. **Option File Updates**:\n   - Arrows point from the "Pulse NOC NMS" and "Kubernetes Kafka Cluster" to a central point labeled "Option File Updates."\n\n4. **Stats, Status and Events**:\n   - Arrows point from the "Pulse NOC NMS" and "Kubernetes Kafka Cluster" to a central point labeled "Stats, Status and Events."\n\n### Primary CDC (Central Data Center) (Standby):\n- Below the "NOC" circle, there is a smaller circle labeled "Primary CDC (Standby)."\n- Inside this circle:\n  - There are three server racks labeled "iGW" with the mode "BAK-DIV."\n  - Another server rack labeled "Pulse SAS NMS" with the mode "Standby."\n  - A third server rack labeled "Kubernetes Kafka Cluster."\n\n### Backup CDC (Central Data Center) (Active):\n- To the right of the "Primary CDC (Standby)" circle, there is another smaller circle labeled "Backup CDC (Active)."\n- Inside this circle:\n  - There are three server racks labeled "iGW" with the mode "PP Mode: Active."\n  - Another server rack labeled "Pulse SAS NMS" with the mode "Active."\n  - A third server rack labeled "Kubernetes Kafka Cluster."\n\n### RF Gateways:\n- At the bottom of the diagram, there are six smaller circles labeled "RF Gateway #1" to "RF Gateway #6."\n- Each of these circles contains an image of a server rack and a device labeled "Hub/ULC."\n\n### Arrows and Connections:\n- Arrows connect the "Primary CDC (Standby)" and "Backup CDC (Active)" to the "NOC" circle, indicating the flow of data and updates.\n- Arrows also connect the "Primary CDC (Standby)" and "Backup CDC (Active)" to the "RF Gateways," indicating the connection and data flow between the central data centers and the remote gateways.\n\n### Modes:\n- The "iGW" in both the "Primary CDC (Standby)" and "Backup CDC (Active)" is labeled with different modes:\n  - "BAK-DIV" in the "Primary CDC (Standby)."\n  - "PP Mode: Active" in the "Backup CDC (Active)."\n\nThis diagram illustrates the network architecture, including the roles of various components and the flow of data and updates between them.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(568.75), np.float64(1881.2499999999998)), (np.float64(568.75), np.float64(2056.25)), (np.float64(743.7499999999999), np.float64(2056.25)), (np.float64(743.7499999999999), np.float64(1881.2499999999998))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 233, 'image_path': '/Users/prathod/Projects/Rag_based_q-a_boat_over_own_doc/src/q&a_boat/figures/figure-233-160.jpg', 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'category': 'Image', 'element_id': 'bf14aaaa8d28111ae5c131952375bbe6', 'source_image': '/Users/prathod/Projects/Rag_based_q-a_boat_over_own_doc/src/q&a_boat/figures/figure-233-160.jpg'}, page_content='[IMAGE DESCRIPTION]\nSource File: /Users/prathod/Projects/Rag_based_q-a_boat_over_own_doc/src/q&a_boat/figures/figure-233-160.jpg\nThe image appears to be a pixelated representation of a gift box with a bow on top. The box is predominantly blue, and the bow is also blue with a lighter blue ribbon. The background is white, and the image is framed by a thin blue border. There is no text, numbers, charts, or diagrams visible in the image. The pixelation suggests it might be from a low-resolution image or a di