nts and labels:\n\n1. **Primary NOC (Network Operations Center)**: Located on the left side of the image, this is the main control center for the network operations.\n2. **Backup NOC (Network Operations Center)**: Located on the right side of the image, this is an alternative control center that can take over in case the primary NOC fails.\n3. **Backbone Network**: This is the main network that connects the Primary NOC and the Backup NOC. It is represented by a large, curved line in the center of the image.\n4. **Primary SAS 1, Primary SAS 2, Primary SAS 3**: These are three separate sites or servers that are connected to the backbone network. They are labeled as "Primary" indicating they are the main operational sites.\n5. **Key Legend**: Located at the bottom right of the image, the key legend explains the symbols used in the diagram:\n   - A blue building icon with a black border is labeled "active," indicating the site is currently operational.\n   - A white building icon with a black border is labeled "standby," indicating the site is in a backup or standby mode.\n\nThe diagram illustrates a network setup where the Primary NOC and the Backup NOC are connected via the backbone network. The three Primary SAS sites are also connected to the backbone network, and the key legend helps to differentiate between active and standby sites.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(805.7291666666666), np.float64(1126.5625)), (np.float64(805.7291666666666), np.float64(2198.4375)), (np.float64(2388.020833333333), np.float64(2198.4375)), (np.float64(2388.020833333333), np.float64(1126.5625))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 236, 'image_path': '/Users/prathod/Projects/Rag_based_q-a_boat_over_own_doc/src/q