n_doc/src/q&a_boat/figures/figure-240-168.jpg'}, page_content='[IMAGE DESCRIPTION]\nSource File: /Users/prathod/Projects/Rag_based_q-a_boat_over_own_doc/src/q&a_boat/figures/figure-240-168.jpg\nThe image appears to be a simple graphic design featuring a stylized representation of a map or globe. The design is composed of two main elements:\n\n1. **Map/Globe Shape**: The central part of the image resembles a map or globe, with a blue outline that suggests landmasses or continents. The shape is irregular, with some areas appearing more prominent than others, giving it a somewhat abstract or stylized appearance.\n\n2. **Blue Stripes**: There are two horizontal blue stripes at the top and bottom of the image. These stripes are solid and do not contain any text or additional design elements.\n\nThe image does not contain any text, numbers, charts, or diagrams other than the stylized map or globe and the blue stripes. The overall color scheme is simple, with blue and white being the primary colors used.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(780.2083333333333), np.float64(1534.8958333333333)), (np.float64(780.2083333333333), np.float64(2442.708333333333)), (np.float64(2413.5416666666665), np.float64(2442.708333333333)), (np.float64(2413.5416666666665), np.float64(1534.8958333333333))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 242, 'image_path': '/Users/prathod/Projects/Rag_based_q-a_boat_over_own_doc/src/q&a_boat/figures/figure-242-169.jpg', 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'category': 'Image', 'element_id': 'e28ae3440f27f1c89c26743ce317d857', 'source_image': '/Users/prathod/Projects/Rag_based_q-a_boat_over_own_doc/src/q&a_boat/figures/figure-242-169.jpg'}, page_content='[IMAGE DESCRIPTION]\nSource File: /Users/prathod/Projects/Rag_based_q-a_boat_over_own_doc/src/q&a_boat/figures/figure-242-169.jpg\nThe image is a detailed block diagram of a satellite communication system, specifically designed for both outbound and inbound transmission and reception. Here is a breakdown of the components and their connections:\n\n### Outbound Section:\n1. **Chassis X and Chassis Y**:\n   - These are the main chassis for the outbound transmission.\n   - Each chassis has four red and four blue connectors labeled as "Tx" (Transmit) and "Rx" (Receive).\n\n2. **Combiner**:\n   - The signals from the "Tx" and "Rx" connectors are combined into four separate paths, each corresponding to a different color (red, blue, green, and yellow).\n\n3. **BUC (Block Upconverter)**:\n   - Each color-coded path is connected to a BUC, which is responsible for upconverting the signal to the desired frequency.\n   - The BUCs are color-coded to match the input signals: red, blue, green, and yellow.\n\n4. **Combiner**:\n   - The output from the BUCs is combined into two paths, each labeled as "RHCP" (Right-Hand Circular Polarization) and "LHCP" (Left-Hand Circular Polarization).\n\n5. **PA (Power Amplifier)**:\n   - The combined signals from the RHCP and LHCP paths are amplified by the PA.\n\n6. **Satellite Antenna**:\n   - The amplified signals are then transmitted through the satellite antenna, which is shown at the bottom right of the diagram.\n\n### Inbound Section:\n1. **Splitter**:\n   - The inbound signals from the satellite are split into four paths, each corresponding to a different color (red, blue, green, and yellow).\n\n2. **BDC (Block Downconverter)**:\n   - Each color-coded path is connected to a BDC, which is responsible for downconverting the signal to a lower frequency.\n   - The BDCs are color-coded to match the input signals: red, blue, green, and yellow.\n\n3. **Splitter**:\n   - The output from the BDCs is split into two paths, each labeled as "RHCP" and "LHCP".\n\n4. **LNA (Low Noise Amplifier)**:\n   - The split signals from the RHCP and LHCP paths are amplified by the LNA.\n\n### Key:\n- The key on the right side of the diagram indicates the color coding for the different IF (Intermediate Frequency) domains:\n  - Red: IF Domain A\n  - Blue: IF Domain B\n  - Green: IF Domain C\n  - Yellow: IF Domain D\n\n### Diagram Legend:\n- The legend on the right side of the diagram also includes the following:\n  - "Outbound" and "Inbound" labels for the direction of the signal flow.\n  - "RHCP" and "LHCP" labels for the polarization of the signals.\n\n### Additional Notes:\n- The diagram includes a small inset on the right side showing the polarization of the signals (RHCP and LHCP) and their corresponding directions (Outbound and Inbound).\n- The diagram is well-organized and uses color coding to differentiate between different domains and polarizations, making it easy to follow the signal flow in both the outbound and inbound directions.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(725.5208333333333), np.float64(430.2083333333333)), (np.float64(725.5208333333333), np.float64(1957.8124999999998)), (np.float64(2468.2291666666665), np.float64(1957.8124999999998)), (np.float64(2468.2291666666665), np.float64(430.2083333333333))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 244, 'image_path': '/Users/prathod/Projects/Rag_based_q-a_boat_over_own_doc/src/q&a_boat/figures/figure-244-170.jpg', 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'category': 'Image', 'element_id': '4437af15773be55e17c27c93ab33651d', 'source_image': '/Users/prathod/Projects/Rag_based_q-a_boat_over_own_doc/src/q&a_boat/figures/figure-244-170.jpg'}, page_content='[IMAGE DESCRIPTION]\nSource File: /Users/prathod/Projects/Rag_based_q-a_boat_over_own_doc/src/q&a_boat/figures/figure-244-170.jpg\nThe image is a detailed diagram illustrating a satellite communication system. Here is a breakdown of the components and their connections:\n\n1. **Satellite**: At the top of the diagram, there is a satellite labeled "Satellite." Green arrows indicate the direction of modulated signals being transmitted from the satellite to user terminals.\n\n2. **User Terminals**: Two user terminals are shown at the bottom right of the diagram. These terminals receive the modulated signals from the satellite.\n\n3. **Primary Site**:\n   - **Web Server**: A web server is connected to the backbone network.\n   - **Backbone Network**: This is a cloud-like representation indicating the backbone network.\n   - **Upstream Router**: This router is connected to the backbone network and the primary site.\n   - **PP (Primary Processor)**: The PP is connected to the upstream router and the switch.\n   - **Switch**: The switch is connected to the PP and the RCM (Radio Communication Module) with IF (Intermediate Frequency) connections.\n   - **RCM (Radio Communication Module)**: The RCM is connected to the switch and has multiple IF connections (labeled as 1, 5, 1, 5, 3, 3) and Tx (Transmit) and Rx (Receive) connections.\n   - **GPS PPS**: A GPS PPS (Precision Pulse Signal) is connected to the RCM.\n   - **IF Domain A**: Red boxes represent IF Domain A connections.\n   - **IF Domain B**: Blue boxes represent IF Domain B connections.\n   - **Standby card, IF Domain A**: Pink boxes represent the standby card for IF Domain A.\n   - **Tunnel**: Brown arrows indicate the tunnel connections.\n   - **User IP Packets**: Purple arrows indicate the user IP packets.\n   - **Modulated Signals**: Green arrows indicate the modulated signals.\n\n4. **Key**: The bottom right corner of the diagram includes a key that explains the color coding:\n   - Red: IF Domain A\n   - Pink: Standby card, IF Domain A\n   - Blue: IF Domain B\n   - Purple: User IP Packets\n   - Brown: Tunnel\n   - Green: Modulated Signals\n   - iNet: Indicates the network infrastructure.\n\nThe diagram illustrates the flow of data and signals from the web server through the backbone network, upstream router, PP, switch, RCM, and finally to the satellite and user terminals, with various connections and protocols involved.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(692.7083333333333), np.float64(1163.0208333333333)), (np.float64(692.7083333333333), np.float64(2748.958333333333)), (np.float64(2501.0416666666665), np.float64(2748.958333333333)), (np.float64(2501.0416666666665), np.float64(1163.0208333333333))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 246, 'image_path': '/Users/prathod/Projects/Rag_based_q-a_boat_over_own_doc/src/q&a_boat/figures/figure-246-171.jpg', 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'category': 'Image', 'element_id': 'f0c0468187d4c7cfd0c00cd0573ed0ef', 'source_image': '/Users/prathod/Projects/Rag_based_q-a_boat_over_own_doc/src/q&a_boat/figures/figure-246-171.jpg'}, page_content='[IMAGE DESCRIPTION]\nSource File: /Users/prathod/Projects/Rag_based_q-a_boat_over_own_doc/src/q&a_boat/figures/figure-246-171.jpg\nThe image is a detailed diagram illustrating the architecture of a satellite communication system. Here is a breakdown of the components and their connections:\n\n1. **Satellite**: At the top of the diagram, there is a satellite labeled "Satellite." It is shown emitting green arrows, which represent modulated signals.\n\n2. **User Terminals**: Below the satellite, there are two user terminals, each with a satellite dish. These terminals are connected to the satellite via the green arrows, indicating the transmission of modulated signals.\n\n3. **Backbone Network**: On the left side of the diagram, there is a cloud labeled "Backbone Network." This represents the backbone infrastructure that connects various components of the system.\n\n4. **Web Server**: Within the backbone network, there is a server labeled "Web Server." This server is connected to the backbone network via a purple arrow, indicating the transmission of user IP packets.\n\n5. **SAS (Satellite Access Station)**: Below the backbone network, there is a section labeled "SAS" (Satellite Access Station). This section includes the following components:\n   - **Upstream Router**: This is connected to the backbone network and the PP (Pseudo-Passive) via a purple arrow.\n   - **PP (Pseudo-Passive)**: This is connected to the upstream router and the switch via a purple arrow.\n   - **Switch**: This is connected to the PP and the RCM (Radio Control Module) via a purple arrow.\n   - **RCM (Radio Control Module)**: This is connected to the switch and the Lineards via a purple arrow.\n   - **Lineards**: These are connected to the RCM and the IF (Intermediate Frequency) connections via a'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(568.75), np.float64(430.2083333333333)), (np.float64(568.75), np.float64(2234.895833333333)), (np.float64(2625.0), np.float64(2234.895833333333)), (np.float64(2625.0), np.float64(430.2083333333333))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 247, 'image_path': '/Users/prathod/Projects/Rag_based_q-a_boat_over_own_doc/s