oat64(568.75), np.float64(1779.1666666666665)), (np.float64(2625.0), np.float64(1779.1666666666665)), (np.float64(2625.0), np.float64(936.9791666666666))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 253, 'image_path': '/Users/prathod/Projects/Rag_based_q-a_boat_over_own_doc/src/q&a_boat/figures/figure-253-179.jpg', 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'category': 'Image', 'element_id': '19852e52ef1b16cb3171bc8d6010d410', 'source_image': '/Users/prathod/Projects/Rag_based_q-a_boat_over_own_doc/src/q&a_boat/figures/figure-253-179.jpg'}, page_content='[IMAGE DESCRIPTION]\nSource File: /Users/prathod/Projects/Rag_based_q-a_boat_over_own_doc/src/q&a_boat/figures/figure-253-179.jpg\nThe image is a detailed diagram of the iDirect Velocity SAS (Satellite Access System) Architecture. Here is a breakdown of the components and their arrangement:\n\n1. **SP Core Network**: This is represented on the left side of the diagram. It consists of four access routers, which are connected to the core network. The access routers are depicted with red lines pointing towards the core network, indicating their role in connecting to the core.\n\n2. **Core Network**: The core network is represented by a cluster of blue boxes labeled "Nexus 5k Core Switch." These switches are interconnected to form a robust core network structure.\n\n3. **Fabric Extenders**: There are four Nexus 2k Fabric Extenders shown in the diagram. These are connected to the core switches and are responsible for extending the network fabric. Each fabric extender is connected to multiple line card chassis, as indicated by the blue lines radiating from each extender.\n\n4. **Line Card Chassis**: These are the physical components that house the protocol processors and other network equipment. There are four line card chassis shown, each connected to a fabric extender.\n\n5. **Protocol Processors**: These are the processing units within the line card chassis. They are responsible for handling the network protocols and data processing.\n\n6. **NMS (Network Management System)**: This is a management system that oversees the operation of the network. It is connected to the line card chassis and is part of the overall network architecture.\n\n7. **SAS (Satellite Access System)**: This is the satellite component of the architecture. It is represented by a satellite dish on the right side of the diagram. The satellite dish is connected to the line card chassis via the fabric extenders and core switches.\n\nThe diagram is structured to show the flow of data from the SP Core Network through the core switches, fabric extenders, and line card chassis, ultimately reaching the satellite access system. The blue lines represent the data flow, and the red lines represent the connection from the access routers to the core network. The green boxes on the right side of the diagram highlight the different components of the architecture.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'detection_class_prob': 0.38352495431900024, 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(324.007568359375), np.float64(401.30731201171875)), (np.float64(324.007568359375), np.float64(524.4569091796875)), (np.float64(411.5444030761719), np.float64(524.4569091796875)), (np.float64(411.5444030761719), np.float64(401.30731201171875))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 255, 'image_path': '/Users/prathod/Projects/Rag_based_q-a_boat_over_own_doc/src/q&a_boat/figures/figure-255-180.jpg', 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad