# Primary NOC (Network Operations Center):\n- **EAP (Emergency Access Point)**: Located in the top left corner, represented by a stack of servers.\n- **NOC NMS (Network Management System)**: Located within the "Primary NOC" circle, represented by a server.\n- **GBWM Cluster**: Also within the "Primary NOC" circle, represented by a server.\n- **Backbone Network**: A cloud-like shape in the center, representing the backbone network that connects all the components.\n\n### Backup NOC:\n- **NOC NMS**: Located within the "Backup NOC" circle, represented by a server.\n- **GBWM Cluster**: Also within the "Backup NOC" circle, represented by a server.\n\n### Backup and Rain Diversity SAS (Satellite Access System):\n- **Satellite Terminals**: Represented by two satellite dishes in the bottom left corner.\n- **Hub Chassis**: Located within the "Primary SAS" circle, represented by a server.\n- **PP Cluster**: Also within the "Primary SAS" circle, represented by a server.\n- **Line Cards**: Located within the "Primary SAS" circle, represented by a server.\n- **SAS NMS**: Located within the "Primary SAS" circle, represented by a server.\n- **Hub Chassis**: Also within the "Backup and Rain Diversity SAS" circle, represented by a server.\n- **PP Cluster**: Also within the "Backup and Rain Diversity SAS" circle, represented by a server.\n- **Line Cards**: Also within the "Backup and Rain Diversity SAS" circle, represented by a server.\n- **SAS NMS**: Also within the "Backup and Rain Diversity SAS" circle, represented by a server.\n\n### EAP (Emergency Access Point):\n- **EAP**: Located in the top right corner, represented by a stack of servers.\n\n### Backbone Network:\n- The backbone network is represented by a cloud-like shape in the center of the diagram, connecting all the components in the "Primary NOC," "Backup NOC," and "Backup and Rain Diversity SAS."\n\n### Summary:\nThe diagram shows a network setup with a primary and backup NOC, a primary and backup SAS, and an EAP. The backbone network connects all these components, ensuring redundancy and failover capabilities. The diagram is designed to illustrate the interconnections and redundancy within the network infrastructure.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(827.6041666666666), np.float64(1965.1041666666665)), (np.float64(827.6041666666666), np.float64(2865.6249999999995)), (np.float64(2366.145833333333), np.float64(2865.6249999999995)), (np.float64(2366.145833333333), np.float64(1965.1041666666665))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 257, 'image_path': '/Users/prathod/Projects/Rag_based_q-a_boat_over_own_doc/src/q&a_boat/figures/figure-257-182.jpg', 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'category': 'Image', 'element_id': 'c82f0b4e023c35ccb399dbe92fba5f91', 'source_image': '/Users/prathod/Projects/Rag_based_q-a_boat_over_own_doc/src/q&a_boat/figures/figure-257-182.jpg'}, page_content='[IMAGE DESCRIPTION]\nSource File: /Users/prathod/Projects/Rag_based_q-a_boat_over_own_doc/src/q&a_boat/figures/figure-257-182.jpg\nThe image is a diagram illustrating a network architecture, likely related to telecommunications or satellite communication systems. Here is a detailed description of the components and their connections:\n\n1. **Datapath Equipment**:\n   - This section includes a satellite dish and several servers labeled as "Datapath equipment."\n   - The satellite dish is connected to a server labeled "Teleport."\n\n2. **Teleport**:\n   - The "Teleport" section includes a server and a database with arrows pointing in and out, indicating data flow or processing.\n\n3. **SAS NMS (Satellite Access System Network Management System)**:\n   - This section includes several servers labeled as "SAS NMS."\n\n4. **OSS/BSS (Operational Support System/Business Support System) (provided by customer)**:\n   - This section includes a server labeled as "OSS/BSS (provided by customer)."\n\n5. **NOC NMS (Network Operations Center Network Management System)**:\n   - This section includes several servers labeled as "NOC NMS."\n\n6. **EAP (Extensible Authentication Protocol)**:\n   - This section includes two firewalls labeled as "EAP."\n\n7. **Internet**:\n   - The "Internet" section is represented by a cloud with a laptop and a server connected to it.\n\n8. **Customer Access**:\n   - This section includes a laptop labeled as "Customer access."\n\n9. **Customer Machine-to-Machine Access**:\n   - This section includes a server labeled as "Customer machine-to-machine access."\n\n10. **NMS Users**:\n    - This section includes two laptops labeled as "NMS Users."\n\nThe diagram shows the flow of data and connections between various components, including the satellite dish, servers, firewalls, and laptops, indicating a complex network setup for managing satellite communications and providing access to different systems and users.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(1006.2499999999999), np.float64(1935.9374999999998)), (np.float64(1006.2499999999999), np.float64(2934.895833333333)), (np.float64(2187.5), np.float64(2934.895833333333)), (np.float64(2187.5), np.float64(1935.9374999999998))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 261, 'image_path': '/Users/prathod/Projects/Rag_based_q-a_boat_over_own_doc/src/q&a_boat/figures/figure-261-183.jpg', 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390da