 into several sections, each representing a step in the process. Here is a detailed description of the flowchart:\n\n### Title and Context:\n-'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(568.75), np.float64(696.3541666666666)), (np.float64(568.75), np.float64(1717.1874999999998)), (np.float64(2625.0), np.float64(1717.1874999999998)), (np.float64(2625.0), np.float64(696.3541666666666))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 301, 'image_path': '/Users/prathod/Projects/Rag_based_q-a_boat_over_own_doc/src/q&a_boat/figures/figure-301-205.jpg', 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'category': 'Image', 'element_id': 'fbb44d4f21c64283faec8cf4f846ff80', 'source_image': '/Users/prathod/Projects/Rag_based_q-a_boat_over_own_doc/src/q&a_boat/figures/figure-301-205.jpg'}, page_content='[IMAGE DESCRIPTION]\nSource File: /Users/prathod/Projects/Rag_based_q-a_boat_over_own_doc/src/q&a_boat/figures/figure-301-205.jpg\nThe image is a diagram illustrating the flow of data in a satellite communication system, specifically focusing on the DVB-S2/ACM (Advanced Coding Modulation) standard. Here\'s a detailed description:\n\n1. **Satellite Dish**: On the left side of the image, there is a depiction of a satellite dish, which is used to transmit and receive signals.\n\n2. **Upstream and Downstream Data Flow**:\n   - The blue arrow labeled "Upstream" points from the satellite dish towards the satellite, indicating the direction of data transmission from the ground station to the satellite.\n   - The orange arrow labeled "Downstream" points from the satellite towards the satellite dish, indicating the direction of data transmission from the satellite to the ground station.\n\n3. **DVB-S2/ACM Standard**:\n   - The blue arrow labeled "Upstream" is also labeled with "DVB-S2/ACM," which refers to the Advanced Coding Modulation standard used for satellite communication. This standard is used for both upstream and downstream data transmission.\n\n4. **TDMA (Time Division Multiple Access)**:\n   - The blue arrow labeled "Upstream" is also labeled with "TDMA," which stands for Time Division Multiple Access. This is a method used to multiplex multiple signals onto a single communication channel by dividing the channel into time slots.\n\n5. **Beam Acquisition Signaling Carrier**:\n   - On the right side of the image, there is a blue oval labeled "Beam Acquisition Signaling Carrier." This is a specific type of carrier signal used for acquiring and locking onto the satellite beam.\n\n6. **Directional Arrows**:\n   - The blue arrow labeled "Upstream" and "TDMA" points towards the satellite, indicating the direction of data transmission from the ground station to the satellite.\n   - The orange arrow labeled "Downstream" points towards the satellite dish, indicating the direction of data transmission from the satellite to the ground station.\n\nThe diagram effectively illustrates the bidirectional data flow in a satellite communication system, highlighting the use of the DVB-S2/ACM standard and TDMA for data transmission and the role of the beam acquisition signaling carrier in the process.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(721.8749999999999), np.float64(845.8333333333333)), (np.float64(721.8749999999999), np.float64(1607.8124999999998)), (np.float64(2471.875), np.float64(1607.8124999999998)), (np.float64(2471.875), np.float64(845.8333333333333))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 302, 'image_path': '/Users/prathod/Projects/Rag_based_q-a_boat_over_own_doc/src/q&a_boat/figures/figure-302-206.jpg', 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'category': 'Image', 'element_id': 'b87fae7e21ef1e41b461d82a20d2e02b', 'source_image': '/Users/prathod/Projects/Rag_based_q-a_boat_over_own_doc/src/q&a_boat/figures/figure-302-206.jpg'}, page_content='[IMAGE DESCRIPTION]\nSource File: /Users/prathod/Projects/Rag_based_q-a_boat_over_own_doc/src/q&a_boat/figures/figure-302-206.jpg\nThe image is a flowchart illustrating the process of packet transmission through a network system, likely involving satellite communication. Here is a detailed description of the image:\n\n1. **Step 1**: The process begins with a "Packet" entering the system through a "LAN Interface."\n2. **Step 2**: The packet is then processed by a "Switch."\n3. **Step 3-6**: The packet continues to a "Satellite Router."\n4. **Step 7**: The packet is received by an "Rx Line Card" and processed by an "iNet."\n5. **Step 8**: The packet is then directed to a "TDMA Aggregator."\n6. **Step 9, 10**: The packet is processed by a "Satellite Terminal Proxy."\n7. **Step 11-13**: The packet is further processed by a "Router."\n8. **Step 14**: The packet is then sent to a "Backbone Network."\n9. **Step 15**: Finally, the packet is transmitted to the "Internet."\n\nThe flowchart uses a combination of rectangles and circles to represent different components and steps in the process. The rectangles are labeled with step numbers and the names of the components, while the circles are labeled with step numbers and the names of the components involved in the final stages of the process. The arrows indicate the direction of the packet\'s movement through the system.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(568.75), np.float64(1126.5625)), (np.float64(568.75), np.float64(1961.4583333333333)), (np.float64(2625.0), np.float64(1961.4583333333333)), (np.float64(2625.0), np.float64(1126.5625))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 303, 'image_path': '/Users/prathod/Projects/Rag_based_q-a_boat_over_own_doc/src/q&a_boat/figures/figure-303-207.jpg', 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'category': 'Image', 'element_id': 'a2a798a3cad98341fd89fe09b7cffdb3', 'source_image': '/Users/prathod/Projects/Rag_based_q-a_boat_over_own_doc/src/q&a_boat/figures/figure-303-207.jpg'}, page_content='[IMAGE DESCRIPTION]\nSource File: /Users/prathod/Projects/Rag_based_q-a_boat_over_own_doc/src/q&a_boat/figures/figure-303-207.jpg\nThe image is a flowchart that illustrates the process of data transmission through a satellite network. The flowchart is divided into two main sections, with steps numbered from 1 to 15.\n\n### Top Section:\n1. **LAN Interface**: The process begins with data entering the LAN Interface.\n2. **Switch**: The data is then sent to a Switch.\n3. **Satellite Router**: The data is routed through a Satellite Router.\n4. **Terminal**: The data is then sent to a Terminal.\n5. **Tx Line Card**: The data is transmitted through a Tx Line Card.\n6. **Steps 9 and 10**: The data is processed at the Tx Line Card.\n7. **Steps 11**: The data is sent to a Terminal.\n8. **Steps 12 and 13**: The data is routed through a Satellite Router.\n9. **Steps 14**: The data is sent to a Switch.\n10. **Steps 15**: The data is finally sent to a LAN Interface.\n\n### Bottom Section:\n1. **Internet**: The process starts with data entering the Internet.\n2. **Packet**: The data is encapsulated into packets.\n3. **Backbone Network**: The packets are sent through a Backbone Network.\n4. **Router**: The packets are routed through a Router.\n5. **Satellite Terminal Proxy**: The packets are processed by a Satellite Terminal Proxy.\n6. **Queueing**: The packets are queued for transmission.\n7. **Steps 5-7**: The packets are processed at the Satellite Terminal Proxy.\n8. **Steps 8**: The packets are queued for transmission.\n9. **Steps 3, 4**: The packets are routed through a Router.\n10. **Steps 1, 2**: The packets are sent through a Backbone Network.\n11. **Internet**: The packets are finally sent back to the Internet.\n\nThe flowchart uses different shapes to represent different components: rectangles for processes, circles for queues, and a cloud for the Internet. The arrows indicate the direction of data flow. Each step is labeled with a number, indicating the sequence of the process.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(590.625), np.float64(1217.7083333333333)), (np.float64(590.625), np.float64(1392.7083333333333)), (np.float64(765.6249999999999), np.float64(1392.7083333333333)), (np.float64(765.6249999999999), np.float64(1217.7083333333333))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 305, 'image_path': '/Users/prathod/Projects/Rag_based_q-a_boat_over_own_doc/src/q&a_boat/figures/figure-305-208.jpg', 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'category': 'Image', 'element_id': 'f2479d5d285028a9fdc21bc87717bd8d', 'source_image': '/Users/prathod/Projects/Rag_based_q-a_boat_over_own_doc/src/q&a_boat/figures/figure-305-208.jpg'}, page_content='[IMAGE DESCRIPTION]\nSource File: /Users/prathod/Projects/Rag_based_q-a_boat_over_own_doc