city.\n   - **Text Below:**\n     - "Total CIR demand < Total Capacity"\n     - "Total MIR demand > Total Capacity"\n     - "Negative Congestion A" for CIR\n     - "Positive Congestion B" for MIR\n\n3. **Case#3:**\n   - **Total Capacity:** Represented by the height of the rectangle.\n   - **MIR Demand:** Shown by a red dashed line above the Total Capacity.\n   - **CIR Demand:** Shown by a blue dashed line above the Total Capacity.\n   - **Text Below:**\n     - "Total CIR demand > Total Capacity"\n     - "Total MIR demand > Total Capacity"\n     - "Positive Congestion for A and B" for CIR & MIR\n\n### Key Points:\n- **A and B** are likely placeholders for different types of demand or categories.\n- The terms "Negative Congestion" and "Positive Congestion" indicate the state of the system in terms of demand relative to capacity.\n- The diagram visually represents the relationship between demand and capacity for both CIR and MIR, showing whether the demand is less than, equal to, or greater than the total capacity.\n\nThis diagram is likely used in a technical or operational context to explain the conditions under which a system might experience congestion or have sufficient capacity to meet demand.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(590.625), np.float64(2136.458333333333)), (np.float64(590.625), np.float64(2311.458333333333)), (np.float64(765.6249999999999), np.float64(2311.458333333333)), (np.float64(765.6249999999999), np.float64(2136.458333333333))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 320, 'image_path': '/Users/prathod/Projects/Rag_based_q-a_boat_over_own_doc/src/q&a_boat/figures/figure-320-223.jpg', 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_uploa