a process involving "iNet" and numerical changes. Here\'s a detailed description:\n\n1. **Circles and Labels**:\n   - There are two circles in the diagram.\n   - The circle on the left is labeled "Base iNet" and has the number "1" inside it.\n   - The circle on the right is labeled "Base iNet + 1" and has the number "2" inside it.\n\n2. **Arrows and Text**:\n   - There are two arrows in the diagram.\n   - The arrow pointing from the "Base iNet" circle to the "Base iNet + 1" circle is labeled "Add 1 iNet."\n   - The arrow pointing from the "Base iNet + 1" circle back to the "Base iNet" circle is labeled "Remove 1 iNet."\n\n3. **Flow of the Process**:\n   - The process starts with "Base iNet" (circle 1).\n   - By adding 1 iNet (as indicated by the arrow), the process moves to "Base iNet + 1" (circle 2).\n   - By removing 1 iNet (as indicated by the arrow), the process returns to "Base iNet" (circle 1).\n\nThis diagram seems to represent a simple cycle or loop where the number of iNets increases and decreases in a controlled manner.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(568.75), np.float64(1804.6874999999998)), (np.float64(568.75), np.float64(2960.4166666666665)), (np.float64(2625.0), np.float64(2960.4166666666665)), (np.float64(2625.0), np.float64(1804.6874999999998))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 332, 'image_path': '/Users/prathod/Projects/Rag_based_q-a_boat_over_own_doc/src/q&a_boat/figures/figure-332-235.jpg', 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'category': 'Image', 'element_id': '024bf55839ea47326765601d52e2b934', 'source_image': '/Users/prathod/Projects/Rag_based_q-a_boat_over_own_doc/src/q&a_boat/figures/figure-332-235.jpg'}, page_content='[IMAGE DESCRIPTION]\nSource File: /Users/prathod/Projects/Rag_based_q-a_boat_over_own_doc/src/q&a_boat/figures/figure-332-235.jpg\nThe image consists of two diagrams side by side, each labeled with a snapshot at a specific time (t0 and t1) and describing the state of beams and their capacity requirements.\n\n### Diagram on the Left:\n- **Title**: "Snapshot at time t0"\n- **Description**: "Blue Beam requires Two iNets to meet capacity."\n- **Visual Elements**:\n  - Multiple circles are drawn, each labeled with "15 Mb/s," indicating the capacity of each beam.\n  - A red circle is labeled "High Demand Area 20 Mb/s," indicating a high-demand area.\n  - A blue circle intersects with the red circle, labeled "15 + 15 Mb/s," suggesting that the blue beam requires two iNets to meet the capacity of the high-demand area.\n\n### Diagram on the Right:\n- **Title**: "Snapshot at time t1"\n- **Description**: "Beams rotate. Red Beam now needs Two iNets to meet capacity."\n- **Visual Elements**:\n  - Similar to the left diagram, multiple circles are drawn, each labeled with "15 Mb/s."\n  - The red circle is again labeled "High Demand Area 20 Mb/s."\n  - The blue circle has rotated and now intersects with the red circle, labeled "15 + 15 Mb/s," indicating that the blue beam still requires two iNets to meet the capacity of the high-demand area.\n  - The red circle has also rotated and now requires two iNets to meet the capacity of the high-demand area, as indicated by the text "15 + 15 Mb/s."\n\n### Summary:\n- Both diagrams illustrate the concept of beam rotation and the requirement of multiple iNets to meet the capacity of a high-demand area.\n- At time t0, the blue beam requires two iNets, and at time t1, the blue beam still requires two iNets, while the red beam also requires two iNets to meet the capacity of the high-demand area.\n- The diagrams use circles to represent beams and their capacities, with the red circle highlighting the high-demand area.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(1181.25), np.float64(2519.270833333333)), (np.float64(1181.25), np.float64(3219.270833333333)), (np.float64(2012.4999999999998), np.float64(3219.270833333333)), (np.float64(2012.4999999999998), np.float64(2519.270833333333))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 333, 'image_path': '/Users/prathod/Projects/Rag_based_q-a_boat_over_own_doc/src/q&a_boat/figures/figure-333-236.jpg', 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'category': 'Image', 'element_id': '2a988b150129e2cf07bc704d59a24cf0', 'source_image': '/Users/prathod/Projects/Rag_based_q-a_boat_over_own_doc/src/q&a_boat/figures/figure-333-236.jpg'}, page_content='[IMAGE DESCRIPTION]\nSource File: /Users/prathod/Projects/Rag_based_q-a_boat_over_own_doc/src/q&a_boat/figures/figure-333-236.jpg\nThe image consists of two overlapping circles, each representing a different beam and time period. Here is a detailed description:\n\n1. **Top Circle:**\n   - The circle is outlined in purple.\n   - Inside the circle, the text reads "Beam 1 Time 1" in orange.\n   - Below that, the text reads "Beam 1 Time 2" in purple.\n\n2. **Bottom Circle:**\n   - The circle is outlined in orange.\n   - Inside the circle, the text reads "Beam 2 Time 1" in orange.\n   - Below that, the text reads "Beam 2 Time 2" in purple.\n\n3. **Overlap:**\n   - The two circles overlap in the middle, creating a shared area.\n   - The shared area contains the text "Beam 1 Time 2" in purple and "Beam 2 Time 2" in purple, indicating a common element or intersection between the two beams and time periods.\n\nThe image appears to be a Venn di