d pointing towards the ground station on the left. However, the beam also diverges and covers the area around the other two ground stations, suggesting a broader coverage or a different type of communication pattern.\n\n### Common Elements:\n- **Text**: The diagrams are labeled (a) and (b) at the bottom left and bottom right corners, respectively.\n- **Color Coding**: The red beam is used to represent the communication or data transmission between the satellite and the ground stations.\n- **Operational Status**: The yellow smiley faces on the ground stations indicate that they are operational.\n\n### Summary:\n- Diagram (a) shows a direct communication link between the satellite and a single ground station.\n- Diagram (b) shows a broader communication pattern where the satellite's beam covers multiple ground stations, suggesting a more extensive communication network or a different type of satellite communication system."), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(568.75), np.float64(586.9791666666666)), (np.float64(568.75), np.float64(1822.9166666666665)), (np.float64(2625.0), np.float64(1822.9166666666665)), (np.float64(2625.0), np.float64(586.9791666666666))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 349, 'image_path': '/Users/prathod/Projects/Rag_based_q-a_boat_over_own_doc/src/q&a_boat/figures/figure-349-249.jpg', 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'category': 'Image', 'element_id': '79f67cb6bf03c49f177d29ca29299cd6', 'source_image': '/Users/prathod/Projects/Rag_based_q-a_boat_over_own_doc/src/q&a_boat/figures/figure-349-249.jpg'}, page_content='[IMAGE DESCRIPTION]\nSource File: /Users/prathod/Projects/Rag_based_q-a_boat_over_own_doc/src/q&a_boat/figures/figure-349-249.jpg\nThe image is a flowchart or diagram illustrating the process of a pulse being processed and transmitted through various components and systems. Here is a detailed description of the image:\n\n1. **Pulse Input**:\n   - The diagram starts with a blue circle labeled "Pulse," indicating the beginning of the process.\n\n2. **Regulatory Area (V1) and Channel Plan (iNet) (V1)**:\n   - The pulse is directed to a section labeled "Regulatory Area (V1)" and "Channel Plan (iNet) (V1)."\n   - Within "Regulatory Area (V1)," the following parameters are listed:\n     - RA ID\n     - PSD/Skew table\n     - Reference Skew Angle\n     - Reference Max C/N Value\n     - db or Angular Skew Tolerance\n   - Within "Channel Plan (iNet) (V1)," the following parameters are listed:\n     - Initial Max Skew Angle\n     - Skew Angle corresponding to worst case allowed PSD\n\n3. **New Section (Highlighted in Blue)**:\n   - A new section is highlighted in blue, labeled "NEW."\n   - This section includes:\n     - Regulatory Area (V2)\n     - RA ID\n     - PSD/Skew table\n     - Default (worst beam in RA):\n       - Reference Skew Angle\n       - Reference Max C/N Value\n       - db or Angular Skew Tolerance\n     - Channel Plan (iNet) (V2)\n       - Initial Maximum Skew Angle\n       - Initial Minimum Skew Angle\n       - Skew Angle corresponding to worst case allowed PSD\n     - RA ID 1:\n       - Reference Skew Angle\n       - Reference Maximum C/N Value\n       - db or Angular Skew Tolerance\n     - RA ID n:\n       - Reference Skew Angle\n       - Reference Maximum C/N Value\n       - db or Angular Skew Tolerance\n\n4. **TIM Acq Param. Descriptor (init TX power)**:\n   - The pulse is directed to a section labeled "TIM Acq Param. Descriptor (init TX power)."\n\n5. **TIM Terminal Param. Descriptor (init min., max. skew)**:\n   - The pulse is directed to a section labeled "TIM Terminal Param. Descriptor (init min., max. skew)."\n\n6. **DFOE string, per iNET PSD/Skew Table; db or angular skew tolerance**:\n   - The pulse is directed to a section labeled "DFOE string, per iNET PSD/Skew Table; db or angular skew tolerance."\n   - It is noted that this section usually overrides DFOE with dynamic skew limits message.\n\n7. **Slot assignments (respective skew)**:\n   - The pulse is directed to a section labeled "Slot assignments (respective skew)."\n\n8. **PP (Pulse Processing)**:\n   - The pulse is directed to a section labeled "PP (Pulse Processing)."\n   - The PP section includes:\n     - TIM Acq Param. Descriptor (init TX power)\n     - TIM Terminal Param. Descriptor (init min., max. skew)\n     - DFOE string, per iNET PSD/Skew Table; db or angular skew tolerance\n     - Slot assignments (respective skew)\n\n9. **Remote**:\n   - The pulse is directed to a section labeled "Remote."\n   - The Remote section includes:\n     - OpenAMIP "K" (min, max skew)\n     - OpenAMIP \'w\' (geolocation, current skew)\n\n10. **Antenna**:\n    - The pulse is directed to a section labeled "Antenna."\n    - The Antenna section includes:\n      - OpenAMIP "K" (min, max skew)\n      - OpenAMIP \'w\' (geolocation, current skew)\n\n11. **Geolocation (geolocation, current skew)**:\n    - The pulse is directed to a section labeled "Geolocation (geolocation, current skew)."\n\nThe diagram uses arrows to indicate the flow of the pulse through the various components and systems,'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(853.1249999999999), np.float64(2092.708333333333)), (np.float64(853.1249999999999), np.float64(2767.1875)), (np.float64(2336.9791666666665), np.float64(2767.1875)), (np.float64(2336.9791666666665), np.float64(2092.708333333333))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'langua