*Allowance Amount**: 100 GB\n- **Rollover**: Maximum 10 GB\n\n### Overage:\n- **Pre-approved overage?**: No\n- **Max Overage**: 50 GB\n\n### Notes:\n- Up to a maximum of 10 GB of allowance can be rolled from one allowance to the next.\n\n### Timeline and Events:\nThe timeline is divided into three months: April 1, May 1, and June 1.\n\n#### April 1:\n- **150 GB**: Input into the system.\n- **100 GB Monthly Allowance**: Applied.\n- **40 GB Remaining**: After applying the allowance, 40 GB is left.\n\n#### May 1:\n- **10 GB Rollover**: 10 GB is rolled over from April's allowance to May.\n- **100 GB Monthly Allowance**: Applied.\n- **40 GB Remaining**: After applying the allowance and rollover, 40 GB is left.\n\n#### June 1:\n- **40 GB Remaining**: The remaining allowance from May is carried forward.\n\n### Events:\n1. **EAI-EVT-723 GSP_FAP_PERIOD_END**: Occurs at the end of the period (April 1).\n2. **EAI-EVT-720 GSP_FAP_CREDIT**: Occurs after the credit is applied.\n3. **EAI-EVT-721 GSP_FAP_ROLLOVER**: Occurs when the rollover is applied.\n4. **EAI-EVT-723 GSP_FAP_PERIOD_END**: Occurs at the end of the period (May 1).\n5. **EAI-EVT-720 GSP_FAP_CREDIT**: Occurs after the credit is applied.\n\n### Visual Elements:\n- **Green Area**: Represents the monthly allowance.\n- **Light Blue Area**: Represents the remaining allowance after the monthly allowance is applied.\n- **Red Dashed Lines**: Indicate the end of the period and the start of the next period.\n- **Numbers (1, 2, 3, 4, 5)**: Correspond to the events listed in the timeline.\n\nThis flowchart effectively illustrates how data allowances are managed, how rollovers work, and the sequence of events that occur at the end of each period."), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(594.2708333333333), np.float64(2872.9166666666665)), (np.float64(594.2708333333333), np.float64(3047.9166666666665))