 with an input of 150 GB of data.\n- **100 GB Monthly Allowance**: This is the monthly data allowance for April.\n- **100 GB Monthly Allowance**: This is the monthly data allowance for May.\n- **June 1**: The flowchart ends with an input of 50 GB of data.\n\n### Middle Section:\n- **Configuration**:\n  - Allowance = Periodic, Monthly\n  - Allowance Amount = 100 GB\n- **Overage**:\n  - Pre-approved overage? No\n  - Max Overage = 50 GB\n- **Rules**: No Rules\n- **Events**:\n  1. EAI-EVT-723 GSP_FAP_PERIOD_END\n  2. EAI-EVT-720 GSP_FAP_CREDIT\n  3. EAI-EVT-694 GSP_FAP_REQUEST_APPROVAL\n  4. EAI-EVT-xxx GSP_FAP_SUSPENDED\n  5. EAI-EVT-xxx GSP_FAP_OVERAGE_ACCEPT\n  6. EAI-EVT-714 GSP_FAP_START_OVERAGE\n  7. EAI-EVT-715 GSP_FAP_SUSPENDED\n  8. EAI-EVT-723 GSP_FAP_PERIOD_END\n  9. EAI-EVT-720 GSP_FAP_CREDIT\n\n### Bottom Section:\n- **No-FAP Area or No-FAP Period or Period with No Usage**: This area represents scenarios where there is no Flexible Allowance Period (FAP).\n- **Overage Charges Authorized by Subscriber**: This area indicates that overage charges are authorized by the subscriber.\n- **Maximum Overage Charges Reached**: This area signifies that the maximum overage charges have been reached.\n\n### Events Timeline:\n- **1**: EAI-EVT-723 GSP_FAP_PERIOD_END\n- **2**: EAI-EVT-720 GSP_FAP_CREDIT\n- **3**: EAI-EVT-694 GSP_FAP_REQUEST_APPROVAL\n- **4**: EAI-EVT-xxx GSP_FAP_SUSPENDED\n- **5**: EAI-EVT-xxx GSP_FAP_OVERAGE_ACCEPT\n- **6**: EAI-EVT-714 GSP_FAP_START_OVERAGE\n- **7**: EAI-EVT-715 GSP_FAP_SUSPENDED\n- **8**: EAI-EVT-723 GSP_FAP_PERIOD_END\n- **9**: EAI-EVT-720 GSP_FAP_CREDIT\n\nThe flowchart uses different colors to represent different states or conditions:\n- **Green**: Represents the monthly allowance.\n- **Light Blue**: Represents the no-FAP area or period.\n- **Orange**: Represents overage charges authorized by the subscriber.\n- **Red**: Represents events and their sequence.\n\nThis flowchart is designed to illustrate the process of managing data usage 