ts/Rag_based_q-a_boat_over_own_doc/src/q&a_boat/figures/figure-367-261.jpg', 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'category': 'Image', 'element_id': '2ef9406d8f400bdc83acb4abcabd9f02', 'source_image': '/Users/prathod/Projects/Rag_based_q-a_boat_over_own_doc/src/q&a_boat/figures/figure-367-261.jpg'}, page_content='[IMAGE DESCRIPTION]\nSource File: /Users/prathod/Projects/Rag_based_q-a_boat_over_own_doc/src/q&a_boat/figures/figure-367-261.jpg\nThe image is a flowchart that outlines the process of managing allowances and top-ups, with a focus on restoration rules. The flowchart includes decision points, actions, and conditions that guide the process. Here is a detailed description:\n\n### Title and Context:\n- The flowchart is titled "Draw from Normal Allowance (fixed or rolling)" and "Increment Normal Allowance for next period."\n- It explains the restoration rule, which can be either a fixed start of the next allowance period or a rolling percentage of the allowance credited to the account.\n\n### Main Process:\n1. **Start:**\n   - The process begins with drawing from the Normal Allowance, which can be either fixed or rolling.\n\n2. **Decision Points:**\n   - **Allowance Depleted?**\n     - If the allowance is depleted, the process moves to the next step.\n   - **Top-Up Available?**\n     - If a top-up is available, the process continues to draw from the top-up account.\n   - **Overage Enabled?**\n     - If overage is enabled, the process checks if overage pre-approved.\n   - **Rollover Enabled?**\n     - If rollover is enabled, the process checks if there are any fixed updates.\n\n3. **Actions:**\n   - **Draw from Top-Up Account:**\n     - If a top-up is available, it is drawn until the top-up account is depleted or the restoration rule occurs.\n   - **Draw from Overage:**\n     - If overage is enabled and pre-approved, it is drawn until the maximum overage bytes are reached or the restoration rule occurs.\n   - **Seek Overage Approval from User:**\n     - If overage is not pre-approved, approval is sought from the user.\n   - **Service Suspended:**\n     - If the service is suspended, it continues until the top-up account is credited or the restoration rule occurs.\n\n4. **Conditions:**\n   - If any normal allowance bytes remain, the next allowance period is credited with rollover bytes.\n   - If the rollover is enabled and there are fixed updates, the process continues to the next step.\n\n5. **End:**\n   - The process ends with incrementing the normal allowance for the next period.\n\n### Additional Notes:\n- The flowchart includes references to "restoration rule" which can be either a fixed start of the next allowance period or a rolling percentage of the allowance credited to the account.\n- There are decision points marked with "Yes" and "No," guiding the flow of the process based on the conditions met.\n\nThis flowchart is designed to illustrate the steps and conditions involved in managing allowances and top-ups, ensuring that the process is clear and systematic.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(696.3541666666666), np.float64(2807.2916666666665)), (np.float64(696.3541666666666), np.float64(2982.2916666666665)), (np.float64(871.3541666666666), np.float64(2982.2916666666665)), (np.float64(871.3541666666666), np.float64(2807.2916666666665))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 368, 'image_path': '/Users/prathod/Projects/Rag_based_q-a_boat_over_own_doc/src/q&a_boat/figures/figure-368-262.jpg', 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'category': 'Image', 'element