a_boat/figures/figure-370-263.jpg\nThe image is a simple, pixelated illustration of a blue gift box with a white ribbon tied around it. The gift box is placed on a white background, and the entire image is framed by a thin blue border. There is no text, numbers, charts, or diagrams present in the image. The style is reminiscent of a pixel art design, commonly used in video games or digital art.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(568.75), np.float64(1319.7916666666665)), (np.float64(568.75), np.float64(2242.1875)), (np.float64(2625.0), np.float64(2242.1875)), (np.float64(2625.0), np.float64(1319.7916666666665))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 371, 'image_path': '/Users/prathod/Projects/Rag_based_q-a_boat_over_own_doc/src/q&a_boat/figures/figure-371-264.jpg', 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'category': 'Image', 'element_id': '9357cb5104b17f2c7f66b98c40cbe182', 'source_image': '/Users/prathod/Projects/Rag_based_q-a_boat_over_own_doc/src/q&a_boat/figures/figure-371-264.jpg'}, page_content='[IMAGE DESCRIPTION]\nSource File: /Users/prathod/Projects/Rag_based_q-a_boat_over_own_doc/src/q&a_boat/figures/figure-371-264.jpg\nThe image is a detailed diagram illustrating a multicast network setup, likely for a satellite communication system. Here\'s a breakdown of the components and their roles:\n\n### Components and Labels:\n1. **Multicast Source**: This is the origin of the multicast traffic, which can be a backbone network, customer private network, or the Internet.\n2. **Backbone, Customer Private Network, and/or Internet**: This represents the network infrastructure that the multicast traffic travels through.\n3. **Access Router**: A device that connects the backbone network to the local area network (LAN).\n4. **SAS LAN (Switched Access Service LAN)**: This is a local area network that connects to the access router.\n5. **NMS (Network Management System)**: A system used for monitoring and managing the network.\n6. **PP (Provider Provider)**: Likely a service provider or a network service.\n7. **IGMP Proxy**: Internet Group Management Protocol proxy, used to manage multicast traffic.\n8. **Tx/Rx Line Cards**: Transmitter and receiver line cards used for sending and receiving data.\n9. **OTA (Over-the-Air)**: Likely refers to the satellite transmission.\n10. **Satellite Terminal**: The device that communicates with the satellite.\n11. **Terminal LAN**: The local area network at the satellite terminal.\n12. **Multicast Listener**: Devices or systems that receive the multicast traffic.\n13. **IGMP Proxy**: Another instance of the Internet Group Management Protocol proxy at the satellite terminal.\n\n### Flow of Multicast Traffic:\n- **Dynamic Multicast**: This is indicated by the IGMPv3 messages flowing between the IGMP Router and the IGMP Host. This suggests that the multicast traffic is dynamically managed and can change over time.\n- **Static Multicast**: This is also indicated by IGMPv3 messages, but it suggests a more fixed setup where the multicast traffic is predefined and does not change.\n- **Persistent Multicast**: This is indicated by IGMPv3 messages as well, but it suggests a long-term setup where the multicast traffic is continuously available.\n\n### Labels and Arrows:\n- Arrows indicate the direction of the multicast traffic flow.\n- The labels "IGMPv2 or IGMPv3" at the bottom right suggest that the multicast traffic can be managed using either IGMPv2 or IGMPv3 protocols.\n\n### Summary:\nThe diagram illustrates a complex network setup where multicast traffic is managed through various devices and protocols, including IGMPv3, to ensure efficient and controlled distribution of multicast data. The setup includes a backbone network, a satellite communication system, and local area networks, all interconnected to manage and deliver multicast traffic to designated listeners.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(988.0208333333333), np.float64(2059.895833333333)), (np.float64(988.0208333333333), np.float64(2821.8749999999995)), (np.float64(2202.083333333333), np.float64(2821.8749999999995)), (np.float64(2202.083333333333), np.float64(2059.895833333333))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 372, 'image_path': '/Users/prathod/Projects/Rag_based_q-a_boat_over_own_doc/src/q&a_boat/figures/figure-372-265.jpg', 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'category': 'Image', 'element_id': 'a05294a098f84d1f9f20855cd03ccc96', 'source_image': '/Users/prathod/Projects/Rag_based_q-a_boat_over_own_doc/src/q&a_boat/figures/figure-372-265.jpg'}, page_content='[IMAGE DESCRIPTION]\nSource File: /Users/prathod/Projects/Rag_based_q-a_boat_over_own_doc/src/q&a_boat/figures/figure-372-265.jpg\nThe image is a Venn diagram with multiple overlapping circles, each labeled with different categories. Here is a detailed description:\n\n1. **Circles and Labels:**\n   - There are two main categories of circles: red and green.\n   - The red circles are labeled as follows:\n     - "2-way SB-1A"\n     - "2-way SB-4A"\n     - "2-way SB-5B"\n     - "2-way SB-6A"\n   - The green circles are labeled as follows:\n     - "2-way SB-2B"\n     - "2-way SB-3B"\n   - There are two additional circles outside the main overlapping area:\n     - "1-way WB-1A" (red)\n     - "1-way WB-1B" (green)\n\n2.