/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(594.2708333333333), np.float64(648.9583333333333)), (np.float64(594.2708333333333), np.float64(1181.25)), (np.float64(2595.833333333333), np.float64(1181.25)), (np.float64(2595.833333333333), np.float64(648.9583333333333))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 383, 'image_path': '/Users/prathod/Projects/Rag_based_q-a_boat_over_own_doc/src/q&a_boat/figures/figure-383-271.jpg', 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'category': 'Image', 'element_id': 'f068d6dbd14b4eac72011dd95959fa84', 'source_image': '/Users/prathod/Projects/Rag_based_q-a_boat_over_own_doc/src/q&a_boat/figures/figure-383-271.jpg'}, page_content='[IMAGE DESCRIPTION]\nSource File: /Users/prathod/Projects/Rag_based_q-a_boat_over_own_doc/src/q&a_boat/figures/figure-383-271.jpg\nThe image is a diagram explaining the concept of a sliding window mechanism in the context of frame-by-frame fulfillment and CIR (Committed Information Rate) fulfillment. Here is a detailed description:\n\n1. **Title and Explanation:**\n   - The top part of the image contains text explaining the concept:\n     - "A total-demand (demand capped by MIR)"\n     - "Pass in the frame-by-frame fulfillment resets previous fails in the window to a Pass"\n     - "Sliding window one frame at a time"\n     - "CIR fulfillment frame by frame"\n     - "CIR delayed fulfillment"\n\n2. **Sliding Window Mechanism:**\n   - The diagram shows a sliding window that moves one frame at a time across a series of frames.\n   - The window is represented by a blue shaded area that slides horizontally across the frames.\n\n3. **Frame-by-Frame Fulfillment:**\n   - The diagram illustrates the process of frame-by-frame fulfillment.\n   - The window starts at the first frame and slides to the right, one frame at a time.\n   - Each frame is labeled as either "Pass" or "FAIL."\n   - When the window slides, it resets any previous "FAIL" frames within the window to "Pass."\n\n4. **CIR Fulfillment:**\n   - The bottom part of the image shows the CIR fulfillment process.\n   - The window slides across the frames, and the "Pass" frames are highlighted in yellow.\n   - The yellow highlighted frames indicate the frames that meet the CIR requirements.\n   - The text "CIR delayed fulfillment" is mentioned, suggesting that the CIR is fulfilled based on the delayed frames.\n\n5. **Arrows and Indicators:**\n   - Red arrows indicate the direction of the sliding window.\n   - Blue arrows point to the frames that are being evaluated for fulfillment.\n   - The yellow highlighting in the bottom part of the diagram indicates the frames that meet the CIR criteria.\n\nThis diagram is used to illustrate how a sliding window mechanism is used to evaluate and fulfill CIR requirements frame by frame, with the ability to reset previous failures to "Pass" as the window slides.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(605.2083333333333), np.float64(1327.0833333333333)), (np.float64(605.2083333333333), np.float64(1855.7291666666665)), (np.float64(2584.895833333333), np.float64(1855.7291666666665)), (np.float64(2584.895833333333), np.float64(1327.0833333333333))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 383, 'image_path': '/Users/prathod/Projects/Rag_based_q-a_boat_over_own_doc/src/q&a_boat/figures/figure-383-272.jpg', 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'category': 'Image', 'element_id': 'fac4e7429e797ac5c9a66990bdf6fae6', 'source_image': '/Users/prathod/Projects/Rag_based_q-a_boat_over_own_doc/src/q&a_boat/figures/figure-383-272.jpg'}, page_content='[IMAGE DESCRIPTION]\nSource File: /Users/prathod/Projects/Rag_based_q-a_boat_over_own_doc/src/q&a_boat/figures/figure-383-272.jpg\nThe image is a diagram explaining the concept of "MIR fulfillment frame by frame" and "MIR delayed fulfillment." Here is a detailed description:\n\n1. **Title and Explanation:**\n   - At the top of the image, there is a title that reads: "A total demand (demand capped by the MIR) Pass in the frame-by-frame fulfillment resets previous fails in the window to a Pass."\n   - Below the title, there is a note: "Sliding window one frame at a time."\n\n2. **Diagram Components:**\n   - The diagram consists of two main sections:\n     - The top section is labeled "MIR fulfillment frame by frame."\n     - The bottom section is labeled "MIR delayed fulfillment."\n\n3. **MIR Fulfillment Frame by Frame:**\n   - This section shows a sequence of frames, each labeled either "Pass" or "FAIL."\n   - The sequence is as follows: Pass, FAIL, FAIL, Pass, FAIL.\n   - There is a red arrow pointing to the "FAIL" frame, indicating that it is the current frame being considered.\n   - The red arrow also points to the "FAIL" frame in the "MIR delayed fulfillment" section, suggesting a connection or relationship between the two.\n\n4. **MIR Delayed Fulfillment:**\n   - This section shows a sequence of frames, each labeled either "Pass" or "FAIL."\n   - The sequence is as follows: Pass, Pass, Pass, Pass, FAIL.\n   - The "FAIL" frame in this section is highlighted in yellow, indicating a failure.\n   - The yellow highlighted "FAIL" frame corresponds to the "FAIL" frame in the "MIR fulfillment frame by frame" section, showing how the system resets previous failures.\n\n5. **Arrows and Connections:**\n   - There are blue arrows pointing from the "FAIL" frames in the "MIR fulfillment frame by frame" section to the "Pass" frames in the "MIR delayed fulfillment" section, indicating the reset of previous failures.\n   - There is a red arrow pointing from the "FAIL" frame in the "MIR fulfillment frame by frame" section to the "FAIL" frame in the "MIR delayed fulfillment" section, indicating the continuation of the failure.\n\n6. **Overall Concept:**\n   - The diagram illustrates how the MIR (Maximum In-Row) system works in terms of frame-by-frame fulfillment and delayed fulfillment.\n   - It shows how previous failures are reset to "Pass" when a "Pass" frame is encountered, and how this affects the overall fulfillment process.\n\nThis diagram is used to explain the behavior of the MIR system in managing and resetting failures in a sequence of frames.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(627.0833333333333), np.float64(2096.3541666666665)), (np.float64(627.0833333333333), np.float64(3354.1666666666665)), (np.float64(2563.020833333333), np.float64(3354.1666666666665)), (np.float64(2563.020833333333), np.float64(2096.3541666666665))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 383, 'image_path': '/Users/prathod/Projects/Rag_based_q-a_boat_over_own_doc/src/q&a_boat/figures/figure-383-273.jpg', 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'category': 'Image', 'element_id': 'f33b78b6dcfa3f339429ac64bf0008ef', 'source_image': '/Users/prathod/Projects/Rag_based_q-a_boat_over_own_doc/src/q&a_boat/figures/figure-383-273.jpg'}, page_content='[IMAGE DESCRIPTION]\nSource File: /Users/prathod/Projects/Rag_based_q-a_boat_over_own_doc/src/q&a_boat/figures/figure-383-273.jpg\nThe image is a table that outlines a process of demand allocation and fulfillment over a series of frames, with a window size of 5 frames. Here is a detailed description:\n\n### Table Structure:\n- The table is divided into several sections, each with specific headers and data entries.\n- The columns represent Frame numbers from 1 to 5.\n- The rows include headers such as "Current Demand," "CIR Demand (CIR = 10 Units)," "CIR Allocation," "New demand = current demand - (previous demand - previous allocation)," "Total New Demand over 5 frames," "Total Allocation over 5 frames," "Excess/Shortage," "Pass/Fail - Frame-by-Frame," and "Last Frame in the window met condition of total allocation = total demand Hence reset all previously failed frames to a state of \'Pass\'."\n\n### Data Entries:\n1. **Frame #**:\n   - Frame 1: 3\n   - Frame 2: 4\n   - Frame 3: 8\n   - Frame 4: 8\n   - Frame 5: 20\n\n2. **Current Demand**:\n   - Frame 1: 3\n   - Frame 2: 4\n   - Frame 3: 8\n   - Frame 4: 8\n   - Frame 5: 20\n\n3. **CIR Demand (CIR = 10 Units)**:\n   - Frame 1: 3\n   - Frame 2: 4\n   - Frame 3: 8\n   - Frame 4: 8\n   - Frame 5: 10\n\n4. **CIR Allocation**:\n   - Frame 1: 1\n   - Frame 2: 1\n   - Frame 3: 2\n   - Frame 4: 3\n   - Frame 5: 10\n\n5. **New demand = current demand - (previous demand - previous allocation)**:\n   - Frame 1: 2\n   - Frame 2: 2\n   - Frame 3: 6\n   - Frame 4: 2\n   - Frame 5: 5\n\n6. **Total New Demand over 5 frames**:\n   - 2 + 2 + 6 + 2 + 5 = 17\n\n7. **Total Allocation over 5 frames**:\n   - 1 + 1 + 2 + 3 + 10 = 17\n\n8. **Excess/Shortage**:\n   - Frame 1: -2\n   - Frame 2: -3\n   - Frame 3: -6\n   - Frame 4: -5\n   - Frame 5: 0\n\n9. **Pass/Fail - Frame-by-Frame**:\n   - Frame 1: F\n   - Frame 2: F\n   - Frame 3: F\n   - Frame 4: F\n   - Frame 5: P\n\n10. **Last Frame in the window met condition of total allocation = total demand Hence reset all previously failed frames to a state of \'Pass\'**:\n    - Frame 1: P\n    - Frame 2: P\n    - Frame 3: P\n    - Frame 4: P\n    - Frame 5: P\n\n### Additional Notes:\n- The table mentions that the last frame in the window met the condition of total allocation equaling total demand, hence resetting all previously failed frames to a state of "Pass."\n- It is noted that frame #0 (not shown) had 1 unit of unfulfilled demand.\n- The total allocation after the delayed fulfillment is 17.\n\nThis table appears to be part of a simulation or algorithm used to manage and fulfill demand over a series of frames, ensuring that the total demand is met by the total allocation, with any excess or shortage being noted and frames being marked as "Pass" or "Fail" accordingly.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(568.75), np.float64(1079.1666666666665)), (np.float64(568.75), np.float64(1254.1666666666665)), (np.float64(743.7499999999999), np.float64(1254.1666666666665)), (np.float64(743.7499999999999), np.float64(1079.1666666666665))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 384, 'image_path': '/Users/prathod/Projects/Rag_based_q-a_boat_over_own_doc/src/q&a_boat/figures/figure-384-274.jpg', 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'category': 'Image', 'element_id': 'feef5faafd92b89ee970d3b6ac786be5', 'source_image': '/Users/prathod/Projects/Rag_based_q-a_boat_over_own_doc/src/q&a_boat/figures/figure-384-274.jpg'}, page_content='[IMAGE DESCRIPTION]\nSource File: /Users/prathod/Projects/Rag_based_q-a_boat_over_own_doc/src/q&a_boat/figures/figure-384-274.jpg\nThe image appears to be a pixelated representation of a gift box with a bow on top. The box is predominantly blue, and the bow is also blue with a lighter blue ribbon. The background is