RIPTION]\nSource File: /Users/prathod/Projects/Rag_based_q-a_boat_over_own_doc/src/q&a_boat/figures/figure-388-278.jpg\nThe image is a detailed diagram explaining the process of calculating the Committed Information Rate (CIR) fulfillment ratio over a 30-second period. Here\'s a breakdown of the content:\n\n1. **Interval Number (downstream)**: This section lists the intervals from 1 to 300, indicating the downstream direction.\n\n2. **Output of CIR fulfillment algorithm**: This section shows the output of the CIR fulfillment algorithm for each interval. The values are represented as 1s and 0s, where 1 indicates that the CIR is fulfilled, and 0 indicates that it is not.\n\n3. **Adjusted CIR Allocation**: This section is divided into two parts:\n   - The first part has "Do not calculate" for intervals 1 to 8 and 294 to 299, and "calculate" for intervals 9 to 293 and 300.\n   - The second part shows the per-frame calculated values for intervals 3 to 8 and 294 to 299. The values are 0.6 and 0.7, which are the adjusted CIR values for these intervals.\n\n4. **The per frame calculated values**: This section shows the actual calculated values for the intervals where the CIR is fulfilled. The values are 1 for intervals 1 to 2, 3 to 8, 294 to 299, and 300.\n\n5. **CIR fulfillment ratio (30 sec period)**: This section calculates the CIR fulfillment ratio for the 30-second period. It assumes that all intervals have a value of 1 except for the intervals where the CIR is not fulfilled. The formula used is:\n   \\[\n   \\text{CIR fulfillment ratio} = \\left( \\frac{\\text{Sum of all 1s}}{\\text{Total number of intervals}} \\right) \\times 100\\%\n   \\]\n   The sum of all 1s is 298 (from intervals 1 to 2, 3 to 8, 294 to 299, and 300) plus 0.6 and 0.7 (from intervals 3 and 294 respectively). Therefore, the total sum is 298 + 0.6 + 0.7 = 299.3. The total number of intervals is 300. Thus, the CIR fulfillment ratio is:\n   \\[\n   \\left( \\frac{299.3}{300} \\right) \\times 100\\% = 99.77\\%\n   \\]\n\nThe diagram visually represents the process of calculating the CIR fulfillment ratio, highlighting the intervals where the CIR is fulfilled and the adjustments made for intervals where the CIR is not fulfilled.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(568.75), np.float64(437.49999999999994)), (np.float64(568.75), np.float64(612.5)), (np.float64(743.7499999999999), np.float64(612.5)), (np.float64(743.7499999999999), np.float64(437.49999999999994))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 389, 'image_path': '/Users/prathod/Projects/Rag_based_q-a_boat_over_own_doc/src/q&a_boat/figures/figure-389-279.jpg', 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'category': 'Image', 'element_id': '581ff8510b2e268a7dadccfdc477789f', 'source_image': '/Users/prathod/Projects/Rag_based_q-a_boat_over_own_doc/src/q&a_boat/figures/figure-389-279.jpg'}, page_content='[IMAGE DESCRIPTION]\nSource File: /Users/prathod/Projects/Rag_based_q-a_boat_over_own_doc/src/q&a_boat/figures/figure-389-279.jpg\nThe image appears to be a pixelated representation of a gift box with a bow on top. The box is predominantly blue, and the bow is also blue with a lighter blue ribbon. The background is white, and the image is framed by a thin blue border. There is no text, numbers, charts, or diagrams visible in the image. The pixelation suggests that the image might be from a low-resolution source or intentionally designed to look pixelated.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(681.7708333333333), np.float64(2165.625)), (np.float64(681.7708333333333), np.float64(3171.8749999999995)), (np.float64(2511.9791666666665), np.float64(3171.8749999999995)), (np.float64(2511.9791666666665), np.float64(2165.625))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 389, 'image_path': '/Users/prathod/Projects/Rag_based_q-a_boat_over_own_doc/src/q&a_boat/figures/figure-389-280.jpg', 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'category': 'Image', 'element_id': 'bdd3bacdbf128caaa8ea6a43d7701ec2', 'source_image': '/Users/prathod/Projects/Rag_based_q-a_boat_over_own_doc/src/q&a_boat/figures/figure-389-280.jpg'}, page_content='[IMAGE DESCRIPTION]\nSource File: /Users/prathod/Projects/Rag_based_q-a_boat_over_own_doc/src/q&a_boat/figures/figure-389-280.jpg\nThe image is a table that outlines different scenarios based on the fulfillment of CIR (Customer Incentive Rate) and MIR (Minimum Incentive Rate) demands at various levels of demand (D). The table is divided into several columns and rows, with the following headers:\n\n1. **Demand Level: D**\n2. **CIR Demand Fulfilled**\n3. **CIR Fulfillment Reported**\n4. **MIR Demand Fulfilled**\n5. **MIR Fulfillment Reported**\n6. **Comments**\n\nThe table is structured as follows:\n\n### Rows:\n1. **D ≤ CIR**\n   - **CIR Demand Fulfilled**: Yes\n   - **CIR Fulfillment Reported**: 1\n   - **MIR Demand Fulfilled**: Yes\n   - **MIR Fulfillment Reported**: 1\n   - **Comments**: No MIR demand & no Allocation MIR considered fulfilled.\n\n2. **D ≤ CIR**\n   - **CIR Demand Fulfilled**: No\n   - **CIR Fulfillment Reported**: 0\n   - **MIR Demand Fulfilled**: 1\n   - **MIR Fulfillment Reported**: 1\n   - **Comments**: No MIR demand & no Allocation MIR considered fulfilled.\n\n3. **CIR ≤ D ≤ MIR**\n   - **CIR Demand Fulfilled**: Yes\n   - **CIR Fulfillment Reported**: 1\n   - **MIR Demand Fulfilled**: Yes\n   - **MIR Fulfillment Reported**: 1\n\n4. **CIR ≤ D ≤ MIR**\n   - **CIR Demand Fulfilled**: Yes\n   - **CIR Fulfillment Reported**: 1\n   - **MIR Demand Fulfilled**: No\n   - **MIR Fulfillment Reported**: 0\n\n5. **CIR ≤ D ≤ MIR**\n   - **CIR Demand Fulfilled**: No\n   - **CIR Fulfillment Reported**: 0\n   - **MIR Demand Fulfilled**: No\n   - **MIR Fulfillment Reported**: 0\n   - **Comments**: MIR demand made but no allocation.\n\n6. **D > MIR**\n   - **CIR Demand Fulfilled**: Yes\n   - **CIR Fulfillment Reported**: 1\n   - **MIR Demand Fulfilled**: Yes\n   - **MIR Fulfillment Reported**: 1\n   - **Comments**: Both CIR & MIR demand are met.\n\n7. **D > MIR**\n   - **CIR Demand Fulfilled**: Yes\n   - **CIR Fulfillment Reported**: 1\n   - **MIR Demand Fulfilled**: No\n   - **MIR Fulfillment Reported**: 0\n   - **Comments**: CIR demand met, MIR demand not met.\n\n8. **D > MIR**\n   - **CIR Demand Fulfilled**: No\n   - **CIR Fulfillment Reported**: 0\n   - **MIR Demand Fulfilled**: No\n   - **MIR Fulfillment Reported**: 0\n   - **Comments**: Neither CIR nor MIR demands are met.\n\n### Explanation:\n- The table categorizes different scenarios based on whether the CIR and MIR demands are fulfilled or not, and whether these fulfillments are reported.\n- The "Demand Level: D" column specifies the level of demand being considered.\n- The "CIR Demand Fulfilled" and "MIR Demand Fulfilled" columns indicate whether the respective demands are met.\n- The "CIR Fulfillment Reported" and "MIR Fulfillment Reported" columns indicate whether these fulfillments have been reported.\n- The "Comments" column provides additional explanations for each scenario.\n\nThis table is likely used in a business or operational context to track and report on the fulfillment of customer and minimum incentive rate demands at different levels of demand.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_23