26-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 402, 'image_path': '/Users/prathod/Projects/Rag_based_q-a_boat_over_own_doc/src/q&a_boat/figures/figure-402-290.jpg', 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'category': 'Image', 'element_id': 'ed6fde27ce97f4510a9d43fca756c0b5', 'source_image': '/Users/prathod/Projects/Rag_based_q-a_boat_over_own_doc/src/q&a_boat/figures/figure-402-290.jpg'}, page_content='[IMAGE DESCRIPTION]\nSource File: /Users/prathod/Projects/Rag_based_q-a_boat_over_own_doc/src/q&a_boat/figures/figure-402-290.jpg\nThe image illustrates a Satellite Virtual Network (SVN) architecture, which is a network design that uses satellite technology to connect various network segments. Here is a detailed description of the image:\n\n1. **Title**: The title at the top of the image reads "Satellite Virtual Network (SVN)".\n\n2. **Network Components**:\n   - **Left Side**: \n     - The network starts with "IPVPN" on the far left, indicating the initial point of the network.\n     - Moving right, it transitions to "MPLS IPVPN," which is a type of Virtual Private Network (VPN) that uses Multiprotocol Label Switching (MPLS) technology.\n     - Further right, it shows "VRFLite IPVPN (IP/VLAN)," which is another type of IPVPN that supports both IP and VLAN services.\n   - **Middle Section**:\n     - The network then moves through an "Ethernet" segment, which is a standard for local area networks (LANs).\n     - Following the Ethernet segment, there is a "Satellite" section, which indicates the use of satellite technology for communication.\n     - The satellite section includes "SAS LAN" and "OTA Satellite Network," which are likely abbreviations for specific satellite network components.\n     - The "PP" (Point-to-Point) connection is shown, which is a direct link between two points.\n   - **Right Side**:\n     - The network continues with another "Ethernet" segment.\n     - This is followed by "Terminal LAN," which is another LAN segment.\n     - The final part of the network shows "Terminal," which might be a device or system that connects to the network.\n     - The image ends with "Subnet" and a laptop icon, indicating the final destination of the network, which is a subnet and a connected device.\n\n3. **Arrows and Direction**:\n   - There are blue arrows at both ends of the image, pointing in opposite directions. The left arrow points from "IPVPN" to "MPLS IPVPN," and the right arrow points from "VRFLite IPVPN (IP/VLAN)" to "IP," indicating the flow of data or the direction of the network.\n\n4. **Other Elements**:\n   - The image includes icons of a laptop and a router, which are used to represent the devices and systems involved in the network.\n   - The overall diagram is a flowchart that visually represents the structure and components of a satellite-based virtual network.\n\nThis image is a comprehensive representation of a satellite-based network architecture, showing the various layers and technologies involved in creating a secure and efficient communication network.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(568.75), np.float64(1863.0208333333333)), (np.float64(568.75), np.float64(2388.020833333333)), (np.float64(2625.0), np.float64(2388.020833333333)), (np.float64(2625.0), np.float64(1863.0208333333333))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 402, 'image_path': '/Users/prathod/Projects/Rag_based_q-a_boat_over_own_doc/src/q&a_boat/figures/figure-402-291.jpg', 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'category': 'Image', 'elemen