'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 449, 'image_path': '/Users/prathod/Projects/Rag_based_q-a_boat_over_own_doc/src/q&a_boat/figures/figure-449-300.jpg', 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'category': 'Image', 'element_id': '357c728ff3b88030f6a69b4737a86e44', 'source_image': '/Users/prathod/Projects/Rag_based_q-a_boat_over_own_doc/src/q&a_boat/figures/figure-449-300.jpg'}, page_content='[IMAGE DESCRIPTION]\nSource File: /Users/prathod/Projects/Rag_based_q-a_boat_over_own_doc/src/q&a_boat/figures/figure-449-300.jpg\nThe image displays a terminal output from a command-line interface, specifically from a system named "sat_router." The command executed is `evtview -s -n 14`, which retrieves the last 14 events from a log file. The output is formatted in a tabular manner with three columns: Timestamp, Event, and Detail.\n\n### Detailed Description:\n\n1. **Timestamp Column:**\n   - The timestamps are in the format `YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM:SS`.\n   - The earliest timestamp is `May 30 18:33:31`.\n   - The latest timestamp is `May 30 19:13:23`.\n\n2. **Event Column:**\n   - The events listed are related to the modem\'s status and operations.\n   - The events are:\n     - `MODEM_STARTING_UP`\n     - `MODEM_STARTING_SEARCH_CYCLE`\n     - `MODEM_TRYING_SERVICE_CHANNEL`\n     - `MODEM_IN_NETWORK`\n     - `MODEM_NETKEY_CHANGE`\n\n3. **Detail Column:**\n   - This column provides additional information about the events.\n   - For the event `MODEM_STARTING_UP`, the detail states: "This terminal\'s modem software is starting up."\n   - For the event `MODEM_STARTING_SEARCH_CYCLE`, the detail states: "This terminal\'s modem is beginning a new carrier search cycle."\n   - For the event `MODEM_TRYING_SERVICE_CHANNEL`, the detail provides specific details:\n     - Satellite longitude: 1.0 degrees\n     - Satellite preference: 7\n     - Carrier frequency: 19925000 kHz\n     - Symbol rate: 10000 KSps\n     - Polarization (rx, tx): LR\n     - Modem location (lat, lon): (-10.1, 350.0)\n   - For the event `MODEM_IN_NETWORK`, the detail states: "This terminal is in network and authenticated on iNet 1471."\n   - For the event `MODEM_NETKEY_CHANGE`, the detail states: "This terminal is adjusting system time by 2238 seconds. Old: Thu May 30 18:36:05 2019. New: Thu May 30 19:13:23 2019."\n\n### Additional Information:\n- The command `evtview` is used to view event logs.\n- The `-s` option likely specifies the start of the log file.\n- The `-n 14` option specifies the number of events to display, which is 14 in this case.\n- The system name is `sat_router`, and the command is run from a user with the username `root` on a system named `iDirectCM`.\n\nThis output provides a chronological log of the modem\'s status and operations, including its attempt to connect to a satellite network and its authentication status.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(623.4375), np.float64(430.2083333333333)), (np.float64(623.4375), np.float64(1356.25)), (np.float64(2566.6666666666665), np.float64(1356.25)), (np.float64(2566.6666666666665), np.float64(430.2083333333333))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 450, 'image_path': '/Users/prathod/Projects/Rag_based_q-a_boat_over_own_doc/src/q&a_boat/figures/figure-450-301.jpg', 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'category': 'Image', 'element_id': '72e0c5d38c6bee004b479963582ff069', 'source_image': '/Users/prathod/Projects/Rag_based_q-a_boat_over_own_doc/src/q&a_boat/figures/figure-450-301.jpg'}, page_content='[IMAGE DESCRIPTION]\nSource File: /Users/prathod/Projects/Rag_based_q-a_boat_over_own_doc/src/q&a_boat/figures/figure-450-301.jpg\nThe image displays a terminal output from a Linux command-line interface, specifically showing the help documentation for the `evtview` tool. The text is formatted in a structured manner, with headings and descriptions for options and parameters.\n\n### Detailed Description:\n\n1. **Title:**\n   - The title at the top of the image reads: "how to use the event viewer tool."\n\n2. **Command Execution:**\n   - The command executed is: `root@iDirectCM:p5 common # evtview --help`\n   - This command is used to display the help documentation for the `evtview` tool.\n\n3. **Tool Name:**\n   - The tool name is: "Events Viewer Tool."\n\n4. **Usage:**\n   - The usage format is: `evtview [OPTIONS] [PARAMS]`\n\n5. **Options:**\n   - Each option is listed with its description:\n     - `-s, --show`: Converts most recent events to human-readable format and prints in a table.\n     - `-a, --all`: Converts all events to human-readable format and prints in a table.\n     - `-l, --log`: Converts all events to human-readable format and saves to output_file.\n     - `-h, --help`: Displays this help and exits.\n\n6. **Parameters:**\n   - Each parameter is listed with its description:\n     - `-i, --input_file <name>`: Reads events (in machine format) from this file. The default input file is `/common/events_record`.\n     - `-o, --output_file <name>`: Outputs events (in human-readable format) to this file. The default output file is `/tmp/events_record`.\n     - `-n, --number <number>`: Specifies the maximum number of events to show. The default is 10 events.\n\n7. **Prompt:**\n   - The command prompt at the bottom of the image is: `root@iDirectCM:p5 common #`\n\n### Additional Notes:\n- The background of the terminal is light green, and the text is in a dark color, which is typical for Linux terminal outputs.\n- The image does not contain any charts or diagrams; it is purely textual and command-based.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(590.625), np.float64(1764.5833333333333)), (np.float64(590.625), np.float64(1939.5833333333333)), (np.float64(765.6249999999999), np.float64(1939.5833333333333)), (np.float64(765.6249999999999), np.float64(1764.5833333333333))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 450, 'image_path': '/Users/prathod/Projects/Rag_based_q-a_boat_over_own_doc/src/q&a_boat/figures/figure-450-302.jpg', 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'category': 'Image', 'element_id': '87b392a8ce16136286a8b3116a3e4b31', 'source_image': '/Users/prathod/Projects/Rag_based_q-a_boat_over_own_doc/src/q&a_boat/figures/figure-450-302.jpg'}, page_content='[IMAGE DESCRIPTION]\nSource File: /Users/prathod/Projects/Rag_based_q-a_boat_over_own_doc/src/q&a_boat/figures/figure-450-302.jpg\nThe image appears to be a pixelated representation of a blue rectangular shape with a white interior. The edges of the rectangle are jagged, indicating that the image is low-resolution or has been pixelated. There is no text, numbers, charts, or diagrams visible within the rectangle. The overall appearance suggests that this might be a simplified or abstract representation of a shape, possibly a gift box or a similar object, given the shape and the way it is presented. The blue color could represent a ribbon or a bow, which is often associated with gift wrapping.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(707.2916666666666), np.float64(430.2083333333333)), (np.float64(707.2916666666666), np.float64(1308.8541666666665)), (np.float64(2482.8125), np.float64(1308.8541666666665)), (np.float64(2482.8125), np.float64(430.2083333333333))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 451, 'image_path': '/Users/prathod/Projects/Rag_based_q-a_boat_over_own_doc/src/q&a_boat/figures/figure-451-303.jpg', 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'category': 'Image', 'element_id': '76a70811a21981f94fed457c0d841384', 'source_image': '/Users/prathod/Projects/Rag_based_q-a_boat_over_own_doc/src/q&a_boat/figures/figure-451-303.jpg'}, page_content='[IMAGE DESCRIPTION]\nSource File: /Users/prathod/Projects/Rag_based_q-a_boat_over_own_doc/src/q&a_boat/figures/figure-451-303.jpg\nThe image is a screenshot of a system status dashboard from iDIRECT, a satellite communication company. The dashboard is divided into several sections, each providing different types of information about the system\'s status and performance.\n\n### Top Section:\n- **Header**: The top of the dashboard has a header with the iDIRECT logo on the left and several status indicators on the right. The indicators are labeled as NET, Status, Tx, Rx1, Rx2, TEMP, and Fan, with corresponding green and yellow lights. The green lights indicate that these components are functioning correctly, while the yellow light for TEMP (temperature) suggests a slight issue, as it is not fully green.\n\n### Main Section:\n- **System Status**:\n  - **Link Status**:\n    - **Network Status**: IN_NETWORK\n    - **Satellite Receiver**: Locked\n    - **Satellite Transmitter**: UNMUTED\n    - **Receive SNR**: 10.8 dB\n  - **Receiver SNR (primary)**: Displays a graph with a value of 11, indicating the Signal-to-Noise Ratio of the primary receiver. The graph shows the SNR over time, with a timestamp of 12:02:02.685.\n  - **Terminal Information**:\n    - **Model Type**: AM-MCL-MCS(146)\n    - **RF Terminal Type**: 6000\n    - **Serial Number**: 1662\n    - **Software Version**: VELOCITY - 2.0.0.0 1363\n    - **Terminal Provisioning Key**: CQAAM7QKAX24U==\n\n### Device Status:\n- **CPU Load**: 8.59%\n- **Memory Use**: 90.24%\n- **Temperature**: 39°C\n\n### Terminal Events:\n- The events are listed with timestamps and descriptions:\n  - **1min 31sec**: MODEM_IN_NETWORK\n  - **28sec**: MODEM_TRYING_SERVICE_CHANNEL\n  - **21sec**: MODEM_STARTING_SEARCH_CYCLE\n  - **8sec**: MODEM_STARTING_UP\n\n### Navigation and Additional Options:\n- The top navigation bar includes options such as Dashboard, Details, Commissioning, Administration, and an admin dropdown.\n- On the right side, there is a section titled "Take me to..." with links to "View Satellite Details," "View Terminal Details," and "View current LAN throughput."\n\n### Overall:\nThe dashboard provides a comprehensive overview of the system\'s status, including network connectivity, receiver performance, terminal details, device status, and recent events. The use of graphs and percentages helps in visualizing the system\'s health and performance.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(988.0208333333333), np.float64(998.9583333333333)), (np.float64(988.0208333333333), np.float64(2552.083333333333)), (np.float64(2202.083333333333), np.float64(2552.083333333333)), (np.float64(2202.083333333333), np.float64(998.9583333333333))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 452, 'image_path': '/Users/prathod/Projects/Rag_based_q-a_boat_over_own_doc/src/q&a_boat/figures/figure-452-304.jpg', 'file_directory': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T', 'filename': 'rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'category': 'Image', 'element_id': '791b86b9a7323eaa19c39ca484080d2c', 'source_image': '/Users/prathod/Projects/Rag_based_q-a_boat_over_own_doc/src/q&a_boat/figures/figure-452-304.jpg'}, page_content='[IMAGE DESCRIPTION]\nSource File: /Users/prathod/Projects/Rag_based_q-a_boat_over_own_doc/src/q&a_boat/figures/figure-452-304.jpg\nThe image appears to be a screenshot of a system event log or status report, likely from a network or communication device. Here\'s a detailed description:\n\n1. **Header**:\n   - The top of the image shows a timestamp: `[18:25:42:609841]`.\n   - Below the timestamp, it says "Events snapshot:".\n\n2. **System Status**:\n   - The system has started up successfully, as indicated by "STARTED UP OK? PASS".\n   - The hardware is functioning correctly, with "SELF TEST PASSED? PASS".\n   - The RX IFL (Input/Forward Link) and TX IFL (Input/Forward Link) connections are confirmed as "PASS".\n   - The temperature is within acceptable limits, as indicated by "TEMPERATURE OK? PASS".\n\n3. **ACU (Access Control Unit) Status**:\n   - The ACU is operational, as shown by "ACU OK? PASS".\n   - Communication with the ACU is confirmed, "COMMUNICATING WITH ACU? PASS".\n\n4. **BUC (Block Upconverter) Status**:\n   - The BUC is operational, "BUC OK? PASS".\n   - Communication with the BUC is confirmed, "COMMUNICATING WITH BUC? N/A".\n   - The BUC has reported no errors, "BUC REPORTED NO ERRORS? N/A".\n   - The BUC is calibrated, "BUC IS CALIBRATED? PASS".\n\n5. **Transmitter Status**:\n   - The transmitter is operational, "Transmitter OK? PASS".\n   - The transmitter is unmuted, "TX UNMUTED? PASS".\n\n6. **Carrier Selection Process**:\n   - The carrier search is in progress, "CARRIER SEARCH IN PROGRESS? PASS".\n   - The device is attempting to download an OTA (Over-the-Air) beam map, "ATTEMPTING TO DOWNLOAD AN OTA BEAM MAP? N/A".\n   - The device is attempting to come into the network, "ATTEMPTING TO COME INTO NETWORK? PASS".\n   - ACU lock is confirmed, "ACU_LOCK? PASS".\n   - Downstream lock is confirmed, "DOWNSTREAM_LOCK? PASS".\n   - A valid SI table has been received, "VALID_SI_TABLE_RECEIVED? PASS".\n   - A valid upstream carrier has been found, "VALID_UPSTREAM_CARRIER_FOUND? PASS".\n   - The transmitter is unmuted, "TX_UNMUTE? PASS".\n   - An acquisition burst has been sent, "ACQ_BURST_SENT? PASS".\n   - An acquisition response has been received, "ACQ_RESPONSE_RECEIVED? PASS".\n   - A traffic slot has been allocated, "TRAFFIC_SLOT_ALLOCATED? PASS".\n   - UCPS (User Control and Protocol Stack) has been received, "UCPS_RECEIVED? PENDING".\n   - BTPS (Block Transfer Protocol Stack) has been received, "BTPS_RECEIVED? PENDING".\n   - Authentication is pending, "AUTHENTICATION? PENDING".\n\n7. **Summary**:\n   - The system is not in the network, as indicated by "IN NETWORK? FAIL".\n\n8. **Footer**:\n   - The footer contains a timestamp: `[18:25:46:057824]`.\n   - It also includes a message: "Authentication succeeded".\n\nThe image is primarily text-based with no charts or diagrams. The status of each item is indicated by "PASS", "N/A" (Not Applicable), or "PENDING". The "FAIL" in the summary indicates a critical issue.'), Document(metadata={'source': '/var/folders/5z/p05w2vpj7b90clpntd1kvyp80000gp/T/rag_upload_2390dad9058e9d21ffdcdecf211d325c.pdf', 'coordinates': {'points': ((np.float64(612.5), np.float64(430.2083333333333)), (np.float64(612.5), np.float64(1771.8749999999998)), (np.float64(2581.25), np.float64(1771.8749999999998)), (np.float64(2581.25), np.float64(430.2083333333333))), 'system': 'PixelSpace', 'layout_width': 2975, 'layout_height': 3850}, 'last_modified': '2026-08-24T13:52:40', 'filetype': 'application/pdf', 'languages': ['eng'], 'page_number': 453, 'image_path': '/Users/prathod/Projects/Rag_based_q-a_boat_over_own_doc/src/q&a_boat/figures/figure-453-305.jpg', 'file_directory':